window.AKK_ZEN_HAREM_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_ZEN_HAREM_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":101,"title":"Chapter 101","paragraphs":["The Empress had been ill for quite some time and only began to recover after the twelfth lunar month began.","Now that the Empress was better, the authority to manage the Six Palaces naturally should be returned to her. On this day, Consort Ning brought the account books from the past few months to the Kunning Palace.","Before even entering the main hall, she saw Ju Yi, one of the Empress's attendants, limping along the corridor.","Meeting Consort Ning, Ju Yi bowed: \"This servant pays her respects to Consort Ning.\"","Consort Ning looked at her curiously: \"Isn't this Ju Yi? Your leg... when was it injured?\"","Being watched, Ju Yi instinctively drew her leg back, her expression also somewhat uncomfortable.","That day, she had rushed into the hall to tell the Empress about the incident of the Marquis of Cheng'en falling from his horse, causing Her Majesty to become so agitated she spat up blood. When the Emperor found out, he ordered her dragged out and given thirty solid strokes of the cane. The beating was severe; she had been bedridden for months and had only been able to get up and move around a few days prior.","Although she could move now, her leg had been left with a lasting problem, and her gait was now rather unsightly.","Seeing her reluctance to speak, Consort Ning didn't press further, merely expressing regret: \"Has Her Majesty the Empress had a physician examine you? Is there any medicine for it?\"","Ju Yi pressed her lips together. The Empress had been ill and listless lately, and hadn't the energy to attend to such matters. She had heard about the beating, of course, and had instructed Mei Yi to send some medicinal ointment over, telling Ju Yi to rest well and resume her duties only after recovering.","Ju Yi did wish the Empress would request a physician for her, but having just been punished, she didn't dare be presumptuous again. She could only wait for a future opportunity to beg the Empress.","\"This Consort happens to have an excellent ointment. I'll have Yang Xue send it over to you later.\"","Ju Yi kept her head lowered. \"This servant's status is lowly. I do not deserve such kindness from Consort Ning.\"","\"Where do such words come from? You are a senior palace maid serving Her Majesty the Empress. I recall the Empress has always valued you highly. Currently... she has merely been temporarily distracted. Once she has more leisure in the future, she will certainly summon a physician for you. Even setting Her Majesty aside, this Consort herself cannot bear to see you suffer. You are so young; if your leg truly becomes permanently disabled, it will likely be difficult for you to marry after leaving the palace.\"","Hearing Consort Ning's words, Ju Yi's eyes gradually grew moist. Because of the incident with the Empress spitting blood, everyone in the Kunning Palace had been giving her the cold shoulder these past days. They used to call her \"Sister Ju Yi,\" but now? Even the little eunuch guarding the gate dared to gossip about her behind her back.","And then there was Mei Yi, always playing the good-natured one. In the past, she had been so close, calling her 'sister.' But after Ju Yi was caned, Mei Yi said with a cold face: \"Don't blame me for not protecting you. Knowing Her Majesty was ill, how could you just blurt out the news about the Marquis of Cheng'en? It's only because nothing worse happened, and His Majesty considered how Her Majesty usually dotes on you, that your head is still on your shoulders!\"","\"I've told you many times before, think before you act, avoid impulsiveness. That day, I was right outside. I don't believe you didn't see me. If only you had spoken to me first, we could have discussed and carefully considered how to break the news to Her Majesty. You would never have ended up lying here like this!\"","\"Spend these days resting in your room and think it over properly!\"","During these months of recuperation, Mei Yi visited her very little, and even Lan Yi and Zhu Yi paid her scant attention.","It showed how false their affections were!","Ju Yi harbored resentment in her heart, forgetting that Mei Yi was busy caring for the Empress, Lan Yi was occupied with the Second Prince, and Zhu Yi with the Eldest Princess. Where would they find the energy to fuss over her? After all, she was recuperating within the Kunning Palace, she lacked no medicine, and if she was ever hungry or thirsty, she could always order a junior maid to help.","Ju Yi overlooked all this, feeling only that these so-called sisters were less caring than Consort Ning.","\"In my condition, how can I still hope to marry?\"","Consort Ning: \"Don't say such things. Ah, it truly is a pity. Among the four of you, I've always thought your looks were the finest. If not for this injury, after leaving the palace you could have even become an official's wife...\"","The more she spoke like this, the more resentment grew in Ju Yi's heart. She resented her loyal service being repaid with a caning. She resented Mei Yi and the others not pleading for leniency after her single mistake. She resented the Empress, who knew she was injured like this, for not summoning a physician, letting her be left with a permanent ailment.","Seeing Ju Yi's expression, Consort Ning's gaze turned thoughtful. Noticing the main hall door opening and someone coming out, she said no more. \"Enough. This Consort's father does have a few protégés. Their backgrounds are humble, but they are talented and handsome men. When the time comes for you to leave service, this Consort would be willing to mention it to the Empress. It would be a good deed.\"","Ju Yi's eyes lit up. She would be twenty-four next year!","\"In your free time, you can also come to the Yikun Palace to chat with Yang Xue and the others.\" Consort Ning said with a faint smile, walking towards the main hall.","Mei Yi had just come out of the hall and bowed to her.","\"Yes, this Consort is here to return the various account books.\"","\"Consort Ning may go right in. Her Majesty the Empress is waiting.\" Mei Yi waited until Consort Ning entered before seeking out Ju Yi. \"What did Consort Ning just say to you?\"","Ju Yi had already composed her expression, her mouth quirking slightly. \"She just saw my leg and asked a few questions.\"","Mentioning her leg, Mei Yi showed a smile. \"Her Majesty just told me she plans to summon Physician Mao, who specializes in bone injuries, to examine you.\"","\"Ju Yi, after this incident, you should learn to be more steady. We of the Kunning Palace serve Her Majesty the Empress after all. Especially you and Zhu Yi, who have served Her Majesty since the Eastern Palace days. Zhu Yi is meticulous, so Her Majesty assigned her to care for the Eldest Princess. You are quick-witted, but you often act without considering the consequences. How can Her Majesty entrust important matters to you like this?\"","Mei Yi was speaking to her with almost brutal frankness, wanting to tell her that Her Majesty had not given up on her and still had high hopes for her. But in Ju Yi's ears, it sounded like: she was not as good as Zhu Yi.","\"Ju Yi, you...\"","\"Sister Mei Yi!\" Ju Yi interrupted her, her voice carrying a barely detectable sob and a thread of resentment. \"I still need to go to the tea room to give instructions. Let's talk later.\"","Mei Yi: \"Very well. Go quickly and return soon.\"","Having handed over her responsibilities, Qi Daiyu reverted to being the idler she was.","It happened to be snowing, so there was no need to go for morning greetings. She could sleep until the sun was high in the sky.","Shiliu and the others knew she had been exhausted recently and felt sorry for her, letting her sleep.","Every morning, Yanqing Residence was quiet, only springing to life when there was movement from the main chamber, the servants then beginning to move about with more noise.","On this day, Qi Daiyu was sleeping soundly when Shiliu shook her awake.","\"What is it?\" she asked blearily, seeing it was still dark outside.","Shiliu: \"Consort Zhuang has gone into labor!\"","Qi Daiyu jolted, instantly awake, sitting up to look for her shoes. \"Wasn't it supposed to be some days later?\"","Yanhe half-knelt to help her put on her shoes. \"There's no fixed timing for a woman giving birth. Once the time is near, it can happen anytime.\"","Without putting on makeup, she hastily pinned up her hair, changed her clothes, and headed out. Shiliu fastened the ties of her cloak as they walked.","\"Take the hand warmer too!\" Putao hurriedly stuffed a hand warmer into Qi Daiyu's arms.","Fortunately, the Changchun Palace and the Qixiang Palace were close by, so Qi Daiyu was the first to arrive. The Qixiang Palace was already bustling with activity.","Qi Daiyu had just arrived when Ye Qiong came right after her, her attire also suggesting a hurried departure.","\"Sister Qi!\"","For the moment, there was no time to speak with her. Qi Daiyu went straight to the delivery room. Afraid the chill on her clothes might cause a disturbance, she only asked from outside her cloak, \"Sister Zhu, are you alright?\"","Qin Saizhu's voice sounded quite spirited. \"Yu'er, you're here. I'm fine! The delivery room was prepared long ago, and the midwives have been staying here at Qixiang Palace. Everything is under control!\" As soon as her water broke, they had immediately moved her into the delivery room.","\"The midwife says it will still be a long while before the baby comes. You should go back and get some sleep!\"","Hearing she still had the energy to joke, Qi Daiyu felt a wave of relief. \"How could I possibly sleep now! The imperial physician should be here soon, and His Majesty and Her Majesty the Empress are likely on their way.\"","Qin Saizhu wasn't in much pain at this moment and could still laugh. \"Then you help me receive His Majesty and Her Majesty the Empress!\"","Qi Daiyu knew nothing about delivering babies and was afraid of being in the way, so she didn't dare stay long.","Once outside, Ye Qiong came up to her. \"How is Sister Qin?\"","Qi Daiyu stopped her from going in. \"She seems well. You shouldn't go in either. The wind is strong outside, and the curtain opening and closing might let in a draft.\"","Ye Qiong's expression faltered slightly. \"Alright! Then I'll stay with you, sister.\"","Qi Daiyu had Shiliu and the others help tidy up the main hall first. The Emperor and Empress would surely sit there for a while when they arrived. Ye Qiong stayed by her side.","The Emperor had spent the night at Chaorong's place. Upon receiving the news, he rushed over immediately, with Chaorong following. On the way, they met the Empress, and the three of them entered together. As soon as the Empress arrived, she took charge of all matters in Qixiang Palace.","Nie Zhiyu had also sent someone to check, but as she was pregnant herself, the Empress instructed her to rest in her own palace. Notices were sent to the other consorts as well, telling them not to come.","As the sky gradually lightened, there was still no movement from the delivery room.","A midwife came out and said, \"Consort Zhuang is having her first child. I'm afraid it will still be quite some time.\"","The Empress smiled. \"It seems this child is of a slow and steady nature.\"","Jiang Yuan already knew Consort Zhuang was carrying a princess. He thought it wasn't bad for a princess to have a calm temperament; it meant she would be gentle and quiet.","He still had to attend the morning court session, so he entrusted her care to the Empress.","\"Your Majesty, rest assured. I will keep watch.\"","By the time the morning court session ended, Consort Zhuang still hadn't gone into active labor. The Empress Dowager came once, but seeing it was still early, she left again. Other consorts also came and went. Only Consort Ning stayed a little longer.","Ye Qiong merely followed behind Qi Daiyu, not daring to look at her.","Consort Ning turned her head and glanced at Yangxue. Yangxue gave an almost imperceptible nod. Consort Ning then said to the Empress, \"Your Majesty, would you like to go back and rest for a while? Let your servant keep watch.\"","The Empress was indeed feeling somewhat fatigued. Seeing it was still early, she nodded. \"I will return in two hours.\"","Passing by Qi Daiyu, the Empress said, \"Noble Lady Hui, you should go rest for a while too.\"","Qi Daiyu shook her head. \"This concubine is fine. I'll stay here. If anything is needed, I can help promptly.\"","Knowing she was close to Consort Zhuang, the Empress didn't insist.","She only instructed the servants to replenish the charcoal in the hall to ensure no one would catch cold.","Qi Daiyu naturally refused to leave. Although the palace appeared harmonious now, and Qin Saizhu was carrying a princess—theoretically, no one should target her—Qi Daiyu wasn't at ease. She had to keep watch personally to feel secure.","Not only did she keep watch outside, she also sent Yanhe into the delivery room. Yanhe was older and had experience caring for a princess, so there was no taboo against her presence.","At one point, Consort Ning went to freshen up.","\"How is it?\" Consort Ning asked in a low voice.","Yangxue replied, \"Lady Ye likely won't make a move. Noble Lady Hui has sent her maid into the delivery room. It's really not a good opportunity to act...\"","Consort Ning showed no urgency. \"Then forget it. Don't alert anyone. We'll think of another way later.\"","Yangxue: \"Yes.\"","The sky gradually darkened, and snow began to fall once more, unnoticed.","Inside the delivery room, after having another bowl of shredded chicken noodles, Qin Saizhu finally began to feel intense pain.","The Qixiang Palace suddenly became noisy and bustling."]},{"number":102,"title":"Chapter 102","paragraphs":["From the early hours of the morning until late at night, Qi Daiyu had sat for almost an entire day, even having her meals hastily delivered to the main hall. After resting, the Empress returned to relieve Consort Ning. Seeing the exhaustion on Qi Daiyu's face, she once again urged her to go back and rest.","Qi Daiyu shook her head. \"I've waited this long; a little longer won't matter now.\"","She looked anxiously towards the birthing chamber.","Two hours had passed since the first signs of labor began, yet Qin Saizhu still had not given birth. Even the Empress, no longer as composed as she initially was, had sent people in several times to check on the situation. The Empress Dowager's attendant, Nanny Zhao, had also come by a few times.","Shortly after the Chou hour (1-3 AM), Jiang Yuan arrived as well.","The Empress bowed. \"Your Majesty, why have you come?\"","Jiang Yuan: \"I couldn't sleep, so I thought I'd come and see.\"","Just then, a royal physician hurried out. Frowning, Jiang Yuan asked him, \"How is Consort Zhuang?\"","The physician's forehead was beaded with sweat. \"Consort Zhuang is having a difficult labor. If this continues, it is very dangerous. This humble servant suggests using a labor-inducing decoction.\" Childbirth was perilous for women, especially first-time mothers. If the baby could not be delivered and too much time passed, both mother and child were at risk.","Upon hearing this, the Empress asked, \"Would this decoction harm the child?\"","The imperial physician kept his head bowed. \"As it is medicinal, its purpose is to help Consort Zhuang deliver the child more quickly.\" All medicine carried some risk, and labor-inducing decoctions were particularly potent, causing greater harm to Consort Zhuang's body. But given the current circumstances, there was no other choice. Saving her life was paramount; everything else was secondary.","Jiang Yuan made the decision immediately. \"Administer the medicine.\"","“Yes, Your Majesty!” The imperial physician was about to retreat when he stopped. “Your Majesty, if... if the situation becomes critical, should we prioritize saving Consort Zhuang or the young prince or princess?”","The hall fell silent. Qi Daiyu stared fixedly at Jiang Yuan, her hands involuntarily clutching her sleeves, terrified she might hear a heartless word from him.","Fortunately, Qin Saizhu held a place in Jiang Yuan's heart. \"Neither Consort Zhuang nor the child is to come to harm, especially Consort Zhuang!\"","These words made his stance clear. The imperial physician, now understanding the priority, hurried off to prepare the medicine.","It will be fine, it will be fine. Qi Daiyu comforted herself inwardly, her mind in turmoil. She frantically searched the \"light screen\" for all possible dangers during childbirth, the variety of answers turning her face pale.","Even in her original world, with its advanced technology, childbirth was never one hundred percent safe. Given Qin Saizhu's current situation, how could she not worry?","The snow fell heavier and heavier. The cries of pain from Qin Saizhu in the birthing chamber grew clearer and louder, interspersed with the midwife's urgent instructions and the worried comforting words of her maids, Zhi Ma and Xiang Chun.","It was extremely chaotic.","Outside the chamber, however, there was a restless, tense silence.","Until a loud, clear cry pierced through Qixiang Palace, shattering the quiet.","Qi Daiyu's eyes lit up.","\"She's given birth! Consort Zhuang has given birth!\"","\"It's a princess! She has borne a little princess!\"","One person after another came out to announce the joyous news. A weight lifted from Jiang Yuan's heart, and a smile appeared on his face. \"A princess is good! A princess is wonderful!\"","The Empress also smiled. \"The Eldest and Second Princesses will have a companion now!\"","Soon, the newborn Third Princess was brought out, swaddled tightly. \"Your Majesty, Your Majesty the Empress, the Third Princess is healthy and strong! Her little legs are full of vigor, and her cries are loud!\"","A corner of the swaddling cloth was lifted, revealing the tiny, red-faced infant crying lustily.","Jiang Yuan took the Third Princess from the midwife. \"She must weigh nearly seven catties!\"","Such a robust size explained why Consort Zhuang's labor had been so difficult.","The Empress said, \"It's good to be robust. She'll be easier to raise and less prone to illness later.\"","Noticing Qi Daiyu still standing in place, she asked curiously, \"Consort Hui, won't you come and take a look?\"","But Qi Daiyu said, \"Your Majesty the Empress, how is... Consort Zhuang?\" She had only seen one midwife come out with the princess. Where were the others?","The Empress was taken aback. Yes, in the joy of the Third Princess's birth, what about Consort Zhuang?","It seemed only then that sounds from the birthing chamber reached them—it was Zhi Ma's shocked cry: \"Mistress!\"","The next moment, a midwife stumbled out. \"Your Majesty, it's terrible! Consort Zhuang... the bleeding beneath Consort Zhuang won't stop...\"","\"What did you say?!\" Qi Daiyu and Jiang Yuan spoke almost simultaneously.","The midwife kowtowed repeatedly. \"Consort Zhuang is likely... is likely...\" Her whole body trembled. When she left, Consort Zhuang was already barely breathing.","Jiang Yuan kicked out at her. \"You're all useless! Where is the imperial physician? Imperial physician!\"","The imperial physician hurried out and knelt, merely shaking his head. \"It's too late...\" The labor-inducing medicine had accelerated the birth process, but it had also caused Consort Zhuang to expend her vital energy. The bleeding below wouldn't cease. He had administered medicine to stanch the bleeding and replenish blood, but the rate of blood loss far outpaced the medicine's effect...","The Third Princess was born safely, but Consort Zhuang... The imperial physician's face was ashen. He knew his head was likely forfeit.","Yet childbirth was inherently perilous; countless mothers fell at this hurdle, some even losing both mother and child. But this was something His Majesty probably would not listen to.","The Taiyi prostrated himself on the ground. \"Consort Zhuang may still have words to say...\" That was all he could offer, hoping the Emperor might spare his family out of regard for his past loyalty.","Jiang Yuan still refused to accept it, but the Empress was much calmer. \"Your Majesty, this humble servant will go in to see Consort Zhuang.\"","Jiang Yuan gave no response. The Empress then walked towards the birthing chamber, pausing as she passed Qi Daiyu. \"Consort Hui, would you like to accompany me inside?\"","Qi Daiyu stood rooted to the spot, unmoving.","She could hear nothing, the words \"Consort Zhuang is failing!\" echoing in her ears.","How could it be... how could it...","It felt as if all the blood in her body had frozen solid. Despite the blazing braziers in the hall, she felt a bone-chilling cold.","Scene after scene flashed before her eyes: The first time she met Qin Saizhu, hearing her hearty laughter before even seeing her, piquing her curiosity. Then the curtain was lifted, revealing a cheerful, round face with dimples—she felt an immediate fondness.","Scenes of the two of them admiring the snow, grilling meat, drinking, and chatting merrily—it seemed to have been a snowy day like this one too.","Her leaning over Qin Saizhu's round, protruding belly to listen for the baby's movements, the two of them discussing what nickname to give the unborn child. Qin Saizhu had even said that after the birth, she wanted to eat the spiciest, most numbing hotpot...","How could it be... how could someone she was laughing with just yesterday be...","The Empress called Qi Daiyu's name once more.","Qi Daiyu blinked. She tried to speak but found no words would come. She could only lift her stiff feet and follow behind the Empress.","She almost stumbled into the birthing chamber.","Upon entering, she was met with an overwhelming, thick scent of blood.","The smell nearly suffocated Qi Daiyu. Her heart felt gripped by a giant hand, making it hard to breathe.","She hardly dared look at the figure on the bed. In just a few short hours, Qin Saizhu's face had grown deathly pale, her eyes terribly swollen.","\"Yu... Yu'er...\" Qin Saizhu struggled to utter a few words, her voice barely a whisper. It was Zhi Ma, kneeling beside her, who heard and cried out, \"Noble Lady Hui, my mistress is calling for you.\"","Qi Daiyu threw herself by the bedside, grasping Qin Saizhu's hand. It was colder than the snow outside.","\"Pearl Sister, I'm here! I'm here!\" Qi Daiyu wanted to say these words, but they stuck in her throat. Tears flowed uncontrollably, dripping onto Qin Saizhu's hand.","Qin Saizhu seemed to sense her speechlessness and forced a faint, strained smile.","\"My child... my child... I entrust to you...\"","\"Help me... help...\"","Her voice was so faint Qi Daiyu had to tilt her head and press her ear close to Qin Saizhu's lips to hear. But after only a few words, the sound ceased, and the hand in her grasp seemed to grow colder still.","\"......\" Qi Daiyu realized what had happened but dared not look up, only clutching the hand tighter.","The women in the delivery room began to weep, their sobs mingling with the Empress's sigh.","Zhi Ma and Xiang Chun wept bitterly, overcome with grief.","Qi Daiyu remained in that position, letting her tears fall.","She did not know how she left the delivery room.","She heard Zhi Ma kneeling on the floor, reporting to the Emperor: \"...My mistress and Noble Lady Hui were always close. Before her passing... my mistress begged Your Majesty to entrust the Third Princess to Noble Lady Hui's care. Please, Your Majesty, grant my mistress her final wish, in recognition of her years of service.\"","She heard the Empress also advise the Emperor: \"Your Majesty, however much you grieve for Consort Zhuang, we must consider the Third Princess. She is still so young and cannot be without care.\"","She heard Jiang Yuan decree: \"Posthumously elevate Consort Zhuang to the rank of Noble Consort Zhuang. She shall be buried with the full honors of her rank and interred in the imperial mausoleum.\"","\"The Third Princess shall be entrusted to Noble Lady Hui for rearing. Noble Lady Hui is hereby elevated to the rank of Consort Hui and shall move to the main hall of the Changchun Palace.\"","\"Consort Hui, will you not thank His Majesty for his grace?\" The Empress quietly tugged at Qi Daiyu's sleeve.","Qi Daiyu woodenly performed the ritual bow. \"I thank Your Majesty for your grace.\"","\"Consort Zhuang is gone?\" Consort Ning asked in surprise, pulling her quilt around her. News of the Third Princess's birth had just arrived, followed closely by the report of Consort Zhuang's death—no, she should now be called \"Noble Consort Zhuang.\"","Yang Xue nodded, her own heart unsettled. \"They say it was a hemorrhage that couldn't be stopped... My lady, our people did not act.\"","Qin Saizhu had overheard her mistress's conversation with the Grand Princess Yanping. To eliminate the threat, Consort Ning naturally could not let Qin Saizhu live.","Qin Saizhu's childbirth had presented the perfect opportunity.","However, Ye Qiong's side had backed down, and while she herself had a backup plan—Yang Xue had previously bribed a midwife—Qi Daiyu had sent Yan He to guard the delivery room, specifically watching the midwives. Unwilling to risk exposure, Consort Ning had called off the plan.","She had thought there would be other chances later.","Who could have guessed that without her lifting a finger, Consort Zhuang had still died.","Thinking of this, Consort Ning gave a light laugh. \"It seems even Heaven is aiding me.\"","Yang Xue was still marveling. \"This Noble Consort Zhuang was truly unfortunate. After serving His Majesty for years and finally conceiving, she made it all the way to delivery, gave birth, but didn't survive herself.\"","Although the Emperor had elevated her rank to Noble Consort Zhuang on the spot, rather than posthumously, granting her that honor, what use was a title when the person was gone?","\"As for Consort Hui, her luck is good. She gained a princess for nothing and was promoted in rank.\" Now she was the mistress of her own palace.","Yang Xue couldn't help but think with some malice: They all say Consort Hui cannot bear children due to old injuries. Could she have deliberately gotten close to Consort Zhuang for this?","Consort Ning glanced at her. Yang Xue didn't understand, but she knew well the dangers of childbirth for women; otherwise, she wouldn't have planned to act during Qin Saizhu's labor.","Without explaining, Consort Ning got out of bed and walked to a specially arranged incense table. She moved the Buddha statue aside, hung up a portrait of Lady Yang, closed her eyes, and pressed her palms together.","After a long while, she opened her eyes and asked Yang Xue, \"Has Ju Yi come during this time?\"","Yang Xue nodded. \"Once. As you instructed, I did not act overly familiar. I just gave her the ointment and expressed some sympathy for her plight.\"","\"Good. She will come again. Treat her as usual.\" Consort Ning said, \"Also, find time to go to the Qixiang Palace. Tell her I wish to see her.\""]},{"number":103,"title":"Chapter 103","paragraphs":["In the western side hall of Qixiang Palace, Ye Qiong sat on the couch wrapped in a quilt.","The clamor from the main hall drifted over faintly.","She had originally intended to stay there and keep watch, but the Empress said the weather was bitterly cold and that one more or one less person made no difference, instructing her to return to her own palace to rest.","Ye Qiong had matters weighing on her mind and did not decline.","Returning to her own bedchamber, she sent Xia Zhi and the others to the main hall to help. Only when she was alone in the room did she cover her face with her hands.","Today, she had intended to make a move against Consort Zhuang...","Fortunately, Noble Lady Hui had stopped her.","If possible, she didn't want to harm Consort Zhuang either. After all, since entering the palace and living in Qixiang Palace, she had indeed received much care from Consort Zhuang.","However, she had already secretly pledged herself to Consort Ning, and she had to follow Consort Ning's orders.","But, did she truly have no selfish motives at all? Ye Qiong mocked herself. If she were completely selfless, why would she have sought Consort Ning's patronage?","Yet, what else could she do? She had entered this palace solely for glory and favor; she was never a kind-hearted person to begin with. Just because Consort Zhuang and Noble Lady Hui thought she was kind, did she really have to be kind? And what use was kindness in this palace? The Emperor wouldn't favor her just because she was kind.","Over a year since entering the palace, among the four most outstanding candidates from the selection, Nie Zhiyu was already a Jieyu and now pregnant, her future promotion predictable; Zhaorong had also become a Meiren, equal in rank to her; Feng Qi, though still a Cairen, received visits from the Emperor to her palace from time to time.","Only she remained.","Ye Qiong counted in her heart: in over a year since entering the palace, the Emperor had come to her place only three times. Apart from the first night of attendance, the other two visits were likely due to the Empress's admonitions. Even when he came, there was no tenderness, as if he were merely fulfilling a duty.","Ye Qiong didn't understand. In terms of looks or talent, she believed she was no worse than the others. Why did the Emperor simply not like her?","What Ye Qiong didn't know was that the Emperor favored those who were bright and charming, gorgeous and voluptuous, and also accepted those who were dignified and graceful, serene and gentle—he simply did not care for the delicate, soft, and submissive type.","And Ye Qiong happened to possess precisely that delicate, soft beauty. The Emperor didn't favor this type; he had only taken her into the palace back then after hearing the Empress praise her character during the selection.","But dislike was dislike. No matter how good Ye Qiong was, Jiang Yuan's first impression of her was poor, so naturally he wouldn't waste time getting to know her better, and thus never discovered her good qualities.","And so, Ye Qiong was gradually neglected.","Ye Qiong had entered the palace for favor and glory, so she was naturally unwilling to be ignored. She had originally thought that being assigned to Qixiang Palace, where Consort Zhuang had long enjoyed favor, might allow her to bask in some reflected glory. Yet, knowing full well the Emperor rarely came to her, Consort Zhuang had never once schemed on her behalf.","Of course, Consort Zhuang had favor herself; why would she need to share it?","Ye Qiong had also tried to seek the Empress's patronage, but the Empress had already chosen Nie Zhiyu and responded to her overtures with indifference.","As for Consort Shu? Ye Qiong hadn't even considered her.","Ye Qiong told herself not to worry; she would find an opportunity.","The opportunity came quickly. She accidentally witnessed a quarrel between Consort Ning and her younger sister and overheard a secret.","Ye Qiong had learned about Consort Ning. She came from a great clan, her family noble and prestigious, her father the current Prime Minister. She was first a Crown Prince's concubine, later becoming Consort Ning. Consort Ning was known as a \"talented woman,\" a person who emphasized rules, neither befriending nor making enemies with others. The Emperor, Empress Dowager, and Empress all trusted her greatly, even entrusting her with matters like palace banquets. She was a \"special person\" in the palace.","But such a person shared one thing in common with Ye Qiong: she lacked the Emperor's favor.","There were various rumors among the palace servants about why Consort Ning was not favored. One said her looks were plain and the Emperor didn't like her; another said the Emperor wanted to depose the Prime Minister, so he couldn't favor the Prime Minister's daughter; there was even a rumor that Consort Ning had nearly become the Crown Princess Consort back then, and the Empress, jealous, forbade the Emperor from favoring Consort Ning...","The truth amidst these rumors was unclear, but Ye Qiong most believed that Consort Ning's appearance was not to the Emperor's liking.","Ye Qiong thought: Consort Ning had status and family but lacked beauty, while she herself had fair looks and only lacked an opportunity. Allying with Consort Ning might be a path.","However, Consort Ning proved much harder to approach than Ye Qiong imagined. It took Ye Qiong a long time and effort to secretly establish contact with Consort Ning, but even then, Consort Ning was slow to agree to help her.","Ye Qiong didn't want to lose more than she gained, so she still maintained good relations with Consort Zhuang, Noble Lady Hui, and others. But the better the relations, the more resentful she grew inside. Only she, only she was not favored.","After Consort Zhuang became pregnant, Ye Qiong's dissatisfaction grew even stronger.","She had thought that since Consort Zhuang was pregnant, perhaps her own opportunity had come. After all, Consort Zhuang couldn't attend to the Emperor while pregnant; if she could steer the Emperor to her, wouldn't that be a way to secure favor? But Consort Zhuang never mentioned it once.","Ye Qiong considered that maybe Consort Zhuang hadn't thought of it. She even specially sent over a plate of pastries she had made, which Consort Zhuang loved, on an occasion when the Emperor was dining in the main hall. Yet the Emperor still didn't come; Consort Zhuang must not have spoken up for her.","Ye Qiong began to feel some resentment towards Qin Saizhu.","However, this resentment wasn't enough to make her harm Qin Saizhu. That changed when Consort Ning sent word: she could pledge herself, but she must use Consort Zhuang's life as her token of submission. Consort Ning wanted her to strike when Qin Saizhu was giving birth—when she was at her weakest, and the servants' attention would be on the newborn prince or princess. That would be her best chance to succeed.","Ye Qiong didn't fully understand why Consort Ning, ignoring the potentially greater threat of the newborn, wanted Consort Zhuang's life instead. But Consort Ning had finally relented, and she had to seize this opportunity.","Ye Qiong spread open her hand. In the nail bed of her right hand were traces of white powder—this was what she had prepared for today. It was a poison from her hometown. Inhaled, it would at most cause vomiting and diarrhea in a normal person. But if used together with rosin, it would cause extreme weakness. If the person happened to be facing danger—such as an injury or childbirth—it would cause their blood to surge and bleed uncontrollably.","Some time ago, she had worn a dress embroidered with pearls. Those pearls had been polished with an oil containing rosin. She had intentionally dropped one in the main hall and later saw that very pearl in the sewing box on the small table by the daybed in the main hall.","Today, she had originally planned to enter the delivery room and quietly sprinkle this poison around Qin Saizhu.","But Noble Lady Hui had stopped her.","At that moment, Ye Qiong couldn't describe what she felt in her heart—regret, but also relief.","\"Could it be that you've actually developed genuine feelings from over a year of false affection?\" Ye Qiong asked herself, cleaning the powder from under her nails. \"Don't deceive even yourself into believing it. You missed this opportunity; next time, you must not soften your heart.\"","Your only goal is favor and glory, Ye Qiong told herself.","Just then, the sound of a baby's cry came from the direction of the main hall.","Ye Qiong let go of the quilt, got up, and prepared herself to go to the main hall to offer congratulations. But before long, Xia Zhi came stumbling in.","\"Your Highness! Consort Zhuang... has passed away!\"","What?!","Ye Qiong was stunned, quickly wondering if Noble Consort Ning had another trick up her sleeve?","The hairpin in her hand fell, and she instinctively reached out to steady herself against the dressing table.","Xiazhi, thinking she was overcome with grief for Consort Zhuang, hurried to support her. \"Consort Zhuang suffered a massive hemorrhage...\"","Ye Qiong was silent. She hadn't acted, yet the result was the same. What did this mean?","With Consort Zhuang dead, it was as Noble Consort Ning wished. So why did she feel this dull, aching pain in her heart?","\"Help me to the main hall!\"","Just as she reached the doorway, Ye Qiong paused again. She bit her lower lip. If she claimed Consort Zhuang's death was her own doing, would that create an opportunity with Noble Consort Ning?","Ye Qiong saw Noble Consort Ning at Qin Saizhu's funeral.","The Emperor had posthumously elevated Consort Zhuang to the rank of Consort Zhuang, ordering her burial with the rites befitting a Consort. Naturally, all the concubines had to attend to pay their respects.","Ye Qiong found an opportunity to walk alongside Noble Consort Ning.","\"So it seems you succeeded?\" Noble Consort Ning looked at her with a hint of surprise.","Ye Qiong kept her eyes downcast, appearing docile. \"Regarding that pearl, this humble concubine will find an opportunity to dispose of it. It will never become a source of trouble.\"","She omitted part of the truth, only saying she had tampered with the pearl. Consort Zhuang had inhaled its effects over time, leaving a hidden ailment in her body that was triggered during childbirth.","Noble Consort Ning found this interesting. She didn't say whether she believed it or not. But Ye Qiong was willing to bear the handle of poisoning Consort Zhuang just to curry favor with her. Someone with such determination was worth throwing a few crumbs to.","Noble Consort Ning then said, \"If you want the Emperor to notice you more, simply dress in a manner opposite to that of Noble Lady Hui.\"","Ye Qiong was confused. Noble Lady Hui shared a similar type of beauty with her and enjoyed considerable favor. Why should she dress opposite to Noble Lady Hui?","Noble Consort Ning: \"Haven't you noticed? First there was Virtuous Consort, then there was Beauty Li, and even Lady Wei, who had no favor initially but now enjoys some—they are all bold and radiant women. The Emperor does not care for frail delicacy. If you dress more brightly and splendidly, perhaps you can catch the Emperor's eye.\"","Hearing Noble Consort Ning's explanation, Ye Qiong could only think it was laughable. She had agonized for so long, never understanding where she fell short, and it turned out to be because of her looks?","But looks are innate. She couldn't very well change her face!","Yet, if she truly remained unknown in the rear palace because of this, Ye Qiong was unwilling.","She said resentfully, \"Then why does the Emperor favor Noble Lady Hui?\"","Noble Consort Ning replied indifferently, \"Who knows? Noble Lady Hui wasn't favored earlier either. It's only in the last couple of years the Emperor began to notice her. Perhaps she possesses some quality that makes the Emperor willing to favor her regardless of her looks.\"","Regarding this point, Noble Consort Ning had also pondered. One cannot interact with someone based solely on appearance, as beauty alone cannot last. Not everyone has a face as exquisite as Virtuous Consort's. Noble Lady Hui must have something the Emperor likes. Noble Consort Ning hadn't had much dealings with Qi Daiyu and couldn't see it yet.","Ye Qiong, however, pondered deeply. She often associated with Qi Daiyu. If she had to say what was different about Qi Daiyu compared to other concubines, it was probably that she was somewhat \"languid\" and \"uncompetitive\"? Occasionally she said surprising things, but could these really attract the Emperor?","Ye Qiong didn't think so.","There must be another reason, one she hadn't discovered.","At the very least, now she knew where she had lost. She would just change accordingly. She couldn't change her face, but she could change her makeup. Changing her clothes could also create a different style.","\"Thank you for your guidance, Noble Consort Ning.\" Ye Qiong bowed. \"In the future, if there is any way this humble concubine can be of use to you, I would dare ten thousand deaths without refusal!\"","Noble Consort Ning smiled faintly. \"There will be.\"","This person had ambition, was ruthless, and skilled at pretense. She indeed needed someone like this to help her realize her heart's desire.","\"Since you are on good terms with Noble Lady Hui and the others, continue associating with them normally. There's no need to reveal your connection to me outwardly.\" Noble Consort Ning planned to cultivate Ye Qiong as a hidden line. Perhaps she would prove useful someday.","This counted as accepting her. Ye Qiong revealed a smile. \"This humble concubine understands.\""]},{"number":104,"title":"Chapter 104","paragraphs":["The inner chamber of Yanqing Residence was dim and heavy with gloom.","On the bed behind the pale blue bed curtains, the quilt was bunched into a lump.","As Consort Li stepped inside, her brow immediately furrowed.","Shiliu, following close behind, had red-rimmed eyes. \"My mistress refuses to speak to anyone. She has been lying like this for three days now.\"","Seeing her mistress in this state filled her with deep worry. The Empress was busy with the funeral arrangements for Consort Zhuang and the New Year festivities, and Consort Nie was with child. Left with no other choice, Shiliu had asked Consort Li to come.","Consort Li instructed her, \"Go and open the windows, let some air in. It's stifling in here.\"","Shiliu wanted to say that her mistress forbade opening them, but seeing the insistence in Consort Li's eyes, she sighed. She was the one who had asked Consort Li to come and offer counsel, so she should follow her lead.","Consort Li walked to the bedside. She initially thought to pull the quilt back directly, but reconsidered, her eyes filling with pity. She merely leaned over and gently lifted a corner of the bedding.","The person inside was curled into a ball, hair disheveled, eyes tightly shut and swollen red—clearly from prolonged weeping.","Though the figure didn't move, Consort Li knew she was awake. \"You won't go to pay your respects? Or attend the burial? If your sisterly bond was so deep, wouldn't it chill Consort Zhuang's heart to not see her off on her final journey?\"","The lying figure sat bolt upright, glaring. \"When did I say I wouldn't go?\"","\"And you'll go looking like this?\" Consort Li gestured for Shiliu to bring water.","Qi Daiyu hung her head, her expression downcast. \"I just wanted to lie here a while longer.\"","She still couldn't accept Qin Saizhu's death. Such a wonderful person, laughing and talking with her just days ago—how could she be gone?","Her heart felt blocked. Only by lying there, buried under the quilt, could she find a little relief.","With that thought, tears began to flow again.","Yan He and Shiliu entered with a basin of water. Yan He wrung out a cloth, and Consort Li took it, placing it over Qi Daiyu's face. The cool touch against her swollen eyes caused a sting, making Qi Daiyu flinch back, but Consort Li held her steady.","\"Do you know how many women in the capital alone die in childbirth each year? Countless! It's only here in the palace, with imperial physicians on constant call, that we see it less,\" Consort Li said. Common folk couldn't even afford a doctor.","\"Just ask Yan He or your wet nurse. I don't believe such things haven't happened in the palace before.\"","Yan He added, \"During the late Emperor's reign, Consort Lan passed away during a difficult birth, both mother and child lost.\"","Qi Daiyu closed her eyes.","\"I know you can't accept Consort Zhuang's passing right now. When my own sister died, I couldn't accept it either. But I came to understand later: everyone dies, it's only a matter of sooner or later. It's fine to grieve, but you must also look forward,\" Consort Li said earnestly.","Her words bordered on inauspicious. Shiliu opened her mouth to caution her but was stopped by Yan He.","Consort Li continued, \"Moreover, no matter how deep your grief, you must not forget those still living.\" She removed the cloth, signaling Shiliu to rewet it, and pointed towards the sounds outside the window for Qi Daiyu to hear. Servants were busy with relocation matters, their noises drifting in, but the clearest sound was the crying of an infant.","\"Consort Zhuang entrusted the Third Princess to you. But these past few days, have you cared for her at all? That child has just lost her birth mother, and now her adoptive mother neglects her. Isn't she pitiful?\"","Qi Daiyu covered her face. \"I just... I just...\"","She just couldn't accept that the child her 'Pearl Sister' fought so hard to bring into the world was the reason for her own promotion to Consort. How could she ever face Qin Saizhu?","Consort Li was so exasperated she nearly rolled her eyes. \"Consort Zhuang would only be pleased! Your promotion means you can care for the Third Princess even better! No one will dare bully her! If you truly wish to honor Consort Zhuang, you should pull yourself together, care for the Third Princess properly, raise her as your own daughter, and see her grown. Only then will your friendship not have been in vain.\"","Taking the cloth back from Shiliu, Consort Li didn't place it on Qi Daiyu's face again, merely handed it to her. \"I won't lecture you further. I know you can reason this out for yourself.\"","Qi Daiyu silently took the cloth from Consort Li's hand.","Though resolved to be strong, after watching Qin Saizhu's coffin sealed and returning home, Qi Daiyu remained despondent.","Only the cries of the Third Princess could rouse her somewhat.","Consort Li was right about one thing: she must take good care of the Third Princess.","The main hall of Changchun Palace had been prepared, its heated floors making it very warm. Qi Daiyu had Yan He arrange a warm chamber within the main hall to care for the Third Princess nearby.","The newborn baby, in a new place, cried incessantly. Qi Daiyu asked Zhi Ma to find some clothes Qin Saizhu often wore and make a small pillow for the Third Princess. Perhaps truly sensing her mother's scent, the Third Princess finally quieted.","Zhi Ma and Xiang Chun's eyes instantly reddened.","\"You two shall stay in my palace from now on, responsible for caring for the Third Princess,\" Qi Daiyu said.","The other servants were to be reassigned, but Zhi Ma and Xiang Chun had been Qin Saizhu's personal maids. It wouldn't be difficult to request them, especially with the reason being to care for the Third Princess. The Emperor and Empress would not object.","Zhi Ma and Xiang Chun were deeply grateful and moved to bow, but Qi Daiyu stopped them.","\"Sister Pearl told me before that Zhi Ma's marriage was already arranged, waiting only for her to reach the right age to leave the palace. As for Xiang Chun, Sister Pearl had also found a good match for you, though she hadn't told you yet...\"","Before she could finish, Xiang Chun knelt. \"Consort Hui, this servant wishes to remain in the palace to care for the Third Princess!\"","Qi Daiyu said, \"I know of your loyalty to my sister. But this concerns your entire life. In the palace, you can only ever be a servant. Outside, you would be a properly wedded mistress of your own household.\" The match Qin Saizhu found for Xiang Chun was indeed excellent, a family with good land and business.","Xiang Chun still shook her head. \"My mistress was so kind to me. I have no way to repay her. Now that she is gone, only the young mistress remains. I am willing to care for the young mistress always, to repay my mistress's kindness.\"","Seeing her determination, Qi Daiyu did not press further. \"Very well. I've heard you helped Sister Pearl manage the Hundred Flavors Pavilion business. You shall continue to do so. When the Third Princess grows up, it will be handed over to her.\"","Xiang Chun was surprised. She had assumed Consort Hui would take direct control. Not that she distrusted Consort Hui—the Hundred Flavors Pavilion had Consort Hui's share, and now with her raising the Third Princess, taking over would be natural. Given their friendship, Consort Hui would certainly not misappropriate it.","But now Consort Hui was entrusting it to her to continue managing. Xiang Chun's eyes grew warm. \"Consort Hui, please rest assured. This servant will manage it well, until the Third Princess comes of age.\"","\"Good. You've all been exhausted these past few days. Go and rest now. You need to be well-rested to care for the Third Princess properly.\"","After the others had left, Qi Daiyu gazed quietly at the child in the swaddling clothes.","She used to not believe that a resemblance to adults could be seen in a newborn, but looking at the Third Princess now, she felt every feature resembled Qin Saizhu.","The eyes were like hers, the nose like hers, the mouth like hers too.","The little dimples on the cheeks were the most similar.","The Third Princess seemed to be sleeping restlessly, letting out a soft whimper, her tiny hands waving in the air. Qi Daiyu offered her finger and it was immediately grasped.","Held tightly.","Qi Daiyu's nose tingled with emotion; she felt like crying again.","Regarding the Third Princess's pet name, Qin Saizhu had spoken of it with Qi Daiyu before.","\"Having been away from home for so many years, what I miss most is my hometown, though I likely will never return in this lifetime. When the child is born, let's call her Siyu... no, the 'Yu' for joy. May her life be filled with happiness.\"","Siyu—this became the Third Princess's pet name. As for her formal name, that would probably have to wait until she came of age for the Emperor to bestow.","Perhaps it was just as the Empress had remarked that day; this child had a very placid temperament. Once she settled into life at Changchun Palace, Siyu's easygoing nature gradually became apparent.","The warm chamber was cozy, and even when Siyu wet herself, the cloth diaper cooled slowly. She wouldn't cry or fuss, simply waiting for the nursemaids to notice on their own.","But the nursemaids, worried that frequent picking up and putting down might cause a chill, typically wouldn't pick her up unless she cried. Moreover, with the doors and windows shut in winter, a slight smell of urine in the room of such a young child was normal. This often led to the nursemaids discovering only after Siyu's little bottom had been soaking for quite some time.","Within a few days, that little bottom was bright red.","Qi Daiyu found it both amusing and endearing. She bought some infant lotion online and gently applied it bit by bit for the little one.","While Qi Daiyu applied the lotion, Siyu would watch her with open eyes. In truth, her eyes weren't fully developed yet and could only perceive light and shadows, but she kept looking, creating the illusion that she was truly seeing her.","Those grape-like, dark, shiny eyes fixed on you were utterly adorable. Qi Daiyu couldn't resist holding her close for a cuddle and a kiss.","\"Hmm, quite smelly.\" Adorable she was, but the fact remained that even the scented lotion couldn't completely mask the milky sourness.","Hearing this, Siyu let out a milky burp, making it even smellier.","Caring for an infant is exhausting work; after all, they are so tiny, and everything requires attention.","To better care for Siyu, Qi Daiyu enrolled in an online elite maternity nurse course, learning various techniques and knowledge for infant care.","It proved quite practical. For instance, baby gas-relief exercises. Performing a set on Siyu after a feeding quickly helped her pass gas. With a comfortable tummy, the little one would soon fall asleep.","Or the various scientific and comfortable holding positions. Sometimes, Siyu, who fussed in others' arms, would immediately settle down once in Qi Daiyu's hands.","Even the wet nurse caring for Siyu remarked that the Third Princess was truly attached to Consort Hui.","Qi Daiyu merely smiled.","That year, during the twelfth lunar month, despite the mourning period for Consort Zhuang, the New Year celebrations would not be entirely abandoned. The white drapes that had hung for several days at Qixiang Palace were taken down, replaced by bright red lanterns and festive couplets.","Out with the old, in with the new; the departed are easily forgotten.","No matter who it was, no matter how grieved, one had to hide the sorrow within and present a smiling face to the world.","This year's New Year's banquet, as the Third Princess's birth mother had just passed and she was not yet a month old, they were excused from attending. Qi Daiyu, needing to care for the Third Princess, was also granted leave and did not have to attend the banquet.","Though she was not there, many still thought of her.","The Northern Li tribute included several fine furs, among them a white bear pelt, which Jiang Yuan had someone deliver to her.","The Empress had a table of warm dishes sent over. Nie Zhiyu sent some fruits.","Consort Li, after the banquet ended, even brought her a flask of wine.","\"I shall share a cup with my sister. Will you share one with your Sister Qin?\"","Qi Daiyu smiled and said, \"Alright.\"","It suddenly occurred to her that the first time she drank after crossing into this world was with Qin Saizhu.","Qi Daiyu poured a cup of wine and sprinkled it beneath the pear tree where Qin Saizhu used to often lie.","Anyone else might forget you, but I will not. Qi Daiyu thought. This was her first friend in this world; how could she ever forget?","She poured another cup for herself and drank it down in one gulp.","So bitter.","In the sky, snow had begun to fall again, unnoticed when it started."]},{"number":105,"title":"Chapter 105","paragraphs":["On the sixth day of the lunar new year, Grandma Qi and Mrs. Wan entered the palace. As usual, they first paid their respects at the Cining Palace and the Kunning Palace.","Perhaps because Qi Daiyu was now a concubine of the Pin rank, the Empress Dowager kept the two for tea this year.","When they arrived at the Changchun Palace later, the old lady remarked, \"The Empress Dowager doesn't seem much different from ordinary folks, just younger and more imposing.\" She had heard the Empress Dowager was already in her fifties, yet she looked like someone in her thirties. Not like herself, an old woman who truly looked the part. Even though she had left the farmlands years ago, she still looked like a farmer's wife.","There was a touch of melancholy in the old lady's tone. But she quickly cheered up again. Today, she had seen the Empress Dowager! This would be a fine story to tell back home, surely making her old sisters green with envy.","Grandma Qi and Mrs. Wan then looked around the main hall of Changchun Palace. \"This is much bigger than the previous place!\"","That was natural. The main hall had five principal rooms, along with east and west side halls, a small kitchen, storerooms, and rear rooms for the servants. There were five storerooms alone. Apart from holding Qi Daiyu's belongings, Qin Saizhu's personal effects had also been moved here, but these were to be left for Si Yu in the future; Qi Daiyu was merely keeping them in trust.","Overall, the main hall was more than twice the size of Yanqing Residence.","The most convenient feature was the underfloor heating. In winter, one wouldn't have to endure the smell of charcoal braziers. If a rug were laid on the floor, one could even walk barefoot.","During the days of the move, Qi Daiyu had been in low spirits, so all the arrangements were completed by Yan He and the others. Except for the study, which was an exact replica of the one in Yanqing Residence, other areas like the dining room, main reception hall, and bedroom had been altered. As it was the New Year, only fine items were used for decoration, making everything look luxurious and exquisite.","Grandma Qi looked here and touched there, utterly fascinated.","Mrs. Wan, meanwhile, held her daughter's arm. \"Might we see the Third Princess?\"","They had received news outside the palace that her daughter was now raising the Third Princess, and this promotion was because of it.","Mrs. Wan was overjoyed. In her mind, whether a woman had a child to rely on made a world of difference, a principle that held true for both common families and the imperial household. Although the Third Princess was not her daughter's biological child, since the Emperor had decreed that her daughter raise her, it was unlikely to change easily. Thus, the Third Princess was her daughter's child.","Having a child meant having support. In terms of status, it naturally provided more stability; as long as one didn't commit major errors, the latter half of life would be secure. In terms of favor, even if the Emperor later doted on new beauties, her daughter wouldn't have to face desolate loneliness, as the child would be her solace.","With these thoughts, even before meeting the Third Princess, Mrs. Wan already regarded her as her own granddaughter and adored her immensely.","When she finally saw her, she couldn't stop calling her \"my precious darling.\" The baby, just a full month old, had shed the wrinkled skin of a newborn, becoming fair, soft, and plump. Her eyes were now open, round and shiny like black grapes, her little mouth red, and her tongue poking out now and then, occasionally blowing tiny bubbles. Such an adorable sight would melt anyone's heart.","The mother-in-law and daughter-in-law vied to hold her.","Si Yu wasn't shy with strangers either, or perhaps she knew Qi Daiyu was nearby and wasn't afraid. She was well-behaved for whoever held her, utterly delighting Grandma Qi and Mrs. Wan. Grandma Qi immediately took off the Buddhist prayer beads from her wrist and gently placed them beside Si Yu's pillow.","\"This string of beads was blessed long ago by Master Linghui. It bathed in incense and prayers before the Buddha for a full forty-nine days. I've worn it for decades, and each bead remains round and lustrous. I originally thought to pass it down as a family heirloom, but today I'll leave it for our Princess.\" The Qi ancestors weren't wealthy and left no valuable items; only this string of beads held some worth.","Master Linghui was once the most renowned monk in Zhao State, with countless followers. Objects blessed by him were once worth a fortune and hard to come by. It was only because Master Linghui did not discriminate based on status and only guided those with a connection that Grandma Qi was fortunate enough to obtain this string of beads.","Mrs. Wan also took a pouch from her sleeve, containing a pair of silver bracelets as thick as a thumb and a tiger-head shaped longevity lock. This year was the Year of the Tiger.","\"Wear the peace bracelets for a lifetime of safety; wear the longevity lock to lock in peace and security. Our Third Princess must grow up safe and sound.\"","Qi Daiyu felt her eyes grow warm. \"Grandmother, Mother...\"","Mrs. Wan smiled and patted her hand. \"These things are what the maternal family ought to prepare anyway.\"","She had heard that Consort Zhuang's hometown was in Sichuan, a long and arduous journey from the capital. They likely didn't yet know about Consort Zhuang's passing and naturally wouldn't have thought to prepare these things. Since she regarded the Third Princess as her own granddaughter, she, as the grandmother, had to be thorough.","After playing for a short while, Si Yu grew sleepy again. Not wanting to disturb her, the women left the warm chamber for the outer room.","Only then did Mrs. Wan ask her daughter how she was faring in the palace, about her health, and whether her winter cough had returned.","Qi Daiyu answered each question.","Mrs. Wan then spoke of family matters, starting with the eldest brother, Qi Chuchu. Qi Chuchu had followed his father-in-law to the border regions, taking his wife and daughter with him.","\"Your sister-in-law is pregnant again!\"","Qi Daiyu: \"What?\" Hadn't Lang Tianyu given birth just half a year ago?","Mrs. Wan: \"I've already written to scold your brother. He has no sense at all! No one at home was pressuring him, yet he doesn't know how to cherish his wife properly! If he were at home, I'd certainly give him a beating!\"","In such matters, she could only scold. It was also a way to show her daughter-in-law that their family wasn't that sort. However, it wasn't appropriate for her, as an elder, to advise against it or interfere too much in the young couple's intimacy...","Qi Daiyu pursed her lips. \"Then have Elder Brother find a good physician and arrange for a midwife early.\" She currently felt some aversion towards childbirth. Even without that, she didn't approve of Lang Tianyu getting pregnant again so soon. Her body hadn't recovered fully just half a year after giving birth.","Mrs. Wan: \"Naturally.\"","After speaking of her son, she moved on to her younger daughter.","\"Your sister's marriage arrangement is about to be settled.\"","Qi Daiyu: \"So soon?\"","She remembered Mrs. Wan mentioning last year the intention to arrange a marriage for Qi Qinglong, and Qi Daiyu had thought it would take some time to consider candidates slowly.","\"If we don't hurry, it might be too late.\" By next spring, there would likely be another imperial selection of consorts. The marriage had to be settled before that.","Mrs. Wan said with a smile, \"We were quite fortunate. Last year, wasn't there the military imperial examination?\"","The civil examination the year before had been grand, while last year's military exam, due to border conflicts, hadn't attracted as much attention. Judging by Mrs. Wan's tone, could it be... \"Is it one of the military graduates?\"","Mrs. Wan nodded. \"The man's name is Zhou Yuan. He placed thirteenth in the military examination. His ancestral home is in Suzhou. His grandfather serves as a Battalion Commander in the Gansu Guard, so the family has some means. He has four brothers and is the youngest. Despite being the youngest, he wasn't spoiled but is very steady.\"","And precisely because he was the youngest son, not expected to inherit the family estate, there was less need to be overly picky about the choice of a daughter-in-law.","Although the Qi family is currently flourishing, their foundation is still shallow, and they lack support from relatives and connections. In terms of marriage alliances, there aren't many suitable choices—at least within the capital, there truly aren't any good options.","There are indeed those willing to seek Qi Qinglong's hand in marriage. However, some are prominent families seeking a match for a lesser son, aiming to win over Qi Caishang, the Vice Director of the Waterways Department. Others are social climbers hoping to curry favor with Qi Daiyu, the imperial consort. None are truly suitable candidates for a proper, stable life.","Mrs. Wan cannot bear to marry her youngest daughter into such situations.","By comparison, the Zhou family is genuinely good. Even having many brothers isn't a bad thing; in fact, in contemporary eyes, numerous brothers signify a thriving family lineage, meaning there's always help available no matter what troubles arise.","It's clear that Mrs. Wan is quite satisfied with this potential son-in-law.","\"Your father took me to meet him. His appearance is also very proper. We just need to find an opportunity for your younger sister to meet him herself,\" Mrs. Wan lowered her voice. \"Actually, what I'm most pleased about is that he has now joined the Capital Garrison Command and will certainly remain in the capital in the future.\"","Instead of returning to his hometown, which means Qi Qinglong could also stay in the capital.","Qi Chuchu and his wife and daughter are at the border, and Qi Daiyu is deep within the palace; both are difficult to see. If her youngest daughter could stay by her side, Mrs. Wan would naturally be overjoyed.","Qi Daiyu said, \"To be able to enter the Capital Garrison Command suggests his capabilities are quite good.\"","Yet she still sighed, \"However, I am still reluctant to let Qinglong marry so early. If possible, could we discuss with his family, asking them to let Qinglong stay at home a few more years? If it's awkward to propose, you can place the blame on me. Say it's to pray for blessings for me, her older sister who has become Consort Hui.\"","With her status, presumably the Zhou family would not refuse.","Mrs. Wan replied, \"There's no need to use your influence. Don't you know your father? If he hadn't considered all this, would he have even mentioned that young man to me? Your father said that Zhou Yuan is only seventeen, right in the midst of gaining experience at the Garrison Command. His three older brothers are already married, so his parents aren't in a hurry for him. If he and Qinglong are both willing, they can first get engaged. We can discuss marriage matters after Qinglong comes of age.\"","Qi Qinglong is currently thirteen, with two years until she comes of age. Discussing marriage after that, and then going through the betrothal rituals like presenting gifts and setting the date, would take about a year. However it's managed, it could be delayed until Qi Qinglong is sixteen.","Only then did Qi Daiyu smile. \"That's good.\"","After talking a while longer and seeing the hour was late, Qi Daiyu watched the two of them leave the palace.","Perhaps because she saw strangers today, Si Yu was exceptionally lively. Usually, she would fall asleep as soon as dusk fell, but today she was still energetic.","Qi Daiyu carried her to the couch and played with her using a rattle-drum.","While they were playing, an announcement came from outside: \"His Majesty has arrived!\"","Qi Daiyu hurriedly put on her shoes to greet him.","\"Rise.\"","Jiang Yuan still carried a chill from outside. Hearing the child's voice inside, he didn't rush in. First, he took off his heavy cloak. Shiliu brought over a basin of hot water. Jiang Yuan wiped his hands with a hot towel, and only then did he take Qi Daiyu's hand and walk inside with her.","\"Haven't seen you these past few days,\" Jiang Yuan said as they walked, then looked back at Qi Daiyu. \"You've grown thinner.\" She looked even more delicate, but Jiang Yuan knew the reason for her weight loss, so he didn't comment further.","He then went to look at Si Yu. Si Yu was unfamiliar with this imperial father, and Jiang Yuan wasn't as approachable as Mrs. Wan and the others. He carried the natural dignity of an emperor, an imposing aura. As soon as he reached out to touch Si Yu, her little mouth puckered, on the verge of crying.","Qi Daiyu immediately extended her index finger for Si Yu to grasp.","Smelling the familiar scent, Si Yu calmed down and even giggled, revealing the little dimples on both cheeks.","Jiang Yuan: \"...\"","His tone was ambiguous. \"You are raising this child extremely well.\" Truly well, with every detail showing meticulous care.","Qi Daiyu said with a smile, \"Does Your Majesty not know? Your concubine has no other talents, but she does have a bit of a knack for raising children.\"","Jiang Yuan then thought about how both the Empress and Consort An were willing to let her care for their princesses. He had also witnessed the changes in the two princesses. She indeed had a talent for childcare.","He also smiled, joking, \"Shall I send the First and Second Princes to you another day for you to look after for a while?\"","Qi Daiyu didn't take this seriously. She would be mad to get involved with the princes.","\"One shouldn't treat people like governesses to be ordered about,\" she said, turning her body away, pretending to be angry."]},{"number":106,"title":"Chapter 106","paragraphs":["\"Are you angry?\" Jiang Yuan leaned in to look at her and sighed, \"How could I truly let you suffer like that?\"","Seeing Qi Daiyu still wouldn't speak, he said meaningfully, \"News has come from the border. A young officer named Qi Chuchu captured a team of Northern Li scouts. I was just thinking about how to reward him...\"","Before he could finish, Qi Daiyu immediately turned to look at him, her eyes sparkling.","\"Speaking of which, this young officer shares your surname. Could he be some distant relative of yours?\" Jiang Yuan's eyes were filled with amusement.","Qi Daiyu had already thrown herself at him, giving his waist a light pinch. \"Your Majesty enjoys teasing your consort!\"","Jiang Yuan caught her hand and pulled her into his embrace. \"Your temper has grown fiercer lately. How would I dare tease you?\" Though he said this, his tone held no trace of anger.","Qi Daiyu, however, felt a twinge of guilt. When she first interacted with the Emperor, she was constantly cautious and fearful, terrified that a single misstep could cost her her head. But as time passed, she realized the emperor was also human, and a rather good-tempered one at that. The limited sense of hierarchy she originally held was occasionally pushed to a corner, manifesting in her words and actions as boldness and willfulness.","And Jiang Yuan, for his part, naturally favored the bold and willful. Qi Daiyu's mannerisms suited his temperament perfectly. Over time, Qi Daiyu sometimes forgot herself, even daring to address Jiang Yuan with the informal \"you and I.\"","Qi Daiyu was like a cat, constantly testing the boundaries set by Jiang Yuan, the master of the palace. The more he indulged her, the bolder she became.","Hearing Jiang Yuan's words now, Qi Daiyu felt a jolt of alarm, reminding herself silently: while affection lasts, a little willfulness is a delight; once affection fades, that same willfulness becomes presumption.","She must constantly remind herself to maintain proper boundaries.","So she nestled obediently in Jiang Yuan's arms. \"It's only because Your Majesty indulges me that I dare to be willful.\"","Jiang Yuan was indeed pleased. He truly liked Qi Daiyu's way of occasionally scratching like a cat without overstepping. She had her own personality and charm, which he found novel and gradually captivating, yet she still held him in awe and never thought of breaking free.","This was where Qi Daiyu differed from the other consorts.","The Empress was dignified and graceful. He regarded her as his wife, bestowing respect and affection, but constrained by her status, she had to conceal her sorrows, joys, angers, and happiness. Sometimes even he couldn't discern her true feelings. Consort Shu wore all her thoughts on her face, but such overt displays of emotion could sometimes feel grating. Consort Zhuang was always smiling, as if nothing could trouble her. Being with her was always lighthearted and joyful. Sadly, the world is unpredictable; Consort Zhuang had already passed away. Concubine Nie was serene and tranquil. Visiting her could calm the most troubled heart; occasionally reading a scroll or playing a game of chess with her was a fine way to relieve weariness.","As for Qi Daiyu, Jiang Yuan sometimes felt she was like a civet cat. When doted on, she would cling sweetly; when neglected, she could still live happily on her own.","Jiang Yuan remembered a period when he deliberately cold-shouldered Qi Daiyu, curious to see her reaction. Yet Qi Daiyu was busy with hotpot and mahjong, enjoying herself immensely every day. It seemed she could live perfectly well even if he never entered her palace again.","To be honest, Jiang Yuan had felt a slight sense of defeat then. He was the Son of Heaven! The Supreme Sovereign!","The consorts of the rear palace all depended on him for their lives. If he didn't visit them for long periods, they would grow melancholic and lament their loneliness. Only Qi Daiyu... she was even more attentive to the Empress than to him...","Jiang Yuan concluded that even if Qi Daiyu was a civet cat, she was one that appeared docile on the surface but was truly wild at heart. This could be seen even in her unrestrained sleeping posture.","Yet such a woman, though infuriating, was also immensely interesting, making him want to conquer her.","To see her become wholly devoted to him.","This was also why Jiang Yuan was willing to favor Qi Daiyu—even though her appearance wasn't originally to his liking.","Perhaps out of habit, he sometimes even thought she was indeed quite beautiful.","A flicker of desire appeared in Jiang Yuan's eyes, but he took no action.","Consort Zhuang had not been gone long. Given her close friendship with Consort Zhuang, she likely had no desire for intimacy with him in the near future.","After composing himself, Jiang Yuan finally spoke: \"I know that Qi Chuchu is your elder brother. Qiu Sheng has already promoted him to a personal guard and petitioned to have him appointed as a Loyalty Manifesting Commandant.\" Fearing she might not understand, Jiang Yuan specifically added, \"Rank six, lower grade.\"","\"You have a good elder brother indeed.\"","Qi Daiyu was so happy she couldn't close her mouth. Military officials indeed rose quickly! Her eldest brother was almost catching up to her nominal father!","\"My brother had little success in his early years. No one in the family ever imagined he could achieve this today. This clearly shows that Lord Qiu has a discerning eye for talent and knows how to employ people well, allowing my brother to display his abilities.\" Qi Daiyu offered a few words of flattery for Qiu Sheng, as he was now Qi Chuchu's direct superior.","\"Qiu Sheng's abilities are indeed good. Otherwise, I wouldn't have felt secure sending him to the border. However, he still falls short of the late Duke Zhongzheng's courage and strategic mind...\" Mentioning the old Marshal Jiang, Jiang Yuan felt deep regret. The old marshal's reputation alone was a natural deterrent at the border. Qiu Sheng was ultimately not quite his equal.","His gaze suddenly turned profound. Northern Li harbored wolfish ambitions. Even if they sought peace now, once their domestic situation stabilized in a few years, they would likely stir up trouble again. Although the Zhao state was founded on military prowess, these years of recuperation and development across the lands had been led primarily by civil officials. The generals in court were either aged or lacked significant experience, creating a gap between generations.","Last year, considering this situation, Jiang Yuan had specially established military examinations and indeed selected some promising talents, but these individuals still needed experience.","In the coming years, he would deliberately nurture some military commanders.","Thinking of this, Jiang Yuan's eyes inevitably fell on Qi Daiyu's head, a hint of amusement coloring his gaze.","She was indeed fortunate...","If that Qi Chuchu truly had capability, she would have a powerful maternal family in the future.","Spring blossoms and autumn moons passed, and in the blink of an eye, a year had gone by. Si Yu had learned to walk. Her daily routine involved clinging to Qi Daiyu's leg whenever she was about to go for morning greetings, preventing her from leaving.","She didn't cry or make a fuss. She would just hug Qi Daiyu's leg, sitting on the threshold, her eyes blinking as she stared.","That pitiful look was enough to melt anyone's heart.","Shiliu was the least able to withstand the Third Princess's adorable assault, almost blurting out: \"Mistress, perhaps you should take leave today?\"","In the entire Changchun Palace, only Qi Daiyu could resist Si Yu's cuteness attack.","Ruthlessly, she placed a hand on Si Yu's head. \"Be good. Wait for me to return.\"","She pulled her leg free and left.","On the way to Kunning Palace, she encountered Consort Li—during the recently passed New Year's banquet, the Emperor had conducted a major round of promotions. Nie Zhiyu, having given birth to the Third Prince, was promoted to Concubine He. Consort Li was promoted to Consort Li, Wei Chaorong was promoted to Concubine, Ye Qiong was promoted to Concubine, Feng Qi was promoted to Consort, and the other Attendants and Beauties were also promoted one rank within their original categories.","\"Her Majesty the Empress has summoned everyone today without fail. Do you know what it's about?\" Consort Li walked side by side with Qi Daiyu. Knowing that Qi Daiyu was close to the Empress, she figured asking her was sure to yield an answer.","Qi Daiyu didn't state it directly, only saying, \"This is the seventh year of the Yanli reign.\"","Consort Li caught on quickly. \"Is it for the imperial selection?\"","It had been three years since the last selection. Now, with spring's arrival, it was indeed time to put it back on the agenda.","Consort Li remarked, \"I see. No wonder the Emperor promoted so many at the New Year's banquet. It seems with new faces coming to the palace, he's giving us old-timers a little compensation.\"","The Emperor wasn't particularly generous with ranks. Consort Ning and Consort An, for instance, hadn't seen a change in their status for years. For others to be promoted, they either had to bear a royal child, enjoy the Emperor's favor, or else wait for a major event like the imperial selection to bring a batch of promotions.","Consort Li enjoyed considerable imperial favor, which was why she rose directly from Beauty to Consort. But if she never bore a royal child, she would likely remain at the rank of Consort for many years.","\"With newcomers arriving, aren't you afraid?\" Qi Daiyu asked jokingly.","\"What do I have to fear? Those unripe young girls?\" Consort Li gave a bewitching smile, full of allure. Her charm was something ordinary people couldn't hope to match. Even if the new girls were beautiful, they likely posed no threat to her.","\"Are you perhaps the one who's afraid?\" Consort Li retorted, turning the question back on Qi Daiyu.","Qi Daiyu replied, \"Naturally, I'm not afraid either.\" She had never been interested in competing for favor. After taking in Si Yu to raise, she had practically entered a state of early retirement, hardly even paying attention to the Emperor anymore.","Though, to be fair, the Emperor hadn't visited the Changchun Palace much this past year either.","When they arrived at the Kunning Palace, they found almost everyone was already there.","Two seats below Consort Ning were empty, reserved precisely for Qi Daiyu and Consort Li.","Actually, based on their titles, the \"Hui\" in Concubine Hui came before the \"An\" in Consort An, so Qi Daiyu should have been seated opposite Consort Ning. However, considering Consort An's seniority, Qi Daiyu had voluntarily given up that seat to her, resulting in the current seating arrangement.","Sitting opposite Qi Daiyu was Nie Zhiyu.","Seeing her arrive, Nie Zhiyu gave her a nod and a smile, which Qi Daiyu returned.","Not long after, Her Majesty the Empress emerged. Today's summons for everyone was indeed about the imperial selection.","\"The imperial selection is a significant matter. I cannot manage it alone. Consort Ning, Concubine Hui, Consort An, you three have experience in this. Along with Concubine He, you shall assist me in handling the affairs.\"","The four of them stood and bowed. \"Yes, Your Majesty.\"","The Empress continued, \"You are all senior members of the palace. When the new ladies enter, you must not bully them arbitrarily based on your seniority. Remember your positions and lead by example. Is that understood?\"","Everyone responded in unison, \"We heed Her Majesty the Empress's instruction.\"","Once the major business was concluded, the Empress, as usual, inquired after the health of the princes and princesses before dismissing everyone. The morning audiences had been just as brief all year.","Qi Daiyu did not leave but followed the Empress into the rear hall. Upon entering, she caught the scent of medicinal herbs.","She sighed inwardly.","This past year, the Empress's health had been steadily declining. The passing of Old Marshal Jiang still affected Her Majesty profoundly, an impact that was both physical and psychological.","Physically, since those episodes of coughing up blood, the Empress's constitution had not been strong.","Psychologically, perhaps because the Jiang family had lost Old Marshal Jiang as their pillar, the Empress had become the family's greatest reliance. She had to plan for the entire Jiang clan, arranging various family affairs which was mentally taxing, all while managing the affairs of the inner palace. This often left her spirit weary.","In the past, the Empress might have been willing to delegate some authority for others to assist. But without Old Marshal Jiang, she instead tightened her grip on power. It was as if only the Empress's seal could offer her a greater sense of security.","The psychological pressure was like a tightly drawn bowstring, which in turn aggravated her physical ailments.","Compared to a year ago, the Empress had grown noticeably thinner.","Qi Daiyu had tried to advise her, but the Empress would only smile and say, \"I know my own limits.\"","After first finishing the medicine brought by Ju Yi and rinsing her mouth, the Empress finally spoke to Qi Daiyu. \"Have you come to ask about Lingyi's matter?\"","Qi Daiyu nodded."]},{"number":107,"title":"Chapter 107","paragraphs":["After the New Year celebrations, the Eldest Princess turned seven. According to palace rules, she was to begin her studies at the Imperial Study come spring.","\"I was just about to discuss this with you. Come, take a look. These are the two candidates I have chosen as Lingyi's study companions. What do you think?\" On the desk were two portraits, and the Empress pointed to each, saying the names of the young girls.","\"One is Chu Tong from the family of the Princess of Yanqing. You've met the child; she's only half a year younger than Lingyi.\" The Princess of Yanqing had a son and a daughter. Her daughter, Chu Tong, had been granted the title of County Princess by the Emperor two years prior. The Princess of Yanqing was on good terms with the Empress, and County Princess Chu Tong had visited the palace numerous times, getting along well with the Eldest Princess. Choosing her as a companion was an excellent choice.","\"The other is my own niece from my family, her childhood name is Yuelan, two years older than Lingyi.\" The Empress smiled. \"There must be one sensible one among them, to prevent them from causing any trouble in the Imperial Study.\"","Being a princess's study companion was no easy task. Not only did one have to leave home to live in the palace, returning only on days of rest, but they were also responsible for looking after the princess, accompanying her in studies and play. At home, they were pampered young ladies, but as a princess's companion, strictly speaking, they became maidservants of a certain status. Of course, if one truly became a companion, the prestige was immense, successfully forging a connection with the imperial family, with endless intangible benefits.","County Princess Chu Tong was already imperial kin; being a princess's companion was the icing on the cake, a reflection of the friendship between the Empress and the Princess of Yanqing. Once she entered the palace, the palace staff would certainly not dare to make things difficult for her.","But Jiang Yuelan was merely a niece from a collateral branch of the Empress's family. How she would fare after entering the palace was hard to say. Yet, if the Empress wished to elevate her niece, this was the only way.","Qi Daiyu then said, \"The candidates chosen by Your Majesty the Empress are naturally beyond reproach.\"","The Empress truly spared no effort in planning for the Jiang family.","\"There is one more matter to entrust to you. Once Chu Tong and Yuelan enter the palace, I intend for them to reside in the Chunxi Hall. Behind Chunxi Hall is the Shou'an Palace, where the elderly imperial concubines reside. If anything happens, they can look out for them. However, Chunxi Hall has been unoccupied for a long time and needs to be cleaned thoroughly. After Lingyi found out, she insisted on decorating the rooms herself. I have no time to manage her, so I must rely on you to keep an eye on her.\"","Qi Daiyu replied, \"Understood.\"","After speaking for a long while, a look of fatigue had already appeared on the Empress's face.","Qi Daiyu ultimately couldn't hold back: \"Your Majesty, please set your mind at ease. Taking good care of your health is more important than anything.\"","Her expression was sincere and her tone earnest. A warm feeling passed through the Empress's heart. \"I am fine. It's just that with age, one picks up some ailments. It's perfectly normal.\"","How could she be considered old? The Empress was only twenty-seven. Her Majesty the Empress Dowager was already past fifty, yet her health remained robust.","The Empress continued with a smile, \"When the new consorts enter the palace, they will all be fresh blossoms in full bloom, making me appear even more faded. Nowadays, even the cosmetics you develop can't conceal my fading looks.\" As she said this, a trace of desolation flashed in her eyes.","One's appearance reflects one's heart. Her heart was utterly weary, and this manifested on her face as a few more wrinkles. A few days ago, the Empress had even discovered she had grown white hairs. She was only twenty-seven, yet she had white hairs.","Qi Daiyu said, \"Then this subject will develop some new products, specially customized for Your Majesty alone.\" She thought perhaps she could look into whether such personalized services existed; they probably did.","The Empress's gaze was gentle. \"You are very thoughtful.\"","Upon returning to Changchun Palace, she found that Nie Zhiyu and Ye Qiong had come. Nie Zhiyu had even brought the Third Prince, who was crawling on the carpet with Si Yu.","It was mainly Si Yu who was crawling. She could already walk, but upon seeing the Third Prince, she deliberately crawled in front of him to tease him. Yet the Third Prince was an inactive child; no matter how Si Yu teased, he remained placidly where he was, neither crying nor making a fuss.","Finding it uninteresting, Si Yu ignored the Third Prince and played with her toys by herself.","\"Why have you come so early today? I have matters to attend to today and no time to keep you company,\" Qi Daiyu said with a laugh.","Then Ye Qiong said somewhat sheepishly, \"It was I who dragged Sister Nie here. I have something to tell you both... I think I might be with child...\"","Qi Daiyu was taken aback, then smiled. \"This is wonderful news! When did this happen? Have you summoned the imperial physician?\"","Ye Qiong smiled faintly. \"Almost three months... I noticed my monthly courses were late, so I summoned the physician and learned the happy news. I wanted to tell you both immediately, but according to the customs of my hometown, the first three months should be kept secret... Elder sisters, you won't blame me, will you?\"","Nie Zhiyu grasped her hand. \"Of course not. Your caution is wise.\"","Qi Daiyu also said, \"Indeed. Now that you are with child, you must be careful in everything you do.\"","That Ye Qiong could conceive was actually not surprising. Over the past year, she had enjoyed considerable favor. Qi Daiyu couldn't recall exactly when it started, but Ye Qiong had suddenly changed her makeup and style. Her once gentle eyebrows were shaped into a high arch, her eye shadow deepened, her entire makeup becoming bold and striking. Coupled with a completely different style of dress from before, it was as if she had become a different person.","If the former Ye Qiong was a pure white magnolia, now she was more like a night-blooming cereus.","With this change in style, Ye Qiong successfully attracted the Emperor's attention. After His Majesty visited her, she diligently showcased her strengths—she played the yangqin exceptionally well and was also quite skilled in riding and archery. During the autumn hunt last October, Ye Qiong seized the opportunity to display her outstanding equestrian and archery skills. After returning to the palace, the Emperor frequently visited her quarters.","This child was most likely conceived around that time.","Ye Qiong said, \"Sister Nie has the Third Prince, Sister Qi has the Third Princess. After I give birth to my child in the future, the three of us will all have a firm footing in the palace.\"","She stroked her abdomen. This child was the result of her planning, conceived just before the imperial selection. Ye Qiong knew that relying solely on a change in makeup could not bind the emperor's favor for long—after all, she couldn't wear makeup day and night. Once new consorts entered the palace, whatever slight affection the Emperor held for her would likely be divided. Only by conceiving an imperial heir could one truly have a foundation to stand on.","And if the child in her belly were a prince, it would grant her even more leverage.","Hearing Ye Qiong's words, Qi Daiyu smiled and said, \"Her Majesty the Empress is magnanimous. When have we ever not had a firm footing?\"","Ye Qiong said, \"I misspoke, I... I'm just worried...\" She lowered her head to look at her abdomen.","Qi Daiyu comforted her, \"The palace is peaceful and harmonious now. Nothing will go wrong.\" In truth, thinking back, the only one who had ever targeted children was Consort Shu. Since Consort Shu was placed under confinement, every concubine who became pregnant afterwards gave birth safely.","Sometimes Qi Daiyu even wished the harem could remain this peaceful forever.","Thinking of this, her admiration for the Empress deepened.","Ye Qiong's heart was filled with bitterness. Consort Hui and Consort He naturally did not know that her worry stemmed from Consort Ning.","Last year, the Emperor had pushed through all opposition to abolish the position of Prime Minister and establish a Grand Secretariat, selecting several officials to enter the cabinet and participate in the decision-making of confidential state affairs. Consort Ning's father, Yang Heng, had even become one of the Chief Grand Secretaries, the other being the Minister of Personnel, Tang Gejian.","Although the Emperor trusted the personally promoted Tang Gejian more, Yang Heng was also a force to be reckoned with.","Ye Qiong's worry lay in this: Consort Ning had always lacked both imperial favor and a son. If she, Ye Qiong, gave birth to a royal heir, and Consort Ning wanted to adopt the child... what should she do?","It wasn't that Ye Qiong was being overly suspicious or seeing shadows where there were none. The very reason she had managed to conceive this child was thanks to the fertility prescription given to her by Consort Ning.","Ye Qiong looked at Qi Daiyu and Nie Zhiyu, wanting to say so much, yet finding herself unable to utter a word.","Could she really expect them to help her?","Ye Qiong dismissed the thought.","This year's selection of imperial consorts coincided with a number of eligible young men in the imperial clan who were yet to marry. Therefore, this palace selection was both for choosing imperial consorts and for selecting brides for the sons of the imperial clan. In the end, twenty women were chosen, but only four entered the palace as imperial consorts.","They were: the daughter of the Regional Military Commissioner of Huguang, Zong Jiayin, granted the title Lady Zong, to reside in the East Side Hall of Jingyang Palace; the daughter of the Qingzhou Guard Military Commissioner, Ji Yuanning, granted the title Lady Ji, to reside in the East Side Hall of Jingren Palace; the daughter of the Qujing Guard Military Commissioner, Fan Ningyan, granted the title Lady Fan, to reside in the East Side Hall of Yongshou Palace; and the daughter of the Prefect of Wenzhou, Kou Yan, granted the title Lady Kou, to reside in the West Side Hall of Yongshou Palace.","Out of four, three were actually daughters of military officers. Those with keen insight had already sensed a certain signal from this.","On the second day after the new consorts entered the palace, they paid their respects at Kunning Palace. On this day, all the consorts of the harem were present.","Zhaorong chuckled coyly, \"I thought I was the only one eager to know what our new sisters are like, but it seems all you sisters share the same curiosity!\"","Consort An: \"Apart from you, Consort Wei, who often asks for leave and doesn't come, everyone else comes daily to pay respects to Her Majesty the Empress. Don't drag others into your own impure motives just because your thoughts are not straightforward.\"","Zhaorong's smile froze. This Consort An, her words were always so unpleasant!","If it were anyone else, Zhaorong wouldn't hesitate to retort, but she was most unwilling to bicker with Consort An, solely because Consort An always wore that same stiff expression. No matter how much Zhaorong said, seeing that unchanging face just made her feel stifled.","So Zhaorong let out a \"hmph\" and ignored Consort An.","Others in the hall secretly smiled, clearly accustomed to this kind of scene.","Not long after, the newcomers arrived.","The consorts waited with bated breath, but upon seeing those who entered, disappointment flashed in many eyes.","Were these the newly entered imperial consorts? They seemed rather unremarkable...","To be fair, all four were outstanding in appearance, the kind who would stand out in a crowd. However, the senior consorts present had all witnessed the beauty of the late Consort Shu. Even though Consort Shu was now under house arrest, there were still those like Consort Hui, Consort He, and Consort Li Zhaoyi, who possessed such looks. A step below them were consorts like Consort Wei and Consort Ye. It had to be said, their standards for beauty had been set very high.","As for these four, the most beautiful one was only about on par with Zhaorong.","\"That one with the heroic and spirited bearing must be Lady Fan, right?\" Consort Lv looked towards one of them, who wore a black inner garment woven with gold thread, over which was a red magnolia-patterned skirt. Her attire was neat and efficient, clearly different from the others.","Fan Ningyan was the most famous among this batch of selected ladies. Rumors said she was skilled with a spear, had once followed her elder brother to suppress bandits, and single-handedly subdued six bandits, displaying remarkable bravery.","Fan Ningyan's gaze was clear and bright. \"Your servant, Fan Ningyan, pays respects to Her Majesty the Empress, and greets all Your Ladyships.\"","It was said the Fan family had raised her like a son, but now, looking at her, her etiquette was impeccable.","The Empress smiled and nodded, \"Rise.\"","\"This consort finds that this Lady Ji looks somewhat familiar,\" Consort Ning suddenly remarked.","Everyone was drawn by her words and looked towards Lady Ji.","In fact, from the moment Lady Ji entered the room, Qi Daiyu's gaze had not left her face.","Under so many stares, Ji Yuanning felt somewhat uneasy and instinctively smiled, revealing the dimples in her cheeks. \"Is there something improper about your servant?\"","Someone remarked, \"Oh my, I didn't notice it before, but with that smile, for a moment I almost thought I was seeing Concubine Zhuang...\""]},{"number":108,"title":"Chapter 108","paragraphs":["Does Ji Yuanning resemble Qin Saizhu?","Not really.","Qin Saizhu was that kind of beauty with a plump, jade-like elegance—a round face, almond-shaped eyes, and two dimples that appeared on both cheeks when she smiled. Her personality was bright and optimistic; she often laughed heartily and was a bit of a chatterbox.","As for Ji Yuanning, her figure was rather slender, with an oval face and a very straight nose. Perhaps because she had just entered the palace, she still seemed somewhat reserved in her interactions with others. When prompted to smile, she would only give a light, closed-mouth smile, though she too had two dimples when she did.","These two, who did not look alike, only seemed vaguely similar at first glance because both possessed the uncommon feature of dimples.","Consort An remarked, \"I can't see any resemblance at all.\"","Nie Zhiyu also said, \"I don't think they look much alike either. There's no need for Lady Ji to be alarmed.\" She was comforting Ji Yuanning, who seemed unsure of what was happening.","Ji Yuanning said gratefully, \"Thank you, Concubine He.\"","\"Alright, it's getting late. Everyone may return now,\" the Empress interrupted the topic, dismissing the others and keeping only Qi Daiyu behind.","It was regarding the matter of Chunxi Hall. \"I have already had people clean Chunxi Hall. You go take a look with Lingyi. Mei Yi will accompany you; she has the keys to the storeroom.\" The quarters for the princess's study companions were to be furnished by the Imperial Household Department as per standard, but the Empress, wanting to please her daughter and also to give face to the Eldest Princess, opened her own private treasury and let the Eldest Princess make her own selections.","The Eldest Princess was already waiting for Qi Daiyu in the courtyard. Today, she had her hair tied up, secured with just a single jade hairpin, and was dressed in male attire. From a distance, she looked like a handsome, clear-eyed young gentleman.","As the two walked along the path, the Eldest Princess held Qi Daiyu's hand. \"Concubine Hui, will the teachers at the Imperial Study be very strict?\"","At this moment, like all children about to start school, the Eldest Princess was already afraid of the teachers even before the lessons began.","Qi Daiyu thought to herself, Your Concubine Hui never attended the Imperial Study either, so how would I know if the teachers are strict?","But she imagined that no matter how strict they were, they would have to temper their temper somewhat when facing a princess student.","\"The teachers at the Imperial Study are all Hanlin Academicians specially selected by His Majesty. Each is immensely learned. When the Princess goes to study, she will certainly learn a great deal. As long as the Princess is diligent and earnest in her studies, how could the teachers possibly lose their temper?\" Qi Daiyu said.","The Eldest Princess thought that made sense and quickly set aside her worries. \"I'll go scout out the Imperial Study first. Next year, Second Sister and Eldest Brother will also start studying there, and then I'll look out for them!\"","She struck a pose with her hands on her hips, looking incredibly proud.","Qi Daiyu couldn't help but smile, but just as she was about to laugh, a little dumpling came charging over from the distance like a firecracker.","\"Concubine Hui! Eldest Sister!\" The little dumpling was panting, his chubby face covered in a sheen of sweat.","Behind him, the Second Princess walked over hurriedly yet without breaking decorum. She first bowed to Qi Daiyu. \"Greetings, Concubine Hui. Eldest Sister.\"","Then she frowned at the Eldest Prince. \"I've told you many times, don't run on the palace paths. If you bump into someone, be careful Father punishes you!\"","The Eldest Prince made a funny face at the Second Princess, his plump cheeks scrunching up, making one want to pinch them.","The Eldest Princess did just that, pinching his cheek. \"Why don't you listen to your Second Sister?\"","The Eldest Prince: \"I just saw Eldest Sister and Concubine Hui!\" He struggled to free himself from the pinching hand, covering his own face, his tone aggrieved: \"Concubine Hui, you secretly took Eldest Sister out to play without me and Second Sister. You're playing favorites!\"","Qi Daiyu: \"...\"","She was caught between laughter and tears.","The Eldest Prince had a bit of a sweet tooth. He wasn't picky and had an excellent appetite, and as he grew older, he became a chubby little fellow.","Ever since the Second Princess once brought the Eldest Prince along to Changchun Palace, where he tasted the pastries, the Eldest Prince had latched onto Qi Daiyu. Whenever the Second Princess went to Changchun Palace, he insisted on following.","There were three girls in Changchun Palace, and no one really played with him, but he didn't mind. He could happily spend a whole day by himself with two plates of pastries. Later, after hearing Qi Daiyu tell stories about the Great Sage, he loved going to Changchun Palace even more.","The Eldest Prince's favorite routine was: go to Changchun Palace — eat pastries — listen to stories — take a plate of pastries back home.","Over time, he actually became quite familiar with Qi Daiyu and the Eldest Princess.","In the past, Qi Daiyu would never have imagined she would grow close to Concubine Shu's son. But strictly speaking, there wasn't any major enmity between her and Concubine Shu. Moreover, the child was innocent; the Eldest Prince was simple-minded and adorable, and she was willing to include him in their play.","Now, Qi Daiyu patted the Eldest Prince's head. \"We're not going out to play. I'm accompanying your Eldest Sister to arrange Chunxi Hall. It's tiring work. Do you still want to come?\"","\"Arrange Chunxi Hall?\" The Eldest Prince couldn't fully understand what that entailed, but it sounded like something novel. He immediately said, \"Yes! I'll go help Concubine Hui!\"","The Second Princess asked curiously, \"Is Eldest Sister's study companion about to enter the palace?\"","Eldest Princess: \"Yes! They'll enter on the fifth of next month. Second Sister, you come with me. Let's discuss how to arrange it together!\"","\"Okay!\" The Second Princess nodded. She would also go to the Imperial Study next year, though she didn't know yet who her companion would be. Today, she could follow her elder sister and learn from the experience, so she could later arrange a room for her own companion herself.","And so, the three children walked hand in hand ahead, leaving Qi Daiyu trailing behind.","Having gotten a bit dusty at Chunxi Hall, Qi Daiyu intended to bathe and change clothes first upon returning to Changchun Palace, but she was informed that Lady Ji had come to Changchun Palace.","Qi Daiyu paused mid-step. \"What is she here for?\"","Yan He crouched down, using a handkerchief to brush the dust off the hem of Qi Daiyu's skirt, speaking in a lowered voice, \"Lady Ji has just entered the palace. Perhaps she has heard that Mistress has a good temperament and has come specifically to pay her respects.\"","After a moment's thought, Qi Daiyu understood what Yan He meant.","A new consort, fresh to the palace and understanding nothing, was at a time when she had no one to rely on. Finding someone to attach herself to could make life in the palace more comfortable and secure.","Her first reaction was: Have I reached the point where others seek to depend on me? Am I that established now?","Then came puzzlement.","Qi Daiyu could understand the desire to seek patronage. When she first arrived, hadn't she quickly decided to cling to the Empress's favor?","She just didn't understand why Ji Yuanning would seek her out.","Ji Yuanning resided in Jingren Palace. Going to Yanxi Palace or Zhongcui Palace would be much closer than coming to Changchun Palace.","Yan He: \"She hasn't attended upon His Majesty yet, so her potential is unclear for now. The Empress certainly won't summon her. Consort An has never enjoyed much favor and isn't a good choice for patronage. Both Concubine He and you are preferable options. However, given the incident during today's morning greetings, Lady Ji must have made some private inquiries, which is likely why she has come to Changchun Palace.\"","Qi Daiyu raised an eyebrow. Had Ji Yuanning found out about her close private friendship with Concubine Zhuang, and thinking she shared similarities with Concubine Zhuang, believed she would be more receptive to overtures?","An inexplicable irritation stirred within Qi Daiyu.","\"Let's go in and see first.\"","Ji Yuanning had been waiting for a while. As soon as she returned from the Empress's palace, she had asked the palace servants attending her about who \"Concubine Zhuang\" was. She learned that Concubine Zhuang was the birth mother of The Third Princess, had passed away while giving birth to her, and afterwards, The Third Princess had been entrusted to Concubine Hui to raise.","Ji Yuanning pulled a palace maid aside and asked, \"Do I look like Concubine Zhuang?\"","The maid was newly assigned and had never seen Concubine Zhuang up close before, only from a distance a few times. In the maid's mind, all the ladies in the palace were beauties, and beauties naturally shared some resemblances. So the maid nodded, \"There's a four or five out of ten likeness.\"","Ji Yuanning's mind became active. She thought, someone who could be granted the title of Concubine and give birth to a princess must have been deeply favored in her lifetime. If the Emperor saw her, wouldn't he inevitably think of Concubine Zhuang? Perhaps, seeing their similar appearances, he might favor her too?","She asked the maid another question, \"What is Consort Hui like? Was she on good terms with Concubine Zhuang?\"","The maid thought for a moment, \"Consort Hui doesn't go out much, so this servant hasn't had contact. However, both Her Majesty the Empress and Consort An were willing to entrust their princesses to Consort Hui's care, so she must be a good person.\" She briefly mentioned the relationships between Consort An and Concubine Shu, Consort Hui and the Empress, Concubine Shu and the Empress—of course, all this was also hearsay from other palace staff.","\"As for the relationship between Consort Hui and Concubine Zhuang, this servant has heard that The Third Princess was specifically requested by Concubine Zhuang on her deathbed to be given to Consort Hui to raise. From this alone, their relationship must have been extremely close!\"","Hearing this, Ji Yuanning felt she had grasped the situation. While practicing palace etiquette at the Southern Mountain Retreat, the instructing matron had warned her that currently, the most favored in the harem were Consort Hui, Concubine He, and Consort Li. Gaining the favor of any of these three could be a way to adapt to palace life more quickly.","Consort Li, she heard, was originally a dancing girl. Ji Yuanning looked down on her.","Concubine He was actually Ji Yuanning's first choice—noble background and with a prince by her side.","But now, having learned these secrets, she needed to reconsider.","Ji Yuanning thought to herself, when new consorts enter the palace, the established ones would surely try to win them over to consolidate their own status and favor. Compared to the other three, given her four or five out of ten resemblance to Concubine Zhuang, and out of regard for past sisterly affection, Consort Hui had no reason not to help her.","So she immediately had people prepare gifts and hurried to Changchun Palace.","As soon as Qi Daiyu entered the hall, the first thing she saw was Si Yu secretly observing from behind a screen. The wet nurse tried to pull her back, but she refused, clinging to the screen and peeking out with half her head, curiously eyeing Ji Yuanning, who sat with her back to the screen.","Qi Daiyu shot her a glare before continuing inside.","\"This concubine pays her respects to Consort Hui!\" Ji Yuanning immediately stood up and curtseyed.","\"No need for such formality. I wasn't aware of your visit, Beauty Ji. You've waited long.\" Qi Daiyu gave a slight gesture of assistance, glanced at the teacup on the table, and turned to Putao, saying, \"It's Beauty Ji's first visit, why serve this grade of tea? I recall Her Majesty the Empress bestowed two jin of Lu'an Guapian tea the other day. Go brew some quickly!\"","She didn't understand nor particularly enjoy tea, so much of the tea bestowed by the Emperor and Empress just gathered dust in the storeroom. It had become a habit for her to have guests help consume it whenever someone visited Changchun Palace.","But Ji Yuanning knew none of this. She only felt that Consort Hui's relationship with the Empress was indeed close—such precious Lu'an Guapian tea, gifted in two-jin quantities! She also felt that Consort Hui must be remembering Concubine Zhuang, hence her warm hospitality.","\"I've long heard that the tea and pastries of Changchun Palace are unparalleled in the palace. Having the honor to taste them today is this concubine's good fortune!\" Ji Yuanning smiled, the dimples on her cheeks becoming more pronounced.","Qi Daiyu's gaze lingered there for a moment, involuntarily thinking of Qin Saizhu again. In the past, it was Qixiang Palace's tea, pastries, and dishes that were considered unparalleled in the palace, even the Emperor enjoyed Qixiang Palace's cooking.","The snacks in Changchun Palace were born from her drawing upon the essence of modern knowledge, but the original dishes of Qixiang Palace came from Qin Saizhu's own innate talent for cuisine.","But a person's death is like a lamp extinguished; few in this palace remember Sister Zhu anymore.","For some reason, though Qi Daiyu had initially been prepared to engage with Ji Yuanning, she now felt a wave of impatience.","Qi Daiyu's smile faded. \"May I ask the purpose of Beauty Ji's visit to my humble abode?\""]},{"number":109,"title":"Chapter 109","paragraphs":["Ji Yuanning did not notice Qi Daiyu's mood.","She smiled gently and said, \"I have long heard that Consort Hui is kind-hearted and gentle in nature. As a newcomer to the palace, I am inevitably apprehensive. If Consort Hui does not find my visits bothersome, might I be permitted to often come to the Changchun Palace to keep you company and converse?\"","Ji Yuanning expected Consort Hui would not refuse, but instead, she heard Qi Daiyu say indifferently, \"Lady Ji, you may not know this, but I am the person in this palace who least enjoys going out. Not only that, I also do not much care for others coming to my palace to find me. I cherish tranquility. Your kind intentions are appreciated.\"","Ji Yuanning's smile stiffened.","Consort Hui cherishes tranquility?","How could the Changchun Palace, where the princes and princesses played daily, be tranquil?","Qi Daiyu wasn't finished: \"Her Majesty the Empress manages the rear palace excellently, and all the consorts are amiable people. You truly have no need to be apprehensive. If you ever truly suffer any grievance, by all means go to the Kunning Palace. Her Majesty the Empress will surely uphold justice for you.\"","A flicker of confusion passed through Ji Yuanning's eyes. She couldn't understand why Consort Hui would reject her overtures of friendship. Could it be that Consort Hui was so confident the Emperor's favor would last forever?","Ji Yuanning put on a wronged expression. \"This concubine has been presumptuous.\" After all, she too had her pride. Having been rejected, she felt she had lost face and was now ill at ease. \"Then this concubine will not disturb Consort Hui any further. This concubine takes her leave.\"","Qi Daiyu did not try to detain her, watching coldly as Ji Yuanning departed.","After the person had left, she suddenly slumped dejectedly into her chair. In truth, she couldn't quite explain why either. From the first moment she saw this Lady Ji, she had felt unable to like her, even instinctively resisting contact with her.","Perhaps it was only because of that phrase \"resembles Consort Zhuang.\"","How could they be similar?","There was only one Elder Sister Zhu. What virtue or ability did Ji Yuanning possess to compare to Elder Sister Zhu?","Qi Daiyu knew such thoughts were terribly unfair to Ji Yuanning, yet she still indulged in them willfully.","Friendship also has its order of arrival. Perhaps she and Ji Yuanning were simply incompatible by nature.","\"Mother—\" Si Yu toddled over, clinging to Qi Daiyu's leg and trying to climb up. Qi Daiyu lifted her leg, scooping the child onto her lap.","Si Yu raised her hand and placed it by Qi Daiyu's mouth. \"Smile!\"","She could tell Qi Daiyu was unhappy.","Qi Daiyu cooperatively showed a smile, resting her forehead against Si Yu's. \"Who taught you such manners, secretly hiding behind the screen to watch guests? That's impolite.\"","Si Yu giggled and leaned back. \"Don't like! Looked around!\"","Qi Daiyu was taken aback. Si Yu didn't know many words yet, but she naturally understood the meaning.","\"You mean, the guest who just came looked around everywhere after entering, and you didn't like her?\"","\"Mm!\" Si Yu nodded.","The wet nurse chimed in at the right moment: \"When Lady Ji arrived, Her Highness the Princess was playing with building blocks in the side hall. This servant originally intended to carry the Princess out to greet her, but who knew that Lady Ji would look around the room upon entering? The Princess saw it and refused to come out.\"","\"No manners.\" Si Yu mumbled, playing with her own hands.","She was talking about Lady Ji.","Because the Eldest Princess and Second Princess often came to Changchun Palace, sometimes they would play with Si Yu. The two of them, acting like adults in front of their little sister, loved to explain rules and etiquette. Once, they talked about details to pay attention to when receiving or visiting guests, one of which was not to wander or look around randomly in someone else's home.","Si Yu remembered. So, when she saw Lady Ji freely examining the main hall's furnishings, she thought Lady Ji had no manners, didn't like her, and was unwilling to go out to see her.","Eldest Sister had also said that they were princesses, and if they didn't like someone, they simply didn't have to see them—that wasn't against the rules.","Qi Daiyu tapped Si Yu's forehead. \"You little clever one.\"","Then she laughed: \"Your Eldest Sister is right. If you don't like someone, you don't have to see them.\"","That Lady Ji... it was better to keep a distance.","Originally thinking that after the Eldest Princess started attending the Imperial Study, Changchun Palace would become a bit quieter. Who knew it not only didn't quiet down, but instead became even livelier? After school, the Eldest Princess brought her two study companions: County Princess Chu Tong and Jiang Yuelan.","Well, that settled it. The Changchun Palace courtyard was now full of girls, some jumping rope, some playing house. The only boy, the Eldest Prince, was pitiful. After being ignored when seeking out his eldest sister, and ignored again when seeking out his second sister, the Eldest Prince became furious.","He stomped all the way to the Kunning Palace and brought back the Second Prince!","When Qi Daiyu, lying on her recliner, saw the Second Prince's short legs following behind the Eldest Prince, huffing and puffing as he stepped into Changchun Palace, she nearly fell off. \"Eldest Prince, how did you bring the Second Prince here? Does Her Majesty the Empress know?\"","\"Of course Mother knows!\" The Eldest Prince planted his hands on his hips. \"Now I have company!\"","\"Too bad Third Brother still can't talk.\" Otherwise, they'd have even more people!","Then they saw the Second Prince straighten his clothes and, with great respect and solemnity, clasp his hands and bow to Qi Daiyu: \"This son pays respects to Consort Hui. Before coming, this son already obtained Mother Empress's permission. For disturbing Consort Hui, please do not blame us.\"","Such a little person, so dead serious, it made Qi Daiyu want to laugh.","Especially after seeing the awkward expressions on the faces of Chu Tong and Jiang Yuelan on the other side due to the Second Prince's performance, she wanted to laugh even more.","If one thought the Second Prince was the type of child who, though young, was serious, sensible, and strictly adhered to rules, they would be wrong. This child only put on this \"act\" in front of strangers. In private, he was a clingy, coquettish little thing!","The contrast was enormous!","\"I won't blame you at all, Second Prince. Please feel free to play.\" Qi Daiyu said, stifling her laughter.","The Second Prince again clasped his hands towards County Princess Chu Tong and Jiang Yuelan: \"Greetings to my two elder cousin-sisters.\"","County Princess Chu Tong and Jiang Yuelan immediately put down the dolls in their hands and returned the courtesy: \"Your Highness, Second Prince.\"","The Eldest Princess restrained herself again and again, not exposing her younger brother's true nature. Consort Hui had said to give younger brother face in front of others.","Only Si Yu acted as if she didn't know the Second Prince. \"Second Brother is crazy...\"","She was promptly muffled by the Second Princess. \"Shh...\"","If you expose your Second Brother, he'll cling to you and cry later!","After about half a month of this commotion, seeing that Changchun Palace was about to turn into the palace kindergarten, Qi Daiyu couldn't take it anymore. She went to the Kunning Palace to find the Empress.","\"This consort believes that the Eldest Prince and Second Princess are gifted and intelligent. Starting at the Imperial Study a year or half a year earlier would be perfectly acceptable. It would also be nice for them to keep the Eldest Princess company.\" Best to also have the Imperial Study tutors increase the study load a bit more. If the Eldest Princess still had time to go to Changchun Palace, it meant the study load wasn't heavy enough.","The Empress couldn't help but laugh. \"This consort was wondering how long you could hold out.\"","With two children of her own, she often had headaches. Seeing Qi Daiyu surrounded by a crowd of children every day, she wondered how long Qi Daiyu could endure.","Qi Daiyu pouted. \"So Her Majesty was watching this consort's amusing struggle.\"","The Empress: \"The children like you. How could this consort bear to stop them?\" It truly was astonishing. Probably in the entire palace, only Qi Daiyu was so beloved by the children.","However, it truly wouldn't do to let anyone get overtired. The Empress said, \"His Majesty mentioned this matter to me yesterday, intending to have the Crown Prince and the Second Princess begin their studies early. But selecting their study companions will take some time, so you'll have to endure a few more days of hard work.\"","The Emperor had the same thought? Qi Daiyu blinked. Could it be that he heard the sounds of laughter emanating from Changchun Palace and feared his sons would neglect their studies for frivolous pursuits?","That was highly possible.","\"Cough, cough! Cough, cough!\"","Just as Qi Daiyu was guiltily wondering if she had taught the two princes anything improper, she heard the Empress suddenly break into a fit of coughing.","\"Your Majesty?\" Qi Daiyu immediately stood up.","\"This consort is fine, cough—\" The Empress's coughing grew worse. Mei Yi hurriedly patted her back and called out towards the door, \"Go quickly and fetch the medicine!\"","Footsteps clattered in the courtyard. The one who entered, however, was not carrying medicine but a eunuch from the Emperor's side. \"Empress, His Majesty has sent this servant to relay a message. An epidemic has broken out in the outskirts of the capital. To prevent it from spreading into the inner palace, movement between all palaces is strictly prohibited. All princes and princesses are to suspend their studies. Each palace is ordered to self-inspect for anyone showing signs of the epidemic. If found, they must be promptly transferred to an empty hall for containment.\"","After the young eunuch finished speaking, silence fell in the hall. Qi Daiyu's heart pounded as she looked at the Empress, who was now suppressing her coughs with visible effort, her face pale and stern. \"Go and reply to His Majesty that this consort knows what must be done. Please set His Majesty's mind at ease.\"","As soon as the eunuch left, the Empress immediately began issuing orders, arranging everything one by one: sealing off areas, checking people, cleaning, spraying medicine...","Only after everything was arranged did the Empress say to Mei Yi, \"Find a palace maid who hasn't entered this hall and summon Chief Physician Xia.\"","Mei Yi's body trembled. \"Your Majesty...\"","The Empress said, \"Go quickly.\" Then she turned an apologetic gaze to Qi Daiyu. \"I'm afraid you must stay here with me.\"","Her coughing had started a few days ago. If the epidemic had already entered the palace, perhaps she...","After the initial chaos, Qi Daiyu instead calmed down. An epidemic from the outskirts wouldn't enter the palace so easily. The Empress's cough might not be related to the epidemic; it could simply be a spring chill.","The air was still and tense. Qi Daiyu noticed carefully that beneath the Empress's seemingly calm exterior, her clasped hands were trembling slightly.","Was Her Majesty also afraid?","Qi Daiyu instinctively reached out and held those hands. \"Your Majesty, everything will be alright,\" she said earnestly.","The Empress was taken aback, then suddenly smiled.","Chief Physician Xia arrived swiftly. After inquiring about the Empress's recent condition, he began taking her pulse. \"Your Majesty seems to have merely caught a chill, resulting in a cough. It is not the epidemic from the outskirts.\"","Mei Yi looked up and let out a sigh of relief. The Empress's expression visibly relaxed as well. But the next moment, Chief Physician Xia continued, \"However, Your Majesty's heart meridian is obstructed, your body is weak and fatigued, and accumulated melancholy has led to illness. Prolonged like this, the prognosis is concerning. This current cough is also partly due to these underlying conditions.\"","When the body weakens, all manner of ailments find their way in.","Qi Daiyu's heart sank. She knew the Empress had been in poor health for nearly a year, but she hadn't realized it was this severe.","She understood the drawbacks of a weak constitution all too well. Her own body was frail, with low immunity, prone to illness from heat or cold. Over the years, she had been extremely careful, never daring to overindulge in ice even during the hottest summers.","And now, the Empress was not only physically weak but also had problems with her heart meridian.","The Empress seemed dazed. Had her health deteriorated to this extent? Her voice was slightly hoarse. \"I ask Chief Physician Xia to treat me.\"","Chief Physician Xia frowned deeply. He had the skill to treat the illness, but for the Empress, medicine alone was not enough. The obstruction in the heart meridian was caused by excessive worry and deeply entrenched, pent-up emotions. Even if his prescription were perfect, if the Empress could not open her heart and find peace, true recovery would be impossible.","The Empress saw his difficulty. \"Chief Physician Xia, please just prescribe the medicine. This consort will cooperate.\" To strive and scheme so diligently, only to lack the health to enjoy the fruits of one's labor—wouldn't that be toiling in vain for others? The Empress, clear-headed after all, quickly realized this could not continue.","\"If Your Majesty understands, then this humble official can be at ease,\" Chief Physician Xia said.","Ju Yi stepped forward. \"Chief Physician, this servant will accompany you to prepare the medicine.\""]},{"number":110,"title":"Chapter 110","paragraphs":["An epidemic raged outside the palace, and Qi Daiyu couldn't help but worry about her family. Returning to the Changchun Palace with a heavy heart, she was surprised to learn that Qi Caishang had already sent a letter ahead of her. Delivered along with the letter were several packages of medicinal herbs.","The letter's contents were simple. The gist was that Qi Caishang had noticed something amiss in the capital's outskirts some time ago and had already instructed Mrs. Wan to prepare ample medicinal supplies. There was also no need to worry about food, as the assorted grains she had sent over previously could sustain the entire family for years. The medicine sent along was prescribed by Doctor Wang from the capital, the same formula being administered to patients in the outskirts. Fearing the epidemic might breach the palace walls and that medical supplies might run short, Qi Caishang had immediately arranged for these to be sent in.","Almost as soon as the items were delivered into the palace, the Emperor issued an order to seal the gates.","Only after reading the letter did Qi Daiyu realize that Qi Caishang, as a Vice Minister of the Waterworks Bureau, frequently inspected the river embankments in the capital's outskirts and would naturally be aware of the epidemic news much sooner than she, confined within the inner palace.","With her family safe, a large part of Qi Daiyu's worry subsided.","Within Changchun Palace, only one young eunuch showed signs of a cough and had to be taken to a specially isolated palace building. Qi Daiyu instructed Shiliu to prepare some silver pieces for the eunuch and had the small kitchen prepare some durable dry rations for him to take along. This was also her way of signaling that he was not being abandoned.","The others showed no symptoms for now, so they could only wait and see.","For a time, the scent of burning mugwort wafted from every palace, Changchun Palace included. A large pot of isatis root broth simmered ceaselessly in the small kitchen. Qi Daiyu secretly poured some disinfectant into the water used to boil the mugwort. Fortunately, the smell of mugwort was strong enough, and the palace servants noticed nothing amiss.","The entire spring passed under this sealed confinement. It wasn't until the epidemic in the capital was brought under control with no new cases that the gates of the various palaces were opened once more.","Seeing the gates of Changchun Palace open, Si Yu couldn't resist wanting to go out and play. She was at that age of boundless curiosity about the world.","Qi Daiyu planned to take her for a stroll in the Imperial Garden. Unexpectedly, Quan Fuhai, the Emperor's attendant, suddenly arrived. \"Concubine Hui, His Majesty requests your presence, along with the Third Princess, at the Mingwu Terrace in the Western Garden to watch a cuju match.\"","Cuju?","Quan Fuhai explained, \"Her Highness the Empress Dowager's birthday is approaching. The Yanqing Princess suggested holding a cuju match, with teams of royal princes and noble ladies competing to add to the festive atmosphere. His Majesty has sent this servant to invite all the mistresses. In fact, I must head to the Xianfu Palace next!\"","Hearing this, Qi Daiyu did not detain him. \"I understand. After we freshen up a bit, the Third Princess and I will proceed.\"","Since they were going to watch cuju, they needed to change into more practical attire. Qi Daiyu changed both her own and Si Yu's clothes into something easier to move in and traveled to the Western Garden by sedan chair.","By the time they reached Mingwu Terrace, it was already bustling with activity.","\"Concubine Hui!\"","\"Greetings to Concubine Hui.\"","\"This must be the Third Princess? How adorable!\"","Those greeting her included princesses, members of the imperial clan, and some of the newer concubines. Qi Daiyu returned their greetings one by one before proceeding to pay her respects to the Empress Dowager and the Empress.","Si Yu imitated her actions.","\"This old one hasn't seen Si Yu in so long. Children change every day; I almost didn't recognize her!\" The Empress Dowager laughed, opening her arms. Si Yu immediately threw herself into the Empress Dowager's embrace. \"Imperial Grandmother!\"","The Empress Dowager settled Si Yu on her lap, patiently answering the child's innocent questions.","Many glances were cast in their direction, and the looks directed at Qi Daiyu were filled with envy.","Wasn't the difference between having a child and not having one in the palace perfectly clear at a moment like this?","Qi Daiyu ignored these looks. She was observing the Empress. After several months apart, the Empress's complexion looked much rosier, and the worry between her brows had lessened. She seemed to be in much better health.","Qi Daiyu couldn't help but grin.","The Empress was puzzled. \"Why such a radiant smile?\"","Qi Daiyu replied, \"This concubine sees Your Majesty in such good spirits and feels happy. Naturally, the smile is radiant.\"","\"What's so happy?\" A commanding voice sounded from behind. The Emperor had arrived.","Everyone except the Empress Dowager knelt in greeting. \"We pay our respects to Your Majesty.\"","\"Rise, all of you. Today, all present are family. No need for such formality. Speak freely and be at ease.\" Jiang Yuan went forward to speak with the Empress Dowager.","Only then did Qi Daiyu notice that Nie Zhiyu and Ji Yuanning had arrived with the Emperor. Ji Yuanning was even draped in the Emperor's cloak. The gazes of the concubines were practically boring holes through that cloak.","Qi Daiyu raised an eyebrow, asking Nie Zhiyu with a look what was going on.","Nie Zhiyu's seat was next to Qi Daiyu's, making it convenient for them to talk.","\"His Majesty summoned me to the Qianqing Palace this morning to serve ink. Seeing the time was about right to head to the Western Garden, we took the path through the Imperial Garden,\" Nie Zhiyu whispered. Nie Zhiyu had excellent penmanship and was often summoned by the Emperor to serve ink.","\"While passing the Imperial Garden, Lady Ji was feeding the fish by the Koi Pond. It's said she used pastries she made herself, which greatly attracted the fish. One koi even jumped ashore in its eagerness, splashing Lady Ji's dress. His Majesty, not wishing for her to be delayed in coming to the Western Garden, gave her his own cloak.\"","Qi Daiyu: \"...\"","\"Why that expression?\" Nie Zhiyu showed no anger at Ji Yuanning stealing the Emperor's attention. \"These new ladies entered the palace only to be met with an epidemic, not seeing His Majesty for months. It's somewhat inevitable that one or two might grow impatient.\"","Qi Daiyu: \"I just... don't quite understand her line of thinking.\" She glanced back at the smug-looking Ji Yuanning. \"And, I mourn for her.\"","Mourn? Nie Zhiyu pondered for a moment, roughly understanding the meaning of the word, and sighed. \"This Lady Ji probably doesn't yet understand His Majesty's temperament.\"","Was giving her the cloak an act of pity?","Not at all. It was to avoid spoiling the Empress Dowager's good mood.","Ji Yuanning's methods were too crude and had crossed a line His Majesty could not tolerate. Once today was over, the imperial favor she sought would not arrive; what would arrive was likely imperial wrath.","\"Enough. It has nothing to do with you or me in any case. Shall we watch the match? The one on the fastest horse is the eldest daughter of the Prince of Huai. Truly, 'the fairer sex does not yield to the men.' She's about to score!\" As Nie Zhiyu's words fell, the Prince of Huai's eldest daughter indeed struck the ball in!","Immediately, drums and gongs sounded in celebration. The children leaning on the railings clapped enthusiastically.","The joyful atmosphere infected Qi Daiyu. She stopped thinking about Ji Yuanning's affairs and focused on watching the competition.","This cuju match was divided into red and blue teams, each with sixteen players. Riding horses and wielding mallets, the objective within half an hour was to drive the ball into the opposing team's goal more times to win.","Involving tactics, horsemanship, reflexes, and teamwork, cuju matches were often fiercely competitive and highly engaging, very popular among the people of Zhao. Some regions even held annual cuju tournaments.","Qi Daiyu, after watching for just a short while, became completely engrossed. Finding the view from the stands too distant, she even activated her recording function to zoom in for a closer look!","On the other side, the Empress was also watching the match with a smile when she heard the Empress Dowager say, \"This old one remembers, your riding skills were exceptional back in the day. You even won first place in the Cuju tournament hosted by Prince Sheng!\"","Jiang Yuan also remarked, \"The Empress's riding was personally taught by Marshal Jiang. Even I feel I fall short in comparison. It has been many years since I last saw the Empress gallop on horseback.\"","While his statement about his own skills being inferior to the Empress's was modest, one could hear the genuine admiration for her prowess.","The Empress smiled faintly, \"This consort is not as bold as in her youth. Frankly, seeing such tall horses now gives me a bit of a fright. Looking at these young ladies on the field, they seem even more outstanding than I was back then.\"","Jiang Yuan placed the Empress's hand on his own knee. \"It is precisely because of your heroic and spirited bearing that paved the way for these women to ride so freely today. As the mother of the realm, your grace deeply pleases this emperor.\"","Immediately, approving murmurs of \"How deep the affection is between the Emperor and Empress!\" rose from those around them.","Noticing the tea before the Empress was finished, Ju Yi refilled it and whispered to Mei Yi, \"Sister Mei Yi, I'll go brew some more tea.\"","Mei Yi replied, \"Mm, be quick!\"","There was a tea room just behind the Mingwu Terrace, currently quite busy. As Ju Yi entered, Suihe from Concubine Shu's side was just leaving. As they passed each other, Ju Yi slipped a small pouch from her sleeve into Suihe's hand. Suihe received it without a change in expression and calmly walked away.","\"Sister Ju Yi.\" Ju Yi's heart had just settled back into place when someone called her name, causing it to leap into her throat again. She turned to find Lianwu, who served Concubine Hui.","\"Oh, it's Lianwu. Are you here to fetch tea too?\" Ju Yi forced a flustered smile. \"Come over here. We can have a chat.\"","Lianwu, who had only called out as a courtesy, was somewhat surprised. Ju Yi, who usually acted rather aloof and dismissive, why was she so friendly today?","It wasn't that Lianwu was overly suspicious. Her own mistress was on good terms with the Empress. Among the Empress's four senior palace maids, the other three had pleasant dispositions, especially Zhuyi, who, because of the Eldest Princess, had the most dealings with the Changchun Palace and was the most familiar. Mei Yi and Lan Yi were also kind to them.","Only Ju Yi had truly looked down her nose at everyone before. Later, for some unknown reason, she was punished and toned down her arrogance somewhat, but she had never acted like this before. Suppressing her unease, Lianwu walked over to Ju Yi and said with a smile, \"The hairpin you're wearing today is so lovely, Sister Ju Yi!\"","Meanwhile, Suihe, having left the tea room, did not return directly to the Mingwu Terrace. Instead, she went to a secluded corner, opened the pouch.","Inside was a prescription. Suihe recognized it at a glance—it was the prescription the Empress used to regulate her health.","A smile appeared on Suihe's face. Consort Ning had promised Ju Yi she would help arrange a good marriage for her. The condition was to provide some information about the Empress, such as her dietary preferences or her state of health.","At first, Ju Yi had been unwilling. But over the past year, under Consort Ning's deliberate shows of concern and offers of benefits, Ju Yi had gradually wavered.","Then, a few months ago, Ju Yi learned that the marriage the Empress had found for her was with a merchant who held a royal warrant. Although his family was immensely wealthy and he had no living elders, he was already twenty-seven, had been married once before, and had a three-year-old daughter. Marrying him would mean becoming a stepwife and a stepmother.","Ju Yi was not very willing. Scholars, farmers, artisans, merchants—she did not want to marry into a merchant family.","Upon learning this, Consort Ning promised to select an official's family for her, where she would be the proper first wife.","This made Ju Yi relent, and today she delivered the Empress's prescription.","A flicker of mockery passed through Suihe's eyes. Ju Yi likely thought that since this prescription was determined by the Chief Imperial Physician, Consort Ning couldn't possibly do anything with it, so this didn't count as betraying the Empress.","But Consort Ning's aims went far beyond just this prescription.","Once Ju Yi took this first step, the second and third would become unavoidable.","Carefully putting away the prescription and tucking the pouch into her sleeve, Suihe returned to the Mingwu Terrace.","Consort Ning seemed to sense something and glanced back. Seeing Suihe with downcast eyes, she turned back as if nothing had happened to watch the cuju match on the field. Only when she took a sip of tea did the rim of her cup hide the smile at the corner of her mouth."]},{"number":111,"title":"Chapter 111","paragraphs":["As the Cuju tournament drew to a close, the situation on the field had become clear. The red team, with the eldest daughter of the Prince of Huai as its core player, maintained a more significant lead. Even when the final gong sounded, the blue team failed to reverse their fortunes.","The red team was victorious, and all its members ascended the platform to receive their rewards. Looking upon the youthful and high-spirited members of the red team, Jiang Yuan was in excellent spirits. He promptly granted official posts to two of the young men and bestowed upon the Prince of Huai's eldest daughter the title of Princess Huayun.","Following the Emperor's rewards came the Empress's turn. The Empress smiled and said, \"Is there anything you desire? Feel free to speak your wish. This palace will try to fulfill it.\"","Some requested rare books, others asked for famous paintings and calligraphy. Finally, it was Princess Huayun's turn.","Princess Huayun performed a curtsy and said, \"Since childhood, I have admired Your Majesty, the Empress. I once heard that Your Majesty's horsemanship was unparalleled in the capital, but being young at the time, I never witnessed it myself. It is my selfish wish to behold Your Majesty's majestic bearing on horseback!\"","Princess Huayun's eyes were filled with hope and earnestness.","The Empress had not expected Princess Huayun to make such a request and did not reply immediately.","Everyone knew the Empress had not practiced riding or archery for many years; it was only natural her skills might have declined. However, with such a large crowd present today, failing to meet expectations could inevitably lead to unfavorable rumors.","Nie Zhiyu stepped forward to help the Empress out of the predicament: \"Your Majesty is not dressed for riding today, which might be inconvenient. Perhaps Princess Huayun would consider another wish?\"","A flicker of disappointment passed through Princess Huayun's eyes. She knew her request was somewhat abrupt, but her curiosity was genuine. Being skilled in horsemanship herself, she held even greater admiration for those who excelled at it. Among women, the Empress's reputation in riding and archery was the most illustrious. She had always regretted being born too late to witness the Empress's former glory.","\"It was presumptuous of me,\" Princess Huayun apologized.","Gazing at the young and vibrant Princess Huayun, the Empress, for reasons unknown, found her mind drifting back to her own younger self many years ago. Back then, she was just an innocent girl, unburdened by responsibilities, still harboring hopes and aspirations.","In those days, she could ride horses and shoot arrows with abandon, even daring to challenge her grandfather to a drinking contest. In her drunken bravado, she had declared she would follow her grandfather to the frontier to fight the enemy, to become a female general who would strike fear into the hearts of the Northern Li!","But somehow, without her noticing, her aspirations had shifted to becoming a qualified Empress, indispensable to His Majesty and praised by the common people.","The Empress's eyes dimmed slightly. As she lowered her gaze, she happened to meet the eyes of Lingyi, her daughter.","In that gaze, there was curiosity, surprise, and inquiry.","The Empress's heart suddenly trembled. She realized that not only had younger generations like Princess Huayun never seen her ride a horse, but her own daughter hadn't either. That was why Lingyi wore such an astonished expression upon hearing her mother once possessed such renown.","An inexplicable surge of fervor arose within the Empress. She declared, \"Since I allowed you to make requests, it would be unreasonable not to grant them.\" She turned to Jiang Yuan: \"Does Your Majesty permit your consort to try?\"","Jiang Yuan naturally would not refuse and instructed Quan Fuhai: \"I recall the Imperial Stables have a fine horse named Feixue (Flying Snow). Have it brought for the Empress.\"","Princess Huayun was overjoyed: \"Thank you, Your Majesty, for fulfilling my wish!\"","The Eldest Princess also exclaimed happily, \"Is Mother going to ride? I've never seen Mother ride a horse before. This is wonderful!\"","The Empress smiled. \"Your Majesty, I shall go change my attire first.\"","The Empress was going to ride!","This unexpected turn of events captured everyone's attention. For the moment, discussions about the recent Cuju tournament were set aside as people vied to move closer for a better view.","\"I wonder if Her Majesty the Empress's horsemanship still matches her former prowess. I was present that year, and the memory remains vivid to this day.\"","\"Isn't there a rumor that it was precisely her dazzling performance at Prince Sheng's estate that year that led the late Emperor to choose her as the Crown Princess?\"","\"Really? Is that true?\"","\"There is such a rumor. People said at the time that the Crown Princess was originally to be Consort Ning, but then it was suddenly changed to the current Empress...\" The noblewomen huddled together, whispering, and some couldn't help but glance furtively at Consort Ning.","\"Actually, it might not have been bad if Consort Ning had become Empress. In her youth, Consort Ning was famously talented and sought after by many families.\"","“Hush! Such words must not be spoken carelessly! The late Emperor's selection of a Crown Princess for the Crown Prince would never hinge on a single Cuju match. There were many considerations! Although Consort Ning is outstanding, Her Majesty the Empress is the chosen one by fate. Just look, who among the common people today does not know of the Empress's maternal grace ruling the land? Moreover, with the Empress presiding over the central palace, everyone in the harem respects her without exception. That is the Empress's capability!”","\"Exactly! Furthermore, the Empress has given birth to the Eldest Princess and the Second Prince, securing her position. Consort Ning, to this day, has no son...\"","Amidst the discussions, the Empress had already changed her clothes and led the horse into the arena below.","Qi Daiyu was fortunate enough to hold Si Yu and stand in the front row. She watched as the Empress leaped up lightly and swung herself onto the horse's back.","\"Bravo!\" Someone, it's unclear who, led a cheer, and others quickly followed.","Just the agility of her mounting revealed her solid foundation. Although there might be an element of flattery, genuine praise was also plentiful.","Qi Daiyu's admiration was quite sincere. To this day, she still felt apprehensive when mounting a horse. Who knew how many years of practice it would take to achieve the Empress's ease.","No one knew how the Empress intended to demonstrate her horsemanship.","They saw Quan Fuhai, after the Empress mounted, hand her a bow, a quiver of arrows, and a polo mallet.","Was she going to shoot arrows from horseback? A question arose in everyone's minds.","Then they saw the Empress sling the bow and quiver across her back. Holding the mallet in one hand, she flicked the reins with the other, and the horse moved forward.","It started at an ordinary pace, then grew faster and faster. The Empress's body rose and fell with the horse's gallop, dust swirling beneath its hooves.","Suddenly, the horse wheeled around. A guard in the distance struck a Cuju ball towards the Empress's direction. Galloping towards it, the Empress used her mallet to drive the ball towards the goal. When the ball was still about a hundred paces from the target, the Empress suddenly struck it fiercely with her mallet, sending it flying towards the goal.","Everyone held their breath. Then, the Empress abruptly pulled hard on the reins. The horse, reacting to the force, reared up on its hind legs. In an exaggeratedly dramatic pose, the Empress drew the bow from her back, aimed, and released an arrow at the flying ball!","\"Boom!\"","The Cuju ball, not yet fallen into the goal, exploded mid-air!","On the Mingwu Terrace, all noise seemed to hit a pause button. Many stared dumbfounded at the scene, and some, unable to contain themselves, cried out in shock.","\"Heavens!\"","What had they just witnessed?","Her Majesty the Empress had shot a rapidly moving Cuju ball from a hundred paces away, all while galloping at high speed on horseback!","This display showcased not only the Empress's superb horsemanship but also her exceptional archery!","\"Excellent!\" Jiang Yuan shouted his approval, his face beaming with shared pride.","The Emperor's exclamation seemed to open the floodgates for fervent praise of the Empress. Commendations and exclamations of astonishment poured forth incessantly.","Princess Huayun's face was flushed crimson, her whole person trembling with excitement. \"Her Majesty the Empress... is truly incredible!\"","\"The Empress is truly formidable!\" Qi Daiyu couldn't help but exclaim. The moment the ball was struck, her heart nearly stopped!","\"Amazing!\" Si Yu, in her arms, kept clapping and tried to tug at Qi Daiyu's sleeve. \"Mother, go!\"","Qi Daiyu quickly shook her head. \"This is something your mother cannot do!\"","This truly was incomparable. Probably no woman present could compare to Her Majesty the Empress.","Qi Daiyu instinctively looked at the reactions of the other consorts and concubines. Most were like her, filled with shock and admiration.","There were exceptions. Consort Ning still wore her usual calm expression, though it held a hint of unfathomable depth that wasn't there before.","Concubine Fan was different too. Her face was full of reverence and eagerness, as if she couldn't wait to try it herself immediately.","The Empress rode her horse directly to the foot of the Mingwu Platform, radiating a confident brilliance Qi Daiyu had never witnessed before, so bold and unrestrained.","\"Mother!\" The Eldest Princess ran down excitedly, with the Second Prince close behind.","The horse was tall, the children small. Looking up at their mother on horseback, they found this perspective both unfamiliar and immensely proud.","\"Mother, you are incredible! Your daughter wishes to practice archery and horsemanship, to someday ride and shoot arrows as skillfully as you, hitting the target from a hundred paces!\" the Eldest Princess declared loudly.","The Empress dismounted and stroked her daughter's head, smiling. \"Good.\"","At that moment, Jiang Yuan descended from the Mingwu Platform, followed by the others.","As the Empress was about to curtsey, Jiang Yuan took her hand and said in a voice only the two could hear, \"Nvying, seeing you win, it was as if I saw the you from our first meeting.\"","No one knew that the rumor circulating among the common folk—about the Crown Princess being decided during a polo match at the Prince Sheng's estate—held a grain of truth.","That day, Jiang Yuan, in plain clothes watching the match, witnessed Jiang Nvying's heroic bearing on the polo field, so bright and dashing, and his heart was captivated.","Afterwards, when his father, the Emperor, was to decide his Crown Princess between the Jiang and Yang families' daughters, Jiang Yuan chose Jiang Nvying without hesitation.","Even the Empress did not know she was the Crown Princess he had personally chosen.","It was just a pity that after many years of marriage, too many factors had seeped into their relationship, and both had changed far too much.","Sometimes Jiang Yuan would miss the Empress of old, but he also knew she could not return to the past, just as he was no longer the man he once was.","Hearing the Emperor's words, the Empress's eyelashes fluttered, her heart a tumult of mixed feelings. She wanted to say something, but now was not the time.","The Empress Dowager and the others had already gathered around.","Princess Yanqing stated bluntly, \"Earlier you claimed your skills had declined, but it seems you were deceiving us!\"","The Empress laughed. \"They truly had grown rusty. But somehow, once on horseback, the familiar feeling returned.\" She herself hadn't expected that after years without practicing archery and horsemanship, she could still achieve that.","Perhaps it was because the children were watching her. She didn't want to disappoint Lingyi.","The Empress Dowager said, \"This shows your foundation is solid. Old Marshal Jiang taught you well!\"","For a woman to possess such skill in archery and horsemanship was truly rare, and even more precious was that this woman was the current Empress. The Empress Dowager knew the Emperor was currently promoting the military examinations. Today's event, once spread, would surely inspire the sons and daughters of Zhao to practice martial arts with greater fervor.","Therefore, the Empress Dowager did not hold back her praise, and the others followed suit, their words of admiration never repeating.","Finally, the Empress excused herself to change her attire and asked Qi Daiyu to accompany her.","\"Quick, support me.\" As soon as Qi Daiyu reached the Empress's side, she heard these words.","Qi Daiyu instinctively complied, taking the Empress's hand, only to find it trembling violently. She paused for a moment, then carefully supported the Empress as they slowly walked out.","Only when they were out of sight did the Empress let out a bitter laugh. \"After all, I am not what I used to be.\"","Years without practice had made it difficult for her to even draw the bow. Though that single arrow hit its mark, her hand was now utterly weak from the strain. Moreover, unaccustomed to riding, her legs were also shaking, making it hard to walk. She had no choice but to let Qi Daiyu help her leave, lest she make a spectacle of herself.","The sight of the Empress forcing herself to persevere made Qi Daiyu's heart ache.","Qi Daiyu said earnestly, \"Your Majesty, you are the most remarkable woman I have ever met.\"","Her admiration came from the heart.","The Empress looked at Qi Daiyu and suddenly smiled."]},{"number":112,"title":"Chapter 112","paragraphs":["The Cuju tournament concluded with the Empress's stunning arrow shot. As expected, news of this quickly spread beyond the palace walls, becoming a hot topic of conversation among the capital's citizens.","Countless people sighed in admiration, noting that the Empress had inherited the style of the old Marshal Jiang. If she had been born a man, the Jiang family would likely have produced another general. To have such a virtuous and courageous Empress was a blessing for the nation of Zhao.","While the capital's populace had a new subject for gossip, so too did the concubines within the rear palace.","The day after the Cuju tournament ended, Beauty Ji was reprimanded by the Emperor for improper conduct. She was stripped of her Beauty rank and sent to the Compassionate Grace Temple to live as a tonsured nun, praying for the Empress Dowager's blessings.","Just yesterday, Beauty Ji had been the envy of all the concubines, draped in the Emperor's cloak. How could she have suddenly provoked the Emperor's wrath and received such a severe punishment?","What was this 'tonsured nun' business if not forcing someone to become a nun? Although the Compassionate Grace Temple was an imperial temple, life there was austere and bitter. Only women who had committed offenses were sent there.","Some consorts sent people to investigate. The events in the Imperial Garden the previous day were no secret, as many had been present. Soon, everyone learned the details.","And upon understanding the specifics, a wave of trepidation washed over them.","The reason for Ji Yuanning's downfall was not that her attempts to win favor were wrong in themselves, but that the methods she employed had crossed the Emperor's bottom line.","The route the Emperor and Consort He took to the Western Garden had been decided randomly. How was it such a coincidence that Beauty Ji was waiting by the fishpond in the Imperial Garden? There was only one possibility: she had bribed a servant from the Qianqing Palace to learn the Emperor's intended path.","Bribing someone from the Qianqing Palace to probe the Emperor's movements was an act the Emperor would never tolerate.","Sure enough, observant individuals noticed that not long after, the Qianqing Palace quietly replaced a number of its staff, and Chief Eunuch Quan Fuhai was seen walking with a limp.","Several eunuchs responsible for the fish in the Imperial Garden were also caned for dereliction of duty, accused of letting the ornamental carp overeat to death. This was the Emperor's displaced anger—the treats Beauty Ji had fed the fish must have been laced with something to make the carp swarm so eagerly.","No one had anticipated that among the new consorts who had entered the palace just a few months prior, one would already fall. This served as a stark warning to the other three newcomers, who immediately became more subdued. They dared not stage any further dramas to compete for favor, let alone entertain thoughts of becoming arrogant due to any affection they might receive. This rather disappointed some older consorts who had been looking forward to watching the newcomers fight amongst themselves.","Qi Daiyu hadn't expected the Emperor's punishment to be so severe either. She still held no fondness for Ji Yuanning, but the thought of such a young girl henceforth keeping company with only dim lamps and ancient Buddha statues stirred a sense of pity within her. The faint, smiling dimples that had once graced that face seemed to appear before her eyes. With a sigh, Qi Daiyu stood up.","\"Pomegranate, bring out that set of complexion cream I made a few days ago. We are going to the Kunning Palace.\"","After briefly explaining her thoughts, Qi Daiyu saw the Empress look at her with an expression that was both exasperated and fond.","\"You, your heart is always so soft.\"","Qi Daiyu felt quite embarrassed under that gaze. It wasn't that her heart was soft. If Ji Yuanning had truly committed some heinous crime, she would never speak up for her. But when it came down to it, neither her previous visit to the Changchun Palace seeking patronage nor her attempt to win favor in the Imperial Garden could be considered a major \"wrongdoing.\"","The Emperor punished Ji Yuanning because she had triggered his suspicious and sensitive nature as a ruler. Qi Daiyu, however, could not view it the same way.","Watching a young girl in the prime of her youth be sent to such an austere and bitter place, where her spirit might wither and her jade-like beauty fade within a few years, Qi Daiyu found she could not harden her heart to it.","Moreover, the request she made was not an excessive one.","\"It truly is no great matter,\" the Empress said. \"Very well, I shall speak to those at the Temple of Compassionate Grace and have them look after the Ji clan member discreetly.\"","In truth, the Empress felt no particular sympathy for Ji Yuanning; she naturally stood firmly on the Emperor's side. However, since Qi Daiyu was pleading for leniency on her behalf, and it was no great affair, granting the request was a simple matter.","She merely sighed inwardly, marveling at Consort Hui's kind heart. Over the years, Qi Daiyu's \"kindness\" had become deeply rooted in the Empress's perception. The Empress understood full well how rare it was to maintain such a disposition after years in the palace. As the saying goes, \"Judge by actions, not by intentions.\" Regardless of what Consort Hui truly thought in her heart, judging solely by her deeds, she was a kind person.","The Empress was willing to trust someone like this.","\"All these years, you have consistently donated silver to the capital's almshouse. Many orphans and elderly have received your beneficence, and quite a few have even had perpetual lamps lit and offerings made for you in the temples.\"","Twenty percent of the annual profits from \"Lotus Blossom Bloom,\" amounting to several thousand taels of silver, was enough to ensure that the several hundred orphans and elderly at the almshouse no longer worried about food and clothing. Many could even learn a trade to support themselves. As the Empress knew, Qi Daiyu's father, Qi Caishang, delivered several books to the almshouse every month. On his days off, he would go to teach the orphans to read and write. Mrs. Qi also frequently sent over food and clothing, clearly acting on Qi Daiyu's instructions.","The Qi family's kindness ran from top to bottom.","These deeds, which Qi Daiyu believed were done discreetly, were in fact known to both the Empress and the Emperor. It was partly for this reason that the Emperor increasingly valued Qi Caishang.","The Empress assumed the Qi family acted on Qi Daiyu's orders, but Qi Daiyu was completely unaware of Qi Caishang and Mrs. Wan's activities!","She had only thought that with so much silver being donated each year, someone should check whether the money was truly being used properly. Naturally, such a task was best entrusted to family, so she had simply informed Qi Caishang.","But Qi Caishang was shrewd. While his heart ached for his foolish daughter sending away such vast sums every year, he knew the matter had reached the Emperor's ears and was irreversible. Since they had to do this good deed, they must strive to gain every possible benefit from it.","For instance, earning his daughter a good reputation!","Qi Caishang ignored Qi Daiyu's instruction to \"observe discreetly.\" He went to the almshouse openly and made it his mission to inform everyone there that the food they ate, the clothes they wore, and the medicine they drank were all paid for by the silver from Lady Qi in the palace!","He not only built a reputation for Qi Daiyu, but also for himself. As an official, a good name was essential, especially for a scholar of his standing! Thus, he delivered several books each month—books were precious items!—and personally taught the children to read and write. He even had his elderly mother and his wife go to deliver kindness.","Qi Caishang did not mention any of this in his letters to Qi Daiyu, so she remained unaware.","Thus, upon hearing the Empress's words now, she could only feel astonishment: \"This... I am not worthy of such honor. I merely...\" She was also quite worried that the Emperor and Empress might think she was seeking fame or had ulterior motives.","The Empress patted her hand reassuringly. \"You have done good deeds; it is only right that you receive admiration.\"","Seeing that the Empress truly bore no intention of blaming her, Qi Daiyu finally set her heart at ease. A secret joy then blossomed within her; it was naturally pleasing to have a good deed remembered by others, bringing a peculiar sense of pride and satisfaction.","After chatting with the Empress a while longer, Qi Daiyu presented the skincare set. This was what she had previously promised the Empress—a custom-made skincare regimen specifically formulated for her. Qi Daiyu had gone to great lengths to understand the Empress's skin type and tolerance. After waiting for so long, she had only received this complete set two days prior.","\"As before, Your Majesty, please have the Imperial Physicians examine it first, and then have someone else test it before you use it yourself,\" Qi Daiyu advised cautiously.","The Empress smiled and said, \"I naturally trust you.\" She instructed Mei Yi to take the items and store them.","As the Emperor was set to inspect the Tiger Guard Camp in the outskirts of the capital, this year's summer was spent within the palace walls.","The palace was not like the Summer Palace; the weather was unbearably hot. With the Emperor absent, the consorts also went out less, each staying within their own palaces.","Over at the Palace of Eternal Spring, Nie Zhiyu and Ye Qiong no longer visited frequently. Only Consort Li from the Palace of Universal Happiness at the rear occasionally came to teach Qi Daiyu the zither when the evening cooled down a little, staying to chat for a while.","Ye Qiong's pregnancy was now more advanced. It was her first time with child, and she suffered from severe morning sickness, developing a particular craving for sour foods. She especially loved the sour plum preserves made in the Palace of Eternal Spring. Qi Daiyu had the cook prepare a good amount and sent them over to satisfy her cravings.","Just after Lian Wu, who had delivered the preserves, left, Lan Yi arrived suddenly, her expression extremely grave.","\"Noble Lady Hui, something has happened to Her Majesty the Empress. Please accompany this servant to the Palace of Earthly Tranquility at once.\"","Something happened to the Empress? Qi Daiyu was shocked and unsettled. \"What has happened to Her Majesty?\"","Lan Yi hesitated slightly. \"Her Majesty was suddenly seized by severe abdominal pain today, accompanied by a terrible headache, and she fainted. The Imperial Physicians were summoned and said the Empress has been poisoned. Her Majesty the Empress Dowager has already arrived at the Palace of Earthly Tranquility and ordered a strict investigation. The Empress's recent diet has been completely normal. The only thing different is that she used the beauty cream you sent, Noble Lady Hui...\"","Given the Empress's trust in Noble Lady Hui, Lan Yi was reluctant to believe Qi Daiyu had done anything. However, the Empress Dowager was furious and had ordered Qi Daiyu to be brought to the Palace of Earthly Tranquility, so she had no choice but to comply.","Qi Daiyu was stunned, her heart thrown into disarray for a moment before she quickly composed herself. She knew better than anyone whether the items she sent contained poison. If the Empress's poisoning was truly caused by that jar of beauty cream, then someone else must have tampered with it. The person behind this was targeting not only the Empress but also her.","Qi Daiyu took a deep breath. \"I will go with you at once.\"","As she walked out, she glanced at Pu Tao and made a discreet hand gesture behind her back: Check the study.","Pu Tao gave an imperceptible nod.","The study in the Palace of Eternal Spring, filled with various tools and instruments, was usually entered only by Qi Daiyu herself. Even the cleaning was not entrusted to others. The placement of every item inside followed a set pattern; Qi Daiyu would notice if anything was added or missing. Moreover, as a precaution, she had secretly installed battery-powered surveillance cameras inside.","If someone wanted to frame her, tampering in the study was the most likely method. To be safe, Qi Daiyu instructed Pu Tao to search it first.","By the time she arrived at the Palace of Earthly Tranquility, the Empress had not yet regained consciousness.","Although Qi Daiyu had been summoned, perhaps because she had previously left a favorable impression on the Empress Dowager, the Empress Dowager's attitude towards her remained relatively mild.","\"The Empress has been poisoned. I ordered an investigation into her recent diet and daily items. The only unusual thing was this beauty cream you presented to her. I had the imperial physicians examine it, and they said it contained Qilan Leaf, which is precisely what caused the Empress's poisoning. Consort Hui, do you have anything to say?\"","Qilan Leaf?","Qi Daiyu had never even heard of such a thing.","She frowned slightly. \"When I presented the beauty cream to Her Majesty the Empress, concerned that it might not suit her complexion, I specifically advised having an imperial physician examine it and having a palace maid test it first. If the cream was poisonous, how could the physicians have failed to detect it? Moreover, there have been no reports of any palace maid being poisoned.\"","As soon as she finished speaking, she noticed Lan Yi looking awkward.","Lan Yi: \"Her Majesty trusted Consort Hui, so she did not summon a physician to examine it and began using it directly...\"","The prolonged illness had indeed taken a toll on the Empress's appearance. No matter how strong-willed she was, she was still a woman. Seeing the wrinkles at the corners of her eyes, she couldn't help but feel anxious. Knowing of Qi Daiyu's talent in skincare and trusting that Qi Daiyu would not harm her, this time she did not call for a physician, nor could she wait for a maid to test it, and used the cream herself.","Who could have known that in just half a month, this would happen."]},{"number":113,"title":"Chapter 113","paragraphs":["After hearing Lanyi's words, Qi Daiyu fell silent for a moment.","The Empress trusting her so deeply was originally a good thing, but this kind of trust had provided an opportunity for those harboring ill intentions to target them both, leaving her with an indescribable feeling in her heart.","After a moment of thought, Qi Daiyu looked at the imperial physician. \"What is this Qilan Leaf?\"","She wore an expression of never having heard of such a thing. The physician dared not recklessly speculate on whether she was telling the truth or not, and merely bowed his head to share what he knew.","\"Qilan Leaf is a special plant from beyond our borders. It resembles an orchid, with petals marked by deep blue, peculiar patterns. It can emit a strange fragrance that lures people to pick it. Its stem is hollow and contains sap. Merchants from beyond the borders discovered that if the sap from the Qilan Leaf is used in medicine, especially when added to face creams commonly used by women, it can smooth the skin and has the effect of delaying skin aging. Many years ago, this substance was highly popular beyond the borders and also spread into our Zhao Kingdom, where it was quite sought after. However, it wasn't long before it was discovered that excessive use of this substance could lead to poisoning. Mild symptoms include abdominal pain, headache, and fainting; severe cases involve stomach ulcers and heart meridian blockages. Subsequently, regulations were established forbidding this substance from flowing into our country.\"","Qi Daiyu: \"Your Majesty the Empress Dowager, since this substance has already been banned, how could I, residing deep within the inner palace, possibly obtain it?\"","The Physician: \"A significant amount of Qilan Leaf was brought in from beyond the borders back then and not all of it was destroyed. It's possible some people still keep it privately.\"","The physician's meaning was that if one was determined to find it, it wasn't impossible, just requiring more effort.","Qi Daiyu: \"I have little contact with the world outside the palace, only occasionally exchanging letters with my family. Apart from letters, any items sent in from outside the palace must be inspected by the Imperial Household Department and registered. If, as this physician says, I wished to seek out Qilan Leaf, I could only ask my maternal family. In that case, Your Majesty the Empress Dowager could simply send someone to the Imperial Household Department to check whether any items sent in by my family over these past few years contained Qilan Leaf.\"","The physician spoke again: \"Judging by the Empress's current symptoms, a considerable quantity of Qilan Leaf would be required. If sent into the palace, it would naturally attract attention. However, if it were already extracted Qilan Leaf sap, concealed in containers not easily noticed, it would be very difficult to detect.\"","This physician's words almost every sentence seemed to target Qi Daiyu. She couldn't help but glance at him. She had found it strange from the moment she arrived why it wasn't Chief Physician Xia who came, but this unfamiliar-looking physician instead.","Qi Daiyu pressed her lips together. \"Your Majesty the Empress Dowager may also send someone to search my palace.\"","Whether she believed Consort Hui or not, the Empress Dowager would inevitably send someone to make a trip.","While waiting for the results during this time, Qi Daiyu wasn't idle either. She began reviewing the stored surveillance footage from the study.","Her current appearance, to others, seemed like she was sitting quietly with lowered eyes, waiting.","The Empress Dowager thought to herself that regardless of whether Consort Hui was involved in the Empress's poisoning, her composure was quite commendable.","Since only Qi Daiyu would enter the Changchun Palace study, and it remained empty at all other times, the surveillance camera was battery-powered, requiring battery changes at regular intervals. Qi Daiyu would also check the surveillance footage then. There had never been anything amiss. So, if there was a problem with the study, it could only have happened recently. Qi Daiyu reviewed the footage quickly, and before long, she noticed something wrong.","Three days ago, someone had entered the study without her knowledge.","When Nanny Zhao returned, she was followed by Lu Wei from Changchun Palace.","Who was Lu Wei?","She was a young palace maid assigned by the Imperial Household Department specifically to serve the princess after Si Yu arrived at Changchun Palace. Around fourteen years old, due to her young age, she was given light duties like sweeping, watering flowers, or playing with Si Yu.","The atmosphere at Changchun Palace was good. Qi Daiyu would sometimes jump rope or kick shuttlecocks with the palace maids in the courtyard. Qi Daiyu had an impression of this Lu Wei and remembered she was good at kicking the shuttlecock and had received a few silver ingots from her.","After entering, Nanny Zhao first glanced subtly at Qi Daiyu, then addressed the Empress Dowager: \"Following your instructions to search Changchun Palace, this old servant found this palace maid acting suspiciously, so I had her restrained and questioned carefully. This maid is timid and confessed everything. I found this in the soil of the flowerbed beneath the corridor of Changchun Palace.\"","She produced an object wrapped in a handkerchief—a jade jar about half the size of a palm, its body still smeared with some soil. The jade jar contained some deep blue liquid.","Nanny Zhao handed the jade jar to the physician. He carefully opened it, and a strong, peculiar fragrance immediately wafted out.","The physician hastily closed the lid. \"Your Majesty the Empress Dowager, this scent is precisely the strange fragrance inherent to Qilan Leaf!\"","The Empress Dowager's expression finally changed, her gaze sharp as a blade as she looked at Qi Daiyu: \"Consort Hui, this object was found in your Changchun Palace. What do you have to say for yourself?\"","Qi Daiyu asked Nanny Zhao: \"May I ask, Nanny Zhao, after you went to Changchun Palace, was it because you noticed this young maid's abnormal demeanor that you felt something was amiss?\"","Nanny Zhao: \"Exactly.\"","\"And what about my personal maids?\"","Nanny Zhao answered without hesitation: \"When this old servant announced the search, they were all cooperative, and their demeanors were all quite normal.\" They were somewhat flustered, but that was perfectly normal when suddenly faced with a palace search. And after seeing the item dug up from the flowerbed, they looked utterly incredulous.","Qi Daiyu then faced the Empress Dowager: \"Then I don't understand. If it were I who intended to harm the Empress, using this so-called Qilan Leaf, why would I entrust such an important item to a minor palace maid instead of to a personal maid or the head matron?\"","\"Some might say that going against expectations like this actually makes it less likely to be noticed,\" Qi Daiyu preempted the argument, \"But the problem is, this young maid serves the Third Princess and has only been at Changchun Palace for barely a year. For the sake of so-called 'going against expectations,' would I really take the risk of entrusting it to someone I don't trust much?\"","\"Furthermore, sending the Empress the beauty cream was half a month ago. For a full half month, wouldn't I be far too careless not to dispose of this Qilan sap?\"","Qi Daiyu slowly knelt down. \"Your Majesty the Empress Dowager, this matter is riddled with inconsistencies. How the Qilan sap entered the palace, and why it appeared in my quarters—I'm afraid there is another hidden truth behind this. I am merely a scapegoat for someone else.\"","The physician moved his lips as if to say something, but he was just a physician; speaking too much might arouse suspicion, so he lowered his head.","It was Nanny Zhao who spoke: \"But how do we know this isn't all deliberately orchestrated by you, Consort Hui, precisely to clear yourself of suspicion?\"","Qi Daiyu understood immediately that Nanny Zhao was offering her a cue. She took the opportunity to continue, \"The person who truly harmed the Empress absolutely cannot be me. What would my motive be for harming Her Majesty? Generally, to harm someone, it's either for revenge or for gain. One wouldn't just act without reason. But I bear no grudge against the Empress at all. She has always shown me great kindness and consideration, for which I am only grateful. How could I harm her? As for gain, what benefit would harming the Empress possibly bring me?\"","Everyone in the palace knew that Consort Hui had always been under the Empress's protection. If one were to name the person in the harem who supported the Empress the most, it would undoubtedly be Consort Hui.","Qi Daiyu gave a cold laugh. \"The person trying to frame me miscalculated one thing. In this entire inner palace, there is no one who wishes more fervently than I do for Her Majesty the Empress to enjoy good health and a long life!\"","Regardless of the truth behind that initial \"life-saving favor\" years ago, her interests and the Empress's had long since become intertwined. Qi Daiyu was not lying; she was absolutely the last person in the palace who would want anything to happen to the Empress. A superior like this was truly a rare find.","Qi Daiyu's argument was logically flawless, leaving even the Empress Dowager unable to find fault.","However, the undeniable fact remained that the pitcher plant juice had been found in the Changchun Palace. The Empress Dowager looked at Lu Wei and said sternly, \"Take this palace maid to the Punishment Office.\" Whether this was a frame-up or Consort Hui was simply too cunning, once this maid entered the Punishment Office, everything would become clear. Once there, one either told the truth and died quickly, or held out and endured hundreds of horrific tortures, unable to even die. The most tight-lipped person in the palace could only hold out until the twelfth punishment at most before talking. This young maid probably wouldn't last past the third.","As the maid was dragged away, the Empress Dowager turned to Qi Daiyu. \"As for Consort Hui, you are temporarily confined to the Changchun...\"","\"Your Majesty, the Empress has awakened!\" It was Mei Yi who hurried in. She glanced at Qi Daiyu before kneeling before the Empress Dowager. \"Reporting to Your Majesty, the Empress says that regarding the poisoning incident, she believes it absolutely could not have been Consort Hui's doing.\"","Qi Daiyu was stunned, a sudden ache in her nose.","The Empress Dowager also hadn't expected the Empress's first words upon waking to be a declaration of Consort Hui's innocence, but she had no time to dwell on it now. \"Since the Empress says so, then Consort Hui, you may return for now. Mei Yi, quickly take me to see the Empress!\"","Qi Daiyu wanted to say she wished to see the Empress too, but she saw Mei Yi subtly shake her head at her. Qi Daiyu had no choice but to let it go.","Exiting the main hall, Qi Daiyu saw the Eldest Princess waiting in the courtyard. She walked over.","The Eldest Princess, her eyes red, looked at her. \"Consort Hui, was it you who made Mother Empress fall unconscious?\"","Qi Daiyu crouched down. The princess was now so tall that Qi Daiyu had to look up at her.","\"Does the Eldest Princess believe I harmed Her Majesty?\"","Some of the servants in Kunning Palace were saying just that—that Consort Hui had been putting on an act all along, just to deceive the Empress and lower her guard.","\"No. You wouldn't harm Mother Empress!\" the Eldest Princess said firmly. She absolutely refused to believe Consort Hui was that kind of person.","Qi Daiyu smiled. \"That's right. I would never harm Her Majesty the Empress.\"","Watching Qi Daiyu's retreating figure, the tears the Eldest Princess had been holding back finally fell. But she quickly wiped them away. A cold severity surfaced on her young face, bearing a fleeting resemblance to the Empress's usual demeanor.","The Eldest Princess instructed Zhuyi, \"Have those gossipmongers bound. We will report them to Father Emperor upon his return. Kunning Palace cannot keep such people.\"","Her mother had told her she was a princess, one of the most esteemed figures in the palace, and she had the right to deal with those who erred.","Consort Hui had also told her that she was still young, and sometimes saying or doing things herself wasn't the best way to solve a problem; it was better to leave it to the adults. She could certainly have those gossipers punished to vent her anger, but rumors might spread that despite her youth, she was vicious and cruel. Therefore, it was better to let Father Emperor handle them.","In this palace, no one was more formidable than Father Emperor.","News of the Empress's poisoning quickly spread throughout the rear palace, eliciting varied reactions from the consorts.","In Yanxi Palace, Consort An was stringing beads when the news arrived. She paused, and the beads in her hand scattered across the floor.","Her usually stiff face was contorted with rare shock.","\"What did you say? The Empress was poisoned by pitcher plant leaves?\"","How could that be possible..."]},{"number":114,"title":"Chapter 114","paragraphs":["As soon as they returned to Changchun Palace, Yanhe, Shiliu, and others came forward to meet them.","\"Your Ladyship!\" Shiliu's face was full of concern.","Having just been searched, Changchun Palace was in some disarray. The palace servants watched cautiously from the shadows.","Before Qi Daiyu could ask, Yanhe spoke up, \"As soon as you left, this servant instructed Xiangchun to take the Third Princess to Zhongcui Palace.\" She had reacted quickly, sensing something was wrong, and immediately sent Si Yu to Nie Zhiyu's place to avoid frightening the child.","Qi Daiyu nodded, then signaled for them to continue the conversation inside.","Once inside the room, Yanhe closed the door. The four senior maids—Shiliu, Putao, Pingguo, and Lianwu—stood surrounding Qi Daiyu.","Shiliu asked, \"Your Ladyship, what exactly happened? This servant heard that the Empress was poisoned. Lanyi summoned you to Kunning Palace and forbade anyone from accompanying you. Then Matron Zhao came to search the palace. Could it be that...\"","Qi Daiyu did not respond to her. Instead, she looked at Putao. \"Did you find anything?\"","Before leaving, she had instructed Putao to check the study.","Putao nodded and took something out from her robe. \"After you left, this servant immediately searched the study. Since you had previously told this servant what all those tools in the study were for, I remembered everything.\"","There were many things in the study: various pottery jars and clay sculptures she had made when bored, as well as various vessels she used to divert attention. Although Qi Daiyu didn't allow others into the study normally, she didn't mind letting Shiliu and the others watch when she was \"putting on an act,\" as having \"witnesses\" made the act more convincing.","When Putao showed curiosity, she would even explain the names of those tools, what was inside them, and their purposes.","Qi Daiyu would thoroughly destroy every one of her \"failed experiments.\" As for the successful products she kept for herself, she would label them clearly by category, ensuring no mix-ups. After observing for so long, Putao could roughly distinguish them—this was precisely why Qi Daiyu had sent her to search the study.","\"This item, this servant found under the daybed. It seemed to have accidentally rolled under there, but this servant knew at a glance it was definitely not from the study.\" Putao handed the object to Qi Daiyu for inspection. It was a thumb-sized wooden gourd with complex, faded patterns on its surface, looking very old.","This object was utterly out of place, not just in the study, but in the entire Changchun Palace.","Qi Daiyu wrapped a handkerchief around her hand before taking the wooden gourd. It was very light. On the top was a bean-sized protrusion. Qi Daiyu felt that area and detected a slight irregularity.","She said, \"Fetch a needle.\"","Shiliu immediately went to get one.","Walking to the window, Qi Daiyu used the light coming through the paper pane. She inserted the needle into the irregular spot and pried it forcefully. With a soft \"click,\" the protruding part popped open and fell to the floor, rolling. Pingguo, quick-eyed, covered it with a handkerchief.","Everyone looked at the gourd body in Qi Daiyu's hand.","Once the hidden top was removed, a peculiar fragrance wafted from the gourd. The scent was not strong, but it was strangely captivating, making one want to take a deep breath.","Qi Daiyu held the gourd a bit farther away and extended her other hand. Yanhe immediately placed her own handkerchief over Qi Daiyu's hand. Qi Daiyu tilted the wooden gourd, and soon some pale blue powder flowed out.","The fragrance emanated from this powder.","\"Fetch some water,\" she said.","Shiliu promptly poured a cup of water. Qi Daiyu poured the powder from her hand into the cup. Before long, the powder dissolved, turning the entire cup of water a deep blue.","\"It's Qilan leaf juice,\" Qi Daiyu stated. \"This fragrance is exactly the same as the scent of the Qilan leaf juice dug up from the flower bed. This powder is likely Qilan leaf pollen.\"","How interesting. Burying it in the flower bed wasn't enough; they had to place it in her study as well.","Shiliu was furious. \"That Lu Wei has some nerve! How dare she frame Your Ladyship!\"","Then she felt puzzled. The outer flower bed was one thing; anyone could go there. It would indeed be possible to act during night watch. But this study was inside the main hall. Lu Wei, a junior maid, had no chance to enter...","Then she heard Qi Daiyu say, \"It wasn't Lu Wei.\"","Putao asked, \"Your Ladyship means someone else entered the study?\"","Yanhe inquired, \"Does Your Ladyship suspect someone?\"","In the entire Changchun Palace, very few could enter the main hall. Eunuchs were immediately ruled out; even Xiao Li and Little Cheng could only enter when summoned by Qi Daiyu. Among the maids, apart from the head maid Yanhe and the four senior maids Shiliu, Putao, Pingguo, and Lianwu, only the four second-rank maids—Xiangli, Hongtao, Sangsen, and Lizhi—as well as Xiangchun and the two wet nurses caring for the Third Princess could enter. However, when Xiangchun and the wet nurses were present, others would inevitably be there too, as they weren't strictly Qi Daiyu's personal maids and required supervision.","So, ultimately, only nine people had the opportunity to enter the main hall and the study.","The fact that their mistress had the five of them follow her inside showed her trust in them. Therefore, the traitor must be among the remaining four.","Who could it be?","\"Whoever it is, I swear I'll chop off her hands!\" Shiliu rarely showed such temper, uttering such harsh words.","She was not only angry that someone harbored ill intent and betrayed their mistress, but also heartbroken.","Xiangli and Hongtao need not be mentioned; they had served since the Yanqing Residence days, and they all addressed each other as sisters. As for Sangsen and Lizhi, she and Putao had been training them as successors, so that after she and Putao left the palace, they could continue to care for their mistress.","Shiliu couldn't understand who among them would betray.","Qi Daiyu couldn't comprehend it either. She considered herself an exceptionally good superior—never harsh towards the servants, easy to talk to, undemanding, and very generous. For what possible reason would someone betray her?","Her face cold, she said, \"Go, without alerting anyone, bring Hongtao here.\"","Yes, the person Qi Daiyu had seen in the surveillance footage was precisely Hongtao.","Under the pretext of cleaning the main hall, she had slipped into the study when no one was looking and hastily thrown the wooden gourd under the daybed.","Hongtao was soon brought in.","Her expression seemed normal, even with a touch of concern in her eyes, as if worried for Qi Daiyu.","After paying her respects, Hongtao asked solicitously, \"Your Ladyship, has something happened?\"","Qi Daiyu got straight to the point, holding up the wooden gourd. \"Hongtao, does this object look familiar to you?\"","Hongtao's gaze fixed on the wooden gourd for a moment, stiffening. She forced a smile and adopted a puzzled expression. \"Your Ladyship, what is this? This servant has never seen it before. How could it be familiar?\"","\"Is that so? Wasn't it you who placed this in my study?\"","Hongtao felt an explosion in her ears, her heart pounding like thunder. Her mind raced, utterly unable to comprehend how Consort Hui knew it was she who had placed the gourd in the study! She had been so confident, certain no one had seen her at the time!","Right, absolutely no one could have discovered it. So, Consort Hui must be trying to trick her?","Hongtao instantly calmed down. It must be Consort Hui trying to trick her. Consort Hui had detected a betrayal but couldn't pinpoint who it was, so she was calling in the suspected individuals one by one. Now it was her turn; perhaps the next would be Xiangli or Sangsen.","So Hongtao knelt down, her eyes reddening. \"This servant does not understand what you are saying, my lady. You gave orders that no one was to enter the study. How would I dare disobey your command?\"","She was putting on quite an act. If Qi Daiyu didn't have surveillance, she might have almost believed it.","\"It seems you are unwilling to talk.\" Worried about the Empress, Qi Daiyu didn't want to waste time on further argument.","She ordered Yanhe, \"Lock her in a room, tie her up, and don't let her sleep until she is willing to talk.\"","Qi Daiyu leaned forward slightly, looking down at Hongtao with an unprecedented coldness in her expression. \"I was easygoing before because I considered you one of my own. But since you don't abide by the rules yourself, don't blame me for being ruthless.\" She straightened up, her posture lofty and imposing. Paired with her cool and aloof face, it sent an involuntary chill through one's heart.","\"I once heard a story. To tame a fierce hawk, a hunter would prevent it from sleeping for many days in a row until its wild nature was worn away. I wondered then, if preventing sleep could tame a hawk's wildness, what would happen to a person if they were prevented from sleeping?\" Qi Daiyu glanced at Hongtao and instructed Yanhe, \"Lock her in a room, tie her up, use wooden sticks to prop her eyelids open, and don't let her sleep.\"","Yanhe bowed her head. \"Yes.\"","Hongtao tried to resist. \"My lady, I have done nothing wrong. Why are you treating me this way... Mmm.\" She attempted to cry out to attract others' attention, but Putao covered her mouth.","After Hongtao was dragged away, Shiliu's face still bore traces of lingering anger. \"Mistress, given Hongtao's status, it's impossible for her to obtain something as rare as Qilan leaves. Someone must be behind this, instructing her. Who is trying to harm you and the Empress?\" That person behind the scenes not only wanted to harm the Empress but also to drive a wedge between you and her. Truly despicable!","Qi Daiyu was also pondering the matter. Logically, the Empress presided over the central palace. Though strict, she was fair. The consorts and concubines might have private grievances, but they shouldn't go so far as to attempt the Empress's life. If it wasn't a personal vendetta, then perhaps... it was for the position of Empress?","Having watched plenty of palace intrigue dramas, Qi Daiyu's ability to make connections was quite good. But she soon frowned again.","For the Empress's position? The Empress and the Emperor shared a deep bond, and she had children to rely on. Her position was extremely secure. Even if the Empress were gone, who in the palace could contend for that position?","Consort Ning, or... Nie Zhiyu?","Consort Ning had family background and seniority. Nie Zhiyu had a prince and her family background was also good. But Consort Ning had always maintained an aloof, non-competitive demeanor, and Nie Zhiyu had aligned herself with the Empress since entering the palace. Neither seemed like someone who would move against the Empress.","Qi Daiyu felt troubled and restless. To find out who it was, they still had to wait for Hongtao to talk.","She also decided she needed to review the videos she had recorded before, to see if she could discover any clues.","Meanwhile, in Yanxi Palace, Consort An dismissed her attendants and entered her bedchamber alone. After ensuring the doors and windows were closed, she walked to the bed, lifted the bedding, revealing a hidden compartment in the bed frame. Consort An reached to touch the small lock on the compartment, and her heart turned cold.","Someone had tampered with this lock.","But Consort An still clung to hope. She opened the compartment, only to find that a small wooden gourd inside had vanished without a trace. Her expression finally grew heavy.","Her Qilan leaf pollen was gone.","Consort An closed her eyes tightly, her fingernails digging into the bedding. She felt the stiff skin on her face aching faintly, a tearing pain that made her feel as if she had been transported back many years.","Back then, not long after giving birth to the Second Princess, her belly was covered in stretch marks, and star-like spots and streaks had appeared on her face.","For the consorts and concubines in the palace, beauty was one of the most important assets. Seeing that the marks on her face wouldn't fade no matter what medicine she used, Consort An thought of something.","It was a rare substance from her mother's homeland, called Qilan leaves.","Qilan leaves were banned from entering Zhao, but Consort An's mother was originally from a foreign region, so obtaining them wasn't difficult. Consort An had brought some with her when she entered the palace.","The world knew that extracting the sap of Qilan leaves for medicine could moisturize the skin and have anti-aging effects. But few knew that if the pollen of the Qilan leaf was dissolved in water and applied to the face, it could restore youthfulness to one's appearance, eliminating any scars or blemishes.","However, such a miraculous substance naturally had side effects. Poisoning from Qilan leaf sap could cause, in mild cases, diarrhea and headaches; in severe cases, gastrointestinal ulcers and heart meridian blockage. As for Qilan leaf pollen, because few used it, its side effects were not clearly known. At that time, Consort An, feeling desperate and wanting only to restore her face to its former state, didn't care about potential side effects.","Moreover, she told herself then, she would only use a little, just a little, and never overdo it.","Later, the blemishes on her face and the stretch marks on her belly indeed faded. But before she could rejoice, she discovered her face was becoming increasingly stiff. Slowly, she couldn't even smile anymore.","Consort An didn't dare reveal her use of Qilan leaf pollen. The imperial physicians only said she had a \"facial paralysis,\" likely a postpartum complication.","But only she knew the real reason.","If asked whether she regretted it, Consort An did not. For her, living with a stiff face was better than living with a face full of blemishes.","So she hid the Qilan leaf pollen well, never showing it to anyone.","But now, that wooden gourd was gone!","If the Qilan leaves that poisoned the Empress came from her...","More than the fear of being traced back to her, Consort An worried about another matter.","Both Qilan leaf sap and Qilan leaf pollen shared a common trait: everyone who wanted to try them told themselves they would only use a little. But the fatal allure of Qilan leaves was addictive..."]},{"number":115,"title":"Chapter 115","paragraphs":["Consort An dared not think further. What was more important to her now was to figure out why the Qilan leaf pollen from the secret compartment had disappeared.","There were few people who could enter her bedchamber and have the opportunity to take the Qilan pollen. Consort An almost instantly narrowed it down to a few suspects. What she needed to do next was to identify the culprit among them! She was determined to find out who was trying to divert the trouble onto her!","While the Changchun Palace and the Yanxi Palace were busy rooting out traitors, the Kunning Palace was no exception.","After waking up, the Empress was lucid for a brief moment. Besides speaking up for Qi Daiyu, she gave Mei Yi another order: pay close attention to the movements of everyone in the Kunning Palace.","If that jar of nourishing cream hadn't been tampered with before it left the Changchun Palace, then it must have been altered within the Kunning Palace. However, the Kunning Palace was different from other places. The Empress managed affairs of all the palaces, and every day, a continuous stream of stewards from various departments came to report, along with titled ladies entering the palace upon request. This greatly expanded the scope of the investigation.","Empress: \"We must investigate both inside and outside the palace, especially within the palace itself. Even Lanyi, Zhuyi, them, and Li Lu must not be overlooked.\" She wasn't suspecting any of them specifically, but it was possible one of them had been used without their knowledge.","Mei Yi was a household servant of the Jiang family who had served her since childhood; the lives of her entire family were tied to the Empress. Betrayal was absolutely impossible, and the Empress trusted Mei Yi the most.","Mei Yi nodded: \"This servant understands completely.\"","The Empress still felt abdominal pain and nausea. Moreover, for some reason, she felt a slight, tearing pain on the skin of her face and could vaguely smell a strange fragrance, which made her somewhat irritable.","\"It seems I have been ill for too long, allowing some to nurture improper thoughts,\" the Empress said with a bitter smile. The exhaustion from a year of trivial duties, coupled with the dual torment of physical and mental illness, had left her in poor condition, and her management of the Kunning Palace had slackened considerably.","Mei Yi said guiltily, \"It was this servant's negligence that caused Your Majesty to suffer.\"","Empress: \"How can I blame you?\" She blamed no one.","As the head senior maid, Mei Yi had many responsibilities. She was also utterly loyal, spending all her time worrying about the Empress's health and recuperation. Lanyi, following her orders, took care of the Second Prince. Zhuyi looked after the Eldest Princess. And Ju Yi had to deliver messages to various places and report back to the Kunning Palace, leaving no spare time either.","Naturally, the management of the Kunning Palace had become lax.","Empress: \"After this matter is settled, we must also promote Hua Hu and Hua Rui.\" Hua Hu and Hua Rui were palace maids the Empress was training for future use. \"When you and Ju Yi marry and leave the palace, I won't be left with no one to rely on.\"","Among the four \"Yi\"s, Lanyi and Zhuyi had already decided to stay in the palace permanently, having put up their hair. As for Mei Yi and Ju Yi, the Empress had already found suitable marriages for them.","Mei Yi had someone she fancied—her cousin, who was somewhat scholarly and had passed the county-level imperial examination two years ago. He was also waiting for Mei Yi to leave the palace. The Empress would release Mei Yi's family from servitude, restoring their status as commoners, and prepare a generous dowry for Mei Yi.","Ju Yi had a proud temperament and couldn't endure hardship. Originally, she could have been matched with an official, but due to a problem with her leg, the choices were fewer. The Empress had finally settled on a merchant who supplied the imperial household. Although it was his second marriage, there were no elders above him. Ju Yi would manage the household as soon as she married. With Ju Yi's connection, the family's business would be very stable. The husband would only cherish Ju Yi and would never let her suffer. Although he had a daughter from his previous marriage, she was only three. If Ju Yi was kind and taught her well, the child would naturally regard her as her birth mother. Once Ju Yi bore a son in the future, her life would be even more comfortable. The merchant status was lower, but it guaranteed a life of wealth. And a low status wasn't a big issue; once Ju Yi had a son, he could later take the imperial examinations and change the family's status.","As the Empress spoke, she started coughing again.","Mei Yi said worriedly, \"Should this servant send an urgent letter to hurry Doctor Xia back?\"","The Emperor had gone to the outskirts of the capital to review troops and had taken Doctor Xia with him, which was why he wasn't in the palace.","Mei Yi thought to herself that perhaps the person who harmed the Empress had dared to act precisely because the Emperor and Doctor Xia were both away.","The Empress was about to say it wasn't necessary when a sudden palpitation struck her.","She clutched her chest, her face abnormally pale. Mei Yi immediately called for help.","Changchun Palace.","In a certain hidden room, Hongtao had originally thought that not being allowed to sleep, compared to punishments like flogging, nail-pulling, or branding, at least spared her physical pain. She could endure it for a while and it would pass.","Therefore, she remained silent, saying nothing, and when she did open her mouth, it was only to say things like \"My mistress has wronged me.\"","Then she was taken into a room.","Xiao Li tied her up, ordered the windows sealed shut so not a sliver of light could enter, then used two wooden sticks to prop open her upper and lower eyelids, preventing her from closing her eyes. Her hair was also tied to a rope hanging from the ceiling beam, so that any attempt to lower her head would painfully pull her scalp.","Xiao Li sneered at her, \"Our mistress is kind-hearted and cannot bear to subject you to physical torture. You just endure this.\" He stuffed a wad of cloth into Hongtao's mouth.","Kind-hearted? Hongtao was more inclined to believe it was because Concubine Hui dared not use illegal torture, hence resorting to these methods that left no visible marks.","Watching the door slowly close, cutting off the last bit of light, Hongtao felt inexplicably panicked, but quickly calmed herself. She just had to endure for a few days. Without evidence, Concubine Hui could do nothing to her.","At first, Hongtao only felt dryness, soreness, and pain in her eyes, tears falling uncontrollably.","Slowly, she began to feel sleepy—the room was too quiet and dark, drowsiness easily overwhelmed her. But with her eyelids propped open, she couldn't close her eyes to sleep, forcing herself to stay awake. She didn't know how long she held on, only that she grew sleepier and sleepier. Even though she couldn't close her eyes, the desire to sleep was unstoppable. Yet, the moment her consciousness started to fade, an intense pain shot through her scalp from the pull, jolting her awake again!","She couldn't sleep. She was unable to sleep.","Hongtao's inner turmoil grew increasingly agitated and oppressive. Compared to hunger, thirst, and the inability to sleep, the sense of unease brought by the pitch-black, utterly lightless room intensified. She tried to make sounds, but only her own muffled whimpers echoed in the room.","Even though it was her own voice, it sent chills down Hongtao's spine.","She couldn't help but think of various terrifying legends.","\"Ah!!!\"","Xiao Li requested an audience with Qi Daiyu.","\"Mistress, Hongtao is ready to confess.\"","Qi Daiyu let out a long sigh of relief. Finally, she was going to talk.","Actually, only two days had passed since Hongtao was locked away, but Qi Daiyu was already growing impatient.","When Hongtao was brought in, she was clearly mentally disturbed, appearing somewhat deranged. The moment she saw Qi Daiyu, she frantically tried to crawl towards her, but was restrained by Xiao Li and Little Cheng.","Seeing her state, Qi Daiyu felt somewhat uncomfortable, a slight pang of pity arising, but she quickly hardened her heart and stared coldly at Hongtao.","\"Master, Mistress! This servant will speak, this servant will tell everything!\" Having not eaten for two days, Hongtao was weak, speaking breathlessly and gasping. Qi Daiyu had someone give her half a cup of water.","Hongtao drank it hastily, her face wet with what could have been tears or tea. \"It was Xi, Xi from the Yanxi Palace! She was the one who gave that thing to this servant!\"","Xi? Yanxi Palace?","Qi Daiyu's heart jolted. It was Consort An! This was truly unexpected.","Qi Daiyu had already experienced Consort An's deep scheming during the incident with Concubine Mei. If Consort An was the one who acted, it was indeed possible.","Yet, she frowned slightly. Why would Consort An want to harm the Empress?","Since giving birth to the Second Princess and contracting that strange illness, Consort An had almost no imperial favor. Even when the Emperor visited Yanxi Palace, it was only to see the Second Princess, rarely staying the night. Moreover, Consort An's family background was average, which was why she remained only at the consort rank. Could there be some past grievance between Consort An and the Empress?","Qi Daiyu wasn't sure.","Consort An had entered the Eastern Palace earlier than the original host, so it was normal for there to be past events the original host didn't know about.","Qi Daiyu hesitated. The situation with the Empress was not good; she had sent someone to inquire and learned the Empress's heart condition had flared up, leaving her unable to manage affairs. The mastermind behind this didn't know she had discovered Hongtao yet and would surely lie low. But if she handed Hongtao over now, it might alert the enemy.","Wait for the Emperor to return to the palace!","The news of the Empress's incident had already been sent out. The Emperor was estimated to return within the next few days. Given the Emperor's regard for the Empress, he would definitely investigate strictly.","Having reasoned this out, Qi Daiyu ordered Xiao Li to take Hongtao away and guard her well, ensuring no news leaked.","Xiao Li grinned. \"Rest assured, Master. This servant handles things thoroughly.\" This was no lie; although he was more slick than Little Cheng, he was also much more clever.","As Xiao Li stepped forward to cover Hongtao's mouth, Shiliu couldn't hold back any longer, asking with hatred in her voice, \"Hongtao, why on earth did you betray our master?\"","Qi Daiyu also couldn't help but look over. She was very curious about this question too.","They saw Hongtao lower her head, shoulders trembling, unsure if she was laughing or crying.","\"Yes, the master is very good to the palace servants. But by following this master, I will never have a chance to rise! Even those little maids Sangsen and Lizhi have climbed up. Why can't I? Where am I inferior to Pingguo or Lianwu?\" They all started serving the master at the same time, they were all second-rank palace maids. Why could Pingguo and Lianwu be promoted, while she remained a second-rank maid?","She was just... unwilling, that's all.","Xi said that she was of age to be released from the palace, which would leave a senior maid position vacant by Consort An's side. Consort An had long thought Hongtao clever. If Hongtao helped Consort An accomplish one thing, Consort An would ask Concubine Hui to transfer Hongtao over.","Shiliu was furious. \"For this?\" For the position of a senior maid, she chose betrayal?","She couldn't help but strike Hongtao. \"Have you forgotten how good the master was to you? Has your conscience been eaten by dogs?\"","Hongtao was full of regret, but still said, \"You entered the Changchun Palace as a senior maid from the start, of course you don't care!\"","Shiliu raised her hand to strike again.","\"Enough. Take her away.\" After hearing Hongtao's reason, Qi Daiyu was the one who accepted it most calmly. Workplace intrigue, reporting on others, and betrayal were all too common. She had previously thought that in this world with its clear distinctions of nobility and baseness, the loyalty between master and servant couldn't be equated with workplace relationships. But she had forgotten: where there are people, there is ambition.","Hongtao's betrayal for a senior maid position might seem laughable to others, but perhaps to Hongtao, she was willing to pay any price to compete for that position.","In the end, it was her own failure to judge character correctly.","She had been pecked in the eye by the hawk she raised! Consort An never would have imagined that the mole would be Xi.","Consort An was meticulous and had her own methods for managing Yanxi Palace. It didn't take much effort to ferret out Xi.","When Xi was brought before Consort An, her face was ashen; she knew she was exposed.","\"When did this start? Were you bought off in recent years, or were you a pawn planted by someone else beside this consort from the very beginning?\" Consort An asked.","Xi knelt on the ground. \"This servant has wronged you, Master.\"","Consort An then understood. Xi was assigned to her when she moved into Yanxi Palace after the Emperor ascended the throne. From that moment on, she was a hidden piece. All these years, she had served diligently, seeming no different from Puying and the others. But when her true master gave the order, she acted.","\"What elaborate planning. Let this consort guess who your true master is.\" Consort An said firmly, \"Consort Ning?\"","Xi's expression didn't change.","\"Or... Concubine Shu?\"","Xi's eyelashes trembled slightly.","Consort An raised her hand and smashed the teacup on the table. \"Well done, Concubine Shu! I underestimated her!\" Thinking about it, in the early days of the Emperor's reign, only a few had the ability to plant people in the harem. She had been close to Concubine Shu, so naturally Concubine Shu would also be wary of her. She just never expected that even after the Yuan family's decline and Concubine Shu's house arrest, she could remain patient, only activating Xi now.","Seeing the situation exposed, Xi stopped pretending. \"When you were pregnant with the Second Princess, the midwife was still found by Concubine Shu. The midwife naturally knew about the marks on your body, but later those marks disappeared. Concubine Shu sensed something was amiss and ordered this servant to keep a careful watch. That hidden compartment hadn't been touched for years. This servant only discovered it by accident once while cleaning the room. After informing Concubine Shu, she told this servant not to act. It wasn't until a few days ago that she ordered this servant to take the wooden gourd from that compartment and place it in the Changchun Palace.\"","\"Consort An, this servant has wronged you. However, this servant's life was saved by Concubine Shu. What Concubine Shu orders this servant to do, this servant cannot refuse. Your Ladyship also need not hope that this servant will expose Concubine Shu. This servant would rather die than betray Concubine Shu.\"","Consort An gnashed her teeth. \"Your duty to Concubine Shu is understandable, and this consort's duty not to let you off is also understandable.\"","She stood up. \"For Concubine Shu to still wield influence under house arrest, she couldn't have managed it alone. It seems this consort must pay a visit to the Chengqian Palace.\"","She had many questions that could only be answered by meeting Concubine Shu.","Fortunately, with the Emperor absent from the palace and the Empress ill, it wasn't difficult for Consort An to enter the Chengqian Palace unnoticed.","After nightfall, Consort An carried a palace lantern and entered the Chengqian Palace, with Puying following behind.","Compared to the splendid Chengqian Palace of years past, the present one was dim and gloomy. Weeds grew in the corners of the courtyard, suggesting the servants in charge of maintenance were not diligent. Of course, now the palace only housed the house-arrested Concubine Shu and the Eldest Prince. The Emperor never visited, so what need was there for meticulous upkeep?","If not for the Eldest Prince residing there, the Chengqian Palace would likely have fallen into complete neglect, becoming a cold palace.","Approaching the main hall, Consort An faintly heard sounds of laughter. She listened carefully; it was Concubine Shu and the Eldest Prince talking.","Eldest Prince: \"I haven't had any pastries from Concubine Hui's palace for several days now!\"","Concubine Shu: \"Eat, eat, eat, all you know is eating! Don't you see how much flesh is on your face now? You're almost a little fatty! If you keep going like this, your Imperial Father won't like you anymore!\"","Eldest Prince: \"He will! Imperial Father always likes to pinch the flesh on my cheeks when he sees me. Concubine Hui said I'm lively and cute, Imperial Father likes me very much! It's you, Mother, who did something wrong, that's why Imperial Father doesn't come to see you. I haven't done anything wrong. If I want to see Imperial Father, I can just go to the Palace of Heavenly Purity and request an audience!\"","Concubine Shu: \"Concubine Hui, Concubine Hui! That Qi Daiyu just gave you some pastries and you're completely charmed. Who is your real mother, after all?\"","Eldest Prince: \"The Empress in the Palace of Earthly Tranquility is my mother according to ritual law. You, Mother, are the mother who gave birth to me. The other ladies are my concubine-mothers. Ah, I have too many mothers!\"","Concubine Shu: \"This child is going to be the death of me!\"","Eldest Prince: \"Mother, don't be angry. Getting angry gives you wrinkles, and then you won't be pretty anymore. Don't worry, when I grow up, I'll take care of you. Concubine Hui says all princes are enfeoffed as kings when they grow up. When that time comes, I'll have my own princely mansion, and I can move you there. Then you won't have to stay in this little Palace of Celestial Favor anymore!\"","Concubine Shu: \"Can't you aim a little higher? What's the use of just being a prince?\"","Eldest Prince: \"Being a prince is great! I want to be a prince!\"","\"Tap, tap,\" the hall door was knocked. The young palace maid who opened the door was startled to see Consort An and immediately turned back to announce her.","They only heard the Eldest Prince rush out like a little firecracker, smiling at Consort An. \"Consort An, why have you come? Are you here to see my mother? Then you should come in quickly, don't let others see you. If Imperial Father finds out, he'll punish you!\"","He looked behind Consort An and mumbled, \"Why didn't you bring Second Sister along?\"","Entering the main hall of the Palace of Celestial Favor again, Consort An couldn't describe her feelings. When she saw the person sitting on the daybed, she was even more taken aback.","The last time she saw Concubine Shu was nearly three years ago, when Concubine Shu had just been confined. Although disheveled, her charm was still evident. But now...","Now, time and despondency hadn't left many traces on Concubine Shu's face. She was still as beautiful as a peony or a Chinese herbaceous peony, only this peony had become an extra-large one...","Consort An's astonishment was something even her stiff face couldn't hide. Concubine Shu, feeling uncomfortable under her gaze, glared and said, \"What are you staring at me for?\" So what if she had gained a few dozen pounds?","With her maternal family's property confiscated and herself under house arrest, a proud person like Concubine Shu was just perpetually furious. She got angry every day and ate a lot. Ironically, the imperial kitchens had orders not to mistreat her, but they wouldn't provide the finest delicacies either, sending meat dishes full of fatty cuts no one liked. Trapped day after day, Concubine Shu grew fatter and fatter.","However, Concubine Shu believed that even fat, she was still a beautiful fat woman.","And that was indeed true.","Concubine Shu guessed why Consort An had come to the Palace of Celestial Favor and told the Eldest Prince to go back first. \"Remember to review your lessons. Your handwriting is hideous. Practice more so your Imperial Father will praise you when he returns to the palace!\"","Eldest Prince: \"Mother, your handwriting is worse than mine!\" With that, he scampered off.","\"That child!\" Once the Eldest Prince left, Concubine Shu wiped the smile from her face and stared at Consort An with an ambiguous expression. \"What important business brings Consort An to my dilapidated Palace of Celestial Favor?\"","Knowing Concubine Shu's temperament well, Consort An didn't beat around the bush. \"Have you gone mad, daring to act against the Empress?\"","Concubine Shu didn't even blink. \"The downfall of my Yuan family couldn't have happened without the Empress's push. If something happens to the Empress, naturally I am pleased.\"","She wished the Empress dead.","Consort An: \"Aren't you afraid of implicating the Eldest Prince?\"","Concubine Shu: \"Why would it implicate the Eldest Prince? The poison the Empress took came from the Qi Lan leaves in your possession, didn't it? What does that have to do with me?\"","Xi would never betray her.","Consort An gritted her teeth. \"Why frame me? We agreed before. I would help you look after the Eldest Prince, and you would keep secret my involvement in Concubine Mei's affair. Wouldn't it be better to just muddle through like that? You're confined. When the Eldest Prince grows up, if he wants to contend for that position, won't he still need my help?\"","Mentioning the Eldest Prince actually made Concubine Shu more agitated.","\"Help me look after the Eldest Prince? Consort An, I indeed kept my word to conceal your affair. But dare you swear that you have never been disloyal to me, that you have genuinely cared for the Eldest Prince?\" Concubine Shu's eyes were venomous.","Consort An faltered. She...","Concubine Shu grabbed Consort An by the collar. \"Consort An, you've always been clever, and I was willing to treat you as my strategist. Yes, my temper isn't good, and I wasn't exactly affectionate towards you. But for the sake of the Eldest Prince, I was willing to protect you. And how did you repay me? The Eldest Prince has a Te Lin constitution, yet you deliberately had people take him to places like the Imperial Garden, full of flowers, nearly causing him to have an asthma attack. Do you think I truly didn't know about this?\"","Consort An: \"I...\"","\"You wanted to eliminate the Eldest Prince, and eliminate me, to truly have no worries left, right?\" Concubine Shu sneered. \"You understand my nature, but do you think I don't understand yours?\" Precisely because she understood, she had never used Xi. She had to keep a hold over Consort An.","Consort An admitted she had underestimated Concubine Shu.","Consort An took a deep breath. \"Yes, I admit, I did have that thought once. But as you can see, the Eldest Prince is alive and well. I am not someone who disregards past ties!\"","She had long since realized that only by letting the Eldest Prince live and grow up well would it be most beneficial for her and the Second Princess. She had no imperial favor, the Second Princess was not valued. In the future, the Second Princess's marriage might also require the Eldest Prince's influence. So she had long resolved to take good care of the Eldest Prince. In fact, she had done so. Whatever the Second Princess had, the Eldest Prince had too, sometimes even more than the Second Princess!","That's why the Eldest Prince was only happy to see her earlier!","\"Do you think by framing me for the poisoning, you can rest easy? You're making a pact with a tiger. What outcome can there be besides harming yourself and the Eldest Prince?\"","Concubine Shu was taken aback and said unnaturally, \"What are you talking about?\"","Consort An: \"At this point, you're still hiding things from me? Confined here in the Palace of Celestial Favor, how do you know about affairs outside? How could you meddle in the affairs of the Palace of Earthly Tranquility? In this palace, who else has that kind of power besides the one in the Palace of Earthly Peace?\""]},{"number":116,"title":"Chapter 116","paragraphs":["Concubine Shu remained silent.","Consort Ning had first sought her out a month ago. At that time, the palace was still under restrictions, and Consort Ning had slipped into the Palace of Heavenly Purity one night, avoiding notice.","When someone she had never previously deigned to notice came to her, Concubine Shu's initial reaction was scorn. Yes, even though she was now the one under house arrest, she still looked down on Consort Ning—clearly lacking the Emperor's favor, yet putting on an air of aloof detachment and solitary refinement, even styling herself as a talented literary woman. Pah! Truly talented women either wrote realist works or were masters in their field, but Consort Ning merely read some sentimental poetry and dabbled in painting before presuming to call herself a talent. How shameless.","If you asked Concubine Shu, Consort Ning was just average-looking and unloved, so she had to gild her image in other ways.","With this mindset, when she heard Consort Ning propose cooperation, Concubine Shu merely sneered.","That was until Consort Ning said: \"The Yuan family has fallen. Your clansmen are still suffering in that pestilential, insect-ridden land. Without covert assistance, I fear your Yuan family won't even be able to preserve its lineage. You pin your hopes on the Eldest Prince growing up to rescue them, but do you truly believe the Eldest Prince will live to adulthood? Can the Empress stand by and watch a first-born son block the path of her own legitimate heir?\"","Consort Ning's words struck directly at Concubine Shu's deepest fears. Her willingness to remain confined in the Palace of Heavenly Purity hinged entirely on placing all her hopes in the Eldest Prince. Once her son grew up, the Yuan family would have a chance to rise again. But as Consort Ning said, would the Empress tolerate the Eldest Prince?","After all, Concubine Shu herself could not tolerate the Second Prince. If not for Consort An's dissuasion earlier, she would have long since made a move when the Empress was pregnant.","Her hatred for the Empress had festered for far too long, perhaps planted from the very beginning in the Eastern Palace, when she was a concubine and the Empress was the Crown Princess. She was clearly more beautiful, and Jiang Yuan spent more nights in her chambers, yet whenever she clashed with the Crown Princess, Jiang Yuan invariably sided with the Empress.","Jiang Yuan doted on her, but he reserved the respect due to a principal wife solely for the Crown Princess.","Later, when Jiang Yuan ascended the throne, the Crown Princess became Empress, and she became Concubine Shu, the conflicts of interest between them grew ever larger, almost irreconcilable.","Concubine Shu did not believe the Empress would kindly allow the Eldest Prince to survive.","Perhaps... the incident where Consort An took the Eldest Prince to the Imperial Gardens was actually orchestrated by the Empress? Maybe Consort An had long since defected to the Empress's side! Such suspicions even crossed Concubine Shu's mind.","When it concerned her son, Concubine Shu, as the person involved, could not think clearly.","\"What do you want?\" Concubine Shu asked Consort Ning.","Consort Ning merely smiled faintly. \"If the Empress were gone, and the Second Prince is still so young, he likely wouldn't survive either. Then, only the Eldest Prince would remain, standing alone at the pinnacle.\"","Concubine Shu hadn't expected Consort Ning's ambitions to be so grand, aiming directly at the Empress. She wasn't foolish and asked in astonishment, \"You want the phoenix throne?\"","She thought Consort Ning was delusional, but soon she became thoughtful. Actually, it wasn't impossible. Though confined to the Palace of Heavenly Purity, the Eldest Prince could still go out, and she could still learn of major events at court and in the palace. She had heard that Consort Ning's father, Yang Heng, was now a Grand Secretary. If the Empress were to pass away, the position of Central Palace couldn't remain vacant indefinitely; a successor would surely be chosen. Consort Ning had the family background, seniority, and with Yang Heng exerting influence at court, she might indeed become the next Empress.","Concubine Shu's mind raced, weighing whether the Empress alive or dead was more advantageous to her. After much thought, she still wanted the Empress dead—the Empress had contributed no small effort to the Yuan family's downfall!","The very thought of the Empress being brought down by someone as inconspicuous as Consort Ning almost made her laugh aloud!","\"Speak. What do you want from me?\" Concubine Shu didn't believe Consort Ning's visit was merely to reveal her own ambition.","But then Consort Ning said, \"I need you to wait. Wait for my message.\"","\"So, that's how you learned about Concubine Hui sending the beauty cream to the Empress?\" Consort An asked, sensing something amiss. It seemed Concubine Shu was still hiding something.","Concubine Shu's eyes flickered. \"Consort Ning only told me that much. The rest were my own arrangements.\"","Consort An took a deep breath. \"I don't know what spell Consort Ning has cast on you, but if you want to die, don't drag me down with you. Use that brain of yours—good for nothing but your looks—and think! Consort Ning dared to approach you; she naturally arranged an escape route for herself. If this comes to light, she'll withdraw unscathed. And you? You know perfectly well how deeply the Emperor treasures the Empress. Do you think your current state can evoke even a shred of pity in His Majesty's heart? With so many new faces in the palace, the Emperor has long since forgotten you!\"","\"Your own death would be one thing, but what about the Eldest Prince? A mother under house arrest already makes his position awkward. If it gets out that his birth mother poisoned the legitimate mother, what face will he have to show the world in the future? How would the Emperor treat him?\"","Consort An, knowing Concubine Shu best, had hit the mark—Concubine Shu did still cling to the notion that the Emperor might still care for her.","Concubine Shu's face paled and flushed. \"The Eldest Prince is still His Majesty's son!\"","Consort An: \"Has this dynasty seen so few princes and imperial kinsmen confined or stripped of their titles?\"","\"Yuan Yaxin, your son could have been a respected prince, enjoying wealth and honor his entire life. He just said that when he grows up, he'll bring you to his princely estate to care for you properly. Aren't you afraid he'll resent you, hate you, for ruining his life?\"","Concubine Shu faltered. \"I...\" The image of her son, with his chubby belly, earnestly making his vow was still before her eyes.","But no matter the regret, having come this far, what room was left for retreat?","Consort An saw her wavering. \"If you turn back now and implicate Consort Ning instead, there's still hope. A'Xi won't betray you. As long as she insists she was instigated by Consort Ning, who deliberately tried to shift the blame onto me, neither of us will face great disaster!\"","That Qilan leaf was indeed hers, but she had only used it on herself, never to harm others. At worst, she'd be charged with failing to manage her subordinates and misjudging character, while Concubine Shu would be completely excluded from the matter.","Seeing Concubine Shu still hesitating, Consort An delivered another blow: \"The Empress is poisoned, her life hanging by a thread. Your wish is nearly fulfilled. Now the most important thing is not to sacrifice yourself in the process. But think: after the Empress dies, if Consort Ning truly ascends to power, will you have any chance of survival? Will the Eldest Prince?\"","These words truly made Concubine Shu shudder. If it were her, she would never leave alive someone who knew so many secrets.","\"You're right. The Empress must die, but Consort Ning cannot live either,\" Concubine Shu murmured.","Consort An let out an almost imperceptible sigh of relief. \"I've said all I can. The Emperor will return within two days at most. Think it over carefully. What I told you three years ago still holds true. I have only a princess. Our mother-daughter's future glory will depend on the Eldest Prince. No matter what, I will do my utmost to protect him.\"","It was getting late. Not daring to linger, Consort An turned and left.","Once they were beyond the confines of Chengqian Palace, Puying asked in a low voice, \"Can Concubine Shu actually bring down Consort Ning?\"","Consort An's face was stiff. \"It's not important. As long as Consort Ning is dragged into this, suspicion will naturally be lifted from me.\" She didn't care about the fate of the Empress, Concubine Shu, or Consort Ning; all she wanted was for A'xi to change her testimony. So, even if Concubine Shu was still hiding something, she didn't care.","Her gaze turned deep and distant, looking towards the direction of Yikun Palace. It was truly hard to imagine that the palace concealed someone so hypocritical, with a Buddha's words and a serpent's heart.","Inside Yikun Palace, Consort Ning was kneeling before a statue of Buddha. Though she knelt, her expression held no reverence. If one were to move the statue aside, they would find a hidden compartment beneath it containing two portraits painted by Consort Ning herself: one of Lady Yang and one of Yang Luoniang.","Consort Ning couldn't quite remember when she had developed the habit of kneeling before this Buddha statue for half an hour before sleep. It seemed only this could grant her a moment of peace.","\"Mother, it seems the Empress is at the end of her strength now.\"","\"Qilan leaves... what an unexpected boon. I originally only intended for Concubine Shu to be the scapegoat, but she proactively told Consort An about possessing the Qilan leaves, saving me a great deal of trouble. From the Empress's past medical records and prescriptions that Ju Yi provided earlier, it's clear the Empress already suffered from a heart condition. Those Qilan leaves would only aggravate it. Even if Imperial Physician Xia rushes back, the Empress won't live much longer.\"","A faint smile flickered in Consort Ning's eyes. She had originally prepared a different poison. After obtaining the Empress's medical records, she had privately consulted physicians to specially concoct a poison tailored to the Empress's constitution. That poison would create a false impression of recovery from the heart ailment for a short time, but within half a month at most, it would cause a fatal reversal of the heart's meridians.","But then that fool Concubine Shu proactively exposed that she had planted someone near Consort An and volunteered to frame both Consort An and Concubine Hui. The more Concubine Shu acted, the safer Consort Ning became, so she was content to sit back and watch.","\"Mother, are you watching over me?\" Consort Ning whispered softly. With everything progressing so smoothly, she felt as if heaven itself was aiding her.","Just as she was murmuring to herself, Suihe quietly entered from behind the screen. \"My Lady, Ju Yi wishes to see you.\"","Consort Ning tilted her head. For Ju Yi to find an opportunity to come out at this time meant the situation in Kunning Palace must be quite dire.","\"Let her in.\"","Ju Yi entered in a state of panicked helplessness. \"Consort Ning, the Empress is launching an investigation! What should I do? The Empress has ordered Mei Yi to conduct a thorough inquiry. She will surely find me out soon. Once discovered, I'm finished!\"","Ju Yi never doubted the Empress's methods. She had been able to add substances to the beauty cream only by leveraging her position of trust and convenience. But precisely because of her position, the likelihood of exposure was much greater once the Empress was determined to investigate.","She had seized a rare chance to come out tonight, hoping to get a solution from Consort Ning.","\"You said you would save me if things went wrong. You must save this servant!\"","Consort Ning had Suihe help Ju Yi to her feet. \"Why the haste? Since I said I would save you, I naturally won't stand by and watch you come to harm.\"","\"Let me ask you, have you disposed of all those things cleanly?\"","Ju Yi nodded. \"I didn't dare keep anything; I burned it all. But only a handful of people can enter the Empress's bedchamber and access the beauty cream. With so many servants in Kunning Palace, someone might have noticed something. I...\"","Consort Ning: \"Since everything has been disposed of cleanly and no related evidence can be found, mere suspicion directed at you is useless. However, you are right. If someone did happen to notice your movements, it would be unfavorable for you. Alright, return to Kunning Palace first. Go find Li Lu; he will help you.\"","Li Lu? Ju Yi's eyes lit up, but then she looked at Consort Ning with a flicker of fear. Had Consort Ning even bribed Li Lu?","As the chief eunuch of Kunning Palace and a deputy chief eunuch of the rear palace, Li Lu certainly had the ability to conceal some of Ju Yi's traces. Ju Yi felt slightly reassured.","\"Thank you, Consort Ning.\"","Consort Ning smiled faintly. \"The Empress still needs you there. It's best you don't stay out too long. Suihe, see Ju Yi back.\"","She glanced at Suihe.","Suihe lowered her eyes. From an angle Ju Yi couldn't see, she cast a look of pity at her.","The Empress no longer had any need for Ju Yi."]},{"number":117,"title":"Chapter 117","paragraphs":["Suihe and Ju Yi had just left when Yang Xue hurried into the hall.","\"Your Highness, Consort An has gone to the Chengqian Palace.\" The palace maid who served Consort Shu had long been bribed by them, so as soon as Consort An went over, Yang Xue received the news.","Yang Xue whispered, \"Consort Shu may not be reliable. If she exposes you... His Majesty will be returning to the palace soon.\"","They had taken advantage of the Emperor and Doctor Xia's absence from the palace to accomplish many things. Once the Emperor returned, they would no longer have such convenience.","\"Yes, His Majesty will be returning soon,\" Consort Ning sighed. \"Therefore, we must make certain people step forward on their own and take responsibility for the matters.\" She pondered for only a moment. \"Do you still have the item I asked you to keep?\"","Yang Xue nodded, \"Of course, it is still here.\"","\"Then deliver it.\" Since the poison has been made, it must have a place to be used.","Yang Xue was startled, \"Your Highness?\"","Consort Ning looked at her. \"What? The one in the Kunning Palace dared to take action, but you dare not when it's the Chengqian Palace?\"","Yang Xue thought about it and realized it was true. Having come this far, what was there left to fear?","\"This servant understands. I will ensure the matter is handled properly.\"","If at first, Yang Xue and Suihe were trembling with fear, after experiencing more and more events and having more blood on their hands, the two of them were no longer so afraid. If Consort Ning achieves her wish, it would mean immense wealth and honor; if not... they were already long past the point of no return.","The next day, Kunning Palace.","Worried about the Empress, Qi Daiyu rushed over early in the morning.","Other consorts and concubines also arrived one after another. With the central palace in trouble, they naturally could not pretend to know nothing. Even coming to express a few words of concern was a show of care for the Empress; otherwise, when the Emperor returned, wouldn't he think them heartless?","Moreover, the Empress Dowager was also coming to the Kunning Palace, so shouldn't they put on a good show as well?","Indeed, when the Empress Dowager saw the consorts and concubines, a look of satisfaction flashed in her eyes.","As the mistress of the inner palace, regardless of her current condition, these consorts and concubines must respect and honor the Empress. That was the rule.","Qi Daiyu paid no mind to the scene in the hall, feeling only a momentary sadness. How many people in this palace were genuinely worried about Her Majesty the Empress's safety?","There were probably even those hoping for the Empress to die quickly.","Just then, some commotion came from the bedchamber.","The Empress was awakened by sheer pain, her entire heart feeling as if it were being sliced and shredded by sharp blades. The intense agony made it almost impossible for her to breathe.","All the imperial physicians were summoned to the Kunning Palace. The Empress Dowager lost her temper, but the physicians remained helpless. They could only prescribe a pain-relieving formula, instructing it to be decocted and given to the Empress first—she had to hold on until Doctor Xia returned.","After taking the medicine, the Empress managed to suppress the pain somewhat. The Empress Dowager said pityingly, \"The Emperor and Doctor Xia are already on their way back.\"","She then mentioned Lu Wei, who had been taken to the Palace of Stern Justice. \"She has confessed, saying she was enticed by Xi from Consort An's side. What a vicious scheme Consort An harbored! This grieving mother will not let her off!\" As she spoke, she had already sent someone to the Yanxi Palace.","Unexpectedly, Consort An came to the Kunning Palace herself, with someone tied up behind her—it was Xi.","Qi Daiyu's heart skipped a beat. What was Consort An doing? Turning herself in? Or playing the victim?","Consort An was dressed in plain clothes, with only a simple hairpin in her hair. She knelt as soon as she entered the Kunning Palace.","\"This consort failed in supervision, unaware that the palace maid by my side had secretly pledged allegiance to another master, harboring malice and poisoning Her Majesty the Empress. I beg the Empress Dowager for punishment!\"","The Empress Dowager's face was dark. \"You say Xi secretly pledged allegiance to another master, meaning the Empress's poisoning has nothing to do with you, and you were also implicated?\"","Consort An shook her head, her eyes—the only part that could reveal emotion—filled with self-blame and remorse. \"This consort cannot escape responsibility. The Qilan leaf that poisoned Her Majesty the Empress came from my hands.\" Choking up, she explained the origin of the Qilan leaf and how she had once used it.","\"This consort took a wrong path back then, causing irreversible consequences, and I still regret it to this day.\" Consort An touched her stiff face. Everyone couldn't help but stare at her face, imagining what it would be like if their own faces became like that.","Zhaorong shook her head violently, refusing to think further. If her face became like Consort An's, she might as well hang herself.","Consort An continued, \"But precisely because I knew the toxicity of the Qilan leaf, I never dared to let this thing be seen by others. Upon hearing that Her Majesty the Empress was poisoned by the Qilan leaf, I immediately realized something was wrong and only then discovered the item was missing.\"","Consort An pointed at Xi. \"Over the past two days, I finally found out that it was she who stole the Qilan leaf pollen from me, so I came immediately to the Kunning Palace to plead for punishment. Your Highness, the Empress Dowager, the toxicity of Qilan leaf pollen and Qilan leaf sap is different, and the consequences are unpredictable. If treated solely as poisoning by Qilan leaf sap, I fear it may not be sufficient.\"","The Empress Dowager immediately summoned a physician to inquire.","The physician looked as if a light had dawned on him. \"No wonder! We, your humble servants, tried to detoxify using the method for Qilan leaf sap, but it didn't work.\"","He then said with difficulty, \"However, this Qilan leaf is a foreign substance, little known in our dynasty. The toxic effects of Qilan leaf pollen are not recorded at all. Even knowing the cause, there is no way to devise an antidote!\"","The physician then asked Consort An, \"May I ask, Consort An, how did you detoxify back then?\"","Consort An smiled bitterly. \"If there were an antidote, how could my face remain stiff and numb to this day? Back then, I knew there would be adverse effects after use but took a chance. I used an extremely small amount, yet still suffered such severe consequences. Moreover, once you use this thing, it's as if you can never give it up...\"","At that time, she knew she couldn't continue, but it was as if she were possessed, uncontrollably wanting to smear the Qilan leaf pollen mixed with water all over her body. So much so that once such thoughts arose, she would tie herself up and rely on her own willpower to resist. It took several months for those urges to finally fade.","Hearing Consort An's words, Qi Daiyu's heart turned cold. A poison that causes addiction—she thought of opium from her original world. Once touched, that thing made life worse than death even with nine lives. How similar Qilan leaf pollen was to it! The Empress's current symptoms were clearly more severe than Consort An's back then, obviously due to a larger dose. Consort An could quit, but could the Empress?","\"This consort cannot shirk responsibility and willingly accepts punishment. But I absolutely never harbored any intention to harm Her Majesty the Empress. I beg the Empress Dowager to uphold justice and find the true culprit!\" Consort An kowtowed.","The Empress Dowager's expression was now unreadable—a difficult-to-cure poison, one that even caused addiction.","Thus, her look at Xi was as if she wished to tear her apart.","Without needing the Empress Dowager's order, Nanny Zhao dragged Xi out.","Xi had already secretly received instructions from Consort Shu and did not stubbornly resist. \"This servant will speak! It was Consort Ning! Consort Ning ordered this servant to do this! This servant has been Consort Ning's person from the start. Consort Ning harbors great ambition and seeks the position of Empress. Having served by Consort An's side for many years, I knew her secret. To share Consort Ning's burdens, I took the initiative to inform her. After Consort Ning learned that Consort An possessed Qilan leaf pollen, she devised this plan to frame someone else.\"","Everyone looked at Consort Ning in shock.","Qi Daiyu's heart also stirred upon hearing this.","Mentioned by name, Consort Ning showed only surprise, not panic. She knelt calmly to defend herself. \"This consort has never done such a thing. This palace maid's words are full of holes and inconsistencies. Leaving aside that she was never my person, even if it were as she says, if I had known Consort An had Qilan leaves, I would have reported it to His Majesty and the Empress immediately.\"","Xi, beaten until she could only lie prone on the ground, cried out towards Consort Ning, \"Consort Ning, wasn't poisoning the Empress your long-standing scheme? You hated the Empress for taking the Crown Princess position and for bearing the imperial heir and princess. You have long wished for the Empress's death! And Concubine Hui—you were jealous of her beauty and favor. Neither of you have children, yet His Majesty would rather let Concubine Hui raise the Second Princess than give her to you. You ordered me to bribe Hong Tao and Lu Wei from the Changchun Palace, wasn't it precisely to frame Concubine Hui?\"","\"Hong Tao?\" The Empress Dowager frowned and looked at Nanny Zhao. \"Wasn't there only a Lu Wei? Who is this Hong Tao?\"","By this point, Qi Daiyu dared not conceal anything further. She stepped forward and said, \"Empress Dowager, after returning to my palace the other day, I thought it over and felt something was amiss. If someone wanted to frame me, bribing only one low-ranking cleaning maid seemed too simplistic a method. Fearing a follow-up scheme, I thoroughly investigated everyone in the Changchun Palace and discovered something suspicious about Hong Tao, the maid who serves my tea. For the past two days, I kept a close watch on this Hong Tao and finally caught her revealing her hand last night. I originally intended to report this to you today.\"","After this brief explanation, Qi Daiyu produced the wooden gourd. \"This object was dug up from beneath the palace wall behind the rear annex of Changchun Palace after Hong Tao confessed. It should be the Qilan leaf pollen Consort An mentioned. Empress Dowager, Hong Tao has already been apprehended by me and can be summoned at any time.\"","As soon as Consort An saw the wooden gourd, she said, \"That is indeed it!\"","The Empress Dowager had someone take the gourd to the imperial physicians, instructing them to continue seeking an antidote.","\"Consort Ning, what do you have to say for yourself?\"","By now, the corners of Consort Ning's eyes were slightly red, yet her back remained straight, as if she would not compromise her dignity even while suffering an injustice.","\"Empress Dowager, since entering the palace, I have always respected the Empress. Everyone in the palace is not blind. I do not understand where these rumors of my dissatisfaction with the Empress come from. Over these years, I have rarely left the Yikun Palace. My relations with the other consorts and concubines, while not close, have never been hostile. I have had very few interactions with Concubine Hui, so why would I harbor such groundless jealousy and hatred towards her?\"","\"I do not know why Xi claims I instructed her. But if my guilt is to be decided based solely on Xi's words, without a single shred of evidence, I cannot accept it and will never admit to it.\"","Consort Ning's demeanor led many to believe her.","After all, Consort Ning's character was well-known to all.","Ye Qiong, supporting her round belly and lower back, spoke up, \"Indeed, this matter is of great importance. How can we lightly believe the incoherent words of a single palace maid?\"","Qi Daiyu, separated from Ye Qiong by two people, glanced at her, a slight frown between her brows. Why did Ye Qiong suddenly jump out to speak in Consort Ning's defense?","Ye Qiong's words seemed to open the floodgates. Another person said, \"Rather than Consort Ning, this concubine finds Consort An more suspicious. If Xi was a spy planted by someone else, you, Consort An, had her serving you for so many years—how could you have never suspected? Moreover, Consort Ning and Consort An have had little interaction. What purpose would there be in planting someone by Consort An's side?\"","This was indeed the most illogical part of Xi's story.","Consort An remained unmoved by such doubts, sticking to her own account. \"If Xi were Consort Ning's person, it's impossible there were no contacts over the years. We need only strictly investigate who Xi has had dealings with these past few years.\"","This also made sense. The Empress Dowager issued an order to investigate.","The prone Xi on the ground suddenly trembled and looked up at Consort An. She wasn't Consort Ning's person, so nothing would be found there, but her connections to Consort Shu's side might not remain hidden.","Xi finally understood. Consort An wasn't trying to help Consort Shu at all; she was only trying to clear her own name!","If Xi could realize this, Consort Ning naturally could as well. Consort Ning lifted her gaze, her eyes meeting Consort An's.","In both their eyes was nothing but cold indifference."]},{"number":118,"title":"Chapter 118","paragraphs":["\"Your Majesty the Empress Dowager! Something terrible has happened!\" While everyone in the hall was still lost in their own thoughts, a palace servant rushed in frantically, disregarding all decorum, and knelt on the floor.","\"Your Majesty, news from Chengqian Palace! Consort Shu... Consort Shu has hanged herself!\"","The servant, terrified, spoke unclearly, her voice trembling, but the meaning of her words was understood by all in the hall. For a moment, there was shock, and also bewilderment.","The bewilderment came mostly from the newer consorts, who couldn't immediately recall who Consort Shu was.","Consort An had the strongest reaction. She turned in disbelief to look at the maid. \"Who did you say has hanged herself?\"","The maid dared not raise her head. \"Cons... Consort Shu...\"","The atmosphere in the hall grew strange. For Consort Shu to take her own life at this moment seemed deeply suspicious no matter how one looked at it.","The Empress Dowager's face darkened. \"Nanny Zhao, go to Chengqian Palace at once.\"","The Empress Dowager's eyes swept over Consort An and Consort Ning. Having spent many years immersed in the depths of the palace, even though she had withdrawn from worldly affairs in recent years, she was not yet senile. They had just pulled out the thread concerning A'xi, with both Consort An and Consort Ning under suspicion, and now Consort Shu emerged. The Empress Dowager's intuition told her something was amiss.","Nanny Zhao went and returned quickly, her expression grave. \"Reporting to Your Majesty, Consort Shu has indeed died by hanging. According to the maid who attended her, half an hour ago, Consort Shu found an excuse to send her out. When the maid returned, she found Consort Shu already...\"","\"Furthermore, the maid discovered this in the room. It appears to be Consort Shu's suicide note. The poisoning of Her Majesty the Empress... may have been Consort Shu's doing.\"","Nanny Zhao presented a letter.","The Empress Dowager took one look and angrily exclaimed, \"Outrageous!\"","Her furious demeanor made everyone curious about what was written on the letter. Qi Daiyu, who was standing nearby, secretly activated her camera towards the opened letter. Reading the words, a surge of anger also rose within her.","\"Jiang Nvying, I'll be waiting for you in hell.\"","Qi Daiyu forced herself to suppress her emotions and said calmly, \"Your Majesty, we must investigate whether this letter was truly written by Consort Shu's own hand.\" Not just the letter, but Consort Shu's death also needed investigation.","The timing of Consort Shu's death was far too coincidental. Even with this letter, Qi Daiyu couldn't fully believe it.","Consort Ning suddenly spoke. \"Why is Consort An so shocked by Consort Shu's death?\"","Consort An looked at Consort Ning. \"I shared an old friendship with Consort Shu. Naturally, I am shocked to hear of her death. What do you mean by that, Consort Ning?\"","\"Is that so?\" Consort Ning resumed her usual detached demeanor. \"It seems Consort An and Consort Shu truly were deeply attached.\"","Consort An's heart trembled. She realized she had fallen into Consort Ning's verbal trap.","Sure enough, Nie Zhiyu said, \"In the past, Consort An was inseparable from Consort Shu. After Consort Shu was confined, you specifically pleaded with the Emperor on her behalf to see her, and since then you have also taken great care of the Eldest Prince. With such profound affection, Consort An, surely you haven't secretly met with Consort Shu at all these past two years?\"","Ye Qiong seemed to suddenly understand something. \"If the poisoning of Her Majesty the Empress was Consort Shu's doing, and Consort Shu couldn't leave Chengqian Palace, she would necessarily need an accomplice. This accomplice...\" She looked at Consort An, the implication in her eyes unmistakable.","In a short time, the situation had changed drastically. Consort An's suspicion skyrocketed.","Consider: the Qilan leaf pollen belonged to Consort An; Consort An was close to Consort Shu; Consort Shu's suicide note was filled with hatred for the Empress. When these conditions were combined, Consort An was far more suspicious than Consort Ning.","Consort An's mind raced. \"The order for Consort Shu's confinement was the Emperor's own decree. How would I dare to disobey and meet her in secret?\"","Consort Ning spoke again. \"Indeed, you wouldn't need to see Consort Shu yourself.\"","Ye Qiong said, \"The Eldest Prince! Consort An, if you had any communication with Consort Shu, you only needed to go through the Eldest Prince!\"","Consort Shu was confined, but the Eldest Prince could freely enter and leave Chengqian Palace. This also meant that if Consort Shu had any ideas, she could convey them to Consort An through the Eldest Prince, and Consort An could give anything to Consort Shu through the Eldest Prince as well!","Now, everyone looked at Consort An differently.","It was as if they had already decided Consort An was the accomplice who conspired with Consort Shu to poison the Empress.","Consort An truly felt her breath catch. She couldn't help but look at Consort Ning. Those eyes were abnormally calm, only revealing a trace of mockery when they met hers.","That trace of mockery said: You've lost.","Consort An prided herself on her intelligence and sometimes regretted not being born a man, so she could have studied for the imperial examinations, become an official, and brought glory to her family. Limited by her family background, she had no choice but to attach herself to Consort Shu, offering strategies and plans to receive the meager scraps that fell from Consort Shu's fingers. Although she had received Consort Shu's favors, Consort An somewhat looked down on her in her heart.","Consort An believed Consort Shu's dominance in the harem was due to sheer luck—heaven had given her beauty, family status, and even her arrogant, domineering, and narcissistic personality was favored by the Emperor. Consort An herself had only that bit of cleverness.","Relying on that cleverness, Consort An often felt she was the most clear-sighted person in the harem. But today she realized she was wrong.","In this harem, there was one person who hid deeper than anyone.","Consort An looked quietly at Consort Ning. She had indeed lost. Not because her calculations were flawed, but because she wasn't as ruthless as Consort Ning.","Consort An knew perfectly well that Consort Shu could not have hanged herself. She was absolutely murdered, and the one who wanted to kill Consort Shu was Consort Ning.","Only with Consort Shu dead could Consort Ning extricate herself completely and pin all the crimes on Consort Shu and Consort An.","Consort An's shoulders suddenly slumped. If her face could make a normal expression at that moment, it would have been a bitter smile. She hadn't anticipated that the persona of deep loyalty she had crafted for herself in the past would become ironclad proof today of her inseparable connection to Consort Shu.","If only she could have been as heartless as Consort Ning, directly killing Consort Shu and A'xi, perhaps she would still have a chance to plead her case.","Consort Shu's death disrupted the investigation's rhythm, yet it also brought clarity to the case of the Empress's poisoning. The connection between Consort Shu and A'xi was quickly uncovered. Upon learning of Consort Shu's death, A'xi bit off her own tongue without hesitation and committed suicide. This only further proved the relationship between A'xi and Consort Shu.","Consort An could not prove her ignorance of the theft of the Qilan leaves. Of course, she could continue to deny it, but what judgment she would receive would have to wait for the Emperor's return.","Having all the consorts stay in Kunning Palace was becoming chaotic. The Empress Dowager dismissed everyone. Qi Daiyu requested to stay, using the excuse of caring for the Eldest Princess and the Second Prince. The Empress Dowager agreed.","After everyone left, Qi Daiyu entered the Empress's bedchamber. The imperial physicians were researching a cure for the Qilan leaf pollen poison. The Empress was still unconscious. Mei Yi saw Qi Daiyu enter and moved aside.","Looking at the Empress's pale face, Qi Daiyu felt terrible too. But she knew nothing of medicine; she couldn't even use her special ability to help detoxify the Empress. In fact, she had already used...","The \"phone\" went through many twists and turns to contact a private doctor. The system would not allow her to reveal the secrets of time travel; what she could send out were all pre-set terminology. Based on these alone, that doctor could not offer any advice.","Qi Daiyu had also wondered if the poison had triggered the Empress's heart condition, and whether she could buy something like heart-saving pills, but she was afraid the medicine might not suit the illness and would instead harm the Empress. Showing it to the imperial physician would also give her no reasonable explanation.","\"Why didn't I study medicine back then!\" Qi Daiyu murmured. She was starting to think she was too useless. How come the time-traveling heroines in novels were all so capable, while she could only watch helplessly as the people she cared about fell ill or passed away one by one? Clearly, her golden finger wasn't weak either.","Qi Daiyu suddenly felt a pang of hatred for her years of complacency. She felt like a fool sitting on a gold mountain without using it, only regretting it when faced with a predicament.","Mei Yi didn't catch her words clearly. \"Consort Hui? Are you alright?\"","Qi Daiyu shook her head. \"I'm fine. I'm going to see the Eldest Princess.\"","Mei Yi saw her out and was about to return to the bedchamber when she saw someone hurrying over, who whispered a few words into Mei Yi's ear.","\"What did you say?!\"","Emperor Jiang Yuan rushed back late that night. Upon returning to the palace, he went straight to Kunning Palace. By then, the Empress had woken up, taken medicine, and fallen asleep again.","Jiang Yuan's stubble was noticeable, clearly showing he had no mind for grooming. He reached out and gently stroked the Empress's pale face for a moment, a storm seeming to brew in his eyes. After a while, Jiang Yuan stepped aside to let Chief Physician Xia examine the Empress's pulse and went to the main hall.","Qi Daiyu, having received the news, also came over from the side hall.","Jiang Yuan's gaze rested on her briefly before he had a chair brought for her.","\"Tell me everything that happened, from the beginning,\" Jiang Yuan's voice was calm, yet Mei Yi, Lan Yi, and the others instinctively knelt.","Mei Yi prostrated herself on the ground and began recounting from when Consort Hui sent the beauty cream to the Empress, all the way to today's events of the Empress Dowager interrogating Consort Ning and Consort An.","And also, Consort Shu's suicide by hanging.","Upon hearing of Consort Shu's suicide, Jiang Yuan clenched his left fist. After a long pause, he said, \"Did the Empress have any arrangements?\" He knew that even while poisoned, the Empress would have made plans during her moments of clarity.","Mei Yi: \"Her Majesty the Empress ordered this servant to investigate the traitor within Kunning Palace...\" She paused, closing her eyes. \"This afternoon, Ju Yi's body was found in a well in the flower nursery.\"","As soon as she received the news, Mei Yi understood. Ju Yi was that traitor. Setting aside anger and grief, with Ju Yi's death, the clue to finding the mastermind behind the scenes was cut off.","Jiang Yuan frowned. \"Did the Empress know about this?\"","Mei Yi: \"This servant did not dare not to tell her.\"","Mei Yi continued, \"Your Majesty, Ju Yi could have been bribed by anyone, but that person absolutely could not have been Consort Shu!\"","During the years when the Empress and Consort Shu were rivals, Ju Yi had done many things to offend Consort Shu. She had even mocked Consort Shu when she was under house arrest. How could she possibly have been bribed by Consort Shu?","\"Your Majesty.\" Qi Daiyu stood up and curtsied. \"The timing of Consort Shu's death is too suspicious. I beg you to issue an edict to have Consort Shu's body examined.\"","As she said this, Qi Daiyu felt anxious. She didn't know if the Emperor would agree, after all, Consort Shu had truly been deeply favored in the past, and her status in the Emperor's heart was not low.","Moreover, people of this time held great reverence for the deceased. Consort Shu held the noble rank of Consort; conducting an autopsy on her body would likely cause an uproar.","But this request, Qi Daiyu had to make.","She suspected Consort Shu did not die by suicide. Perhaps, by uncovering the truth of Consort Shu's death, they could catch the real culprit.","Silence, a long silence.","Jiang Yuan stared at Qi Daiyu, as if weighing and considering her words.","Then Jiang Yuan said, \"While I was away from the palace, the Empress was poisoned, Consort Shu hanged herself, and a maid serving the Empress in Kunning Palace also met a violent end. Good, very good. I had no idea what kind of malicious, poisonous hearts were hidden within my own harem.\"","\"Weren't Consort Shu, Consort Ning, and Consort An all suspected? Quan Fuhai!\"","Quan Fuhai bowed. \"Your servant is here.\"","Jiang Yuan said calmly, \"Take all the palace servants from Chengqian Palace, Yikun Palace, and Yanxi Palace to the well where Ju Yi's body was found. Kill them, one by one.\"","He wanted to see how much venom could still be hidden when faced with life and death."]},{"number":119,"title":"Chapter 119: The One Hundred and Nineteenth","paragraphs":["When the Son of Heaven rages, the entire palace trembles thrice.","Jiang Yuan uttered horrifying words in an utterly calm tone. Quan Fuhai instantly broke out in beads of sweat on his forehead, yet he dared not utter a single word of admonishment. He knew perfectly well that if he spoke even one extra word now, the first to die would be him.","Quan Fuhai silently retreated to carry out the order, inwardly lamenting his wretched fate. What a sin, truly a sin! The palace servants from three palaces combined number over a hundred. If they were all killed one by one, they could fill that well!","Among them were certainly many innocent people, but the Emperor was clearly determined to stop evil with killing; they could only die. There was also a way not to die: if the guilty party's psychological defenses crumbled and they confessed all the secrets.","The benefit of this approach was quickly grasped by Qi Daiyu as well, but the thought of the scene to come still made her heart turn cold. Yet, what chilled her even more was yet to come.","Then she heard Jiang Yuan add, \"Bring all the imperial consorts and their personal palace maids and eunuchs to the scene. Let them all open their eyes wide and see clearly what fate awaits those who play mind games and scheme against their superiors in this palace!\"","Previously, petty squabbles were one thing—fighting over a piece of jewelry or a bolt of cloth. Jiang Yuan paid no mind to these tricks of vying for favor. Sometimes, when he was weary from busy government affairs, they even served as a bit of entertainment.","If the fights got too heated, the Empress would handle everything. Matters of the rear palace were, after all, the Empress's duty to manage! If there was something the Empress couldn't handle and it reached him, demotions, punishments, or even death sentences would, at most, stir a momentary ripple in Jiang Yuan's heart, soon forgotten.","Ultimately, of all the women in the rear palace, there were very few Jiang Yuan truly cared about. Among them, the Empress was undoubtedly the most important.","Whether out of affection or her status.","What infuriated Jiang Yuan most about the Empress's poisoning was this: if someone dared to lay hands on the Empress, who stood at the pinnacle of power in the rear palace, would the person behind it dare one day to move against him, the Emperor?","This single point alone sent this sovereign into an uncontrollable rage, murderous intent surging.","What were a hundred or so lives? Jiang Yuan even wanted to sift through the entire palace.","Thus, before dawn, all the imperial consorts and a number of palace servants were brought to the abandoned well in the Imperial Garden.","There used to be an opera pavilion nearby. Last year, heavy snow collapsed part of its roof, and as the area was remote and seldom visited, the Imperial Household Department repaired it after spring and repurposed it as a flower room.","With so many people arriving now, the Director of the Imperial Household Department, Xu Jilai, was on high alert. He couldn't quite grasp the Emperor's intention. Since it was to witness an execution, it was surely to establish authority. But if so many consorts were frightened into illness, his directorship would likely come to an end.","Xu Jilai was a shrewd man. He had people bring out many chairs and stools from the opera pavilion and sent his junior eunuchs to make a trip to the Kunning Palace to fetch two imperial physicians at all costs. This way, if any consort fell ill, a physician could attend to them immediately.","While Xu Jilai was arranging these things, the consorts were still bewildered. With such a grand display, what was about to happen?","The highest-ranking present was Consort Nie Zhiyu. Some, feeling anxious, cautiously asked Nie Zhiyu.","Nie Zhiyu did not answer, only frowned at Ye Qiong, who had a prominent belly. \"Stay close to me later.\"","Ye Qiong nodded, whispering, \"Sister, what is His Majesty going to do?\"","Nie Zhiyu: \"It can only be concerning the Empress's matter.\" As she spoke, her eyes searched for Qi Daiyu. Yan He, Xiao Li, and others from the Changchun Palace had also been brought over, but Qi Daiyu was not among them. Nie Zhiyu remembered Qi Daiyu should have stayed at Kunning Palace last night.","Just as she was thinking this, she saw Qi Daiyu arriving behind the Emperor.","The consorts hurriedly performed their courtesies. Then they saw several squads of Imperial Guards escorting a group of palace servants into view, followed by Consort Ning and Consort An, their faces ashen.","Consort Ning never imagined that the Emperor's first act upon returning would be to take away all their palace servants. It happened too fast. When Quan Fuhai arrived at the Yikun Palace, she didn't even have time to prepare, and could only watch helplessly as the Imperial Guards took away Yangxue, Suihe, and the others.","Yet, even then, Consort Ning clung to a sliver of hope. If they were just taken to the Discipline Office, and if Yangxue and Suihe could endure for a few days, she would find a way to save them. But upon hearing the Emperor's order for her to follow as well, and being brought to this abandoned well, Consort Ning finally felt a surge of panic.","Jiang Yuan's gaze swept past Consort Ning and Consort An. He glanced at the arranged chairs and stools but said nothing to Xu Jilai.","He sat down leisurely in the central chair at the head, flicked the jade pendant at his waist, and said, \"Bring them forward.\"","Qi Daiyu took the opportunity to move to Yan He and the others. As Yan He supported Qi Daiyu's arm, she nodded slightly, meaning: the Third Princess has been settled.","Only then did Qi Daiyu feel relieved. She also sat on a chair. Thinking of what was about to happen, her hands trembled slightly.","They saw Imperial Guard Commander Wei Meng lead several men carrying over a corpse. The corpse's head was a bloody mess, and its limbs were bent at unnatural angles.","At the sudden sight of such a horrifying scene, many let out screams, which they forcibly stifled when the Emperor's gaze turned their way, nearly biting their tongues in the process.","Quan Fuhai used his sharp, thin voice to announce, \"This is Ju Yi from Kunning Palace. Ju Yi, audacious to the extreme, poisoned Her Majesty the Empress. She deserved to die ten thousand times over! Hatefully, she was killed and discarded in this abandoned well, and her murderer hides among you!\"","Quan Fuhai pointed at the palace servants from the Chengqian Palace, Yanxi Palace, and Yikun Palace. Many paled.","Quan Fuhai made a gesture of cupping his hands in salute. \"By His Majesty's decree, if you wish to live, speak all you know. If what you say holds value, your life may be spared. If not... then don't blame this humble servant for being merciless with the blade.\"","\"Who shall go first?\" Quan Fuhai's eyes swept over these people. Those his gaze fell upon retreated in terror.","The order of selection was naturally not random. Concubine Shu's death was suspicious; logically, the maid who served her would most likely know something and should be kept a while longer.","Between Consort Ning and Consort An, Consort An was more suspect. Starting with someone from Yanxi Palace would yield better results.","Thus, Quan Fuhai's gaze settled on the chief eunuch of Yanxi Palace.","A single stroke from an Imperial Guard's blade, and blood splattered.","Qi Daiyu closed her eyes. Even though there was still some distance, she felt as if the eunuch had died right in front of her. She could clearly hear the sharp intakes of breath from Yan He, Shiliu, and the others behind her.","\"Ah!!\"","Screams and pleas for mercy erupted from all around. Some of the fainter-hearted directly fainted. Two consorts also fainted. Jiang Yuan raised a hand, and Xu Jilai immediately had his men carry them away.","Ye Qiong, supporting her lower back, felt only panic and confusion, with a faint pain creeping from her abdomen. Nie Zhiyu noticed her discomfort and, forcing down her own nausea and fear, prepared to speak to the Emperor.","\"Your Majesty, Concubine Ye is still with child. Such a bloody scene might be harmful to the imperial heir. Could she be permitted to leave first?\"","Ye Qiong also pleaded pitifully, \"Your Majesty...\"","Although furious, Jiang Yuan had not lost his reason. Ultimately mindful of the fetus in Ye Qiong's womb, he said, \"Escort Concubine Ye to the theater pavilion over there.\"","However, that place was not far from here; even if she couldn't see the scene, she could still hear the sounds. Ye Qiong wanted to say more, but upon meeting Jiang Yuan's gaze, she swallowed her words. Before leaving, she instinctively glanced back towards Consort Ning's direction.","Then, lowering her head hurriedly, she bit her lip. If Consort Ning were to fall today, it might actually be a good thing for her...","Once Ye Qiong had left, Jiang Yuan ordered Quan Fuhai to continue.","The next one was Pu Jiu, who served by Consort An's side.","\"Don't kill me! Don't kill me!\" Pu Jiu pushed herself backward with her hands on the ground, her eyes filled with terror as she looked at Consort An, begging her to speak up and save her. But before her plea even faded, a long sword pierced her chest.","Pu Jiu's eyes widened, as if she hadn't yet processed what happened, before her entire body slumped to the side, falling right next to Puying. When the sword was pulled out, blood splattered all over Puying.","Puying's lips trembled uncontrollably, her pupils filled with the image of Pu Jiu collapsing.","Quan Fuhai deliberately skipped over her. The imperial guards executed several more palace maids and eunuchs before finally stopping in front of Puying.","Seeing the imperial guard raise his long sword, Puying screamed, \"Don't kill me! I'll talk! I'll tell everything!\"","If it were a normal interrogation process, or even if she had been taken to the Punishment Office for torture, Puying would not have betrayed Consort An. After all, for personal maids like her, especially those who had served their mistress since childhood, the lives and fates of their entire families were tied to their mistress. They would rather die themselves than betray her.","But the impact of watching the people of Yanxi Palace die one by one before her eyes was too great. Puying's reason completely shattered. Her fear of death overwhelmed her loyalty to Consort An, and her mind echoed only Quan Fuhai's words: \"If what you say is valuable, your life may be spared.\"","\"I'll tell everything, don't kill me! Don't kill me!\" Clearly terrified by the killings, Puying clutched at Quan Fuhai's robe hem, begging for mercy, not even sparing a glance for Consort An.","Consort An... Consort An's clenched hands loosened. She was not a heartless person, and besides, she shared years of master-servant bond with Puying and Pu Jiu. When Pu Jiu died, she had nearly lost control. Now, hearing Puying's words, she actually felt a trace of relief.","She truly had not harmed the Empress, but her hands were not clean of blood either. Once the Emperor learned of those things, he would likely not spare her. Consort An did not blame Puying. She was only somewhat worried: if the Emperor sentenced her to death, what would become of her Bao En?","With Puying setting the precedent, several more people began to beg for mercy. Serving in various palaces, they all knew some secrets to varying degrees. Father Quan had said that revealing valuable information could save their lives—what if the things they knew were enough to spare them?","Quan Fuhai didn't care if anyone was trying to muddy the waters. As long as someone raised their hand, he had them taken away for interrogation. After all, if their information proved false, they would still lose their lives.","Father Yu from the Punishment Office had been waiting. They had their own methods for interrogation. They didn't group people together but separated them, allowing for cross-checking of testimonies to prevent fabrication, and occasionally obtaining more detailed supplementary information.","These people, desperate to live, truly told everything—from major scandals like what shady deeds they had helped their masters commit, to minor matters like eunuchs drinking and gambling in private, and even things like which eunuch and which palace maid had formed a secret partnership. They held nothing back.","They not only confessed about their own palaces but also about other palaces. The servants had their own private networks, and some things their masters thought they didn't know had actually spread secretly long ago.","Sheet after sheet of testimony was delivered to Jiang Yuan. Reading them, his expression grew increasingly grim. These papers recorded the hidden affairs of every palace.","Consort An had also been involved in Concubine Mei's miscarriage. Moreover, Consort An had schemed against selected palace ladies.","The Empress had planted someone in Chengqian Palace; the nanny by the Eldest Prince's side was the Empress's person.","Consort Ning had secret dealings with Yanping.","...","Among the affairs of each palace, some concerned Jiang Yuan, others he didn't care about, but almost every palace was far from clean.","Reading through them, the cleanest turned out to be Changchun Palace.","Jiang Yuan couldn't help but glance at Qi Daiyu. The testimonies regarding Changchun Palace were all things like: \"Consort Hui is obsessed with mahjong, the whole palace follows her lead, servants staying up all night playing are listless,\" \"The constant hammering noises from Changchun Palace disturbing the peace are because Consort Hui wants to build a trampoline in the courtyard,\" \"Consort Hui coaxing the Eldest Prince to eat candy was actually feeding him medicine to expel worms\"...","It was truly absurd, yet with a peculiar kind of purity.","Jiang Yuan saw that Qi Daiyu's face was pale. She seemed very frightened, her nails digging into her palms.","Remembering her timid nature, Jiang Yuan summoned a young eunuch. \"Go bring a bowl of sweet soup for Consort Hui.\""]},{"number":120,"title":"Chapter 120","paragraphs":["The stirring in his heart was but a fleeting moment; Jiang Yuan's eyes soon darkened.","Quan Fuhai, observing the emperor's expression, signaled the imperial guard. This time, the guard's long sword was pointed at the palace maid serving Consort Shu.","The maid's name was Xiao Xiang. After Mingcui's death, and with Diancui and other palace attendants expelled from the palace under various pretexts, Xiao Xiang was newly assigned to serve Consort Shu. To say 'serve' was an overstatement; her role was more about surveillance and control. After all, Consort Shu was a convicted criminal, only retaining her title for the sake of the eldest prince and unable to enjoy the privileges of her rank.","Being assigned to a disgraced consort doomed Xiao Xiang's prospects to gloom. Though resentful, she hadn't dared to mistreat Consort Shu—until Consort Ning approached her.","After pledging loyalty to Consort Ning, Xiao Xiang's task was to open the gates of Chengqian Palace whenever Her Ladyship required, allowing Consong Ning's people to enter and speak with Consort Shu. This originally didn't seem a grave crime, until Yangxue handed Xiao Xiang that pill and ordered her to feed it to Consort Shu.","Watching the sword that had already claimed several lives draw nearer, Xiao Xiang's terror grew.","She knew in her heart that even if she confessed her deeds, she wouldn't survive. Yet, she couldn't help hoping—perhaps her death would be slower? Not like those others who stopped breathing the instant the sword fell.","Xiao Xiang's eyes involuntarily searched the scene for Consort Ning. She wanted to scream that it was all Consort Ning's doing! That Consort Ning had coerced her!","Consort Ning saw Xiao Xiang's impending breakdown and could no longer maintain her facade of composure.","Xiao Xiang must not speak. A flash of ruthlessness crossed Consort Ning's eyes as her gaze fell upon Yangxue's face, and she subtly twisted a string of prayer beads on her wrist.","Yangxue was already weeping profusely. Seeing Consort Ning's gesture, her eyes filled with desperate plea, but she was met only with the harsh severity in Consort Ning's gaze.","Yangxue knew all too well what that gesture meant.","She and Suihe were born servants of the Yang family. Her parents, brothers, and sisters—all were under the Yang household's control. If Her Ladyship's schemes were exposed, her entire family would perish. But if she alone were sacrificed, her family might yet remain safe.","The imperial guard's sword was almost upon Xiao Xiang. Just as Xiao Xiang was about to cry out, Yangxue rose with an air of utter despair, appearing almost deranged.","\"Ahhh! Don't kill me! I know nothing! Don't kill me!\"","Yangxue wailed hysterically. As Quan Fuhai ordered men to seize her, Yangxue seemed to struggle but then suddenly lunged toward the guard's sword!","\"Thud!\"","The long sword pierced her heart, and Yangxue's cries ceased abruptly.","\"Yangxue!\" The composed Consort Ning lost her calm. She stood up, stumbling toward Yangxue's body. The guards moved to block her, but fearing they might actually harm her, they hesitated momentarily—just long enough for Consort Ning to reach Yangxue's corpse.","\"Yangxue...\" Suihe knelt beside the body, looking as if she wanted to touch it but didn't dare. \"Your Ladyship, Yangxue, she... she...\"","\"Yangxue!\" Consort Ning's face contorted in anguish, tears streaming down as if she had lost a beloved kin. She turned a furious gaze toward the Emperor. \"Your Majesty, to find the culprit who harmed the Empress, you would not hesitate to kill so many innocent people? If the Empress knew of your methods, would her conscience not be tormented? You speak of seeking justice for Her Majesty, but where is the justice for these palace servants?\"","Consort Ning's words sounded like the rash utterances of overwhelming grief, yet the huddled, terrified servants, upon hearing them, began to show expressions of resentment. They had done nothing wrong, yet here they were, facing the threat of death. The Empress's plight was pitiable, but were they, the innocent, not pitiable too?","Jiang Yuan narrowed his eyes. \"Consort Ning, return to your place.\"","He glanced at Quan Fuhai, who immediately stepped forward to assist Consort Ning, only to be shoved away by her.","Consort Ning, who had always cultivated an image of a refined, aloof, and elegant literary talent, now stood with her robes stained with blood, adding a cold, unyielding aura like a plum blossom in a blizzard. Her hairpins askew and hair disheveled, she seemed to care for nothing but demanding justice for her maid.","\"Your Majesty, I understand your wish to purge the palace, but is creating such slaughter truly for the best? If word spreads, how will the common people view the imperial family? How will they view you?\"","Everyone understood the deeper implication in Consort Ning's words. The massacre of so many servants would undoubtedly cause an uproar in the capital. Once the cause and details spread, the dark secrets of the harem would become fodder for public gossip. Where then would the imperial family's dignity be? Its authority?","Should everyone be allowed to know the harem was such a den of intrigue and deceit?","\"Does Your Majesty wish for the people of the realm to call you tyrannical and cruel?\"","Consort Ning's question landed with heavy force. Suihe, kneeling on the ground, trembled uncontrollably. She knew Consort Ning was taking a desperate gamble, but if Her Ladyship truly enraged the Emperor, everything might be over before any secrets could even be uncovered!","\"Tyrannical? Cruel?\"","Jiang Yuan let out a low laugh. He realized today's events had truly shattered many of his previous perceptions. For the first time, he learned that Consort Ning possessed such audacity, daring to speak to him in this manner.","Consort Ning held firm under the pressure of Jiang Yuan's gaze, stating resolutely, \"I was bestowed upon Your Majesty by the late Emperor as a secondary consort, personally enfeoffed by you as Consort Ning, and entered into the imperial jade records. I know my words are unpleasant to hear, but my heart is solely devoted to Your Majesty's welfare and the good name of the imperial house. I beg Your Majesty to reconsider!\"","Jiang Yuan stood up. He walked over to stand before Consort Ning, looking down at her from his height. The Emperor's eyes were filled with anger—displeasure at anyone daring to defy his command, and irritation at the words Consort Ning had spoken.","\"For my welfare? For the imperial house's good name? Consort Ning, who do you think you are?\" Jiang Yuan used his jade pendant to lift Consort Ning's chin, his voice cool and laced with casual disdain.","\"If I want them dead, they die.\"","\"If I want you dead, you die.\"","\"What are you, to presume to judge me?\"","He was the Emperor, possessing the realm and holding supreme power. His merits and faults would be recorded by history and judged by posterity.","Consort Ning's pupils contracted. Jiang Yuan's words stripped away her dignity, leaving her feeling utterly exposed and wounded, especially before so many consorts and servants. It was undeniably a humiliation.","Though it was midsummer and she was clothed, Consort Ning felt a piercing, bone-deep cold.","Jiang Yuan commanded, \"Quan Fuhai, slap her face.\"","Not only would he strip her of dignity, he would trample her self-respect underfoot.","The covert glances from all around made Consort Ning tremble. She didn't look back, but she could feel the mockery and pity in those gazes.","Quan Fuhai took a handkerchief from his sleeve and wrapped it around his hand. \"Consort Ning, my apologies!\"","Just as he raised his hand, a shout came from not far away: \"Stop!\"","Everyone looked over. The Empress Dowager had arrived.","The commotion was so great that news naturally reached the Cining Palace as well. It was just that the Empress Dowager, getting on in years, slept deeply, which was why she arrived somewhat later.","\"Your greetings to Her Majesty the Empress Dowager!\"","\"May Her Majesty the Empress Dowager enjoy fortune, longevity, and peace!\"","Seeing the Empress Dowager arrive, the consorts collectively breathed a sigh of relief. Perhaps only Her Majesty could dissuade the Emperor.","The Empress Dowager had indeed come to advise the Emperor. She could understand his desire to cut the Gordian knot, but as the Empress Dowager, she also had to consider the entire rear palace. Palace maids and eunuchs were never ants to be crushed lightly; there were plenty of courts in history that had been deceived or even thrown into chaos by them. The relationships among the palace servants were intricate and complex. For the Emperor to execute so many eunuchs and maids at once might intimidate the majority of the remaining servants, but it was hard to guarantee that none would harbor resentment and secretly plot mischief.","The Empress Dowager absolutely would not allow any harm to come to the Emperor.","Naturally, she did not approve of the Emperor making such a grand spectacle for the sake of the Empress.","To the Empress Dowager, ten thousand Empresses were not as important as one Emperor.","The two moved to the theater study and spoke for the time it takes an incense stick to burn. When they returned, the anger on Jiang Yuan's face had dissipated.","Consort Ning was still kneeling, tears on her face shed for Yangxue.","The Empress Dowager then had Nanny Zhao go to help her up. \"My child, why must you suffer so?\" The Empress Dowager had also heard Consort Ning's earlier words. In all fairness, she rather agreed with them; this was also why she had always appreciated Consort Ning—she had a sense of the bigger picture and understood propriety.","Consort Ning, however, did not rise. She said slowly, \"Today's matter is to investigate the true culprit who poisoned Her Majesty the Empress. Since His Majesty has ordered the detention of the servants from the Chengqian Palace, Yanxi Palace, and my own Yikun Palace, he naturally suspects Consort An and this humble consort as well.\"","\"This consort should not interfere in this matter. But Yangxue and Suihe have served me since childhood; I treat them like my own younger sisters. Yangxue is already dead. No matter what, I cannot stand by and watch Suihe face danger as well. Your Majesty, this consort's innocence, this consort will prove it herself.\"","A wretched smile appeared on Consort Ning's face. Then she suddenly stood up and rushed towards the imperial guard holding the sword. Under the guard's horrified gaze, she grasped the blade and thrust it into herself.","\"Ah!\"","\"Your Ladyship!\"","\"Consort Ning!!\"","The scene instantly descended into chaos. Quan Fuhai shrieked, ordering the imperial physicians to save her.","Jiang Yuan had not expected Consort Ning to stake her life to prove her innocence. That resolute posture held no trace of pretense. He was somewhat shocked; today's Consort Ning had truly given him an immense shock. He even had the illusion that he was meeting her for the first time.","On the other side, Qi Daiyu was also startled by Consort Ning's sudden action, and her suspicion towards her wavered slightly.","Could it be that Consort Ning truly had nothing to do with this?","Because of Consort Ning's incident, the remaining palace servants, except for Suihe, were taken away. They would undergo interrogation but had temporarily escaped the threat of death.","Qi Daiyu exchanged a few brief words with Nie Zhiyu before they each returned to their palaces.","The horizon was already showing the first light of dawn. The palace paths today were unusually quiet. Yanhe and the others were still immersed in the earlier bloodshed and did not speak either.","Qi Daiyu felt a churning nausea in her stomach and walked somewhat numbly and mechanically.","Until she suddenly heard suppressed, heart-wrenching sobs.","Shiliu, who was supporting Qi Daiyu, involuntarily tightened her grip, saying fearfully, \"Mistress, that sound...\" Having just witnessed so many deaths, she couldn't help but think of something terrifying.","Qi Daiyu was also startled, but upon listening carefully, the crying didn't sound like an adult's; it seemed more like a child's, and somewhat familiar.","She had Little Li and the others search nearby. Finally, they found the source of the crying inside a water vat.","\"The Eldest Prince?\" Qi Daiyu was taken aback, seeing the Eldest Prince clad only in thin inner garments, curled up and weeping inside the vat.","Little Cheng hurriedly lifted the Eldest Prince out. Qi Daiyu crouched down and took the prince's icy hands. \"Why is the Eldest Prince here all alone? Are you cold? Where are the servants attending you?\" Even if everyone from Chengqian Palace had been taken away, the Emperor would surely have assigned people specifically to watch over the Eldest Prince.","The little chubby boy's eyes were swollen from crying. \"Auntie Hui, my mother-concubine is dead! I don't have a mother-concubine anymore!\"","A child's crying is always heartrending. Qi Daiyu felt a pang of sorrow. \"Eldest Prince...\"","\"Auntie Hui, they say my mother-concubine was a bad person, that she did wrong and that's why she died. My tutor says those who do wrong should be punished. But I didn't want Mother-concubine to die! I haven't grown up yet, I haven't brought Mother-concubine to my princely estate. I didn't want Mother-concubine to die!\"","The Eldest Prince cried until he was almost breathless. He couldn't comprehend the enmity between adults, nor did he understand what role his birth mother had played in the poisoning of the Empress Mother he respected most. He only knew that the mother-concubine who told him to eat less and urged him to strive hard was gone.","He would never see his mother-concubine again.","Qi Daiyu wanted to say some words to comfort the Eldest Prince, but facing the child's innocent, pure eyes, she found she couldn't say anything."]},{"number":121,"title":"Chapter 121","paragraphs":["Qi Daiyu was just about to have Shiliu take the eldest prince back when she heard the prince stop crying. Sniffling, he said, \"That day, I heard Mother Consort and Consort An talking. Everyone in the palace is saying that Mother Consort conspired with Consort An to poison the Empress Mother. Consort Hui, is that true?\"","\"What did you say? You heard Consort Shu and Consort An talking?\" Qi Daiyu was startled. \"Your Highness, when was this? Do you remember what they said?\"","\"Yesterday... no, the day before! Consort An came to see Mother Consort. Mother Consort told me to go back to my own room. I was almost there when I remembered I hadn't taken the wooden horse carriage you gave me, Consort Hui, so I went back!\" As a result, he saw the main hall's doors tightly shut. The eldest prince thought his mother consort and Consort An were sneaking treats behind his back again—this had happened before. He had brought pastries from his father back to Chengqian Palace, and his mother consort, after telling him not to eat too many, had been caught secretly eating them herself.","The prince thought, when Consort An comes visiting, she must have brought something, right? That's the custom for guests. Probably pastries. How awful of Mother Consort to eat them all by herself!","Determined to catch her this time and tease her properly, the eldest prince didn't enter immediately. Instead, he hid outside the door and eavesdropped for a while. He was still so small that the people inside didn't notice him at all.","However, the prince couldn't remember Consort Shu and Consort An's conversation very clearly. \"I just heard Consort An scolding Mother Consort, and she threatened her!\"","Qi Daiyu didn't believe it outright. Children have vivid imaginations. Sometimes, adult conversations are misinterpreted by children, and events can gain all sorts of fabricated details when retold by a child. This isn't necessarily lying; it's just that their cognitive and expressive abilities aren't fully developed.","Qi Daiyu knew well that when talking to children, one must avoid leading or suggestive questions. She patiently asked, \"Consort An and Consort Shu were speaking very loudly? You felt they were arguing?\"","\"Yes! They were really fierce!\"","\"What did Consort An say when she argued?\"","The eldest prince tried hard to recall. \"Consort An said Mother Consort had no brains! She also mentioned me, saying I wouldn't become a prince, that Father would strip me of my title and make me a commoner!\" He had been so angry hearing that! He would never be made a commoner by his father!","\"Consort An also scolded Consort Ning! She said Consort Ning wouldn't let Mother Consort live, wouldn't let me live...\" The prince suddenly covered his mouth. He remembered another sentence. He had heard his mother consort say, \"The Empress must die, and Consort Ning cannot live either.\" Tears instantly welled up in his eyes. His mother consort really did harm the Empress Mother, wuwuwu.","Meanwhile, Qi Daiyu was left with nothing but shock. Consort Ning, Consort Ning! Consort Ning was indeed involved in this!","Consort Ning had pretended so well, even attempting suicide to prove her innocence. Qi Daiyu had almost believed Consort Ning was blameless!","At that moment, Lianwu, who was standing nearby, let out a soft \"Oh!\" She whispered, \"Mistress, I just remembered. On the day of the Cuju tournament, when I went to the tea room, I think I saw Suihe and Juyi from Consort Ning's palace passing something between them. At the time, I didn't think much of it, assuming it was just something like tea leaves. But now that I think about it, it was strange. I called out to Juyi then, and she was startled. After that, she was unusually enthusiastic towards me, very different from her usual self!\"","If it weren't for hearing the eldest prince mention Consort Ning now and suspecting Consort Ning's involvement in the Empress's poisoning, Lianwu would never have recalled this incident.","Consort Ning, Consort Shu, Juyi... Qi Daiyu thought back to the conflicting accounts from Consort Ning and Consort An these past few days. A thread seemed to connect in her mind.","She instructed Shiliu, \"Take His Highness to Her Majesty the Empress Dowager.\" Chengqian Palace was no longer safe for him, but the Empress Dowager would certainly not neglect the eldest prince.","Shiliu replied, \"Yes.\"","Returning to Changchun Palace, Qi Daiyu had someone prepare hot water. She needed to sort out her thoughts. Strangely, even after witnessing such a bloody scene earlier, she had only felt nauseated at the time. Now that she was back, it was as if nothing had happened.","Remembering how she had nightmares for days after seeing palace maids being caned, Qi Daiyu mocked herself for having grown tougher.","While soaking in the bath, she reviewed the recordings from the past few days. During idle times before, she had watched many crime dramas, especially those focusing on micro-expressions and psychology, and had read related books. After all, in front of these consorts and concubines who could maintain perfect composure no matter what happened, only micro-expressions could offer a glimpse into their true thoughts and emotions.","Qi Daiyu was no expert, but she barely qualified as an amateur.","Too many bizarre and serious events had occurred recently, straining even the best composure. Qi Daiyu had indeed managed to discern quite a bit.","However, these observations could only corroborate her own suspicions; they couldn't serve as evidence.","After her bath, Putao came to report, \"Xiangchun has something to tell you.\"","Xiangchun?","Qi Daiyu was taken aback. After Zhi Ma left the palace, Xiangchun had devoted herself to caring for Siyu. Had something happened to Siyu?","\"Have her come in quickly!\"","Upon entering the hall, Xiangchun first reassured Qi Daiyu, \"It's not about the Third Princess. It's about Consort Ning...\"","Others might not know, but Xiangchun was aware that Consort Ning was not the \"aloof and refined\" person the outside world believed her to be.","Her own mistress had said that Consort Ning was deep and ruthless, not to be provoked lightly.","But the incident a few days ago where Consort Hui was framed had left Xiangchun deeply conflicted. Consort Hui was kind and treated the Third Princess as her own. For the sake of the Third Princess, she couldn't just stand by and watch Consort Hui face disaster.","It was only upon hearing now that Consort Ning had attempted suicide to prove her innocence that Xiangchun finally resolved to speak. She had to tell Consort Hui about that matter, to ensure Consort Hui wouldn't be fooled by Consort Ning's facade!","\"Previously, I and Consort Zhuang accidentally witnessed Consort Ning speaking with the Eldest Princess, Yeping...\"","Xiangchun told Qi Daiyu everything she knew. \"...Later, Consort Ning also sought out my mistress. Not many days after that, the incident of Zeng Qiming killing his wife occurred. My mistress even said it was all arranged by Consort Ning! Consort Hui, Consort Ning is absolutely not the genuine person you think she is. She is extremely skilled at disguise, meticulous in her schemes, and most adept at clearing her own suspicion and shifting all blame onto others!\"","Carried away by emotion, Xiangchun also revealed the cause of death of that Lady Wu from the Eastern Palace.","But after saying so much, she saw Qi Daiyu remain silent, only her eyes turning red.","\"Consort Hui?\"","Qi Daiyu asked her directly, \"Let me ask you this, and you need to think carefully. Was Consort Ning related to Sister Zhu's death?\"","Given Consort Ning's character as described by Xiangchun, if Qin Sizhu had learned about Consort Ning's conversation with Yeping, would Consort Ning have let Qin Sizhu live?","If not, the time of Qin Sizhu's childbirth would have been the perfect opportunity.","Qi Daiyu thought of Ye Qiong's unusual behavior in the recordings and her actions on the day Qin Sizhu gave birth. A shocking and infuriating conjecture surfaced in her mind.","Xiang Chun was left speechless. She wanted to say that she had been in the delivery room that day and indeed nothing unexpected had happened; her mistress had suddenly suffered a postpartum hemorrhage. But seeing Hui Bin's expression, she became uncertain again. Yes, would Consort Ning really let her mistress go? With Consort Ning's cunning, couldn't she devise a method to deceive everyone?","Qi Daiyu saw that Xiang Chun was also unsure. \"Return to Qixiang Palace immediately and carefully inspect everything Sister Zhu used in her lifetime, along with all her other belongings.\"","Then she stood up. \"Yan He, accompany me to Kunning Palace!\"","If Consort Ning was the murderer who caused Qin Suzhu's death, she absolutely would not let her off!","In Kunning Palace, the return of Chief Physician Xia had indeed brought the Empress hope for survival.","As the most skilled physician in the Imperial Hospital, Chief Physician Xia had seen and heard more than others. Regarding the poison from Qilan leaf pollen, his opinion was: \"I do indeed know of a medicine that can counteract the poison of Qilan leaf pollen. However, that medicine is extremely potent. Given Her Majesty the Empress's current physical condition, she absolutely cannot withstand it. Even if we try other methods to nourish her body, at most, she can only hold on for a few more years.\"","Jiang Yuan, having received the news, hurried over and heard the Empress say, \"Administer the medicine to me.\"","She smiled faintly. \"To live a few more years would be a gain for me.\"","Jiang Yuan's gaze was deep and heavy; he did not speak.","By the time Qi Daiyu arrived at Kunning Palace, the Empress had already taken the medicine, and her complexion looked much better than before. The Qilan leaf pollen had poisoned the Empress, yet due to its peculiar properties, it also rejuvenated her skin. All the wrinkles on the Empress's face had vanished; her skin was fair and radiant, almost poreless.","The Empress was not unattractive to begin with, and this transformation elevated her beauty further. Combined with the noble, dignified aura cultivated over years, she was dazzling to behold, yet also inspired a sense of awe that made one hesitant to look directly.","Upon entering, Qi Daiyu was stunned for a long moment before she remembered to perform the proper greeting.","\"You've come.\" The Empress leaned against the bedpost and smiled at Qi Daiyu. Before Qi Daiyu could speak, she said, \"It's about Consort Ning, isn't it?\"","Qi Daiyu was startled. \"Your Majesty, you know?\"","She hadn't known before, but these past few days had been enough for the Empress to investigate some matters. Combined with the recent commotion and a woman's unique intuition, the Empress was now basically certain that the one who truly wanted to harm her was Consort Ning. As for Consort Shu, she was likely a pawn who had been deceived.","The Empress sighed softly. \"It was I who sent someone to invite the Empress Dowager.\"","Only then did Qi Daiyu understand why the Emperor ceased his investigation after the Empress Dowager spoke a few words to him.","Qi Daiyu was puzzled. \"Why?\" If the Empress Dowager had arrived just a little later, perhaps Consort Ning would have been exposed!","The Empress said gravely, \"Because I am the Empress. Regardless of what the Emperor may think in his heart, to outsiders, it would appear that the Emperor slaughtered palace servants over internal strife among consorts. I cannot stand by and watch the Emperor bear the reputation of being 'cruel' and 'indiscriminate in killing.'\"","\"But His Majesty might not care about such things!\"","\"I care!\" The Empress was very solemn. \"The Emperor and I are one as husband and wife. I must consider what the Emperor has not considered and worry about what the Emperor has not worried about.\"","Qi Daiyu could not fully comprehend the Empress's mindset. Did the Empress love the Emperor that much? She didn't think this stemmed from love.","\"Moreover, what if we did uncover it was Consort Ning?\" The Empress lowered her voice. \"The Qilan leaves belonged to Consort An. The servant Axi who stole the pollen was Consort Shu's person. The one who poisoned me was Ju Yi. At most, Consort Ning would only bear the charge of instigation. She has likely already prepared her retreat, saying she merely spoke a few careless jokes to Consort Shu who then took them seriously. Given that, what can we do to Consort Ning?\"","Qi Daiyu said, \"But the Emperor, the Emperor would...\"","As long as the Emperor was determined and insisted on executing Consort Ning, it could be done!","A hint of pity appeared in the Empress's eyes, as if pitying Qi Daiyu's naivety. \"Silly girl, without concrete evidence, the Emperor will not kill Consort Ning. There is still Grand Secretary Yang at court.\"","The Emperor may not care about a mere Consort Ning, but he cares greatly about a Grand Secretary.","Qi Daiyu was unwilling to accept this reasoning. Consort Ning was suspected of causing Qin Suzhu's death and had targeted the Empress. To watch such a person continue to live with a clean reputation was something she could not bear.","The Empress saw through her thoughts. \"Rest assured, I naturally will not let Consort Ning off. But as I have told you before, patience in small matters prevents great plans from being ruined. Temporary forbearance is for a more effective blow against the enemy. Consort Ning gambled with her life this time, but His Majesty is not foolish. The doubts from this incident will surely plant seeds of suspicion in His Majesty's heart. In the future, we will have many opportunities.\"","What she didn't say was that she had already begun preparing her counterattack.","Some struggles extend beyond the harem.","Qi Daiyu remained silent for a moment but still held to her belief: never give the enemy a chance to catch their breath.","\"Empress, if I can deal with Consort Ning, would you allow me to try?\"","The Empress raised her eyebrows in surprise. \"You have thought of a method?\"","Qi Daiyu: \"I'm not sure if it will work, but I wish to try.\"","The Empress suddenly smiled. \"Very well. Since you have a method, go and try. At worst, I will cover for you. After all, I still have a few years left to live; I will certainly be able to protect you.\"","Qi Daiyu's eyes lit up. \"Then may I truly proceed?\"","\"Mm. If you require anything, Mei Yi and the others will assist you.\"","Having received her answer, Qi Daiyu hurriedly left. Mei Yi brought in the warmed medicine. \"Your Majesty, are you truly at ease letting Hui Bin confront Consort Ning like this?\"","She always felt that with Hui Bin's kind and gentle nature, she would be no match for Consort Ning.","Only then did a trace of weariness appear on the Empress's face. \"Mei Yi, Chief Physician Xia says I have only a few years left to live.\" At least three, at most seven. Her life would reach its end in that span.","Mei Yi's eyes reddened.","\"But, my Lingyi and Sheng'er are still so young. I must make arrangements for them. In this harem, the one I trust most now is Hui Bin.\" Even the Emperor, she could no longer trust. Though the Emperor probably no longer trusted her either.","\"But Hui Bin is kind-hearted and soft-natured, hardly capable of handling such affairs. I must teach her properly while I am still alive. This confrontation with Consort Ning is an excellent opportunity. If she can handle Consort Ning on her own, it will prove I have not misjudged her. If she cannot, at least it will show her the extent to which conflicts among consorts can go.\"","From the Empress's perspective, Qi Daiyu's background was known, providing a solid foundation of trust. Her character was upright and kind. Most crucially, the Empress knew Qi Daiyu had no desire to bear children. Qi Daiyu had been preventing pregnancy, and after Consort Zhuang's death, she developed a shadow over childbirth. Thus, Qi Daiyu had only the Third Princess by her side.","Such a person was the only one the Empress could entrust with confidence.","After finishing the medicine, the Empress's mouth was filled with bitterness. She had at most seven years left. In these seven years, she had far too much to do.","\"Enough, I shall help her after all. Regarding that Xiao Xiang from the Palace of Severe Punishment, has her family background been investigated?\"","Meiyi replied, \"It has been investigated.\" The Palace Rectifier of the Palace Affairs Office was one of their people; it was not difficult to look into a maid's household registration.","\"That Xiao Xiang's family lives in Lang County nearby. Both her parents are alive and well. She has an elder brother and two younger sisters.\" However, both younger sisters had been sent to work as maidservants in wealthy households.","The Empress Dowager said, \"Send someone to her family. Cut off one of her brother's fingers and deliver it to the Palace of Severe Punishment.\"","Meiyi bowed her head. \"As you command.\"","The Empress Dowager lowered her gaze. The Emperor's method of using execution to stop evil was not wrong, but that did not mean there were no other ways.","Consort Ning wanted her life. As for Consort Ning's own life, she preferred to take it herself.","However, thinking of Qi Daiyu's eager and enthusiastic demeanor, a flicker of amusement passed through the Empress Dowager's eyes. If that girl proved capable, she might as well let her have it.","In the Palace of Earthly Tranquility, Consort Ning had narrowly escaped death. The imperial physician said the sword thrust had penetrated deep into her vitals; had it gone slightly higher, it might have pierced her heart.","It was this slight difference that had saved her life.","During her unconsciousness, Consort Ning had awakened briefly from the pain. In that brief moment, she was certain she had survived.","The corner of her pale lips curved slightly.","See, even heaven was on her side."]},{"number":122,"title":"Chapter 122","paragraphs":["Upon returning to Changchun Palace, Putao immediately came forward to meet her.","\"My Lady, His Majesty is here.\"","At this hour? Qi Daiyu looked at the sky. After the chaos of last night, why wasn't the Emperor resting at the Palace of Heavenly Purity? Why had he come to her Changchun Palace?","She entered the room slowly and saw the Emperor lying on a low daybed. His eyes were closed, and she couldn't tell if he was asleep or just resting. Siyu sat quietly beside him, playing with building blocks. When the child heard Qi Daiyu enter, she grinned, showing a few tiny baby teeth.","As Siyu moved, Jiang Yuan opened his eyes. When he looked over, Qi Daiyu hurriedly lowered her gaze. She remembered how he had coldly and ruthlessly uttered the word \"Kill,\" and she almost seemed to smell the metallic scent of blood again.","Qi Daiyu bowed. \"Your servant greets Your Majesty.\"","\"Mm. Come here.\" Jiang Yuan reached out his hand toward her.","Qi Daiyu suppressed her unease and gave him her hand, sitting on the edge of the bed. \"Why has Your Majesty come?\"","Jiang Yuan shifted his body and rested his head on her lap. \"Mm.\"","Having ridden dozens of kilometers back to the palace overnight, then dealing with the turmoil of the night and visiting the Palace of Earthly Tranquility this morning, Jiang Yuan's body was not made of iron. He was supposed to return to the Palace of Heavenly Purity to rest, but for some reason, he had wandered to Changchun Palace.","Entering the hall and seeing the uniquely styled decor and the pile of strange cloth dolls on the bed no longer felt odd to him. Instead, it brought a strange sense of peace.","Putao had already cleverly carried Siyu away, leaving only the two of them in the room.","\"Massage my head.\"","Hearing his command, Qi Daiyu raised her hands, but she hesitated to let them fall.","Sensing something was wrong, Jiang Yuan opened his eyes and quirked an eyebrow. \"Are you afraid of me?\"","\"...No.\"","Jiang Yuan grabbed her hand and pulled it down. Qi Daiyu was forced to lean over, her face inches from his. Her heart pounded—not out of romance, but out of fear.","The man before her was handsome and capable, and his temperament wasn't strictly good or bad. In her past life, he would have been considered a brilliant young talent. But no matter how good such a man might be, she could have pursued him if she liked him or rejected him if she didn't.","But with this man, she had no choice. She had to \"like\" him.","If she showed even a hint of dislike and angered him, her fate would be no different from the palace servants who were treated like livestock the day before.","Jiang Yuan caressed her face and chuckled. \"Were you frightened last night? Ayu, don't be afraid. You are different from them. I would never treat you like that.\"","They are different from you, too, he thought. They each had their secrets and ugliness. But she was exactly as she appeared—lazy and pleasure-seeking, without any grand talents, yet simple and kind.","Therefore, he naturally wouldn't treat her that way.","When Jiang Yuan spoke, his expression was so gentle it gave Qi Daiyu the illusion that she was no longer just a favored pet, but someone truly cherished.","She didn't understand why his attitude had changed. She only wondered: when Consort Shu was in favor, did the Emperor look at her this way? And before that, when the Empress first entered the Eastern Palace, did he look at her like this?","She slowly sat up straight and placed her hands on his temples, rubbing them gently. She spoke softly: \"Your Majesty, I have just returned from the Palace of Earthly Tranquility. The Empress told me she was the one who invited the Empress Dowager. I didn't understand why, so I asked her. She said it's because she is Your Majesty's wife, and as husband and wife, they are one. She must think of what you haven't and worry about what you haven't.\"","Jiang Yuan sat up and looked at her quietly, waiting for her to continue.","Qi Daiyu's heart tightened. \"The Empress is so good. You must not let the murderer who poisoned her go!\"","\"Only that?\" Jiang Yuan laughed.","Qi Daiyu breathed a secret sigh of relief. \"Yes!\"","After the Emperor left, Qi Daiyu sat alone for a long time. Jiang Yuan had told her that although he had spared the servants for now, the poisoning case would continue to be investigated, albeit through more moderate means. However, once the culprit was caught, he would show no mercy.","According to the Empress's analysis, if they didn't intervene, the blame for the poisoning would likely fall on Concubine An.","The Empress's strategy was to plan before acting. Since they had already identified Consort Ning as the suspect, they would wait for a future opportunity to strike back.","But Qi Daiyu had probably watched too many TV shows and read too many novels; she didn't dare give her enemy a chance to counterattack. The thought that Consort Ning might have killed Qin Sezhu and was now cunningly trying to frame her for poisoning the Empress made her blood boil.","Did they really think she was a pushover?","Early the next morning, Qi Daiyu went out, this time to Qixiang Palace.","Since Qin Sezhu's passing, she had never returned there. Only Ye Qiong would visit her at Changchun Palace.","Ye Qiong lived in the western side hall of Qixiang Palace. When the palace servants saw Qi Daiyu, they greeted her warmly. \"Concubine Hui, you've come at an awkward time. Lady Ye was a bit shaken yesterday and is still sleeping. Please wait a moment, and I will go inform her.\"","\"Mm.\"","She didn't wait long. Ye Qiong appeared in casual clothes, her hair tied in a simple bun. Her face was pale and appeared small, yet she radiated the unique softness of a pregnant woman.","Ye Qiong said, \"Sister, please don't mind my appearance. I was truly frightened yesterday and had no heart for dressing up. Since you aren't a stranger, I didn't bother to fix myself up.\"","She smiled, but seeing Qi Daiyu just staring at her without a word or a smile, she became awkward. \"Sister Qi, what's wrong? Did something happen?\"","Qi Daiyu still didn't speak. She simply took an object from her sleeve and placed it on the table. It was a seemingly ordinary pearl with a tiny hole in it.","At the sight of the pearl, Ye Qiong froze. Her hand, which was supporting her lower back, tightened. After a long silence, she forced a smile. \"What... is this?\"","Qi Daiyu said coldly, \"This pearl was found among Sister Sezhu's belongings. It contains rosin. If I remember correctly, you have a dress embroidered with pearls.\"","\"I do have one, but I haven't worn it in a long time. Sister Qi, what are you trying to say?\" Ye Qiong avoided her gaze. \"I'm really not feeling well. If you have something to say, let's talk another day. Chun Zhi...\"","\"What did you and Consort Ning do to Sister Sezhu?\"","Qi Daiyu's words struck like a bolt of lightning in Ye Qiong's ears. She looked up in disbelief. Her connection with Consort Ning had always been secretive. How could Qi Daiyu know? But Qi Daiyu spoke with such confidence that Ye Qiong couldn't help but wonder if she had left a trail somewhere. Still, she tried to deny it.","\"I don't know what you're talking about...\"","\"Ye Qiong, Sister Sezhu treated you well, didn't she? From the moment you entered the palace, you were assigned to Qixiang Palace. You didn't have to pay respects to a high-ranking mistress like the others or suffer under her thumb. She took you under her wing, introduced you to the other concubines, and helped you gain a foothold. Why did you betray her?\" Qi Daiyu could hardly hide her agitation, her voice laced with a fury she hadn't even realized she possessed.","Admittedly, within the imperial harem, she had few true confidantes. Qin Suzhu was one. Later, the Noble Consort Li, whose values aligned with hers, could also be counted as one.","Nie Zhiyu and Ye Qiong were not at the level of confidantes, but they could still laugh and converse together. She asked herself, she had never done anything to wrong Ye Qiong.","She had never imagined that Ye Qiong's longstanding friendliness was all a facade!","Ye Qiong had cloaked herself in a guise of kindness to befriend them, yet in secret, she relied on Consort Ning, and had even targeted Qin Suzhu!","\"I didn't do it!\" Qi Daiyu's overly certain expression made Ye Qiong think she already possessed concrete evidence. Panicked and guilty, Ye Qiong cried, \"I didn't harm Sister Qin!\"","\"Yes, I admit I almost strayed down the wrong path, but I didn't take that final step.\" Tears streamed down Ye Qiong's face. \"I wanted to fight for a higher position, I wanted favor and glory. Is that wrong? Sister Qin couldn't help me, so I could only choose to rely on Consort Ning. I never expected Consort Ning's condition would be for me to harm Sister Qin. I hesitated, but I truly didn't do it.\"","\"Even if you report this to the Empress or His Majesty, I haven't actually hurt Sister Qin.\"","Ye Qiong's expression was too sincere. If this was still an act at this point, then her acting skills were truly exceptional.","Yet, even if Ye Qiong hadn't harmed Sister Qin, the fact that she was truly Consort Ning's person chilled Qi Daiyu's heart. Suppressing the turmoil of emotions within her with great effort, she took a deep breath. \"So, when did you connect with Consort Ning?\"","At this point, Ye Qiong seemed somewhat resigned. \"It was during the New Year's banquet a few years ago. I accidentally overheard Consort Ning talking with her sister...\"","Qi Daiyu hadn't expected to gain such an unexpected lead. Her original purpose in confronting Ye Qiong directly was precisely to see if she could obtain some leverage over Consort Ning from her. After all, someone like Ye Qiong, who acted one way to your face and another behind your back, surely wouldn't submit to being controlled by Consort Ning without a backup plan.","Now, hearing Ye Qiong's account, Qi Daiyu fell into thought. So, did Consort Ning know from the very beginning about Yang Luoniang being abused by Zeng Qiming? Moreover, Yang Luoniang was married off to Zeng Qiming on Consort Ning's orders...","Feeling another wave of contempt for Consort Ning in her heart, she noticed Ye Qiong had suddenly stopped speaking.","Only now did Ye Qiong realize something was amiss. \"You... were you tricking me into talking?\"","Discovered, Qi Daiyu remained unflustered. \"Whether you harmed Sister Qin or not, you know the truth in your own heart.\" She glanced at Ye Qiong's prominent belly. \"You say you sided with Consort Ning for wealth, for status. I don't think that's wrong in itself, and I won't condemn you for it. However, whether your friendship with Sister Qin, with me, with Zhiyu was genuine or had ulterior motives, I now hold serious doubts.\"","\"Let's have less contact in the future,\" she said, standing up. \"At the very least, you've already gotten what you wanted, haven't you?\"","Qi Daiyu couldn't be certain Ye Qiong had truly not harmed Qin Suzhu, but neither could she be certain she had. This knot would forever remain in her heart, making it impossible for her to interact with Ye Qiong as she had before.","Watching Qi Daiyu's retreating figure, Ye Qiong opened her mouth but no words came out. She admitted, her initial motives had indeed been calculated. She had even truly contemplated harming Qin Suzhu to curry favor with Consort Ning. Yet, these years of sisterly affection had not left her heart entirely untouched...","Tears slowly fell as Ye Qiong pressed a hand against her faintly aching stomach.","Qi Daiyu did not dwell on the matter of Ye Qiong. Upon returning to Changchun Palace, she poured all her energy into another matter.","She had been pondering how to deal with Consort Ning. After meeting Ye Qiong, Qi Daiyu had an idea.","It was hard to imagine what could possibly break a woman who even dared to commit suicide. But according to Xiangchun, Consort Ning harbored intense hatred for Zeng Qiming, who had killed Yang Luoniang. Clearly, Yang Luoniang's tragedy was of Consort Ning's own making, yet she sought revenge for her. Did this mean Yang Luoniang held a special place in Consort Ning's heart?","Qi Daiyu searched for a long time and finally found footage of Yang Luoniang from the New Year's banquet several years prior.","Looking at the girl who resembled a fairy, Qi Daiyu sighed inwardly. Silently offering an apology to Yang Luoniang in her heart, Qi Daiyu opened her video editing software.","She also opened a shopping app and ordered a bird-shaped drone, the kind with a projection function."]},{"number":123,"title":"Chapter 123","paragraphs":["That night, when all was quiet and still, a window in the bedchamber of the Changchun Palace was quietly opened.","Qi Daiyu leaned against the window sill, studying the drone in her hand. The instruction manual pressed under the desk was all crumpled, and she had lost count of how many times she had rewatched the tutorial video. Now, she was about to begin her \"test flight.\"","The bird-like appearance provided the drone with the perfect camouflage. Qi Daiyu had even asked Xiao Li to collect some feathers and glue them on. While this slightly affected the drone's performance, in a world with no concept of drones, it was more than sufficient, especially on a pitch-black night.","After flying a loop around the imperial palace without any patrolling guards noticing anything amiss—or perhaps they did, but only thought a bird had flown past—Qi Daiyu gained considerable confidence. She then piloted the drone to the Yikun Palace, landing it by the window of Consort Ning's bedchamber.","Currently, apart from Suihe, all the other servants in the Yikun Palace were temporarily assigned by the Imperial Household Department. There weren't many, let alone loyal ones. The eunuch on night watch at the palace gate was already fast asleep, and Suihe, who was keeping watch inside the room, didn't notice a \"bird\" perched at the window.","Having confirmed the location, Qi Daiyu controlled the drone back to the Changchun Palace, then to the Yikun Palace again, and back to Changchun, repeating this several times to set a fixed route. This way, she only needed to set the timer, and the drone could fly to the destination on its own and return within the allotted time.","And this operation could be done entirely through the \"phone light screen.\"","Qi Daiyu yawned and fell onto the bed to sleep.","Everything was ready. It was time for the show to begin.","The next day, Qi Daiyu gave Little Cheng and Putao a task. Both were somewhat surprised. \"Your Ladyship, this... will it work?\"","Qi Daiyu said, \"Just do as I say. Don't worry about the rest.\"","Little Cheng and Putao were utterly loyal and asked no further questions. \"Rest assured, Master. Leave this matter to your servants. We definitely won't ruin your plans.\"","When night fell and the time was about right, Qi Daiyu sent Shiliu to invite the Emperor. \"Just say I have something to discuss with His Majesty.\"","Such a lively show couldn't miss the Emperor's presence.","As soon as Shiliu left, Qi Daiyu opened that window. With a thought directed at the light screen invisible to others before her eyes, the drone silently took off.","Qi Daiyu felt a bit nervous. She had already loaded the edited video into the drone. Later, that video would be projected using the projection function. It was a video she had personally recorded, voiced, and edited. It absolutely had to work!","At this moment in the Yikun Palace, Consort Ning had taken her medicine and fallen asleep. Suihe, carrying the empty bowl, went out and saw the deserted courtyard, feeling rather angry. The servants temporarily sent by the Imperial Household Department were not diligent in their service. Even though it was still early, they had all returned to their own quarters. Suihe was just thinking of calling a young maid to wash the empty bowl when she saw Putao from Consort Hui's side suddenly arrive.","Suihe's heart skipped a beat. \"Putao, why are you here? Did something happen with Consort Hui? Why didn't the gate-keeping eunuch announce you? These lazy, cunning lot! Once Her Ladyship recovers from her injuries, they must be dealt with!\"","Suihe couldn't hide her embarrassment. After all, Consort Ning was currently the only Consort in the rear palace, yet she had no one reliable to use! Thinking of the original servants of the Chengqian Palace still in the Prison for Internal Discipline, Suihe felt fear again. These past two days, besides caring for Consort Ning, she had been secretly maneuvering, using Grand Secretary Yang's influence to prevent those people from saying things they shouldn't.","This was the slim chance of survival Consort Ning had fought so hard for, and Suihe naturally dared not relax. She was utterly exhausted, both physically and mentally.","Putao chuckled softly. \"I came to find you, Sister Suihe, precisely for an important matter. Consort Ning is injured, and I'm afraid scars will be left later. My mistress has a box of ointment for removing scars with excellent results. Lianwu was accidentally scalded before, and after using it for a few days, not a single mark remained. Sister Suihe, why don't you come with me to fetch it?\"","Suihe was somewhat tempted. Her Ladyship's wounds were not small, and scars would indeed be a headache later. Moreover, Consort Hui's skills in skincare were now well-known throughout the palace—after all, even the Empress was willing to use the beauty cream made by Consort Hui.","But... Suihe's eyes flickered as she looked at Putao. It was her own mistress who had suggested the plan to frame Consort Hui before. Suihe felt a pang of guilt.","\"Better not...\"","\"Sister Suihe, I deeply admire Consort Ning's noble and unyielding character. Even if my mistress doesn't say it, she has always held Consort Ning in high regard. Besides, at a time like this, surely you don't think my mistress would harm Consort Ning, do you?\"","With such a major incident just happening, who would dare to harm anyone now?","\"Let's go. It's just a stone's throw away. We'll be quick, and you can return sooner to care for Consort Ning!\" The Changchun Palace and Yikun Palace were very close. Without another word, Putao pulled Suihe out. Suihe had no choice but to temporarily place the tray on the stone table in the courtyard.","But as soon as they stepped out of the palace gate, a sharp pain struck the back of Suihe's neck, and her vision went dark.","Putao finally let out a sigh of relief, seeing Little Cheng next to the unconscious gate-keeping eunuch. \"Quick, hide both of them well. I'll go open the window!\" She lifted her skirt and ran back into the courtyard. Following Qi Daiyu's instructions, she opened the window of Consort Ning's bedchamber, then returned to help Little Cheng hide the people.","Focused solely on carrying out their orders, the two didn't notice a \"bird\" flying overhead.","Inside the bedchamber, a faint blue light projected into the room. A translucent, illusory figure of a woman materialized in mid-air. It was Yang Luoniang.","Qi Daiyu had designed the lines herself for the video recording, then used AI face-swapping technology to replace the face with Yang Luoniang's. She had also collected Yang Luoniang's voice from her New Year's banquet greetings for voiceprint synthesis. Unfortunately, due to limited source material, the voice was only thirty to forty percent similar. Adding some ethereal sound effects, in such an environment, it was enough to pass as real.","The sound of the window opening didn't wake Consort Ning. It wasn't until she heard a voice.","\"Sister, sister...\"","The somewhat familiar voice made Consort Ning frown in her sleep.","\"Sister, why did you do this to Luoniang? Luoniang hurts so much, sister!\"","Consort Ning's eyelashes trembled, as if struggling to wake up.","\"Sister, please save Luoniang. Luoniang will be obedient. Luoniang won't compete for favor with sister. Sister, please save Luoniang...\"","Consort Ning's eyes snapped open on the bed. She could clearly hear her own heartbeat. Had she just dreamed of Luoniang?","Her feelings towards this younger sister were complex. When they were very young, they had been very close. Luoniang was like a little shadow, following her around all day. Luoniang's favorite thing was hearing people praise her elder sister. In Luoniang's heart, no noble lady in the capital could compare to her sister, Yang Minzhen.","Later, Yang Minzhen entered the Eastern Palace, making it difficult to see her family, and her bond with Yang Luoniang faded considerably. By the time they met again, Yang Luoniang had grown into a graceful young maiden, still somewhat green but hinting at boundless future beauty. At that time, Consort Ning faintly felt a twinge of jealousy, one she herself hadn't even fully recognized. This jealousy could no longer be contained when she heard Lady Yang say she wanted Yang Luoniang to enter the palace.","Thus, Consort Ning discussed with her father, Yang Heng, and arranged for Yang Luoniang to marry Zeng Qiming. When she learned that Yang Luoniang was actually being abused by Zeng Qiming, Consort Ning felt shock, heartache, and also a strange, perverse sense of pleasure. She couldn't explain where that pleasure came from and was ashamed of having such thoughts. Yet, the combination of these emotions led her not to choose to help her younger sister immediately.","It wasn't until she heard the news of Yang Luoniang's death, followed shortly by Lady Yang's suicide by poison, that the guilt in her heart reached its peak. Only then did Consort Ning realize with a start what she had done wrong. But she did not punish herself; instead, she chose to punish Zeng Qiming, to avenge Yang Luoniang.","After Zeng Qiming's death, Consort Ning felt she had already avenged Yang Luoniang and cleared her debt. She owed Yang Luoniang nothing anymore.","So why, just now in that dream, was she trembling and weeping?","The wound ached fiercely, and her throat was parched. Consort Ning called out, \"Suihe.\"","No one answered.","Enduring the pain, Consort Ning slowly sat up. She lifted the bed curtain to call out again, but upon seeing the figure in the room, her pupils contracted sharply. Immense terror enveloped her, and for a moment, it felt as if all the blood in her body had frozen.","Yang Luoniang!","It wasn't just a dream; it was Luoniang calling her, Luoniang had come for her!","But Luoniang was clearly dead. She was a ghost!","Yang Luoniang stared fixedly \"at\" her, her face an abnormally deathly pale, her entire body emitting a faint blue glow, like a vengeful spirit crawled out from some deep hell.","A vengeful spirit! Yes, a vengeful spirit!","This realization shattered Consort Ning's reason. She frantically and clumsily scrambled backward, trying to retreat to the corner of the bed, but her eyes remained uncontrollably fixed on Yang Luoniang. She saw Yang Luoniang open her mouth. \"Elder Sister, why didn't you save me? Why didn't you save me?\"","Consort Ning heard her own voice speak. \"I already avenged you! Zeng Qiming, Zeng Qiming is already dead!\"","Yang Luoniang continued speaking, \"Elder Sister, he hit me, it hurt so much. There wasn't a single patch of good flesh left on my body. Elder Sister, why did you marry me off to Zeng Qiming? I am your younger sister!\" Her voice twisted strangely. \"You hated me. You were jealous of me. You didn't want me to have a good life!\"","\"Elder Sister, you were afraid. You knew your looks couldn't compare to mine. You feared I would enter the palace and share your favor. You feared the Emperor's eyes would no longer hold you. You feared you would no longer be the pride of our parents' hearts. You feared that in the future, everyone would only know Yang Luoniang, and not you, Yang Minzhen!\"","\"I did not!\" Consort Ning shrieked, her mind laid bare. She ignored the blood seeping from the wound on her chest. \"How could I possibly be jealous of you! I am the legitimate eldest daughter of the Yang family! I am His Majesty's Consort Ning! How could I be jealous of you!\"","Yang Luoniang's figure suddenly loomed larger, twisting into a grotesque smile. \"You weren't just jealous of me. You were jealous of everyone better and more outstanding than you! You were jealous of Consort Shu for receiving more favor, jealous of the Empress for taking the Crown Princess position that should have been yours. Elder Sister, do you truly think His Majesty cannot see your dark heart?\"","\"Ah!!\" Terrified by Yang Luoniang's sudden approach, Consort Ning tried to dodge but accidentally fell to the floor. She waved her arms, shielding her head. \"You're lying! The Crown Princess position was rightfully mine! It was Jiang Nvying, it was Jiang Nvying who intervened and snatched the Crown Princess position away from me! I was the most talented in the capital, my conduct was peerless, sought after by a hundred families. I should have been the Crown Princess! I should have been the Empress!\"","\"So, Elder Sister, you poisoned the Empress. Did you think you could ascend to the empress's throne once she died?\"","After saying this, \"Yang Luoniang\" suddenly vanished. The hall plunged into darkness. Before Consort Ning could even sigh in relief, suddenly, from all directions—there were \"Yang Luoniangs\" everywhere!","Countless Yang Luoniangs spoke in unison.","\"Elder Sister, you are delusional!\"","\"Elder Sister, you are delusional!\"","\"Elder Sister, you are delusional!\"","The horrifying scene utterly shattered Consort Ning's mental defenses. She screamed in terror, mixed with anger at being mocked by \"Yang Luoniang.\"","\"The empress's throne will be mine! Once the Empress dies, no one else in the palace will be my match. The Emperor cannot go forever without appointing a new empress. When that time comes, the empress's throne will definitely be mine!\" Consort Ning seemed to have gone mad, the blood on her chest now thoroughly soaking her garments. \"The Empress is about to die. She probably won't even realize until her last breath that her life was ended by my hand!\"","Consort Ning did not yet know that Chief Physician Xia had already found the medicine to treat the Empress.","It was as if she were boasting of her achievements to Yang Luoniang. \"All these years, the Empress Dowager and the Empress have had me assist in managing palace affairs frequently. In this rear palace, it's not only the Empress who has confidantes; I have mine too. I've already ordered Suihe to act. Those people caught and sent to the Discipline Office are of no consequence. Once Little Cheng dies, the murderer can only be Consort An. I attempted suicide first; who would suspect me?\"","\"His Majesty... His Majesty won't kill me. With my father here, the Emperor cannot kill me. Mother, Luoniang, I know, I know you hate Father, but Father is still useful. I still need to keep him. Later, I will avenge you!\"","\"Mother, I will become Empress. I will not fail your expectations. I will definitely become Empress. I am your most accomplished daughter! I am!\"","Blood loss made her body cold and weak, her vision swimming with spots. Consort Ning lay on the floor, nearly babbling incoherently. She did not notice that \"Yang Luoniang\" had already disappeared.","It wasn't until the doors to her bedchamber were pushed open, and light streamed in, illuminating Consort Ning—huddled in a corner, clothes disheveled, utterly wretched—that she realized.","With great difficulty, Consort Ning raised her head toward the source of the light.","She saw... the Emperor, his face ashen with rage.","Time rewinds to approximately the time it takes an incense stick to burn. In Changchun Palace, Qi Daiyu waited for the Emperor.","Qi Daiyu rarely took the initiative to send someone for him. Jiang Yuan, currently full of goodwill towards her, naturally would not refuse to come.","\"Your maid said you had something to discuss with Us. What is it?\"","Yan He stepped forward holding a box. Qi Daiyu pointed to it and gave her prepared explanation. \"This is a scar-removing ointment I prepared. I thought... perhaps Consort Ning might have use for it.\"","\"You want to give this to Consort Ning?\" Jiang Yuan was somewhat surprised. Although Consort Ning didn't seem like the one who poisoned the Empress, she wasn't completely cleared of suspicion yet. He knew Qi Daiyu was close to the Empress; she was actually thinking of sending scar ointment to Consort Ning?","Qi Daiyu pursed her lips. \"Your Majesty, I heard that Consort Ning's injuries are severe, and the wounds are likely to leave scars. No woman wishes to have ugly scars mar her skin. I am merely putting myself in her place. If Consort Ning truly is the one who harmed Her Majesty the Empress, as you have said, you would show no mercy, and she would have no use for this scar-removing ointment. But if she is not guilty, then she has suffered this ordeal for nothing. This ointment can serve as a small token of apology from me, on behalf of the Empress.\"","Seeing her earnest expression, Jiang Yuan was reminded of the silver she had donated to the almshouse.","She was always so kind-hearted.","Jiang Yuan: \"If that's the case, you could have simply sent someone to deliver it to Consort Ning yourself. Why did you go out of your way to come and find me?\"","Qi Daiyu shot him a glance, a charmingly coquettish manner instantly appearing. \"I wouldn't dare to send anything on my own authority.\"","Her look amused Jiang Yuan. \"So, you want me to vouch for your innocence?\"","In his view, Qi Daiyu had been frightened by the previous incident and no longer dared to send things casually to the other palaces. This time, when she sent the scar ointment, she had deliberately gone through him, the Emperor, so that if any trouble arose later, he would be her witness.","\"Then will Your Majesty agree or not?\" Estimating that the time was almost right, Qi Daiyu felt some inner anxiety.","Jiang Yuan was in a mood to indulge her. \"Since you specifically asked me, of course I must agree.\" He was about to order Quan Fuhai to deliver the ointment to the Palace of Earthly Tranquility.","But Qi Daiyu stopped him. \"Your Majesty, since Consort Ning was injured, I have not yet visited her. The other sisters in the palace are also concerned about her condition, but due to the circumstances... they dare not disturb her. As it is still early, perhaps I could accompany Your Majesty to the Palace of Earthly Tranquility? We could deliver the ointment along the way. Then tomorrow, when other consorts inquire, I can inform them of Consort Ning's condition and set their minds at ease.\"","Having said all this, Jiang Yuan could hardly refuse. Besides, he hadn't found the time to visit Consort Ning since her injury. He might as well go now.","The Palace of Eternal Spring was right next to the Palace of Earthly Tranquility, very close. Upon entering the courtyard of the latter, they found it deserted. Faint noises could be heard coming from the bedchamber.","Qi Daiyu clicked the return button on the light screen. The drone's projection shut down, and the \"little bird\" automatically returned along its pre-set route. Everyone present merely sensed a bird flying overhead, noticing nothing amiss.","Seeing that not even a night-duty eunuch was present, Jiang Yuan frowned. As they approached the bedchamber and heard Consort Ning's screams from within, his steps halted. Quan Fuhai, holding a palace lantern, was about to open the door when Jiang Yuan stopped him.","\"Wait.\"","Consort Ning's voice was piercingly clear in the quiet night air. Her shocking words caused beads of sweat to break out on the foreheads of the attending palace servants, who silently dropped to their knees one by one.","Qi Daiyu was inwardly overjoyed, but on the surface, she feigned alarm and made to kneel as well. Jiang Yuan, however, grasped her hand.","Consort Ning's words grew increasingly outrageous. Standing beside Jiang Yuan, Qi Daiyu clearly heard a cold, furious snort of laughter escape his throat. Then, Jiang Yuan kicked open the door before them.","\"Consort Ning, you deserve to die a thousand deaths!\""]},{"number":124,"title":"Chapter 124","paragraphs":["The Emperor's appearance was far too sudden. Consort Ning had no time to react before she was seized. Dizzy and vision blurring, she only heard the Emperor's cold laugh.","\"Guards! Hear my decree. Consort Ning harbors a vicious heart unworthy of her rank. She is stripped of her position and title and is to be sent to the Discipline Office for interrogation!\"","The next second, she fainted.","Even so, Jiang Yuan did not change his mind. Quan Fuhai immediately waved his hand, ordering people to take Consort Ning away. At this point, no one cared that Consort Ning was still injured—everyone knew that after uttering such treasonous words, Consort Ning was finished!","After Consort Ning was taken away, the atmosphere grew somewhat quiet. Qi Daiyu's hand was still held by Jiang Yuan, and it hurt a little.","\"Your Majesty?\" she said softly, only to see Jiang Yuan look at her with sharp eyes.","Qi Daiyu's heart skipped a beat, but her expression remained normal, even showing a trace of grievance. She lifted her arm. \"My hand... it hurts...\"","She knew what Jiang Yuan suspected. Her timing in suddenly inviting him to Yikun Palace, coinciding perfectly with Consort Ning exposing her own crime of poisoning the Empress, and Consort Ning's obviously abnormal state just now—it would be strange if Jiang Yuan didn't suspect she had played a part in it.","But Qi Daiyu was not worried about her own situation.","Firstly, her reason for coming to Yikun Palace was perfectly reasonable. The persona of being \"simple and kind-hearted,\" though not deliberately crafted by Qi Daiyu, had somehow been firmly established early on and was deeply rooted in the minds of the Emperor and Empress. As a \"kind-hearted\" person, her concern for Consort Ning was not out of place.","Secondly, the drone should have already flown back to Changchun Palace by now. Once she returned, she would discard it into the \"phone recycle bin\" for destruction. Even if the Emperor turned the palace upside down, he would never find evidence of her \"playing ghostly tricks.\" Moreover, she had been in Changchun Palace all day and had only now come to Yikun Palace with the Emperor, having had no contact with Consort Ning. Even if Little Cheng and Putao's movements were discovered, the two of them did not know the specifics of what Qi Daiyu had done.","Finally, she still had the Empress as a fallback. If Little Cheng and Putao were truly discovered, Her Majesty the Empress would certainly save them.","And Jiang Yuan did indeed harbor brief suspicions towards Qi Daiyu, but these doubts quickly dissipated.","It wasn't entirely due to trusting Qi Daiyu's kindness. In Jiang Yuan's view, with her level of cunning, she simply couldn't compare to Consort Ning. How could she possibly design such a scheme?","Jiang Yuan privately suspected that this matter was more likely the work of the Empress, with Qi Daiyu merely following the Empress's orders to lure him there.","Seeing Qi Daiyu's aggrieved expression, Jiang Yuan loosened his grip slightly but did not let go of her hand. \"I will escort you back first.\"","True to his earlier words, once he found the person who poisoned the Empress, Jiang Yuan showed no mercy. The very next morning during court, as Yang Heng stepped forward and bowed, ready to speak, Jiang Yuan said, \"What is it? Does Grand Secretary Yang intend to uphold justice at the expense of his kin once more?\"","Yang Heng's face instantly turned pale.","\"A father's failure to teach is his fault. As a father, you raised such a vicious woman. Yang Heng, are you fit for the position of Chief Grand Secretary? With such family conduct, such character, you still wish to be a teacher to all scholars? If all scholars learned from you, how much loyalty and integrity would remain in this court?\"","These words were too damning. Yang Heng fell to his knees with a thud, sweat pouring down his forehead. Members of the Yang faction looked at each other, not one daring to step forward and plead for him.","Jiang Yuan declared, \"Yang Heng, you are a malignant tumor!\"","This final verdict utterly ended Yang Heng's political career. That very day, after court adjourned, news spread from the Yang residence that Yang Heng had suffered a stroke. The next day, Yang Heng petitioned to resign from his official post and retire to his hometown.","In the rear palace, at Kunning Palace, Qi Daiyu helped the Empress slowly walk to the couch and sit down.","\"Consort Ning has confessed to all her actions,\" Qi Daiyu said happily.","After being taken to the Discipline Office and regaining consciousness, Consort Ning also realized she had been tricked. She tried to resist, quickly claiming that someone was practicing witchcraft in the palace, that she had been manipulated into saying those things, and that someone was trying to frame her.","But the most suspicious person, Consort An, was already under control and couldn't possibly have acted against her. Moreover, Consort Ning couldn't explain the many details in her confession that only she herself should have known.","After Consort Ning entered the Discipline Office, that maid, Xiao Xiang, admitted that Consort Ning had once given her a dose of poison, ordering her to feed it to Consort Shu. Consort Shu's \"suicide by hanging\" was a result of her staging the scene.","Soon after, a palace maid temporarily assigned by the Imperial Household Department to serve at Yikun Palace came forward voluntarily. She stated that she had heard movement in the main hall and went to investigate, only to see a faint, eerie blue light glowing in Consort Ning's bedchamber. Consort Ning was also saying things like \"younger sister\" and \"I'm sorry,\" as if she had encountered a ghost. The scene was too frightening, and she ran away in terror.","Thus, various rumors began to spread throughout the palace. Some said Consort Ning had killed many people, and now their ghosts had come for her; others said Consort Ning had killed her own younger sister and was being haunted by a vengeful spirit, driving her mad.","Tales of ghosts and spirits always stir people's hearts. Everywhere, it was said that Consort Ning was injured and thus weak in yang energy, making her vulnerable to possession by vengeful spirits.","Indeed, Qi Daiyu hadn't expected that the palace staff would spontaneously provide a plausible explanation for this inexplicable event!","After Consort Ning's personal maid, Suihe, was taken to the Discipline Office, she initially wanted to expose how Putao had tricked her. However, upon hearing that Consort Ning had been driven mad by the haunting of Yang Luoniang's spirit, she lost all hope and confessed everything.","When Yang Heng also resigned from office, Consort Ning seemed to finally realize there was no room left for maneuver and admitted to her crimes.","Qi Daiyu said, \"Your Majesty, regarding that Xiao Xiang... you applied pressure behind the scenes, didn't you?\"","She suspected the Empress had also fueled the recent rumors circulating in the palace.","The Empress gave Qi Daiyu an appreciative look. \"I couldn't leave you to fight alone.\" Naturally, she had to help clean things up thoroughly.","The Empress had done even more than Qi Daiyu imagined. She had someone cut off one of Xiao Xiang's brother's fingers and present it to Xiao Xiang. Under the terror of her family facing death, Xiao Xiang confessed everything. It was the Empress who told her to hold back initially, waiting for the outcome of Qi Daiyu's plan.","As for Suihe, her ability to hear about Consort Ning's situation in the Discipline Office was also due to the Empress's covert instructions.","And those rumors in the palace about Consort Ning seeing ghosts? Indeed, the Empress had a hand in them.","Thinking of Consort Ning's obviously abnormal self-exposure, the Empress looked at Qi Daiyu with a profound gaze. Naturally, she had many questions in her heart, but she asked none of them.","This left Qi Daiyu, who had prepared a set of explanations in advance, somewhat at a loss. She took the initiative, asking, \"Your Majesty, is there nothing you wish to ask me?\"","The Empress shook her head. \"I only need to know that you did very well. That is enough.\"","When you doubt someone, don't use them; when you use someone, don't doubt them. The Empress did not need to know what methods Qi Daiyu had employed. In fact, she should be pleased that Qi Daiyu possessed such means. It proved she had not misjudged the person; Qi Daiyu was not incapable. She had the ability to protect herself and to strike back.","\"This matter is settled, but the palace still needs to function. However, my health is not what it used to be, and I can no longer manage everything personally as before. You and Consort He will have to assist me more.\"","Qi Daiyu's face fell into a pained expression, but the Empress ignored her attempt at coquetry. \"Consort Hui, you are the one I trust most in this palace.\"","Seeing the Empress speak so earnestly, Qi Daiyu also set aside her playful demeanor and replied seriously, \"I understand, Your Majesty.\"","When leaving the main hall, Qi Daiyu saw the Eldest Princess practicing archery in the courtyard. The arrows had specially made wooden heads, and the target was hung on a tree not far away. Though she was a beginner, the Eldest Princess's posture was already quite proper.","The Second Prince sat primly on a stone stool, counting the hits for his elder sister.","Noticing Qi Daiyu's exit, the Eldest Princess put down her bow. \"Consort Hui!\"","Qi Daiyu took out a handkerchief to wipe the sweat from the princess's forehead, then examined her hands. The Eldest Princess's hands were not delicate; old calluses from learning the guzheng remained, and new blisters had formed from gripping the bow. \"After you finish practicing, come to the Changchun Palace. I'll lance those blisters and apply some ointment to prevent scars later.\"","The Eldest Princess's eyes sparkled. \"Consort Hui, you support me practicing archery?\"","Qi Daiyu smiled. \"Of course. Did someone say something to you?\"","The Eldest Princess replied, \"When the Empress Dowager came to see Mother Empress, she saw me practicing. She said I'm a princess, that I can live well without enduring the hardship of archery practice, and that learning such things easily leads to injuring oneself.\"","Qi Daiyu asked, \"But do you want to learn?\"","\"I do!\" She wanted to very much. \"I want to be like Mother Empress, riding horses and shooting arrows! Mother Empress agreed to let me practice too. These wooden arrowheads were specially made for me on her orders.\"","\"Not only do I want to learn archery, I also want to learn spear techniques, to learn martial arts!\" The Eldest Princess's expression darkened. \"Consort Hui, if I learn these, will no one be able to hurt Mother Empress then? You said before that to avoid being bullied, one must first stand strong oneself.\"","Her thinking was simple: once she mastered martial arts, anyone who dared harm the Empress would get a beating from her! Once those people were afraid of being beaten by her, they wouldn't dare harm the Empress or her brother anymore. After all, she was a princess; she could beat up anyone!","Qi Daiyu didn't answer the princess's question directly, only encouraged her: \"Since you want to learn, then learn! But learning these things will be truly arduous. You must have the perseverance to persist.\" She sighed inwardly; it seemed the Empress's poisoning had greatly affected the Eldest Princess.","\"I will!\" the Eldest Princess declared firmly. \"I will definitely persevere!\"","\"Persevere!\" the Second Prince chimed in.","His earnest little manner made both Qi Daiyu and the Eldest Princess laugh simultaneously.","After laughing, the Eldest Princess again looked troubled. \"Oh, Consort Hui, if you have time, could you accompany me to see Second Sister?\"","Qi Daiyu was taken aback.","Consort Ning's plot against the Empress had been brought to light, but the Emperor showed no intention of leniency towards Consort An either. Puying had confessed to some of Consort An's past misdeeds, and Consort An was now under house arrest in the Yanxi Palace, forbidden even visits from the Second Princess.","The Eldest Princess and the Second Princess had always been on good terms. Previously, when the Eldest Princess believed Consort An had poisoned the Empress, she couldn't help but resent the Second Princess. But now that the truth was out, the Eldest Princess felt the Second Princess was pitiable. Especially after overhearing palace servants whispering that Consort An might be executed—if that happened, Second Sister would be heartbroken!","\"Eldest Princess, don't worry just yet. Perhaps things aren't as bad as they seem.\"","As Qi Daiyu had roughly guessed, in Jiang Yuan's heart, he might not care deeply for any consort, but he would not disregard his own children. Therefore, he always showed an extra measure of indulgence towards the mothers of his children.","Although the Second Princess was not particularly favored, she was, after all, Jiang Yuan's daughter, and still very young. If Consort An were disposed of, the Second Princess would undoubtedly be devastated. Thus, Consort An, under house arrest in Yanxi Palace, received an imperial decree: confined to Yanxi Palace until the Second Princess's marriage.","In other words, Consort An's life now had a countdown, but this outcome was the greatest mercy she could receive. She understood perfectly well, however, that this mercy was not for her, but for the Second Princess.","Half a month later, the Palace Discipline Office transported a batch of corpses out of the palace. Yang Minzhen's body was among them, bloodied and indistinguishable from the others. These corpses would be taken to the mass burial grounds. To have no one claim one's body, no grave nor tomb, was considered one of the most miserable ends for common people of that time. One wonders if Yang Minzhen ever imagined such an outcome when she committed those acts.","As for those palace servants who were truly innocent, they were expelled from the palace.","With a number of servants gone, the Imperial Household Department petitioned for a minor selection. The Empress entrusted this matter to Qi Daiyu to handle.","By the time the minor selection was completed and the new servants were sent to the Southern Mountain Villa for training, it was already mid-August.","Outside, autumn rain fell steadily, while inside the Changchun Palace, days passed peacefully.","Siyu nestled in Qi Daiyu's arms as the two worked on pottery together.","A few days earlier, Qi Daiyu had told Siyu the story of \"Chenxiang Rescues His Mother.\" Unexpectedly, Siyu became fascinated by the Howling Celestial Dog and expressed a desire to raise a puppy. She said it on a whim, but the servants below had to run their legs off. To find a dog with good looks and a gentle temperament required careful selection and training before it could be presented.","To amuse her, they were now attempting to make a clay puppy.","Shiliu returned from outside the palace, stamped her feet, and shook off the rainwater. \"Mistress, Lady Ye has gone into labor!\"","Qi Daiyu was startled, calculating the time. \"...It's not time yet, is it?\"","It was only the eighth month.","Shiliu said, \"I reckon she was still frightened by what happened before.\"","Qi Daiyu pressed her lips together. Childbirth was a serious matter, and a premature birth even more so. She ought to go and see.","She coaxed Siyu, \"I'll leave the puppy's legs to you. I'm going out for a while. I'm sure you'll have it finished by the time I return?\"","Siyu declared, \"Of course! I'm super capable!\"","After giving Siyu a kiss on the forehead, Qi Daiyu washed her hands, changed her clothes, and went to the Qixiang Palace.","She was slightly delayed, and by the time she arrived, most people were already there, though the Emperor had not yet come.","Qi Daiyu walked directly towards Nie Zhiyu and Consort Li Zhao Yi.","Nie Zhiyu gave her a slight smile; both their eyes held a trace of helplessness and concern.","Regarding that matter with Ye Qiong, Qi Daiyu had not kept it from Nie Zhiyu. To her surprise, Nie Zhiyu said, \"Actually, I had guessed some of it, but I didn't dare think too deeply. Schemes and deceit are commonplace in the rear palace. It's too difficult to find genuine friendship; maintaining surface harmony is already hard enough. I am relieved she turned back from the brink and didn't truly harm Sister Consort Zhuang. Otherwise, it would have truly betrayed our years of camaraderie. From now on... let's just interact normally.\"","This was Nie Zhiyu's attitude, and Qi Daiyu herself felt quite conflicted, unsure of how to deal with Ye Qiong. To pretend nothing had happened was something she couldn't do. Yet to truly treat her as a stranger, she couldn't harden her heart enough, after all, they had gotten along so pleasantly over the past three or four years.","And so, they remained in this awkward state.","From the delivery room came Ye Qiong's cries of pain, such miserable sounds that reminded Qi Daiyu of the day Qin Suzhu gave birth to Siyu.","A chill slowly crept up from her spine, and Qi Daiyu felt cold all over.","Fortunately, although Ye Qiong had a premature birth, the delivery was quick. The midwife came out to announce the happy news, \"Consort Ye has given birth to a young prince!\"","That chill instantly vanished.","Hearing the little one's cries, Qi Daiyu suddenly smiled.","Forget it, judge by actions, not intentions. There's still a long road ahead.","When she left Qixiang Palace, the rain had stopped, and the sky was a clear, washed azure.","Qi Daiyu paused to admire the view for a moment and took a photo.","As soon as she entered Changchun Palace, she heard Siyu talking to herself, \"This is the left front leg, this is the left hind leg, Tiantian, you have legs now!\"","Qi Daiyu's face relaxed into a smile. She pressed the post button and called out loudly, \"Siyu, I'm back!\"","[The rain has stopped. jpg]"]},{"number":125,"title":"Chapter 125: Extra Story 01","paragraphs":["The sixteenth year of Yanli's reign.","Four newly entered imperial consorts gathered for a small gathering in the Imperial Garden.","Yan Cairen, with her charming appearance and dressed in a light cyan gown embroidered with chrysanthemums, idly twisted the handkerchief in her hand. She glanced sideways at Zhao Cairen and Chen Xuanshi, who were sitting on the other side playing cat's cradle, as well as Liu Xuanshi, who was playing chess by herself.","Yan Cairen: \"I say, dear sisters, aren't you the least bit anxious? It's been half a month since we entered the palace, and we haven't even caught a glimpse of His Majesty's face.\"","Zhao Cairen gave a faint smile but said nothing. Since the Emperor hadn't summoned any of the newcomers, what was there to be anxious about?","It was Chen Xuanshi's turn to manipulate the cat's cradle. She spoke without thinking: \"Being anxious is useless anyway. It's not like we can just run off to the Qianqing Palace on our own to request an audience with His Majesty, can we?\"","Yan Cairen grew impatient. \"Well, even if we can't see His Majesty, it would be good to see Consort Hui or Consort Shun!\"","Zhao Cairen: \"Sister Yan, I heard even before entering the palace that Consort Hui has a reserved temperament and dislikes disturbances. Although she currently manages the affairs of the six palaces, she seldom receives people easily. She is only close with a few senior consorts. We've just entered the palace; Consort Hui isn't familiar with us, so naturally, she won't summon us.\"","Mentioning Consort Hui, Chen Xuanshi stopped playing with the string. \"I heard Consort Hui is of peerless beauty, is that true? I was fortunate enough to see Consort Xi a couple of days ago—the one who gave birth to the Fourth Prince. She was so kind and also extremely beautiful. I was thinking, if Consort Xi is that beautiful, how stunning must Consort Hui be?\"","Yan Cairen curled her lips smugly. \"I have actually seen Consort Hui.\"","Drawing everyone's attention to herself, Yan Cairen unconsciously straightened her posture. \"It was at the New Year's banquet two years ago. I saw her when I entered the palace with my family for the banquet.\"","She had the highest family status among the four. The other three hadn't had the opportunity to attend the New Year's banquet.","Yan Cairen lowered her voice: \"Consort Hui is indeed beautiful, but privately, I think Consort Li surpasses her!\"","Chen Xuanshi then said, \"I heard from the senior maid in my palace that Consort Hui, Consort Shun, and Consort Li are extremely close. They often play mahjong together. Oh, do you know about mahjong? I heard it was something Consort Hui invented.\"","\"Who in the capital doesn't know about mahjong?\" Yan Cairen pouted. Mahjong had become popular years ago. Nowadays, there were even dedicated mahjong parlors in the capital; her own family ran one.","She added, \"And not only did Consort Hui invent mahjong, but also something called 'playing cards.' Pfft, such a strange name. What kind of person do you think could invent these things?\"","As soon as her words fell, Liu Xuanshi, who had been silent all along, stood up. \"Sisters, it's best not to discuss high-ranking consorts outside, lest trouble come from careless words. It's getting late. This concubine will take her leave first.\"","Watching her retreating figure, Yan Cairen sneered, \"What's she being so aloof about?\"","Zhao Cairen smiled and said, \"Sister Yan, you probably don't know. This Liu Xuanshi is related to Consort Hui by kinship. Naturally, she can't bear to hear you discussing Consort Hui.\"","This was truly something Yan Cairen didn't know. \"She's related to Consort Hui? Isn't Consort Hui's maiden name Qi?\"","Since they were selected as palace ladies, their families had made comprehensive arrangements, including gathering information on the family backgrounds and preferences of the high-ranking consorts in the palace. Consort Hui, being the highest-ranking consort in the rear palace now, was someone every candidate's family would try to learn about.","Consort Hui's father, Lord Qi, currently served as the second-rank Governor of Jiangning. He had only one son and two daughters. The eldest son married the daughter of General Lang, the Cavalry General. The youngest daughter was already married to Zhou Yue, the sixth-rank Commander of the Military and Horses Department.","They hadn't heard of any relatives with the surname Liu.","Zhao Cairen: \"Liu Xuanshi's cousin is precisely the wife of Consort Hui's elder brother.\" Although it's a bit roundabout, how could it not count as a kinship relation?","Upon learning this secret, the expressions of the three women changed differently. Finally, Yan Cairen put on a scornful look: \"So what if she has that kinship relation? It's not like Consort Hui treats her any specially.\" She was just like them—having entered the palace for half a month without even stepping into the gates of Changchun Palace.","Zhao Cairen said quietly, \"But she is still different from us after all. Currently, Consort Hui holds the highest rank in the rear palace and manages palace authority. Even if she isn't close to Liu Xuanshi, she certainly won't mistreat her. But us...\"","These words made both Yan Cairen and Chen Xuanshi somewhat nervous. Chen Xuanshi couldn't hold back her words, \"Then, Sister Zhao, do you have any good ideas?\"","Zhao Cairen, however, put away the cat's cradle string. \"What are you saying? What good ideas could I possibly have? At most, it's about seeking the protection of a powerful patron. If one patron doesn't work, wouldn't seeking another suffice?\"","Yan Cairen and Chen Xuanshi both became thoughtful.","The discussion in the Imperial Garden continued, while the subject of their discussion, Qi Daiyu, had just finished a round of mahjong. Her ears aching from Zhaorong's chatter, she gave up her seat to Zhaorong.","She stood up, and Nie Zhiyu also stood up, giving her seat to Ye Qiong. She then walked with Qi Daiyu to the lounge chairs in the outside pavilion and lay down.","Occasional sounds of mahjong tiles clacking and the voices of Zhaorong and the others drifted out.","\"My ears are almost numb from Consort Wei's chattering. She wasn't this talkative before, was she? When did she become so chatty?\" Qi Daiyu couldn't help but rub her ears.","Actually, Zhaorong wasn't particularly close to her, so by rights she shouldn't have come to Changchun Palace. But some time ago, Qi Daiyu had organized a \"Mahjong God\" tournament in the palace. Zhaorong was knocked out among the top five, and ever since she had set her sights on Qi Daiyu, Nie Zhiyu, Ye Qiong, and Consort Li—the final four. From then on, whenever there was a mahjong game at Changchun Palace, she would eagerly show up.","If there was no seat for her, she would watch from the sidelines. Watching was fine, but she particularly liked to comment.","Qi Daiyu's regular mahjong partners were Nie Zhiyu, Consort Li, and Feng Qi. Feng Qi was shy and timid, not good at socializing, especially feeling socially anxious around unfamiliar people. It was only after playing mahjong with them for a long time that she could interact normally. Zhaorong was an unfamiliar person to Feng Qi, yet Zhaorong would sit right next to Feng Qi and boss her around about which tiles to play. Seeing Feng Qi's ears and eyes turning red, Qi Daiyu simply gave up her seat and let Zhaorong play.","Nie Zhiyu laughed upon hearing Qi Daiyu's words. After laughing, she asked her, \"By the way, those newly entered palace ladies, are you really not going to see them?\"","Qi Daiyu: \"Why should I see them? They are imperial consorts, meant to serve the Emperor, not me. If a meeting is necessary, it will happen when the time comes. Why make a special point of seeing them?\"","Perhaps because she was getting older, or perhaps because there were more and more people in the palace, she was becoming increasingly impatient with making new friends.","\"You!\" Nie Zhiyu was used to Qi Daiyu saying such unconventional things. Sometimes, she found them quite reasonable.","\"Alright, I can't control whether you want to see those people or not. But you must manage the affairs of the palace, right? Her Majesty the Empress entrusted the palace authority to you. You can't always avoid your duties!\"","Mentioning the Empress, Qi Daiyu lowered her gaze.","The Empress was poisoned by the Yang clan many years ago. To counteract the poison, she took potent medicine, which left her body severely depleted. She held on for eight years before passing away last year, shortly after presiding over the Grand Princess's coming-of-age ceremony.","The responsibility of managing the Six Palaces was not something the Empress handed over to Qi Daiyu just before her death. In fact, for the two years prior to her passing, the Empress had already largely withdrawn from daily affairs, having Qi Daiyu assist in administering the inner court.","But who was Qi Daiyu? She had long vowed to live a life of leisure in this lifetime. Asking her to manage such a vast harem was no different from asking for her life!","However, the Empress insisted, and her objections were useless. A brilliant idea then struck Qi Daiyu: \"If you can't lead a team, you'll work yourself to death.\" She could simply delegate the work to others!","For instance, Nie Zhiyu was a perfect candidate. Her character and abilities had been affirmed by the late Empress! Matters concerning personnel transfers and overall coordination within the palace could be handed to her.","Then there was Consort Li. She was familiar with the procedures for banquets, songs, and dances, so the palace affairs related to feasts were assigned to her.","And Ye Qiong—didn't she crave power and glory? Then let her do more work; more labor deserves more reward.","Even Zhaorong and Feng Qi were given tasks.","Two years prior, the Emperor had generously promoted the ranks of the harem consorts en masse. Nie Zhiyu was now Shunfei (Noble Consort Shun), the former Li Zhaoyi was now Lipin (Consort Li), Ye Qiong was promoted to Xipin (Consort Xi), Zhaorong was promoted to Wei Zhaoyi (Consort Wei), and Feng Qi was promoted to Jieyu (Lady Jieyu)...","High-ranking consorts commanded respect from subordinates when handling affairs, which conveniently worked to Qi Daiyu's advantage.","Qi Daiyu didn't let the lower-ranking consorts off the hook either. So what if their rank was low? Couldn't they manage the flower nursery? At the very least, wasn't distributing mung bean soup or ginger soup to the palace staff simple enough?","She then divided the Eastern and Western Palaces into two departments. The Eastern Palace was headed by Nie Zhiyu, and the Western Palace by Ye Qiong, establishing a hierarchical management system. If any issues arose within someone's area of responsibility, they would report to the consort one level above. Only if Nie Zhiyu and Ye Qiong encountered something they couldn't handle would they bring it to Qi Daiyu for a decision—though such situations were rare. Even if they occurred, Qi Daiyu wouldn't make the decision herself. Instead, she would seek out the Empress. After the Empress passed away, she would wait until the Emperor visited the Changchun Palace and let him decide.","In short, Qi Daiyu successfully turned herself into a commander without troops.","At first, she was somewhat apprehensive, worried she might ruin the stable situation the Empress had established. But perhaps everyone knew she had the Empress's backing, or perhaps each person cherished their hard-won authority. Surprisingly, everything proceeded peacefully and smoothly.","After that, even the squabbles born of jealousy decreased significantly.","Qi Daiyu could only sigh in admiration: indeed, palace intrigues happened because the consorts had too much free time. Now, with work to do, who still had the mind for scheming?","The Empress found this outcome both amusing and exasperating, but she also felt that this might be the most suitable management style for Qi Daiyu and thus let her have her way.","And so, the inner court began to operate in this peculiar manner.","It has continued peacefully to this day.","So why did Nie Zhiyu come to persuade Qi Daiyu not to shirk her duties at this time? It was because she saw how leisurely and carefree Qi Daiyu was every day and felt deeply envious...","She also wanted to slack off.","Qi Daiyu tried to fob her off: \"Who says I'm slacking off? Haven't I been busy lately with selecting a suitable consort for the Grand Princess? The Emperor said the Grand Princess's consort must be an exceptional talent, one in ten thousand. I really must choose carefully!\"","Nie Zhiyu was startled: \"The Grand Princess is already selecting a consort?\" After saying this, she realized it was a silly question. Of course—the Grand Princess was already sixteen this year, so it was indeed time to start considering candidates.","Qi Daiyu smiled. The Emperor doted on the Grand Princess and would certainly be reluctant to let her marry too early. Even though they were starting to look now, it was only to avoid missing out on promising young men. Even if a candidate were chosen, the Grand Princess wouldn't marry too soon.","As the two chatted and drank tea, Sangsen entered from outside the palace.","Five years ago, after Qi Daiyu found good matches for Pomegranate and Grape and saw them married off from the palace, Sangsen and Lychee took over the duties of senior palace maids in the Changchun Palace. The once young and inexperienced girls were now addressed respectfully as \"elder sister\" by the younger maids and eunuchs.","However, Sangsen's steps were hurried, and her face wore an anxious expression. \"Mistress, I just returned from near the Imperial Study,\" she said, glancing at Nie Zhiyu hesitantly. \"The Grand Princess, along with the Second and Third Princesses, got into a fight with the Prince of Beili. The Eldest Prince and the Third Prince were trying to mediate on the sidelines and accidentally got caught up in it. The Eldest Prince has a black eye, and the Third Prince fell, scraping the skin off his palm...\"","Upon hearing this, both Qi Daiyu and Nie Zhiyu straightened up.","Nie Zhiyu asked, \"How did they start fighting for no reason?\" Then, worried about her son, she added, \"This won't do. I must go and see.\""]},{"number":126,"title":"Chapter 126: Extra Story 02","paragraphs":["Regarding this Northern Calendar prince, there is also a story to tell.","Many years ago, after Marshal Jiang's great victory over Northern Calendar, Northern Calendar surrendered. However, after only a few years of peace, once the new Northern Calendar emperor had eliminated his rivals and secured the throne, he again turned his ambitions towards Zhao Nation.","Unfortunately, Jiang Yuan was well-prepared, having consistently supported military commanders and trained new troops. When Northern Calendar sent its army, it was thoroughly defeated by Zhao Nation's forces. Jiang Yuan pressed the advantage, capturing ten Northern Calendar cities in succession, and even personally led the final campaign to capture the Northern Calendar emperor—though Qi Daiyu rather doubted the veracity of that \"personally captured\" claim.","The captured Northern Calendar emperor, Feng Deshou, could not bear the humiliation and committed suicide. Northern Calendar's military morale completely collapsed. Feng Deshou's younger brother, Feng Deman, seized the opportunity to take the throne, actively surrendered, and pledged allegiance, turning Northern Calendar into a vassal state of Zhao Nation. To show sincerity, Feng Deman sent his legitimate son, Feng Yucheng, to Zhao Nation as a hostage.","To demonstrate the magnanimity of a great nation, Jiang Yuan enfeoffed Feng Yucheng as Prince Li, allowing him to reside in the Xiefang Palace with the imperial princes and study in the Imperial Study.","While Feng Yucheng enjoyed treatment similar to that of a prince, he was, after all, a hostage from Northern Calendar, and could not compare to the supremely precious and noble Princess Yong'an. The problem, however, lay in the fact that Feng Yucheng was a sickly weakling with a frail constitution. If he were truly injured, for the sake of the larger situation, the Emperor would inevitably have to reprimand the Grand Princess a few words.","Thinking of this, Qi Daiyu could no longer stay put. She decided to go with Nie Zhiyu to see what exactly had happened.","Before even stepping into the Imperial Study, Qi Daiyu heard the Crown Prince's cries of pain.","\"Eldest Sister, you were too heavy-handed! Look at my face, such a large bruise! You've ruined my handsome looks, how am I supposed to face anyone now?\"","\"Ouch, ouch! You clumsy, clumsy servant, be gentler! Do you want to pain me to death?\"","\"Third Sister, stop laughing! If you keep laughing, I'll never bring you delicious treats again!\"","Qi Daiyu walked in to see the tall and burly Crown Prince with a black eye, resembling a panda. Seated beside him was the Third Prince, with a scraped patch of skin on his right palm. The Second Princess stood before them, instructing the young eunuch to carefully apply medicine.","Si Yu was giggling at the two of them, while the Grand Princess wore a dark expression, looking very angry.","Chu Tong the Commandery Princess, Jiang Yuelan, and others were also present.","When Qi Daiyu and Nie Zhiyu entered, everyone immediately paid their respects.","\"Greetings to Consort Hui, Consort Shun.\"","\"Consort Hui!\" The Crown Prince \"howled\" and rushed over, \"You must uphold justice for your son! Look at my face, it was all Eldest Sister's doing!\"","Nearly six feet tall, stout, and solidly built like a small mountain, he was speaking in a coquettish tone.","Si Yu retorted, \"That's not how it was at all! You and Third Brother were trying to break up the fight, and Eldest Sister accidentally swung her fist and hit your face.\" Then the Crown Prince stumbled and bumped into the Third Prince, who lost his footing, fell to the ground, and scraped his hand.","Having failed in his complaint, the Crown Prince glared at Si Yu.","Si Yu, not to be outdone, glared back.","Ignoring the silent battle between these two, Qi Daiyu scanned the room and noticed two people were missing: Feng Yucheng and Jiang Huai.","\"What exactly happened? Where is Prince Li?\"","It was only then that the Grand Princess spoke up, \"I accidentally broke his wrist. I set it back! But he wasn't reassured, so I had someone send him to the Imperial Hospital.\"","As Qi Daiyu was about to ask for details, Quan Fuhai arrived.","\"By His Majesty's decree, the Grand Princess is summoned to the Hall of Mental Cultivation. Ah, Consort Hui is also here. His Majesty happens to have matters to discuss with you as well.\"","Qi Daiyu had to ask Nie Zhiyu to escort the children back, while she and the Grand Princess headed for the Hall of Mental Cultivation.","Having the palace attendants keep their distance, Qi Daiyu lowered her voice, \"For no good reason, why did you hit that Feng Yucheng?\"","The Grand Princess looked somewhat uncomfortable. \"That person puts on airs all day long. I find him extremely annoying.\"","\"Was it because of Jiang Huai?\" A hint of gossip appeared on Qi Daiyu's face.","Jiang Huai was the legitimate eldest son of Jiang Ruxun, the adopted younger brother of the Empress.","When the Second Prince was five years old, the Emperor issued an edict enfeoffing the Second Prince as Crown Prince. He selected Tang Cong, son of Tang Gejian (Chief Grand Secretary and Minister of Personnel), and Jiang Huai, son of Jiang Ruxun (Vice Minister of the Court of Judicial Review), as the Crown Prince's study companions.","Judging by his father's official rank, Jiang Huai was not quite qualified to be a Crown Prince's companion. But the Jiang family was the Empress's maternal family and the Crown Prince's maternal uncle's family. From that perspective, Jiang Huai was actually quite suitable.","\"Consort Hui!\" the Grand Princess chided, \"It wasn't for him at all!\"","Qi Daiyu just smiled.","She looked at the Grand Princess with gentle and gratified eyes.","If the late Empress had any regrets before her passing, it was probably not being able to see the Grand Princess marry with her own eyes, or even having enough time to select a consort for the Grand Princess. Actually, the Empress could have insisted on deciding if she wished, but she preferred the Grand Princess to meet a suitable, beloved partner on her own.","The Grand Princess was now sixteen, graceful and elegant, more beautiful than flowers.","\"Ah, don't look at me like that! I won't talk to you anymore!\" The Grand Princess stamped her foot and walked ahead sullenly.","When they reached the Hall of Mental Cultivation, the Crown Prince was waiting outside the hall doors.","He spent an hour each day learning by the Emperor's side, so he had not been in the Imperial Study when the Grand Princess hit Feng Yucheng.","At eleven years old, the Crown Prince already carried himself like a young adult, as steadfast as a pine or bamboo, calm and steady—this was his demeanor when outsiders were present.","Seeing the two approach, the Crown Prince bowed formally and respectfully, \"Greetings to Consort Hui. Eldest Sister.\"","Then he lowered his voice, \"Eldest Sister, when you go in later, act a bit coquettish, soften your tone.\"","He winked at the Grand Princess.","The Grand Princess pursed her lips and went in first.","Qi Daiyu took the opportunity to ask the Crown Prince a few questions about his recent meals and such.","\"Lan Yi is serving you in the Eastern Palace. She is the most reliable, so I'm quite at ease. But you mustn't strain yourself too much either. Balance work with rest, and absolutely no more staying up late to study.\"","Last year, the Crown Prince moved to the Eastern Palace, and Lan Yi went with him to become the Chief Stewardess there. Lan Yi was naturally loyal to the Crown Prince, but she also strongly wished for him to excel, so she urged him rather strictly in his studies. Two months ago, the Crown Prince caught a chill from reading late at night and fell ill.","Qi Daiyu wanted him to relax a little and not push himself too hard.","The corner of the Crown Prince's mouth twitched upwards, then he composed himself again. \"Consort Hui, rest assured, your son understands.\"","Qi Daiyu: \"By the way, my palace made egg tarts today. I'll have Lianwu send two over to the Eastern Palace later. Or you can have Xiao Yinzi go fetch them from the Changchun Palace.\"","The Crown Prince had a sweet tooth. \"Could it be... four?\"","Qi Daiyu laughed. \"Alright, four! But no more!\"","After the Crown Prince left, Qi Daiyu finally entered the Hall of Mental Cultivation. Inside, Jiang Yuan was speaking, while the Grand Princess stood with her head bowed, twisting her fingers.","Years had passed. Jiang Yuan was now nearly forty. He had grown a beard, and his majesty was even more imposing than before, often causing people to tremble with fear from a single glance.","At this moment, however, he wore the expression of someone at a loss with the Grand Princess.","\"Even if you had to hit him, couldn't you have found a secluded spot, or had someone else do it for you? You just had to do it in broad daylight, and in a place like the Study Hall! The Study Hall is for your studies, not for brawling!\"","\"Never mind whether some censor might hear of this and impeach you, you must think of your own reputation! A princess, leading her two younger sisters to beat up a man, even injuring a brother-in-arms? What will people think of you? You are a princess of the realm!\"","Just then, he saw Qi Daiyu enter. Jiang Yuan turned to her, saying, \"I told you long ago she shouldn't have been allowed to learn those martial arts. But you and the Empress indulged her. Look at her now—what other young lady is like her? You two have truly spoiled her rotten!\"","The Eldest Princess was defiant. \"Why can't a woman learn martial arts? I want to learn them, and I've learned them well—I'm no worse than any boy. I might even go to the battlefield someday!\"","\"You!\" Jiang Yuan was so angry his beard seemed to bristle.","Qi Daiyu poured tea for both of them. \"When has your father ever truly forbidden you? Have you forgotten, the Master Liao who teaches you martial arts was personally selected by His Majesty as an expert. Just a few months ago, when His Majesty inspected the Tiger Guard camp at the capital's outskirts, he specifically took you along.\"","To be fair, Jiang Yuan was extremely indulgent towards the Eldest Princess. If she wanted to learn martial arts, he found her a master. If she wanted to leave the palace, he granted her a token allowing her to come and go as she pleased. He basically gave her whatever she asked for.","His earlier words were merely spoken in anger.","\"As for the nonsense about women not learning martial arts, that's utterly false. During the war with Northern Li, the Red Tassel Army rendered great service!\"","The Red Tassel Army, Zhao Kingdom's only female guard unit, comprised just five hundred women. It was established by Jiang Yuan himself, initially facing skepticism from all the officials. Jiang Yuan had forcefully overruled them, declaring, \"The Empress's archery skills can hit a target from a hundred paces. Were she to don armor and go to battle, she would be a heroine! Our Zhao Kingdom is vast, and among its countless women, there must be extraordinary talents. By establishing this female guard and broadly recruiting talented women to strengthen our armies, I am planning for the long term.\"","The name \"Red Tassel\" was personally chosen by the Empress.","Hearing Qi Daiyu say this, the Eldest Princess realized her mistake. She turned to her father, cooing, \"Father, I know I was wrong. I shouldn't have beaten Feng Yucheng in public. But he was truly despicable, he actually...\"","\"Actually what?\" Jiang Yuan glared at her. \"Actually bullied Jiang Huai?\"","The Eldest Princess's eyes widened. \"You knew?! You knew and you still scolded me!\"","\"Feng Yucheng is a Commandery Prince, while Jiang Huai is but a commoner with no official rank. For Feng Yucheng to order Jiang Huai to kneel, what fault is there in that according to propriety?\"","The Eldest Princess retorted, \"By the rules of etiquette, perhaps not. But Feng Yucheng's intent was to humiliate him! Of course I couldn't stand by and watch!\"","Jiang Yuan's expression suddenly shifted to a teasing one. \"So you felt a pang of pity for that Jiang Huai, is that it?\"","\"Who's feeling sorry for him! Don't talk nonsense, Father. Jiang Huai is my cousin; it's only right that I protect him!\" Even as she said this, the Eldest Princess's face flushed red.","Her bashfulness was not lost on Jiang Yuan and Qi Daiyu.","Jiang Yuan settled into his seat leisurely, his tone meaningful. \"Some time ago, the Northern Li envoy submitted a memorial, seeking to propose a marriage alliance for their Commandery Prince, Feng Yucheng. While Feng Yucheng's health is somewhat frail, he is handsome and his literary talent is genuinely good. Moreover, as a hostage, he must remain in the capital his whole life, so the princess wouldn't have to marry far away. He is indeed a rather suitable candidate for consort...\"","\"He's a toad lusting after swan meat! Who would want to marry him? Is he even worthy? He falls ill if a breeze blows too strong. Marrying him would be like being widowed while he's still alive!\"","These words were quite improper. Jiang Yuan looked at Qi Daiyu: These words clearly came from your teaching.","Qi Daiyu guiltily rubbed her nose.","Jiang Yuan continued, \"Then who do you want for a consort? Jiang Huai?\"","\"Father!\" This time the Eldest Princess was truly flustered and annoyed. Without another word, she turned and ran out of the room.","\"Ah!\" Jiang Yuan sighed and took a sip of tea. \"Judging by Lingyi's reaction, I fear she has truly set her heart on that Jiang Huai.\"","Qi Daiyu said, \"Young Master Jiang is refined, gentle, elegant, steady, and sincere. He is no less worthy than Commandery Prince Feng.\"","\"I know. Jiang Huai is a fine young man. I'm just wondering whether Lingyi genuinely has feelings for him, or if it's for the sake of the Jiang family.\"","The Jiang family now only had Jiang Ruhuan serving at court, and even he was merely a fourth-rank Vice Minister of the Court of Judicial Review—a single pillar struggling to hold up the structure. The Jiang family was far from its former glory. If they were fortunate enough to have a princess marry into the family, the Jiangs' prominence could naturally continue for many more years.","Jiang Yuan was worried the Eldest Princess might sacrifice herself to help the Jiang family.","In truth, in Qi Daiyu's heart, Jiang Huai was far better than Feng Yucheng. Of course, if Jiang Huai were truly the Eldest Princess's blood cousin, Qi Daiyu would do everything possible to make the princess dislike him—one must avoid close-kin marriage.","But Jiang Ruhuan was actually the Empress's adopted younger brother. Calculating the kinship, Jiang Huai and the Eldest Princess were fourth-degree collateral relatives, not considered close kin. In Qi Daiyu's original world, that would meet the requirements for marriage.","Therefore, Qi Daiyu naturally had no objection.","\"Based on my understanding of the Eldest Princess, her feelings for Jiang Huai are genuine.\""]},{"number":127,"title":"Chapter 127: Extra Story 03","paragraphs":["\"What do you mean?\" Jiang Yuan was very concerned about the Eldest Princess's thoughts.","Qi Daiyu thought for a moment and recounted something in a low voice.","Jiang Yuan: \"Is that true?\"","If so, then the Eldest Princess did have some feelings for Jiang Huai.","\"Your Majesty should just know this in your heart. Please don't mention it in front of the Eldest Princess, or she'll be upset with me.\" If it weren't for the need to reassure the emperor, Qi Daiyu wouldn't have told him.","\"Naturally, I understand.\" Jiang Yuan snorted, \"She is indeed close to you.\"","Qi Daiyu raised her eyebrows proudly. It wasn't a boast, but all the princes and princesses in the palace liked her, especially the princesses, who were willing to share their secrets and worries with her.","\"Eunuch Quan said Your Majesty summoned me because you had something to discuss. What is it?\"","Mentioning this, Jiang Yuan handed her the top memorial on his desk, gesturing for her to read it.","Since he could show it to her, it certainly wasn't a confidential state document. Qi Daiyu opened it quietly but was startled.","The memorial was about tax revenues from the Jiang and Huai regions, and the person who wrote it was none other than her father, Qi Caishang.","Qi Daiyu didn't dare to read it in detail. \"Your Majesty?\"","Jiang Yuan: \"This year's harvest in the Jiang and Huai regions is exceptionally good. Minister Qi's memorial also says the local people live in peace and contentment. I was thinking that since my accession, I have never embarked on an imperial tour. Perhaps this year we could travel to Jiang and Huai to see for ourselves if the people's lives are truly as good as described in this memorial.\"","An imperial tour!","Qi Daiyu's eyes lit up. If the emperor goes on a tour, he must bring consorts, right? Then she would have a chance to go along!","Having transmigrated into this world for so many years, she finally had a chance to leave the capital! And to go to the prosperous Jiangnan region!","Suppressing her inner excitement, she asked, \"Has Your Majesty decided on the date for the journey, and what do you need me to do?\"","After years of companionship, how could Qi Daiyu's emotions escape Jiang Yuan's notice? He smiled meaningfully, \"Tentatively set for August. We'll travel down the Grand Canal, passing through Jizhou, Guanghai, Sunan, Jiangning, and Huaizhou.\"","And by boat! Qi Daiyu could barely suppress the smile at the corner of her mouth!","\"With Elder Tang overseeing court affairs, there should be no worries. I plan to bring all the princes and princesses as well, so they can see the mountains and rivers of our Zhao Kingdom and experience the lives of the common people. As for the consorts, you will be in charge of the arrangements. However, the rear palace cannot be left unattended. You currently hold the highest rank...\" Jiang Yuan deliberately dragged out his sentence.","The next moment, he saw Qi Daiyu's beautiful eyes widen in alarm.","Jiang Yuan chuckled, \"I will have Nanny Lian oversee the rear palace.\" Nanny Lian was the emperor's former wet nurse, a highly experienced and respected nanny in the palace.","With her watching over things, nothing would go wrong in the palace.","\"Your Majesty was deliberately teasing me!\"","Jiang Yuan absolutely was, and he burst into hearty laughter.","Meanwhile, after leaving the Hall of Mental Cultivation, the Eldest Princess intended to go horseback riding at the South Garden riding grounds but encountered Jiang Huai.","The young man was dressed in blue robes, his posture tall and straight, his gaze clear and bright.","\"Greetings, Your Highness the Eldest Princess.\" Jiang Huai bowed with his hands clasped.","The Eldest Princess walked slowly closer. \"Didn't I tell you to return home? Why are you still in the palace?\"","Although she was the one who struck Feng Yucheng, the incident ultimately stemmed from Jiang Huai. The Eldest Princess, worried the emperor might blame Jiang Huai, had told him to leave the palace first.","Who knew he hadn't left, and by the looks of it, had been waiting here for quite some time.","Jiang Huai smiled gently, \"Your Highness stood up for me. It is only right that I express my gratitude.\"","The Eldest Princess pursed her lips, \"I wasn't standing up for you. I just couldn't stand Feng Yucheng's arrogant manner.\"","Jiang Huai fell silent for a moment. \"My apologies for misspeaking.\"","His response annoyed the Eldest Princess instead. \"Jiang Huai, are you a blockhead? That there are still girls who like you like this... they must be blind.\"","She was referring to an incident during the Lantern Festival in the first month.","During the Lantern Festival, the capital traditionally held lantern fairs and temple festivities. The Eldest Princess, craving excitement, had left the palace.","Finding it boring to wander the fair alone, she thought of looking for Jiang Huai, but unexpectedly saw him walking with a young woman.","The Eldest Princess later found out that the young woman was from the Xue family in the capital and had a rather good reputation.","Jiang Huai explained helplessly, \"Your Highness, I explained before. That night the streets were crowded, and it was dark. Miss Xue had become separated from her maid. Being alone was unsafe, so I merely escorted her back to the Xue residence.\" Moreover, knowing the Eldest Princess was leaving the palace, he had thought of the delicious yuanxiao (sweet dumplings) from a shop called Li's near the Xue residence, planning to bring some for her to try.","The Eldest Princess muttered, \"What a coincidence that she got separated from her maid and just happened to run into you...\"","Her voice was too soft. Jiang Huai didn't catch it. \"Pardon?\"","\"Nothing.\" The Eldest Princess's mood unexpectedly improved. Noticing the food box in Jiang Huai's hand, she asked, \"What's that you're holding?\"","Jiang Huai lifted the food box. \"Roast chicken from Wang's at the foot of Zhuqing Mountain.\"","\"The one at the foot of Zhuqing Mountain?\" Zhuqing Mountain was twenty li from the capital, a trip of several hours there and back.","Jiang Huai: \"Yes.\" He had set out at Yin hour (3-5 am) this morning, arrived at Zhuqing Mountain by Chen hour (7-9 am), bought the first roast chicken of the day, and hurried back, even taking leave from his duties in the morning for this.","\"You mentioned wanting to eat it a couple of days ago? This food box is specially made; the chicken is still warm.\"","When did she say she wanted to eat it?","The Eldest Princess was about to ask when she suddenly remembered she had indeed said something like that a few days ago, only...","\"It was my Third Sister who wanted to eat roast chicken. She asked me to send someone out of the palace to buy one for her.\" The Eldest Princess laughed.","One year, she had taken the Second and Third Princesses fishing at a manor near Zhuqing Mountain. They had tried Wang's roast chicken at the foot of the mountain, and ever since, Si Yu had been unable to forget it. She had been mentioning it again a few days ago. As the eldest sister with a palace exit token, Si Yu had asked her for the favor.","Jiang Huai: \"...\" He looked at the food box in his hand. \"I misunderstood.\"","Seeing a hint of disappointment between his brows, the Eldest Princess snatched the food box. \"She's had an upset stomach these past few days and can't eat greasy food. I'll accept it on her behalf. Perfect timing, I feel like having some too!\"","Jiang Huai's eyes brightened again, filled with a smiling light.","The Eldest Princess felt uncomfortable under his gaze. \"Let's go over there!\"","They found a pavilion to sit in. Naturally, someone brought bowls and chopsticks.","Zhu Yi helped dismantle the roast chicken, then withdrew with the others, leaving the two space to talk.","The Eldest Princess took a bite. It was the same flavor as before. It tasted delicious at first, but gradually she began to feel something was off.","She put down her chopsticks, her face slightly flushed. \"Why do you keep staring at me?\"","Jiang Huai's eyes held a smile. \"Your Highness enjoys it so much.\"","\"They say 'beauty is a feast for the eyes.' Do you find me more appealing, or this roast chicken?\" Before Jiang Huai could answer, the Eldest Princess felt she had asked a silly question and her face grew even redder. \"Never mind, don't answer that.\"","But Jiang Huai answered seriously, \"Your Highness is very beautiful.\" Surpassing all things in this world.","The Eldest Princess stared at him, stunned. After a long while, she said softly, \"Jiang Huai, Father is going to select a consort for me.\"","Jiang Huai's breathing instantly grew rapid. Under the stone table, his fists clenched tightly, yet his gaze dimmed. Given the Jiang family's current status and his own background, he was unworthy of the Yong'an Princess.","Jiang Huai forced a smile. \"The candidate His Majesty selects for the princess will surely be the finest talent in the world.\"","The Eldest Princess said, \"My late mother once told me that I am the most unfettered person in this world. My future husband need not be chosen for his family lineage, his abilities, or his appearance, but solely according to my own heart's desire.\"","Jiang Huai's heart leapt into his throat.","However, the Eldest Princess's words suddenly took a turn. \"Jiang Huai, what kind of person do you think I am?\"","Jiang Huai did not hesitate. \"Your Highness is both the most exquisite peony in the world and a female eagle soaring across the vast sky.\" As dazzling as the sun and moon, yet as free as the gentle breeze—that was why he couldn't help but follow her with his eyes, and also why he felt unworthy in comparison.","The Eldest Princess extended her hand. Her fair skin was not delicate; her palms, the space between her thumb and forefinger, and her fingertips were all calloused. Some calluses came from practicing the zither, some from drawing the bow, and others from wielding a spear.","Looking at those hands, Jiang Huai's eyes held heartache, admiration, appreciation, and pride.","As the Crown Prince's study companion, he had many opportunities to see the Eldest Princess and naturally knew how diligently she pursued the things she loved.","The Eldest Princess declared, \"Next year, I will ask my royal father to send me to the Red Tassel Guard. I will spare no effort to become a general of the Red Tassel Guard.\"","\"Jiang Huai, five years. If after five years, my feelings remain unchanged, and your feelings remain unchanged, I will choose you to be my consort.\"","The Eldest Princess waited for Jiang Huai's reaction.","She saw clear delight and excitement flash across his face, but then he fell into deep thought.","The Eldest Princess suddenly felt anxious. Could it be that Jiang Huai was unwilling to wait even five years? That would truly disappoint her...","Noticing her change in expression, Jiang Huai hurriedly explained, \"I was just thinking... the Red Tassel Guard is near the Tiger Warrior Camp. But the recruitment period has already passed. I need to figure out who to approach to get into the Tiger Warrior Camp...\"","\"You're going to the Tiger Warrior Camp?\" The Eldest Princess raised an eyebrow. Jiang Huai was a scholar. Although he had studied martial arts for several years, his skills were average—he wasn't even a match for her.","Jiang Huai nodded. \"I naturally want to be closer to you.\"","His gaze was so intense that the Eldest Princess felt her face begin to burn.","She stood up and walked towards the edge of the pavilion. \"Feel like going for a gallop?\"","Jiang Huai replied, \"Yes!\"","Zhu Yi watched the golden couple from afar, covering her mouth to hide a smile.","Then, a touch of worry crept in. If the Eldest Princess truly joined the Red Tassel Guard, she would have to endure many hardships. Later, she must go to the Palace of Eternal Spring to beg Consort Hui to prepare more hand salves and sun-protecting ointments.","Hmm, it was best to start preparing right away!"]},{"number":128,"title":"Chapter 128: Extra Story 04","paragraphs":["In front of the Qi residence in Jiangning, a carriage slowly came to a halt.","Qi Caishang, clad in official robes, stepped down from the carriage, followed by another man.","Though past fifty, Qi Caishang did not have a single white hair, still presenting the elegant demeanor of a scholar. At this moment, however, this \"scholar's\" steps were unsteady, and his gaze somewhat unfocused.","\"Magistrate Liu, no need to see me off, no need! I'm... hic... already at my own doorstep. No need to escort me further!\"","Qi Caishang ushered Magistrate Liu towards the carriage and instructed a servant, \"You, make sure to see Magistrate Liu safely home! If... if anything happens to him, I... I won't let you off!\"","Magistrate Liu wore an obsequious smile. \"Lord Qi, your esteemed presence today brought immense honor to my humble abode. With the Imperial entourage about to arrive in Jiangning, we are all rather anxious. When the time comes, we sincerely hope you will put in a good word for us before His Majesty!\"","This Magistrate Liu was the Prefect of Jiangning. A very shrewd man, his administrative record was neither remarkable nor flawed. However, as Jiangning was inherently prosperous, even his lack of major accomplishments made his tenure appear respectable. Having served as Prefect for five years, barring any unforeseen circumstances, he would either be laterally transferred to another prefecture next year or promoted to the capital.","But then, an unforeseen circumstance did arrive.","The Emperor had suddenly decreed an imperial tour, and Jiangning was on the designated route. From the moment he received the news, Magistrate Liu had been on tenterhooks, fearing that any misstep in hosting the Emperor or incurring His Majesty's displeasure would ruin his chance for promotion!","After much deliberation, Magistrate Liu recalled that the eldest daughter of Provincial Inspector Qi Caishang, who had arrived two years prior, was none other than Consort Hui in the palace. If he could win over Lord Qi, then when the Emperor arrived, even if issues arose, he would have Lord Qi to support him from the sidelines.","Thus, today, Magistrate Liu had specially hosted a banquet at his residence, inviting Qi Caishang as the guest of honor. All the officials, big and small, in Jiangning attended. During the feast, they toasted Qi Caishang one after another, and he felt he had heard a lifetime's worth of flattery in a single sitting.","Now, faced with Magistrate Liu's reminder, Qi Caishang still played the part of the drunkard. \"Hmph, quickly now, off you go home, home!\"","Only then did Magistrate Liu board the carriage, still saying as he went, \"No need to see me off, no need! You there, quickly support your master, don't let him fall!\"","As the carriage clip-clopped away, Qi Caishang, who had been leaning on his servant, straightened up instantly. The haze cleared from his eyes. He sniffed his damp sleeve, then exhaled a breath, frowning. \"My wife is going to lecture me again.\"","He then spat in the direction the carriage had gone. \"Trying to get me to put in a good word by forcing drink on me? I'll put in a good word for a cudgel!\"","The servant beside him seemed accustomed to his master's two-faced nature—the gentleman in public and the rascal in private. Suppressing his inner exasperation, he said, \"Master, you should hurry back inside. The mistress has been waiting for you all day!\"","\"Wasn't I busy? Always nagging, nagging, that's all she knows!\" Despite his words, Qi Caishang quickened his pace.","He knew perfectly well what Mrs. Wan was anxious about. With the Imperial entourage soon arriving in Jiangning, Mrs. Wan was hoping to see Yu'er. Since his appointment as Provincial Inspector of Jiangning and her accompanying him here, mother and daughter hadn't seen each other for two years.","But this foolish woman—Yu'er was an imperial consort. How could it be so easy to see her? Especially outside the palace.","Yet, Qi Caishang himself was itching with the same desire. In previous years, Mrs. Wan could still enter the palace during festivals, but he himself hadn't laid eyes on his daughter in over a decade. He always had to wait for Mrs. Wan to return home and tell him how their daughter was doing, how lively and lovely the Third Princess was.","Qi Caishang was filled with nothing but envy.","Jiangning had no imperial traveling palace. This imperial tour had been decreed and launched with such haste that local officials had no time to construct one. However, Jiangning was the former fiefdom of a prince, and there was a princely mansion here. When the Imperial entourage arrived, they would lodge at this mansion.","Since it was a princely mansion, the restrictions probably wouldn't be as strict as in the palace... right?","Lost in these thoughts, he entered the residence. Mrs. Wan was waiting in the courtyard.","As he approached, she caught the smell of alcohol on him. Covering her nose with a handkerchief, she looked at him with disgust. \"How much did you drink? You reek!\"","\"Heh heh,\" Qi Caishang laughed. \"Magistrate Liu and the others invited me to a banquet. How could I refuse?\"","Mentioning this reminded Mrs. Wan of the gifts delivered to the residence today, filling her with unease. \"All those things sent over today, several cartloads... should we really accept them? I haven't had them logged or stored in the warehouse yet. Should I have them returned tomorrow?\"","\"No need! I went through all that trouble dealing with those people. If you return the gifts, they'll just get even more anxious. Don't worry, I have a plan regarding this matter.\"","\"If you say so.\" When it came to important matters, Mrs. Wan trusted Qi Caishang's judgment.","Mrs. Wan then asked, \"When exactly will the Imperial entourage arrive? Is it confirmed they'll stay at the princely mansion? Will Yu'er have a chance to come out? Or could I go to the mansion to see her then?\"","\"I've been preparing so many things lately—several chests of fabric alone, all Suzhou embroidery, for both Yu'er and the Third Princess. The materials and patterns are of the finest quality. I've also collected some novel trinkets; Yu'er is sure to like them...\"","As Mrs. Wan chattered on, Qi Caishang teased her, \"You only prepared things for your eldest daughter? What about our son and younger daughter?\"","Mrs. Wan glared at him. \"Haven't I prepared plenty for them every year? Last year, Qinglong even came to Jiangning with her child and stayed for a while. It's only my Yu'er... in the blink of an eye, another two years without seeing her. I wonder if the child has grown thin again...\"","As she spoke, Mrs. Wan's eyes reddened.","The Qi family was no longer the destitute household of the past. Not to mention that Qi Daiyu was now the illustrious Consort Hui, Qi Caishang himself held a second-rank official position. People came to curry favor at the Qi residence in an endless stream. As the matriarch, Mrs. Wan naturally basked in this reflected glory. With children and grandchildren around her knees, her life was truly comfortable. Yet, if there was any regret in her heart, it was surely for her eldest daughter.","A mother's heart aches for her daughter. Everyone saw only Consort Hui's splendor, but Mrs. Wan understood the principle that accompanying a ruler was like accompanying a tiger. Sometimes she would wake from sleep in the middle of the night, terrified that her daughter might have said the wrong thing or made a misstep in the palace, incurring the Emperor's displeasure and suffering as a result.","To this day, she regretted not having arranged a marriage for Yu'er earlier. Then Yu'er wouldn't have had to enter the palace.","They wouldn't be separated by flesh and blood, finding it so difficult to even meet.","\"You, you're talking nonsense again,\" Qi Caishang said helplessly. \"How do you know that Yu'er would have definitely lived a good life if she hadn't entered the palace? Think about it, with the lowly official post I held back then, what kind of good husband could I have found for Yu'er? Marrying her into a low-ranking family would have meant a life of hardship, and Yu'er's frail health couldn't have endured manual labor. As for a high-ranking family, it's almost certain they would have looked down on our family and treated Yu'er with contempt.\"","Qi Caishang was also at a loss. Their family had humble origins, peasants for generations, with him being the only scholar produced after several. He managed to pass the imperial examinations, becoming a low-ranking official, but the meager salary wasn't enough for the whole family to live comfortably. In fact, in earlier years, Qi Caishang hadn't even aspired to advance, content with an ordinary life.","It was only later, spurred by his elderly father's serious illness and lack of money for treatment, along with worries about his eldest daughter's situation in the palace, that Qi Caishang began to scheme for a better future.","In recent years, from Qi Daiyu's perspective, Qi Caishang had become a master of relentless striving.","Not only did Qi Caishang drive himself hard, but he was also perceptive of people's hearts, skilled at social maneuvering, and possessed the dignified appearance of a scholarly gentleman. In official circles, he widely befriended court ministers, and before the emperor, he could display absolute loyalty.","For a farmer's son to become a court official, Qi Caishang was undoubtedly capable. It was precisely because of this that within nine years, he rose from a Vice Director in the Waterways Bureau to Left Vice Minister of the Ministry of Works, and two years ago was appointed as the Governor of Jiangning, showing the emperor's high regard for him.","Qi Caishang didn't just push himself; he also spurred on his son, Qi Chuchu.","In his early years, Qi Chuchu followed his father-in-law, General Lang, to the border regions. There, he captured a spy from Beili and was promoted to Loyalty-Displaying Commandant. Later, during the war with Beili, Qi Chuchu also achieved numerous military merits, even killing an important enemy commander at the cost of losing an arm.","After Zhaoguo's great victory, rewards were distributed based on merit. Qi Chuchu was appointed a fourth-rank Illustrious Might General and now serves as the Deputy Commander of the Tiger Guard Camp near the capital, training soldiers.","Then there was his son-in-law, Zhou Yue. Zhou Yue wasn't from the capital, but as the youngest son of the Zhou family, he wasn't required to inherit the family business and thus stayed in the capital. Before Qi Chuchu returned to the capital, Zhou Yue and Qinglong lived with the Qi family for many years, becoming no different from a real son.","Qi Caishang taught Zhou Yue many skills for dealing with people and the world. Zhou Yue himself was a military officer and benefited from the emperor's current favor towards military officials, making his official career exceptionally smooth. He is now the Commander of the Capital Gendarmerie.","One could say the Qi family's fortunes were improving steadily. Yet, it was precisely this that made the couple feel increasingly that they had wronged their eldest daughter.","Because of this, in recent years, Qi Caishang had become even more intensely focused on social climbing and scheming. He wanted to become a high official, one so indispensable that even the emperor couldn't do without him. That way, if only for his sake, the emperor wouldn't let Yu'er suffer.","Qi Caishang sighed. \"At worst, when the Imperial entourage arrives, I'll plead with His Majesty. At the very least, to let you see Yu'er once.\"","Hearing this, Mrs. Wan immediately brightened up. \"Then I'll go check if there's anything else we need to add!\"","With that, she headed towards the storeroom, loudly instructing the maids to bring the inventory ledger to select more fine items.","\"Add what? Being able to see her once is already incredible, and you still want to send gifts!\" Qi Caishang said, but a smile appeared on his face.","On the twenty-sixth day of the tenth month, the banks of the river in Jiangning were packed with commoners. Soldiers from the garrison and the city defense troops were responsible for maintaining order, but the people's enthusiasm was so great that it still caused a few disturbances.","On the dock, Qi Caishang stood at the forefront of the Jiangning officials, occasionally hearing the exasperated voice of Prefect Liu.","Finally, the silhouette of large ships appeared in the distance on the river, and the people craned their necks in anticipation.","A magnificent and grand fleet sailed into view. The first three ships carried the imperial guard. The fourth was the Dragon Boat. This vessel was a behemoth, resplendent and magnificent, exuding imperial grandeur.","\"Long live the Emperor! Long live, long live, long live!\"","\"Long live the Emperor! Long live, long live, long live!\"","No one knew who started it, but the commoners knelt down one after another, shouting excitedly.","So, when Qi Daiyu stepped out of the cabin, this was the scene that greeted her: tens of thousands of people kneeling on the ground.","Qi Daiyu: \"...\"","She felt a bit panicked. Would this shorten her lifespan?"]},{"number":129,"title":"Chapter 129: Extra Story 05","paragraphs":["The Prince's Mansion in Jiangning naturally could not compare to the imperial palace, but its architectural style was more suited to the Jiangnan region, possessing a unique charm of its own.","Eunuchs had arrived earlier to prepare the place, so upon Qi Daiyu and the others' arrival in Jiangning, they could move in directly. Due to limited space, most imperial consorts shared courtyards, typically one high-ranking consort with two or three lower-ranking ones.","Sharing a courtyard with Qi Daiyu were Feng Qi and Fan Ningyan. Both were familiar to her and on good terms, making for a peaceful coexistence.","The princes and princesses resided in the front courtyards. This was the first time Siyu had lived apart from Qi Daiyu. Far from being sad, she was extremely excited, prompting Qi Daiyu to tap her forehead and call her a \"heartless little thing.\"","Siyu hugged Qi Daiyu's arm, cooing, \"I heard my maternal grandparents are right here in Jiangning. I begged Eldest Sister to take me out, so I can visit them on your behalf, Mother!\"","Hearing this, Qi Daiyu felt a stir in her heart. \"Siyu, would you like to visit your uncle?\"","Siyu tilted her head. \"Eldest Uncle is with the entourage, haven't I seen him already on the journey?\" The Emperor was touring, so officers from the Tiger Guard and Imperial Forest Guard were mobilized, including Qi Chuchu. Thus, Siyu had already seen Qi Chuchu during the earlier part of the trip.","Qi Daiyu shook her head. \"It's your uncle from the Qin family, your birth mother's brother.\"","Qi Daiyu had never hidden Qin Saizhu's existence from Siyu. She would even tell Siyu stories about Qin Saizhu from time to time. Every year, on Qin Saizhu's birthday and death anniversary, she would take Siyu to the Qixiang Palace to remember her.","Qin Saizhu's maiden family was in Sichuan, but Qi Daiyu had heard that her younger brother had been appointed a few years prior as the Assistant Prefect of Anzhou, under Jiangning's jurisdiction. Since the Emperor's tour had reached Jiangning, all officials, big and small, were now in the prefectural city, so Qin Lian should be there too.","Siyu blinked. All her impressions of her birth mother came from Qi Daiyu's stories. Admittedly, she felt immense gratitude towards her birth mother and was often curious about her appearance, but she truly held no particular feelings for the Qin family or that Qin uncle.","However, seeing the expectant look on Qi Daiyu's face, Siyu grinned, revealing dimples on her cheeks just like Qin Saizhu's. \"Then tomorrow, I'll first visit my maternal grandparents, and then go see Uncle Qin!\"","Qi Daiyu smiled too. \"Good.\"","Meanwhile, in the mansion's study, Qi Caishang, in full official attire, knelt properly on the ground, reporting to Jiang Yuan on the state of Jiangning's officials and the people's livelihood.","Jiang Yuan was looking down at the lengthy memorial he had written. Seizing the opportunity, Qi Caishang secretly studied the Emperor.","Tsk, even after all these years, he still wasn't used to having the Emperor as a son-in-law... well, not exactly a son-in-law either. Strictly speaking, his daughter was only the Emperor's consort.","Thinking this, Qi Caishang felt even more discontent and his scrutiny of Jiang Yuan grew more critical.","His posture was imposing, his grip on the brush firm. Having personally been on the battlefield, his physical foundation was good, not the frail, weak type of a sickly person.","He had grown a beard, adding to his imperial majesty, but the dark circles under his eyes spoke of chronic fatigue. Combined with the wrinkles that inevitably came with age, his looks had diminished somewhat. He's not even as good-looking as I am, and I'm already fifty-six! Qi Caishang thought rather darkly.","If he weren't the Emperor, if he weren't the Emperor... he might not even be worthy of his Daiyu. He comforted himself: Strictly speaking, the Emperor isn't really Daiyu's husband either. So what is he? A kept man?","Qi Caishang was startled by his own thought, then chuckled inwardly at his own audacity. After all, he was only thinking it.","Although Qi Caishang thought this way, it didn't mean he lacked respect for the Emperor. If he were evaluating him as an emperor—who was he to evaluate the emperor? But from the perspective of evaluating a son-in-law, in Qi Caishang's heart, Jiang Yuan as a \"son-in-law\" couldn't hold a candle to Zhou Yue at all.","Zhou Yue was so good! Willing to strive, filial, and treated his Qinglong well. He had only Qinglong as his principal wife, no messy concubines or maidservants. Now that was a good son-in-law!","Jiang Yuan finished reading the memorial and looked up, catching the complex expression on Qi Caishang's face. Puzzled, he said, \"Minister Qi?\"","Qi Caishang snapped back to attention, assuming a solemn expression. \"Your Majesty.\"","Jiang Yuan put down the memorial with a smile. \"On Our journey south, everything We have seen matches what is written in your memorial. The people live and work in peace, the fields are full of harvest signs. You have not spoken falsely.\"","Provincial Governors were the Emperor's trusted ministers, acting as his eyes and ears. But governors were also officials, also human. There had been cases of governors being bribed and corrupted by local officials, falsifying reports.","Jiang Yuan's \"surprise inspection\" this time was precisely to guard against Qi Caishang deceiving him in the memorial. The tour was a sudden decision, leaving almost no time for preparation before departure. With such tight timing, local officials had little chance to fabricate anything.","Therefore, at least fifty or sixty percent of what he had seen along the way was genuine. And even fifty or sixty percent was excellent.","For an emperor, nothing brought greater satisfaction than seeing the people under his rule well-fed and well-clothed.","Seeing the Emperor's satisfied expression, the shrewd Qi Caishang immediately flattered, \"This is all due to Your Majesty's diligent governance. Your Majesty is most wise!\"","Flattery was always pleasant to hear. Jiang Yuan's smile widened.","\"For your service as Governor of Jiangning, your contribution is not small. Well then, is there anything you wish to request? As long as it is not excessive, it can be granted.\"","Qi Caishang's eyes lit up. He actually did have something!","But he couldn't just say it directly.","So he hesitated for a long while, putting on an expression of great reluctance yet feeling compelled to speak. \"Your Majesty, this subject does indeed have an impertinent request. Ever since learning the imperial carriage would reach Jiangning, the people have been overjoyed. Officials like Minister Liu were especially delighted and specifically built a 'Garden of Integrity and Loyalty' in the southern suburbs, humbly requesting Your Majesty to grace it with a visit.\"","Garden of Integrity and Loyalty? The intention behind the name was plain to see.","Flattery from local officials was nothing strange. What Jiang Yuan cared about was something else. He raised an eyebrow. \"Minister Qi, are you seeking merit on behalf of Minister Liu and the others?\"","Qi Caishang then gave a bitter smile, pulling out another memorial from his robe and presenting it. \"This subject would feel uneasy not speaking of it!\"","Jiang Yuan opened the memorial, his smile growing even wider. \"Are these all the gifts you've received?\"","Indeed, the memorial listed all the various gifts Qi Caishang had received over the years.","Qi Caishang: \"Your Majesty trusted this subject to appoint me as Governor of Jiangning. Even back in the capital, I knew: being an official is difficult; being a good official is even harder. These past two years, I have truly been trembling with fear, unable to sleep at night. But water that is too clear has no fish. If I had arrogantly refused all these things, it would have been too difficult to integrate into the local official circles. Helplessly, I had no choice but to accept these items.\"","\"However, this subject dared not use them privately. I ordered my wife to store them all safely and register them in this ledger. Your Majesty, everything I have received in these two years is listed in this register. Your Majesty need only send someone to my residence to inspect and collect them.\"","Jiang Yuan, however, waved his hand. \"Since it was given to you, you should keep it. As you said, 'water too clear breeds no fish.' I still need you to continue being my eyes and ears here in Jiangning.\" As he spoke, he lowered his head to examine the items listed in the booklet.","Truly a place of wealth and luxury. Some of these items were no worse than those used in the palace. The officials of Jiangning truly had audacious courage! A cold glint flashed in Jiang Yuan's eyes.","Hearing the Emperor instruct him to keep the items, Qi Caishang inwardly rejoiced. Just as he expected! If the Emperor hadn't known about these things, it would have been a grave crime of corruption. But by reporting them proactively to the Emperor, given His Majesty's broad-mindedness and vision, he would naturally look down upon such trifles!","He would only tell him to keep them.","And now that these items had passed under the Emperor's gaze, he could use them with complete peace of mind.","\"Your humble servant thanks Your Majesty for the generous gifts,\" he said, framing it all as imperial bestowals.","Jiang Yuan had already formed his own thoughts on the matter and set it aside. He then asked Qi Caishang, \"This hardly counts as a reward. Is there anything else you wish to request?\"","The moment was ripe. Qi Caishang chuckled, nearly revealing his true nature. \"Your Majesty, if there is one thing your servant truly wishes to request, there is indeed a matter. When your servant came to Jiangning two years ago, my elderly mother and wife followed me here. Now, my mother is advanced in years, and her health is declining. Her only wish is to see her grandchildren one more time. I have one son and two daughters. Seeing my eldest son and youngest daughter is not difficult, but my eldest daughter... that is, Consort Hui... is exceedingly hard to meet.\"","\"Your Majesty, I earnestly beseech you, in consideration of my mother's loving heart, to grant Consort Hui the honor of a provincial family visit. Perhaps... this may be the last chance for grandmother and granddaughter to see each other in this lifetime.\"","As Qi Caishang spoke, his eyes reddened. His words were extremely earnest, presenting the very picture of a filial son.","Jiang Yuan hadn't expected Qi Caishang's request to be this.","He hesitated.","Qi Caishang was a minister he valued, and Qi Daiyu was his beloved Consort Hui. If they were in the capital, allowing Consort Hui a family visit would be nothing.","But now they were outside the palace. The Qi residence in Jiangning could hardly be considered the proper family home. Allowing Consort Hui to visit...","But soon, Jiang Yuan thought of the Empress Dowager.","These past few years, the Empress Dowager's health had also been failing. Sometimes, in her drowsy moments, she would often murmur about his sister, whom fate had taken. Jiang Yuan thought that perhaps in old age, people always yearn for family reunions. He could somewhat understand Qi Caishang's sentiment.","Thus, he said, \"I will have the Crown Prince and General Mingwei escort Consort Hui for the provincial visit.\" He paused briefly, then added, \"And the Third Princess as well.\"","The Crown Prince, as the eldest son, was now thirteen and capable enough to be of use. With her own brother, Qi Chuchu, providing escort, Consort Hui's visit should be without incident.","As for why he included Siyu, Jiang Yuan felt that even if he didn't issue the edict, Siyu would surely pester him until he did. He might as well save himself the trouble and order it now.","He had actually succeeded!","Qi Caishang immediately knelt and kowtowed again. \"Your Majesty's gracious kindness! Your Majesty's gracious kindness!\" This kneel was filled with genuine sincerity.","As for the matter of the provincial visit, Qi Daiyu only learned about it after Siyu had already returned from her outing.","At that time, Siyu was sharing her experience with her. \"Grandmother was so happy to see me! She made all sorts of delicious pastries for me to eat. My stomach was practically stuffed full!\"","\"Uncle Qin was very different from what I imagined, but he was very kind to me too. When I left, he gave me lots of chili peppers. He said they could be used to make hot pot base, that my mother loved the hometown-style hot pot seasoning the most. Mother, shall we try it sometime?\"","Qi Daiyu smiled and said, \"Alright.\"","Then, Quan Fuhai arrived with the news of the provincial visit.","The teacup in Qi Daiyu's hand immediately fell to the floor.","Provincial... visit?","To be honest, the thought of reuniting with Mrs. Wan and the old lady again made her quite happy. But previous meetings had always been within the palace, constrained by palace regulations and worries about too many eyes and ears and walls having ears. Their conversations had never delved too deep, and the exchange of emotions remained somewhat superficial.","But a provincial visit... that would truly be returning to her maiden home.","For no particular reason, Qi Daiyu suddenly began to feel nervous."]},{"number":130,"title":"Chapter 130: Extra Story 06","paragraphs":["That morning, Qi Daiyu surprisingly did not sleep in—ever since morning greetings were no longer required, she hadn't gotten up early a single day except for important holidays.","In fact, she wasn't just awake; she hadn't slept at all last night.","She had suffered from insomnia.","The feeling was strange. Clearly, she was already familiar with Mrs. Wan and the Old Dowager. Clearly, she could now normally address Mrs. Wan as \"Mother.\" Yet, the thought of returning to the Qi Residence still made her nervous, utterly unable to sleep.","Sighing, Qi Daiyu simply got up.","In the outer chamber, Lizhi heard the movement and came in. \"Your Highness?\"","\"Let's wash up,\" Qi Daiyu said.","Thus, half the courtyard sprang into activity—some carrying water, others fetching the morning meal.","Qi Daiyu rinsed her mouth and washed her face, letting Dongzao do her hair. When it came time to choose jewelry, despite a box full of dazzling ornaments, Qi Daiyu felt none were suitable.","The palace maids exchanged glances. Her Highness seemed a bit odd today.","Finally, after her hair and makeup were done, she faced the dilemma of choosing clothes.","Beautiful garments were laid out one by one, but Qi Daiyu only shook her head.","In the end, it was Yanhe who suggested, \"This servant remembers that a few years ago, Madam Qi sent a bolt of crimson brocade into the palace. It was made into a wide-sleeved gown, which was also brought along this time. Would Your Highness like to try it on?\"","\"Mm.\"","Once she put it on, Qi Daiyu immediately felt it was right. She had many clothes, and this wide-sleeved gown had only been worn once. It still looked as good as new. With her delicate, cool beauty, the vibrant crimson did not clash but rather resembled a touch of vermilion blending into pure white snow, lending the snow itself a hint of radiant glow.","Yanhe knelt to adjust Qi Daiyu's skirt, asking with a smile, \"Is Your Highness perhaps feeling... apprehensive about returning home?\"","Qi Daiyu was taken aback. Apprehensive about returning home? Her current state of mind did indeed have that flavor.","After the noon meal, the edict permitting the journey finally arrived from the Emperor.","Surrounded by a crowd of attendants, Qi Daiyu, along with Siyu, exited through the main gate of the princely residence and boarded the carriage.","The entire procession for the home visit was magnificent.","Guards cleared the way, followed by eight eunuchs holding plaques that read \"Make Way, Do Not Gaze,\" and eight palace maids carrying lanterns and scattering flower petals. Behind them was the Green Phoenix Carriage, befitting the consort rank.","The interior of the carriage was spacious, equipped with a tea table, a low couch, and other necessities, even including a separate partitioned space for answering nature's call.","Behind the Green Phoenix Carriage were twelve more carriages, all laden with gifts bestowed by the Emperor for the Qi family. Twelve carriages were also the maximum for the consort rank; the Empress's procession would have sixteen.","Such a spectacle had already drawn many commoners to watch. They dared not make noise, only using their eyes to express their inner excitement. Many children couldn't help but point at the guards, then look back at their parents.","The Emperor had specifically assigned Qi Chuchu to escort them. Naturally, Qi Chuchu wouldn't miss the chance to boost his sister's prestige. He directly deployed his subordinates from the Tiger Guard Battalion as the escort. Each elite soldier from the Tiger Guard was burly and imposing, and sitting atop their horses, the effect was incredibly imposing!","No wonder they captivated the children.","But the most eye-catching was at the front of the procession: the Eldest Prince, seated on a white horse.","The Eldest Prince was stoutly built. To support his weight, the white steed beneath him was also a carefully selected, robust horse. Already tall, the Eldest Prince on horseback truly stood out from the crowd.","To show off his might, the Eldest Prince had specially strapped a spear to his back today.","His physique and bearing, seen from a distance, made him look exactly like a general returning victorious from battle.","Only, this general's face looked a bit too youthful.","Unaware of the commoners' inner doubts, the Eldest Prince was feeling quite pleased with himself.","Ever since his Imperial Father entrusted him with escorting Consort Hui for her home visit, he had been discussing with the Crown Prince and the Third Prince how to casually display his own awe-inspiring majesty. It had taken considerable effort to come up with this image.","Heh heh, they must all be utterly intimidated by this Prince, right? the Eldest Prince thought smugly.","\"Big Brother must be feeling so smug right now!\" Siyu used a term she learned from Qi Daiyu. \"It must have been Second Brother who coaxed him into it. He doesn't even consider how his build makes that spear on his back look like a short stick—not imposing at all! Mother, don't you think so?\"","Siyu received no response and turned curiously. \"Mother?\"","Only then did Qi Daiyu snap back to attention. \"Hmm?\" She hadn't been listening to Siyu at all.","\"What's wrong with you? You've been off since early morning...\" Siyu's words suddenly halted as she looked toward the screen partitioning off the chamber pot area at the back of the carriage.","Qi Daiyu followed her gaze. Beneath that screen, a pair of red embroidered shoes was visible.","It should have been a frightening scene, but Qi Daiyu revealed a helpless smile. \"Eldest Princess?\"","The next moment, a head peeked out from behind the screen. It was indeed the Eldest Princess.","\"Elder Sister! How are you on the carriage?\" Siyu laughed in delight.","The Eldest Princess unceremoniously sat down beside Siyu. \"You'll be away for several days. I'd be so bored all alone! I don't care, I'm coming to the Qi Residence too!\"","She looked pleadingly at Qi Daiyu.","Qi Daiyu hesitated. \"Wouldn't this be against protocol...\" Siyu could accompany her because Siyu was registered under her name. Legally, Siyu was her daughter, going to the Qi family to visit her maternal grandparents. If the Eldest Princess also went to the Qi Residence, it wouldn't be a home visit but an imperial inspection. The Qi family would have to drop everything to receive Her Highness, the Eldest Princess.","\"That's why I sneaked onto the carriage! We can just say I'm a little palace maid attending to you, Consort Hui!\"","Qi Daiyu: \"...\"","The Qi family weren't fools. Besides, the Eldest Princess's demeanor and attire clearly marked her as no ordinary person.","Eldest Princess: \"The commoners don't need to know! Consort Hui, don't worry, I've already told Imperial Father!\" Although it was via a note sent by Zhuyi, and she hadn't received a reply yet.","\"He agreed!\" No reply counted as agreement, right?","Qi Daiyu: \"...Very well.\"","Ever since the Eldest Princess resolved to join the Red Tassel Guard next year, the Emperor had been practically spoiling her rotten lately. He wouldn't get angry over such a small matter.","The procession began to move slowly. The princely residence wasn't far from the Qi Residence, just a journey through two main streets.","And these two streets were lined with commoners.","A consort's home visit was a rare sight, a spectacle usually only seen by the capital's residents. Now they in Jiangning could witness it too! Thus, every household came out to watch the excitement, eager to see how beautiful a palace consort truly was—were they really like celestial maidens descending to earth, as the operas said?","Inevitably, the commoners found it difficult to catch a glimpse of Qi Daiyu's true appearance, not just because of the distance. The palace maids and eunuchs shielded her completely. Qi Daiyu was like a precious, delicate golden canary, protected by the cage of protocol.","In contrast, the Eldest Princess and Siyu had much more freedom, observing the Qi family with natural and poised grace.","\"Your subject (Your subject's wife) pays respects to Consort Hui!\" Qi Caishang led the assembled family members in kneeling and bowing.","Qi Daiyu did not reach out to help him up. This was a necessary part of the protocol. If Qi Caishang didn't perform it, the censors would surely submit a memorial impeaching him the very next day.","But watching the white-haired old lady also kneel before her, Qi Daiyu's eyes reddened. She couldn't help but think of a famous scene from a classic novel she had read in her past life.","So, this was how it felt.","\"Rise,\" Qi Daiyu said, forcefully suppressing the emotions within her.","Next, a eunuch began to read the imperial edict and congratulatory address, a process that took a full quarter of an hour before the main formalities were finally completed.","At this point, everyone except the guard detachment could return. The guards would surround and protect the Qi residence until the provincial family visit concluded and Qi Daiyu returned to the Prince's mansion.","Of course, the eunuchs and palace maids attending to Qi Daiyu were still to follow her.","Thus, Qi Daiyu finally stepped into the Qi family home.","Upon reaching the main hall, it was now her turn to pay respects to the old lady, Qi Caishang, and Mrs. Wan.","She had no psychological burden about it and was just about to kneel when a pair of large hands stopped her.","Looking up, it was Qi Caishang.","Over the years, the letters exchanged between Qi Daiyu and Qi Caishang, if stacked, would be taller than the Eldest Prince. Yet, their actual face-to-face meetings had been limited to a few distant glimpses during palace banquets. Speaking this closely was a first.","This was also the first time Qi Daiyu had examined her \"nominal father\" at such close range.","With just one glance, Qi Daiyu was certain the original body's beauty was inherited from Qi Caishang. It wasn't that Mrs. Wan was unattractive; her features were of a dignified, broad type, not quite aligning with the current era's aesthetic preferences.","Qi Caishang's appearance, however, could be praised as \"handsome\" in any era.","Even now, at an age where he could be a grandfather, he not only lacked a single white hair but also had very few wrinkles. Qi Caishang disliked facial hair and thus was clean-shaven, making him look even younger.","Qi Daiyu suddenly recalled a rumor she had heard in Jiangning these past two days: \"In the west city dwells Master Qi, with jade-like countenance and graceful bearing, a gentleman fair ladies seek.\"","This \"Master Qi\"... could it possibly be referring to Qi Caishang?","While Qi Daiyu was observing Qi Caishang, he was also studying her.","His daughter was thin... well, actually, not really.","His daughter's constitution looked frailer... well, actually, it seemed much better than before.","His daughter had grown... even more beautiful than in her childhood.","Heh, truly his daughter.","It was just her temperament... Qi Caishang's heart gave a slight tremble. Compared to before she entered the palace, she had changed far, far too much.","Qi Caishang still vividly remembered the day his eldest daughter entered the palace—her expression, full of grievance and stubbornness, fear and reluctance, like a young fawn, begging for her parents' protection yet also wanting to do something for them.","His Yu'er... Her mother had caught a severe chill while pregnant with her and stubbornly refused medication. She was born safely after a scare, but with a congenital weakness from the womb. The family felt they had wronged this child. Though their means were modest, they raised her as a precious jewel, never letting her do a single chore, not even allowing her to touch cold water. Due to her delicate health, she was hardly allowed outside and had little social interaction, which fostered a timid and sensitive nature. She was especially unable to bear grievance; when wronged, her tears would fall as if the whole world had betrayed her, making one's heart ache so much they'd wish to pluck the moon from the sky to offer her.","Raised this way, apart from her upbringing and manners, she wasn't much different from the young ladies of wealthy households.","And precisely because she was raised so well, her beauty not obscured by labor, she caught the eye of nobility during the selection and was chosen as a Talented Lady for the Crown Prince.","When he learned his eldest daughter had been selected, aside from his reluctance, Qi Caishang initially wasn't overly worried. In his view, his Yu'er was so lovely in appearance, inspiring instant pity; she was born to be cherished. How could the Crown Prince not like her?","Sure enough, once the Emperor ascended the throne, Yu'er was conferred the title of Jieyu! This rank was not low, showing the Emperor must have been quite fond of Yu'er.","Yet, for some reason, the letters sent into the palace stopped receiving replies. And as fewer and fewer messages came out from the palace, the dread in Qi Caishang's heart grew heavier and heavier.","But his official rank was too low, so low that he couldn't even find connections to inquire about his daughter's situation within the palace.","Then, immediately after, Old Master Qi fell gravely ill, and the household's income could no longer cover its expenses.","The old master's illness was critical, and he kept thinking of his granddaughter in the palace. Qi Caishang considered sending another letter; if his eldest daughter could reply with a few words of concern to ease the old master's mind, it would be good.","Who could have known that the letter sent in sank like a stone in a lake.","The night Old Master Qi passed away, he was still murmuring about his granddaughter in the palace.","At that time, Qi Caishang felt a trace of resentment, thinking Yu'er probably saw the family as a burden and looked down on them now.","It took a long time for this feeling to fade.","It wasn't until the incident with Qi Chuchu's former wife occurred, and the family was truly at its wit's end, that Qi Caishang swallowed his pride and wrote to his daughter to borrow money. He might usually be shameless and thick-skinned, always seeking small advantages and benefits, but that was always based on knowing the other party was doing well. He had no clarity at all about Yu'er's circumstances.","Fortunately, that time, Yu'er replied.","With thoughts surging, Qi Caishang looked at this daughter who was both familiar and strange, filled with profound emotion.","Well, of course. After spending so many years in a place like the imperial palace, how could her temperament not change?","But whether she changed or not, what did it matter? She was still his daughter."]},{"number":131,"title":"Chapter 131: Extra Story 07","paragraphs":["\"Alright, you father and daughter, staring at each other like that—what's going on? Do your eyes have no room for the rest of us?\" Mrs. Wan said with a laugh.","Qi Caishang: \"It's just that we haven't seen each other for so many years!\" Of course he had to take a good, long look.","He then cupped his hands towards the Eldest Prince and the Eldest Princess. \"This humble official has been discourteous.\"","In the presence of outsiders, he was always the picture of refined elegance and grace.","The Eldest Princess was very friendly and curious towards Consort Hui's family. She said with a smile, \"It's only natural, bound by kinship, to be overcome with emotion. It's unavoidable. Father Emperor permitted Consort Hui to visit her family to fulfill the reunion of flesh and blood. My coming here privately is somewhat improper. Minister Qi, please do not stand on ceremony regarding our status; simply treat us as ordinary juniors.\"","The Eldest Prince paid even less mind. He was staring unblinkingly at a youth standing beside Qi Caishang.","The youth had dark skin. Judging by his face alone, he wasn't old, and his height wasn't particularly tall either, but his sturdy, robust build was exceptionally noticeable, especially his bulging arms, which looked incredibly strong—clearly someone trained in martial arts.","The Eldest Prince looked at himself, then at the youth, his heart itching with a desire to challenge him to a match to see who was more formidable.","Noticing the Eldest Prince's gaze, Qi Caishang beckoned the youth forward, both to introduce him to the Eldest Prince and to allow Qi Daiyu to recognize him. \"This is Shulüe.\"","Qi Shulüe, son of Qi Chuchu, only ten years old this year.","Qi Shulüe had a sturdy build, but his nature was honest, simple, and somewhat shy. He scratched the back of his head. \"Aunt.\"","As he greeted her, he looked curiously at this aunt he had never met before. Hehe, his aunt was truly beautiful, just like his father said, like a fairy descended to earth.","\"This child is so well-built,\" Qi Daiyu praised sincerely, then looked at the two young girls beside Qi Shulüe. The slightly older one wore a blue dress, gentle and elegant; the younger one in pink was as lovely as jade and snow.","Qi Daiyu's gaze softened. \"These must be Shutao and Yashu?\"","Qi Shutao, Qi Chuchu's eldest daughter, twelve years old this year. Zhou Yashu, Qi Qinglong's daughter, six years old this year.","Qi Daiyu then looked at Lang Tianyu and Qi Qinglong, saying helplessly, \"Sister-in-law, Qinglong, why have you all come?\"","This was really making too grand an occasion of it.","Mrs. Wan: \"You've finally managed to return home. Of course I had to call them all.\" Upon learning the Emperor had approved the family visit, she had hurriedly sent a letter to the capital, asking her daughter-in-law and grandchildren to come. It was a pity Zhou Yue couldn't leave the city without permission, so Qinglong had to bring Yashu alone.","Otherwise, that would have been a true full family gathering!","Qi Caishang: \"Yes, it's right that you should return, so the whole family can gather.\"","\"Alright now, let's not all stand here. Today I've invited the most famous Lanhua Troupe from Jiangning. The stage is already set up. The 'Shuimo' tunes here in Jiangning are different from the opera troupes in the capital—you must listen! Let's go watch the opera and chat as we do!\" Mrs. Wan said.","The old lady chimed in cheerfully, \"Yes, watch the opera, watch the opera!\"","The group then made their way to the garden.","Qi Daiyu took the initiative to support the old lady. Though the old lady was advanced in years and her body was still healthy, her memory was not what it used to be. Sometimes she couldn't even recognize who Qi Caishang was. At first, she let Qi Daiyu support her, but after walking a short while, she no longer recognized her. Mrs. Wan then took over from Qi Daiyu. \"When people get old, it's like this.\"","Qi Daiyu had no choice but to walk alongside Lang Tianyu and Qi Qinglong. The atmosphere among the three was somewhat awkward.","It couldn't be helped; no matter how close the relationship, years of separation always create distance.","Ever since Qi Chuchu returned to the capital, Mrs. Wan had taken Lang Tianyu into the palace a few times. Lang Tianyu, being intelligent and considerate, always made sure to leave ample time for mother and daughter to talk privately. Consequently, Qi Daiyu's relationship with her was polite but not close.","As for Qi Qinglong, before Qi Daiyu entered the palace, Mrs. Wan never took her in. After she married Zhou Yue, she became pregnant not long after and thereafter focused entirely on her child, with even less opportunity to enter the palace. Zhou Yue's official rank wasn't high enough to bring his wife to palace banquets either, so Qi Qinglong and Qi Daiyu had had no contact over these years.","Even though in Qi Qinglong's memory, she and her elder sister had been extremely close before the latter entered the palace, after so many years apart and with the difference in status now, she truly didn't know what to say to her elder sister.","The three awkward individuals could only try their best to find topics of conversation.","The easiest topic was children.","Lang Tianyu looked back and said with a smile, \"The children, however, have become familiar quickly.\"","Qi Daiyu also looked back.","She saw the Eldest Prince had already huddled together with Qi Shulüe, muttering about who knows what.","The Eldest Princess and Siyu were walking with Shutao and Yashu. Siyu already had one arm linked through Shutao's and was holding Yashu's hand with the other.","Lang Tianyu's gaze fell on Siyu. \"I heard from Mother-in-law that the Third Princess visited the family home some days ago and later went to visit Minister Qin. That's when I learned that Consort Zhuang was actually an old friend of mine.\"","Qi Daiyu was surprised. \"Oh?\"","Lang Tianyu smiled wryly. \"When I was still very young, my father once served as Assistant Prefect of Yuzhou. That's when I met Sister Qin. But not many years later, my father was transferred, and our family moved with him to his new post. For the next few years, Sister Qin and I kept in touch through letters, until she told me she was going to the capital, and then we lost contact. Later, I heard she had been assigned to His Majesty, who was then the Crown Prince.\"","Times had changed, and the close childhood friend had embarked on a completely different life path.","She still remembered when she first married Qi Chuchu and saw her mother-in-law worrying about her younger sister-in-law in the palace, Lang Tianyu mentioned she had an old friend also in the palace. At that time, no one knew the person she referred to was Qin Saizhu. Even Lang Tianyu herself wasn't clear about what rank her Sister Qin held in the palace.","It wasn't until a couple of days ago when she came to Jiangning and heard Mrs. Wan mention Qin Lian that she found the name familiar, asked a few more questions, and discovered that the Third Princess's mother, Consort Zhuang, was her former good friend.","After clarifying all this, Lang Tianyu was filled with sighs. During the years she and Qin Saizhu were close, they had even joked that Lang Tianyu should marry Qin Lian directly in the future, so they would become family, and any child Qin Saizhu had would call Lang Tianyu \"Aunt.\"","Who would have thought she would marry Qi Chuchu, Qin Saizhu would pass away after giving birth, the Third Princess would be raised by Qi Daiyu, and now could also call her \"Aunt.\"","Truly, fate plays strange tricks.","After listening, Qi Daiyu fell silent for a long time.","She still couldn't come to terms with Qin Saizhu's death.","Perhaps because Qin Saizhu's death was too sudden, too unexpected; or perhaps because Qin Saizhu was the first friend she made after arriving in this world.","Since her transmigration, Qi Daiyu had gained many friends. Like the Empress, who had helped her greatly—she respected and admired her, a relationship both teacher and friend; like Nie Zhiyu, both were gentle and even-tempered people—she felt at ease and comfortable with her, a bond of sworn sisters; like Consort Li, who possessed advanced ideas and an unrestrained soul—she felt close to and appreciated her, a true soulmate.","But these people's friendships with her were more or less tinged with self-interest.","Only Qin Suzhu was the one genuine heart Qi Daiyu encountered in the deceitful depths of the palace—a heart that sought nothing and asked for no return in kind.","A genuine heart is so rare that every time she remembered that woman with the deep dimples when she smiled, her own heart ached unbearably.","Seeing Qi Daiyu remain silent, Lang Tianyu knew she shouldn't have brought this up and quickly changed the subject. \"I heard today's opera troupe is performing exceptionally well...\"","Qi Qinglong chimed in: \"Yes, especially their 'Little Orchid'...\"","Qi Daiyu, aware of their good intentions, also put on an expectant expression. \"Then I must listen carefully today.\"","As for whether the Orchid Troupe's opera was good or not, Qi Daiyu wasn't very sure.","Because halfway through the performance, she fell asleep.","During intermissions in the opera, Qi Caishang would occasionally glance back at his daughter, only to find Qi Daiyu slumped in her chair with her eyes closed. For a moment, his heart skipped a beat, fearing something had happened to her. Noticing her steady breathing and realizing she was simply asleep, his heart settled back into place.","Mrs. Wan was about to wake Qi Daiyu but was stopped by Qi Caishang.","Qi Caishang mouthed the words: Let her sleep. It's a good chance for us to have a proper look at our daughter. It's been so many years since we've really looked at the child.","Mrs. Wan wanted to say it wasn't appropriate, but in her heart, she felt Qi Caishang had a point. She looked up at the sky; it was midday with the sun shining, so there was no worry about her catching a chill.","So Mrs. Wan stayed silent. The couple, stealthily and as if admiring a priceless treasure, gazed greedily at their daughter's sleeping face.","Qi Daiyu had a dream.","In the dream, her soul seemed to float into mid-air.","The opera was still being performed on stage, but the audience below had changed.","The Eldest Prince, the Eldest Princess, and the others were gone. Only she, Qi Caishang, Mrs. Wan, the Old Lady, Qi Chuchu, and Qi Qinglong remained.","She herself had changed too, no longer adorned in luxurious attire. She wore clothes sewn by Mrs. Wan's own hands, with only a plain silver hairpin in her hair—one bought by Qi Caishang with half a year's worth of saved-up private funds, one for her and one for Qinglong.","The Old Lady listened to the opera cheerfully while picking over mung beans in a winnowing basket. The old woman's eyes weren't good, so occasionally a bad bean slipped through.","Qi Qinglong pestered Qi Chuchu to play cat's cradle. Qi Chuchu, being strong, accidentally snapped the string. Qinglong was so angry she cried, chasing Qi Chuchu all around the courtyard with a broom.","Qi Caishang lounged improperly in a deck chair, fanning himself and critiquing the performers on stage.","Mrs. Wan, who had been mending clothes, got a mouthful of dust stirred up by Qi Chuchu and Qi Qinglong's chase and started grumbling.","And she, covering her mouth with a handkerchief, laughed until she started coughing. Seeing her cough, Qi Chuchu and Qi Qinglong immediately stopped their chase, one pouring her tea and the other patting her back.","When the coughing subsided, she laughed again, collapsing with laughter into Mrs. Wan's arms.","The laughter was so lighthearted.","Then, the whole family laughed.","The opera on stage continued singing.","\"Spring's hues weave crimson dreams, fragrance lies amidst smiling blooms, don't cry, don't cry, father and mother are here to soothe, here to soothe...\"","...","Qi Daiyu stayed at the Qi family home for five days.","Five days was enough for a not-so-familiar family to become familiar.","On the last night, it was even Qi Daiyu, Mrs. Wan, and Qi Qinglong who slept together.","The mother and her two daughters talked late into the night. As Mrs. Wan was drifting off to sleep, she heard Qi Daiyu murmur.","She leaned in to listen.","\"Mama...\"","\"This child!\" Mrs. Wan chuckled. The address \"Mama\" was typically only used in ordinary commoner households; those of slightly higher status called their mothers \"Mother\" or \"Madam.\" In the Qi family, only the children had called her that when they were first learning to talk.","Mrs. Wan thought Qi Daiyu, in her sleep, had reverted to her childhood and used the address from her early years. Mrs. Wan couldn't help but remember how soft and adorable her daughter was as a little girl, and her heart instantly melted.","Mrs. Wan then drew Qi Daiyu closer into her embrace, gently patting her back, just as she did when lulling her to sleep as a child.","\"Mama's here, Mama's right here.\""]},{"number":132,"title":"Chapter 132: Extra Chapter 08","paragraphs":["The joyful days of the home visit passed in a flash.","Since Siyu had left yesterday with the Eldest Princess, on the return journey today, only Qi Daiyu was in the carriage—she had sent Yan He and the others to the carriage behind.","Listlessly, she lounged, scrolling through her \"phone.\"","Opening the trending page, her eyes were met with over a dozen consecutive \"explosive\" tags. It turned out a mega top-tier celebrity had had their reputation collapse, and to such an extent that they were now eating state-provided meals and treading sewing machines.","As luck would have it, Qi Daiyu had followed several of this star's dramas before and was somewhat of a casual fan. She immediately transformed into a gossip enthusiast, delving into the cause and progression of the incident.","After finishing the complete scoop, Qi Daiyu suddenly realized something was off. Why hadn't they arrived at the Prince's mansion yet?","She moved to the window and called out a question. Xiao Li, who had been following alongside the carriage, promptly replied, \"A quarter-hour ago, His Majesty sent someone to fetch Your Ladyship to the Fragrant Garden. This servant informed you, but you didn't respond. This servant thought you had fallen asleep.\"","Qi Daiyu: \"...\" She had been so engrossed in the gossip she hadn't heard Xiao Li at all.","Where was the Fragrant Garden?","It was the Lianzhong Garden built by Prefect Liu and others. The Emperor had indeed graced it with a visit, and after doing so, had changed its name to Fragrant Garden.","During Qi Daiyu's few days at the Qi residence, Jiang Yuan had not had a moment of leisure.","First, he led the Crown Prince on an incognito inspection tour of the counties and villages around Jiangning to secretly investigate the people's livelihood. Then, he reviewed official case records to check for any unjust, false, or wrongly decided cases. In short, during this period, Jiangning's official circles were jittery and filled with apprehension. On the surface, nothing had happened yet, but everyone knew in their hearts that the real reckoning would only begin after the Emperor returned to the palace.","The carriage drove directly into the Fragrant Garden. Qi Daiyu lifted a corner of the curtain to admire the garden scenery. It was still architecture and landscaping steeped in the Jiangnan style. The garden was extremely vast, not inferior to the Prince's mansion. As it was for leisure, it featured mostly various scenic landscapes, with not many buildings.","The carriage stopped in front of a courtyard named \"Falling Moon Lodge.\"","\"Consort Hui, His Majesty is inside.\"","Qi Daiyu alighted from the carriage and walked in, looking around as she went.","This cluster of buildings was constructed by the water, comprising three to five rooms with a long waterside corridor. Reeds were planted along the lake shore, forming a broad, lovely expanse.","Entering the room, Qi Daiyu didn't see Jiang Yuan. Walking further in, she discovered that the wall on the other side, which should have been windows, had been removed and rebuilt into a platform overlooking the water. On the platform were rush cushions and a small table. Jiang Yuan was sitting on one of the cushions, holding a fishing rod.","He was dressed in plain gray cloth clothes, with a straw hat on his head—the full attire of a fisherman.","Seeing him like this for the first time, Qi Daiyu couldn't help but laugh out loud.","Hearing the noise, Jiang Yuan turned his head. Unperturbed, he smiled and asked, \"Well? Does it have the carefree air of 'a jug of wine, a fishing rod'?\"","A jug of wine, a fishing rod, how many in this world are as happy as I?","Qi Daiyu performed a curtsy: \"What brings Your Majesty such fine spirits today?\"","Jiang Yuan: \"Two days ago, I went with Sheng'er to a village called Peach Blossom Village. We met an old fisherman angling alone on the river. I had a mind to emulate him, but I couldn't quite capture the old man's leisurely ease.\" He had been sitting here for an hour without catching a single fish.","With that, Jiang Yuan extended his hand, inviting Qi Daiyu to sit beside him.","Qi Daiyu removed her shoes and, using Jiang Yuan's hand for support, sat on another rush cushion.","The lake water was only inches below the platform; with the movement of the waves, it could even lap onto the platform's surface.","The water looked clear. Tempted, Qi Daiyu reached her hand into the lake, feeling its coolness.","Amusement tinged Jiang Yuan's voice: \"Aren't you afraid of falling in?\"","\"How could I? Your Majesty is here,\" Qi Daiyu replied without turning her head.","Her mood was evidently relaxed and carefree.","Jiang Yuan: \"It seems you were very happy at home? How is your grandmother's health?\"","During her days at the Qi residence, Qi Daiyu had learned how Qi Caishang had managed to request the home visit from the Emperor. Her expression remained normal as she said, \"Her health is passable, but her spirit is not what it used to be. This time when I returned, she almost didn't recognize me.\"","She added, \"I must also thank Your Majesty for your gracious favor, allowing me to return home and reunite with my family.\" As she was genuinely grateful at heart, the smile she directed at Jiang Yuan was especially sweet.","That smile dazzled Jiang Yuan's eyes. Glancing at Qi Daiyu's hand in the water, he set aside his fishing rod and pulled her hand out.","\"The water is too cold. Be careful not to catch a chill.\"","As he spoke, he used a handkerchief to gently dry her hand.","These hands had been exquisitely cared for—pale, delicate, soft and boneless. Jiang Yuan couldn't resist holding and toying with them, pressing the knuckles one by one.","After all these years, Qi Daiyu could now interact with Jiang Yuan without changing expression and could calmly attend to her bedchamber duties. But it was only with these intimate, couple-like details that she still couldn't adapt.","This kind of secretive, ambiguous intimacy shouldn't exist between her and the Emperor.","So, Qi Daiyu grasped Jiang Yuan's hand in return, stopping his kneading motions, her eyes innocent yet mischievous: \"Your Majesty, I'm hungry.\"","She hadn't had lunch yet.","Jiang Yuan smiled helplessly and ordered the meal to be served.","While waiting, Jiang Yuan resumed fishing, listening as Qi Daiyu shared amusing anecdotes from her days at the Qi residence.","Before long, Quan Fuhai led the palace attendants in. \"Your Majesty, shall the meal be served inside or...?\"","\"Set it up right here.\"","So, Quan Fuhai directed the attendants to replace the small table on the platform with a larger one, and dish after dish was laid upon it.","There were various types of dishes, but the ones that most delighted Qi Daiyu were the several plates of seafood.","Noticing her gaze, Quan Fuhai eagerly explained: \"These were just transported from the coastal area, extremely fresh. These items are troublesome to transport and difficult to preserve, hence they are rare in the capital. Jiangning is close to the coast; they can be delivered via waterways in just two hours, kept chilled with ice along the way, and were still alive upon arrival. To best bring out the flavor of these ingredients, even the chef was brought over from the coast.\"","Of course, that chef, upon learning he could cook for the Emperor, would have gladly brought his entire family.","Qi Daiyu sampled the various seafood. Her favorite was the drunken crab—not only was the meat deliciously fresh, but it also carried a rich aroma of wine.","Seeing her fondness for it, Jiang Yuan ordered a palace maid specifically to shell the crab for her.","Quan Fuhai stood to the side, wanting to speak but hesitating. To properly infuse the crab with flavor, this dish used premium white liquor. As far as he knew, Consort Hui had little tolerance for alcohol...","By the time a plate of drunken crab was nearly finished, Jiang Yuan finally noticed something was amiss, but it was too late. Across from him, Qi Daiyu's cheeks were slightly flushed, and her eyes held a hint of daze.","She herself didn't seem aware of her condition yet. Catching his gaze, she grinned at him dreamily.","Jiang Yuan frowned. \"Quan Fuhai, clear everything away.\" Worried she might be upset, he added, \"Crab is cooling in nature. Too much is not good.\"","Taking it all away just like that? Qi Daiyu pouted but did not protest, allowing the attendants to carry the table away.","Quan Fuhai hastily led everyone out.","With the obstruction between them gone, Qi Daiyu's eyes immediately fell upon the fishing rod beside Jiang Yuan and the empty fish basket, devoid of even a single fish.","She suddenly clutched her stomach, laughing heartily, and pointed at Jiang Yuan. \"Hahaha! Empty-handed fisherman!\"","Jiang Yuan didn't understand the meaning of \"Empty-handed fisherman,\" but he sensed mockery from Qi Daiyu's loud laughter. He narrowed his eyes and asked, \"What is an 'Empty-handed fisherman'?\"","The alcohol had greatly boosted Qi Daiyu's courage. She laughed heartily, \"An Empty-handed fisherman is someone who can't catch a single fish! Hahaha, Your Majesty, you're so lame! 'Lame' means... you're no good!\"","He was no good?","Jiang Yuan's face darkened instantly.","Looking at Qi Daiyu, who was laughing without a care for her image, he pulled her into his arms and asked through gritted teeth, \"Who's no good?\"","This movement made the dizziness hit harder. Qi Daiyu felt her mind go blank for a moment. She shook her head, trying to clear the double vision, but the images kept shifting—sometimes looking like Jiang Yuan, sometimes like a fish, then transforming into a butterfly, fluttering towards the lake.","\"Butterfly!\" Qi Daiyu tried to catch the butterfly and ended up slapping Jiang Yuan squarely on the face.","\"Qi! Dai! Yu!\" Jiang Yuan suddenly remembered years ago when this woman, drunk, had also slapped him. Now history was repeating itself!","Yet, the woman before him was completely unaware of what she had done, merely giggling foolishly.","But seeing her pure, unguarded smile, he found he couldn't stay angry.","After all these years, she truly hadn't changed a bit.","He scooped her up into his arms, carried her to the inner chamber, placed her on the bed, and removed her shoes and socks.","Thinking to make her more comfortable by taking off her outer robe, he had just undone her belt when her hand caught his.","Jiang Yuan looked up to see her eyes welling up with tears.","\"Sister Zhu, you came to see me?\"","Jiang Yuan: \"...?\"","Qi Daiyu suddenly wrapped her arms around his neck, sobbing, mumbling things like \"Sister Zhu, I've missed you so much,\" and then wailing, \"Your Majesty the Empress, let me tell you a secret, the Eldest Princess has a sweetheart!\"","One moment she was mistaking him for Si Yu, insisting on coaxing him to sleep; the next, she was nuzzling into his chest, calling him \"Mama.\"","Jiang Yuan: \"...\"","They say drunken words are sober thoughts. His Consort Hui certainly had a lot of people on her mind when she was drunk.","But as Jiang Yuan listened, he realized he hadn't heard his own name mentioned once.","So, he cupped Qi Daiyu's face, forcing her to look at him. \"Look clearly. Who am I?\"","Qi Daiyu blinked. The figure before her was severely distorted. She hesitated, \"A... Big Monkey?\"","He didn't understand the term, but he was sure it wasn't a compliment.","Jiang Yuan began contemplating how to punish Consort Hui.","Though utterly disoriented by the drink, Qi Daiyu somehow sensed the danger. She immediately clung to the \"Big Monkey's\" neck.","Rubbing her face against him, she murmured, \"Cuddles.\"","Quite the opportunist. Jiang Yuan raised an eyebrow.","\"Don't think this will make me let you off.\" His thumb pressed against Qi Daiyu's lips, gently rubbing. The rouge from her lips smudged onto her cheek, creating a vivid, alluring stain.","He hadn't had any particular intentions before, but now a fire had been stirred within him.","Jiang Yuan gripped Qi Daiyu's waist and turned, pinning her beneath him.","...","After their passion, the light of the setting sun shimmered on the lake, its reflection bouncing off the water and through the window, filling the room.","Satiated, Jiang Yuan held Qi Daiyu, quietly watching her sleeping face.","The effects of the wine hadn't fully worn off. The corners of her eyes were still red, and he knew they would be swollen tomorrow.","Thinking of all the people she had mumbled about while drunk, especially the Empress, Jiang Yuan's gaze turned dark.","The Empress had been very close to her, even teaching her how to manage palace affairs when the Empress's own life was nearing its end. Perhaps Qi Daiyu saw it as the Empress's trust in her, but Jiang Yuan knew better. While the Empress did trust her, she was also using her.","The more grateful Qi Daiyu felt towards the Empress, the more devoted she would be to the Eldest Princess and the Crown Prince.","The Empress had always been clever. She had known the Qi family would rise ever since he began favoring Qi Caishang. So, she treated Consort Hui better and better. Later, when he sent troops to the northern frontier and promoted military officers, the Empress keenly realized that the Qi family—with a son and a son-in-law both serving as military officers—would become the new nobility. And the Qi family had simple social connections, without complicated marital alliances, making them ideal loyal ministers.","If the Qi family could pledge loyalty to the Crown Prince, it would be a significant boost for him.","To win over the Qi family, Consort Hui was the perfect entry point.","He and the Empress had been husband and wife; they understood each other too well. Just as the Empress knew he had developed reservations after uncovering certain things, and thus no longer trusted him to wholeheartedly support the Crown Prince, choosing instead to use Consort Hui to pull in the Qi family, he was equally aware of the Empress's calculations.","He did not interfere with, and even tacitly allowed, the Empress's actions. After all, the Crown Prince was his chosen heir. Anything beneficial to the Crown Prince, he would not oppose—just as his own father had done for him.","The late Emperor had doted on Consort Yu, yet soon after designating him as heir, Consort Yu passed away—yes, the world believed it was Consort Yu's death that prompted the late Emperor to begin grooming him, the legitimate son of the Empress. Jiang Yuan had believed that too in his youth. It wasn't until he grew up and became an emperor and a father himself that he realized the truth: the late Emperor had chosen him as Crown Prince first, and then, for his safety, had ruthlessly eliminated Consort Yu, who was then the most favored consort in the harem.","Such was the cold, ruthless heart of an emperor.","But...","Jiang Yuan's hand slid to Qi Daiyu's smooth abdomen.","He knew Consort Hui had been injured before, but she had recovered fully.","Yet, despite sharing his bed for years, she had never conceived.","The Empress had been willing to trust her, to confidently entrust the Eldest Princess and Crown Prince to her care, to let her manage the Six Palaces, all based on one premise: she would not become pregnant and bear a prince who could threaten the Crown Prince's position.","Had she ever considered these hidden truths?","Gazing at the woman's peaceful sleeping face, Jiang Yuan's heart swelled with guilt.","It had been a year since the Empress passed away. Recently, there had been occasional memorials from court officials requesting the appointment of a new Empress.","Within the harem, few consorts were suitable to become the next Empress. Unless he selected someone from outside the palace, which Jiang Yuan was unwilling to do.","He and the Empress had been married since their youth. Although their relationship had changed over the years due to various factors, he was willing to give her respect and would always maintain her dignity—just as when the Empress died, he suspended court for a month, letting the whole world know the Emperor deeply cherished Empress Jingxian.","Thinking of this, Jiang Yuan gently woke Qi Daiyu and asked softly, \"Do you want to be Empress?\"","Qi Daiyu was utterly exhausted, her head throbbing dully. Hazily hearing Jiang Yuan's question, she answered without thinking, \"No! I absolutely don't want to!\"","Being Empress was so much work; she'd be crazy to want that. Besides, the position of Empress belonged to Her Majesty the Empress. It could only be hers.","It was the answer he expected. Jiang Yuan smiled.","Given her kind nature and her feelings for the late Empress, she had probably never even considered becoming the next Empress, likely never entertained the thought.","\"Then, be my Imperial Noble Consort,\" Jiang Yuan said quietly.","The Imperial Noble Consort, a position equivalent to a deputy empress, could oversee the harem when the empress's position was vacant. This would also silence the murmurs of the court.","Jiang Yuan: \"Speaking of which, your previous promotions all happened outside my expectations.\"","When she was promoted to Jieyu, it was for saving the Empress. When she became Consort Hui, it was for saving the Eldest Princess and with the Empress's strong support. When she was elevated to Consort Hui, it was because the Empress needed her to assist in managing the Six Palaces and had specifically requested the edict from him.","Jiang Yuan chuckled wryly. Despite her being arguably the most favored among the consorts, he had never once taken the initiative to promote her rank.","\"It seems the fault lies with me this time.\"","He offered a rare apology, though the inebriated woman failed to hear it.","Jiang Yuan didn't mind whether she heard him or not. \"Noble Consort Hui,\" he murmured, \"this time, I shall compensate you with a grand and lavish investiture ceremony.\""]},{"number":133,"title":"Chapter 133: Extra Story 09","paragraphs":["From the moment Jiang Sheng was born, he was the most noble legitimate son of the empress.","The starting point of his life was a destination that ninety-nine percent of the people in the world could never reach in their entire lives.","According to the words of Noble Consort Hui in the palace, his life was destined to be one of \"cool, domineering, wild, dazzling, smooth, and Long Aotian.\" Moreover, unlike the ordinary \"Long Aotian,\" he genuinely had a throne to inherit.","Jiang Sheng happily accepted \"Long Aotian\" as his childhood nickname.","Aotian, looking down upon all heroes and rivaling the heavens—what a mighty and imposing name, perfectly suited to his aura.","Yes, despite Jiang Sheng's outwardly serious, composed, and calm demeanor, leading outsiders to marvel, \"The Crown Prince is as steady as Mount Tai at such a young age, truly a born prodigy!\"","In reality, he was a secretly eccentric, chuunibyou, narcissistic, scheming, and clingy monster—this was also Noble Consort Hui's assessment of him.","When he was still very young, Jiang Sheng only displayed the single character trait of \"being privately clingy.\" At that time, his birth mother, the empress, was still alive, and he had three targets for his clinginess: his mother, Consort Hui, and his eldest imperial sister.","Being clingy with his mother required perfect timing and measure because she placed immense importance on him and was dedicated to cultivating him into the most perfect prince. How could a perfect prince exhibit such childish behavior as being clingy? Even though he was indeed a child back then. Therefore, he could only be clingy when his mother was in a good mood, using it to get what he wanted.","With Consort Hui, he didn't need to watch the clock. According to Consort Hui herself, she was a \"face connoisseur\" and a \"baby creature enthusiast\" (where did Consort Hui always come up with these strange terms?), utterly incapable of resisting an adorable youngster like him. He only needed to whimper a couple of times or hug Consort Hui for a cuddle, and she would never refuse anything he wanted.","However, Consort Hui was cunning! If he wanted to eat more sweets, she would divide the usual portion into several smaller plates to trick him, and being young, he truly believed he had eaten more. Or, if he proposed other ideas, Consort Hui would always suggest something else that interested him to divert his attention, and then he would forget his original thought.","Jiang Sheng's favorite was being clingy with his eldest imperial sister. His eldest sister was determined to protect their mother and him, granting his every wish almost without fail. Jiang Sheng grew accustomed to her doting. It lasted until the night after their mother passed away, when the phoenix coffin was sent to the imperial mausoleum. He saw his eldest sister, who had been putting on a strong front and hadn't cried, holding her \"Mianmian\" and silently weeping, her eyes red and swollen, her lips marked with bite impressions.","From that moment on, Jiang Sheng never acted clingy with his eldest sister again. He began learning to be good to her, just as she had been to him.","As he grew older, the \"clingy\" aspect of his personality became hidden, while simultaneously, \"chuunibyou narcissism\" proliferated. Jiang Sheng didn't quite understand what \"chuunibyou\" meant; he knew what \"narcissism\" was, but he refused to admit to it.","He believed himself to be accomplished in both civil and military arts, a towering figure of talent and strategy, as handsome as Pan An, as mighty as Xiang Yu, with a heart encompassing the world—was this narcissism? Clearly, this was simply the truth.","After all, he had such a heroic and divine emperor for a father; it was only natural that he, too, was a heaven-sent prodigy.","But soon, Jiang Sheng began to doubt himself—he started attending court to observe governance.","By then, he was already the Crown Prince, second only to the emperor, the chosen successor. His father, the emperor, had decreed that he attend court daily to observe state affairs.","It was only after attending court that Jiang Sheng realized the kind of treacherous environment his father lived in every day. Those usually respectful and smiling faces gradually took on a sinister and cunning aspect in Jiang Sheng's mind. Among them were good officials who served the country and its people, but they all had private interests. They formed cliques for personal gain, attacked rival factions, and treated the world as a chessboard and the common people as pawns to consolidate their own power and benefits!","They even dared to encroach upon imperial authority!","Unforgivable! Heinous beyond measure!","During his initial days at court, Jiang Sheng burned with inner fury daily. For the first time, he felt the loneliness and chilling fear of being surrounded by wolves. His father was the emperor, the most exalted existence under heaven, and the entire Zhao Kingdom belonged to their family. Yet, even someone as mighty as his father could not act entirely as he wished.","During that period, even the gaze Jiang Sheng directed at his most respected Grand Tutor was tinged with vigilance and suspicion.","This mindset and these feelings persisted for two years. Every day, he watched his father's actions, pondered the reasons behind them, and silently absorbed the lessons. Thus, he came to understand why his father had him attend court.","His father was teaching him the art of rulership.","A ruler needed schemes, methods, and resolute decisiveness—all of which could be trained in a relatively short time. Only the most crucial skill of \"balance\" required years of trial and error, experimentation, and accumulation.","Officials are human, and humans have private interests. Private interests give rise to benefits, and people band together because of these shared benefits.","What his father wanted him to learn was to find a balance among these interest groups to consolidate imperial power.","The immersion in court sessions allowed Jiang Sheng to mature rapidly. He became increasingly adept at not letting his emotions show on his face, hiding all his ambitions and desires in the deepest recesses of his heart.","He learned to be cold-hearted, he learned indifference, he learned solitude.","He remembered one day when he and his eldest sister were dining with Consort Hui. Consort Hui suddenly fell silent, looked at him for a long time, and then said, \"You are becoming more and more like your father.\"","Was being like his father a bad thing?","He was destined to become the supreme emperor, revered by all, just like his father.","He should resemble his father.","For Jiang Sheng, his father was not as close as his mother, his eldest sister, or Consort Hui had been. But if he had to choose the person he admired most in his heart, it would undoubtedly be his father—who in the palace didn't feel the same way?","Soon, in the year Jiang Sheng turned eighteen, he faced the same dilemma his father had at that age.","He needed to select a Crown Princess.","The Crown Princess, the future empress—such an important position required the most meticulous selection of candidates.","But Jiang Sheng was luckier than his father had been.","The present Zhao Kingdom commanded respect from all directions, was powerful and prosperous, with imperial authority firmly established. There were no internal troubles or external threats, and he was the Crown Prince firmly supported by his father. Therefore, Jiang Sheng did not particularly need a powerful maternal clan to consolidate his position.","But that didn't mean he couldn't have one, nor did it mean the Crown Princess would come from a lowly or insignificant family. The imperial family cared most about face.","Jiang Sheng's luck lay only in the fact that he could choose a more personally agreeable young lady from a broader range of candidates.","The selection process lasted three months, and in the end, three choices were placed before Jiang Sheng.","The first young woman is named He Shuying, the granddaughter of Master He Yuan, Dean of Maoshan Academy. He Yuan himself once achieved the highest honor in the imperial examinations, served as the Crown Prince's Grand Tutor, later left his official post to establish Maoshan Academy, cultivating scholars for the realm. Although he holds no official rank or noble title, his literary reputation is extremely prominent within the Zhao Kingdom, and many court officials respectfully address him as \"Master He.\"","With the Northern Li pacified, the court will undoubtedly promote civil officials for many years to come. Enfeoffing He Yuan's granddaughter as Crown Princess could help Jiang Sheng win the hearts of the kingdom's literati.","The second young woman is Qi Shutao. She is the granddaughter of Minister of Revenue Qi Caishang, the eldest daughter of Tiger Guard Commander Qi Chuchu, and also the niece of Imperial Noble Consort Hui. Qi Caishang is a key minister his father cultivated to assist him, and with the connection through Imperial Noble Consort Hui, the Qi family are staunch supporters of the Crown Prince. Barring unforeseen events, Qi Caishang will be a pillar of his court upon ascension. The Tiger Guard is also of great importance. The Qi family boasts strength in both civil and military affairs. Enfeoffing Qi Shutao as Crown Princess would be like adding wings to a tiger for Jiang Sheng—an enhancement to an already strong position.","Furthermore, with no Empress in the palace, only the Imperial Noble Consort, acting with the authority of a deputy, manages the six palaces. According to protocol, once a Crown Princess is established, the authority over the inner palace should be transferred to her. If it were someone else, disputes over this authority would likely arise (though Jiang Sheng suspected Imperial Noble Consort Hui might actually be quite happy to relinquish it, given her temperament). But if the Crown Princess were Imperial Noble Consort Hui's own niece, she could presumably integrate into the inner palace swiftly.","The third young woman is Jiang Yuelan. In terms of lineage, Jiang Yuelan's is actually the most prestigious. The Jiang family is an established aristocratic clan with deep roots and includes the meritorious Marshal Jiang. Where she slightly falls short compared to the other two is that her father is only a minor official, the kind obtained through monetary contribution, holding no real power.","However, Jiang Yuelan's background as a descendant of the Empress's clan is her greatest advantage.","Jiang Yuelan served as the Eldest Princess's study companion, and Jiang Sheng had met her a few times, leaving a favorable impression. Jiang Sheng had always known how much his late mother cared for the Jiang family. Currently, Jiang Ruheng is the only Jiang family member of note in court. If he were to marry Jiang Yuelan as Crown Princess, the Jiang family would surely regain its former prosperity.","But...","Perhaps his pressures weren't as heavy as his father's in his time, or perhaps he had listened to too many of the romantic tales Imperial Noble Consort Hui loved to recount, Jiang Sheng still hoped that his future Crown Princess would be someone who truly understood his heart and shared his sentiments.","So, did he have a woman he admired in his heart?","When this question arose, a mischievously clever figure surfaced in Jiang Sheng's mind.","On this day, Jiang Sheng went to the Palace of Eternal Spring.","The Palace of Eternal Spring was located in a remote part of the palace grounds, yet it was the liveliest place. Consorts, princes, and princesses all loved to visit, solely because Imperial Noble Consort Hui, who resided there, was always concocting some novel amusement.","In Jiang Sheng's memory, the Palace of Eternal Spring was a place of beauty. Many happy hours of his childhood were spent there. Back then, after finishing the studies assigned by his mother, his greatest anticipation was for his eldest sister to take him to the Palace of Eternal Spring to play. Once there, he would nestle in Imperial Noble Consort Hui's embrace, eating sweet pastries while listening to her stories about the Great Sage.","Entering the palace and seeing the familiar setup in the courtyard, Jiang Sheng couldn't help but smile.","The Palace of Eternal Spring was full of children's playthings: swings, a trampoline, a slide, even a small sandpit. In the past, it was for them to play (Jiang Sheng knew Imperial Noble Consort Hui would secretly play too); now it was for his fifth brother, fourth sister, and fifth sister.","As soon as he appeared, the large white dog named \"Batiao,\" who had been lying under the osmanthus tree, ran over, wagging its tail excitedly.","Batiao was Siyu's dog, now almost ten years old—an elderly dog. Batiao had a very gentle temperament, especially fond of bustling activity. It used to love circling around the children; now, older and with less energy, it preferred lying under the tree watching them play.","And in the osmanthus tree, there was a plump orange tabby cat named \"Liutong.\" This cat was acquired by Imperial Noble Consort Hui after Batiao, notoriously greedy, and loved to jump into the tree for a nap after eating.","\"A happy life with both a cat and a dog\"—that was Imperial Noble Consort Hui's reason for getting the cat, though Jiang Sheng didn't quite understand why having both meant happiness.","\"Batiao, where is Imperial Noble Consort Hui?\" Jiang Sheng asked.","Batiao barked once towards the main hall, then barked twice more.","\"There are guests?\" Jiang Sheng understood Batiao's meaning.","Then Lizhi, the maid attending Imperial Noble Consort Hui, came out smiling to greet him. \"Greetings, Your Highness the Crown Prince. The Eldest Prince's wife has brought the young Commandery Princess to pay respects and is currently keeping Her Ladyship company. Consort Xian and Consort De are also present.\"","Jiang Sheng understood.","Two years ago, his father enfeoffed his eldest brother, Jiang Hao, as the Prince of Chu. That same year, Jiang Hao married Lady Fan. Earlier this year, Lady Fan gave birth to a daughter. As the family's first grandchild, she was greatly doted on by his father, who personally bestowed upon her the title of Commandery Princess.","This Lady Fan was from the same clan as Consort De, Fan Ningyan, within the palace. Whenever Lady Fan came to pay respects to Imperial Noble Consort Hui, Consort De would always come to the Palace of Eternal Spring.","Jiang Sheng entered the main hall, greeting the elders present with his usual composure.","To Consort Xian, he said, \"I noticed my third brother has developed blisters at the corner of his mouth these past few days, likely due to the autumn dryness. Consort Xian might consider sending him some loquat syrup to clear the heat.\"","Nie Zhiyu had been promoted to Consort Xian six years prior. Hearing Jiang Sheng's words, she complained, \"It must be from eating too much roasted mutton. Ever since returning from the autumn hunt, he demands a dish of roasted mutton on the table every single day. No wonder he's getting heated!\"","She then smilingly requested of Jiang Sheng, \"Please, Crown Prince, help me admonish him on my behalf. He pays less and less heed to my words these days, but he will certainly listen to you.\"","Jiang Sheng agreed with a smile.","Simultaneously, he inwardly admired her. No wonder Consort Xian's path in the palace had been smooth since her entry, and his third brother had grown up safely. Consort Xian's skill with words was truly remarkable.","Among princes, no matter how close they were in childhood, friction was almost inevitable as they grew up. This was especially true for the first few princes, whose age gaps were not large.","Among Jiang Sheng's brothers, the eldest prince, though holding the \"firstborn\" status, had a mother whose virtue was flawed and a maternal family exiled far away. His father's early enfeoffment of him as a prince made his stance clear: the eldest prince was destined to have no claim to the throne. The eldest prince himself was simple-minded, content to be a carefree prince, so their relationship remained quite good.","The fifth prince was the youngest, just over six years old. His birth mother, Consort Li, enjoyed imperial favor but came from a lowly background, making the fifth prince's chances in any succession struggle minuscule.","The only threats to Jiang Sheng were his third and fourth brothers.","Fortunately, the third brother's mother, Consort Xian Nie Zhiyu, only desired a peaceful life. She had taught her son since childhood to respect the Crown Prince and to follow his second elder brother in all matters.","Jiang Sheng had once asked Imperial Noble Consort Hui, didn't Consort Xian have any ambition?","After thinking for a moment, Lady Hui's reply was: \"Perhaps because her own path here was difficult, she only wishes for her child to live a safe and uneventful life?\"","Later, Jiang Sheng specifically inquired and learned that Consort Xian's life had indeed been full of hardships. Originally the granddaughter of the Prince Xiang's household, she discovered she had been switched at birth just before her betrothal was finalized. She returned to her biological Nie family for only a few days before being sent to the palace for the imperial selection.","After giving birth to the Third Prince, both the Prince Xiang's household and the Nie family sought audience with Consort Xian, but she refused to see them all, even forbidding them from contacting the Third Prince. She did not even send anyone from the palace to offer condolences when the old Princess Consort of Prince Xiang's household, who had raised Consort Xian, passed away.","Consort Xian severed her own familial ties, yet she did not wish for her son to fight with his brothers. Therefore, she instilled this teaching in the Third Prince from a young age.","Nowadays, the Third Prince is at his most rebellious age, sometimes not even listening to Consort Xian's words, yet he dares not disobey his Second Brother, the Crown Prince.","As for the Fourth Prince... Jiang Sheng was unwilling to discuss him.","After paying his respects to the elders, Jiang Sheng then turned his gaze to his little niece. \"My eldest brother boasts in my ear all day about how well-behaved his daughter is. Now that I've seen her, it seems he wasn't exaggerating.\" With that, he took a jade pendant from his waist and presented it as a meeting gift for his little niece.","The wife of the First Prince accepted it on her daughter's behalf and expressed her thanks.","Qi Daiyu teased him: \"Then why don't you hurry up and settle on a marriage arrangement?\"","Jiang Sheng clasped his hands: \"It is precisely for this matter that I have come.\"","This indicated he had something to discuss. Nie Zhiyu tactfully found an excuse to lead Consort De and the First Prince's wife away, giving the two space to talk.","Qi Daiyu was curious. \"Have you decided on someone?\"","She also found it strange in her heart. If he had chosen, he should have reported directly to the Emperor. Why come to the Changchun Palace instead?","Could it be...","\"The person I wish to marry is connected to you, Lady Hui. Naturally, I should first seek your opinion.\"","Qi Daiyu paused. \"Is it Shu Tao?\"","To her surprise, Jiang Sheng shook his head.","\"Then who?\" Who else could it be, related to her?","Jiang Sheng, unusually, showed a hint of bashfulness. \"It is the daughter of Commander Zhou of the Huguang Regional Military Commission.\"","After hearing this, Qi Daiyu was silent for a long while before finally saying softly, \"When did you ever meet Ya Shu?\"","Shu Tao had accompanied the Wan family to palace banquets before, so Jiang Sheng might have had a chance to see her. But Ya Shu had never been to the palace. Jiang Sheng couldn't possibly have developed feelings for Ya Shu without reason; they must have met privately.","Jiang Sheng: \"During the southern inspection tour to Jiangning, when you returned to the Qi family home.\"","Qi Daiyu was taken aback. There was such an incident. On the fourth day of her stay at the Qi residence, the Crown Prince had once visited incognito, staying only for an evening meal before leaving. But that was so long ago!","Moreover, she stared at him wide-eyed, \"Ya Shu was only six years old then!\"","Jiang Sheng immediately understood her misunderstanding and quickly waved his hands. \"I meant that was the first time I met A Shu... Miss Zhou.\" He smiled wryly. \"Miss Zhou was just a child then. How could I possibly have had any such thoughts for her...\" He himself was just a child back then.","However, their first meeting had indeed left a deep impression on Jiang Sheng.","That little girl who was climbing the crape myrtle tree to rob a bird's nest, only to be startled by him and fall from the tree—if he hadn't reacted quickly and caught her, she would have surely fallen and cried.","\"After that, it was after returning to the capital. Over the years, Si Yu often visited the Qi residence. When I went to pick her up to return to the palace... I also happened to see her a few times.\"","Happened to? Qi Daiyu didn't believe that for a second. Her gossipy heart stirred, but she also knew Jiang Sheng definitely wouldn't tell the whole truth. It seemed she would have to find an opportunity to ask Si Yu, or ask Ya Shu directly.","Although she now understood the cause and effect, Qi Daiyu was still hesitant. \"But Ya Shu is not even fourteen yet this year. She's too young.\" Still a child. She was unwilling to let her niece marry so early.","Jiang Sheng, however, said, \"I am willing to wait.\" Since his heart was set, he had naturally considered everything thoroughly. \"I will request His Majesty the Emperor to grant the marriage first. Then, I would ask you, Lady, to bring Miss Zhou into the palace under the identity of the future Crown Princess, to keep her by your side and provide guidance for two years. After that, the grand wedding ceremony can be held.\"","After all, once the Crown Princess is chosen, palace instructors would be sent to teach her palace rules and etiquette. Since A Shu is your niece, Lady Hui, why not bring her directly into the palace? A Shu is young, which is perfect for learning and gaining experience ahead of time. With your protection, Lady Hui, she certainly won't be wronged.","Qi Daiyu hadn't expected he had already thought this far ahead.","Two years later, Zhou Yashu would be sixteen. Though still quite young, in this world, it is a perfectly normal age to marry. Even if not as Crown Princess, the Zhou family would arrange another marriage for her.","Thinking this, Qi Daiyu found it hard to object further.","She asked again, \"I've watched you grow up. If you have a girl you care for, I am naturally happy and would not interfere. But Ya Shu is my niece. I must ask you one more thing: you wish to make Ya Shu your Crown Princess. Does Ya Shu know about this?\"","The subtext of this question was: You care for Ya Shu, but does Ya Shu care for you?","Qi Daiyu: \"One-sided affection is ultimately not as good as mutual affection, right?\"","Qi Daiyu didn't know what connection existed between the Crown Prince and Zhou Yashu, but she feared this might all be just the Crown Prince's unilateral feelings, which could trap Ya Shu in a lifetime without freedom.","Therefore, she wanted to give Ya Shu a choice. If Ya Shu was unwilling, she would use all her past rapport to stop the Crown Prince from marrying Ya Shu. If Ya Shu also cared for the Crown Prince...","At the very least, Ya Shu would possess the sincere heart of a young man.","Qi Daiyu didn't know what Jiang Sheng did, but a month later, Ya Shu, through Si Yu, requested an audience to see her in the palace.","During this meeting, Qi Daiyu met the grown-up Ya Shu, lively and elegant.","The young girl, her ears tinged red, told her: \"Brother Sheng... is very good.\"","In those clear, intelligent eyes was the unique longing and sweetness of a girl tasting love for the first time.","All the words—\"Being Crown Princess is not as simple as you think,\" \"Have you considered that when the Crown Prince ascends the throne, he will have other consorts,\" \"The Crown Prince is not like your father; he won't promise you 'one man, one woman for a lifetime'\"—all these words clogged in Qi Daiyu's throat as she looked into those eyes.","She couldn't say them.","Perhaps even if she said them, the girl at this moment wouldn't listen.","So Qi Daiyu could only smile and say, \"Good.\"","That day, Zhou Yashu smiled especially brightly. Leaning on her aunt's shoulder, she softly recounted her past encounters with Jiang Sheng. She just didn't understand why, even though her aunt was smiling, she could see a hidden sadness on her aunt's face.","In the twenty-fifth year of the Yanli era, the Crown Prince married Lady Zhou, who took up residence in the Eastern Palace."]},{"number":134,"title":"Chapter 134: Extra Chapter 010","paragraphs":["Siyu had known since childhood that her mother was not her birth mother.","Her birth mother was the late Consort Zhuang.","Her mother had never hidden this from her; in fact, she often spoke of her birth mother.","Every time Siyu saw the radiant smile on her mother's face when she spoke of her birth mother, she would wonder: what kind of person was her birth mother, to be remembered so fondly for so many years?","But if you asked how much she missed her birth mother, the truth was, not overwhelmingly so. She had received so much love that the regret of her birth mother not being by her side was largely filled.","Siyu believed she must be the happiest child in the palace.","The princes, of course, had it tougher. Their education was always much stricter than that of the princesses. Although palace rules stated that princes must begin daily studies from the age of five, Siyu knew that her brothers and younger brothers were all tutored by their own mothers from the age of two or three, already immersed in the arduous sea of learning.","Among the princesses, take the Eldest Princess, for example. She had been enfeoffed as the Princess of Yong'an since childhood and even had her own fiefdom. But the Empress placed high hopes on her; every day she had to study her lessons, learn the qin, and practice archery. It was truly hard work.","Then there was the Second Princess, who always seemed burdened with worries. Siyu rarely saw her laugh heartily.","But she was different. Her mother never had high demands of her. A phrase her mother often said was: \"You are fortunate to be a princess of a powerful nation. You can do most of the things that the vast majority of women in this world cannot. I ask nothing of you, only that you do as you wish and find joy in what you do.\"","Siyu understood the meaning behind her mother's words.","Her mother had told her many stories, some set in fictional dynasties, where women were often at the mercy of fate. Even princesses could suffer tragic destinies due to weak nations and foolish emperors.","She was different. The Zhao Kingdom was powerful, with myriad states paying tribute. It would only be a matter of her setting her sights on a prince from another kingdom and having him brought to her; there was no possibility of her being sent away for a political marriage. Her father, the Emperor, though he valued the princes more, would never mistreat the princesses. In fact, because princesses did not have to inherit the great enterprise of the state, they were indulged and treated even more favorably.","She truly was fortunate, Siyu thought.","This fortune was not just because of her status as a princess, but also because she had a very, very good mother.","Siyu couldn't quite articulate what made her mother better than the other consorts, but she simply felt that her mother was different from all the other ladies in the palace—no, from all the women in this world.","What Siyu felt most deeply was her mother's attitude towards the Emperor.","No one was not in awe of the Emperor. Even the Crown Prince brother was full of reverence and caution when facing their father.","Naturally, her mother was also in awe of the Emperor, but Siyu felt that her mother's awe was like an ant's fear of a colossal creature, like a person's fear of life and death itself.","What her mother feared was the power in the Emperor's hands, not the Emperor himself.","Siyu remembered once asking her mother about this in confusion. At that time, a look of nostalgia and confidence, never seen before, appeared on her mother's face. Then her mother asked in return: \"Do you know Marx?\"","Siyu was bewildered.","Who was Marx? A foreigner? Siyu knew of foreigners; there were foreign craftsmen in the palace, and their names were all very strange.","Her mother asked again: \"Do you know communism?\"","Siyu was even more confused.","What kind of 'ism'? And what was an 'ism' anyway?","Her mother continued: \"Do you know the Five-Starred Red Flag?\"","This Siyu knew: \"The flag with stars on it?\"","Her mother smiled without answering.","Siyu, unable to figure it out and unwilling to give up, pestered her mother for a long time. Finally, her mother said: \"Perhaps there exists a world like this: a place without distinctions between nobles, commoners, and slaves, where everyone is equal. Regardless of gender, everyone can achieve merit, establish careers, realize their own value, and do what they wish to do.\"","\"How could such a world possibly exist?\" Siyu blurted out.","\"Why couldn't it?\" her mother retorted.","Have you actually seen such a world? Such a question surfaced in Siyu's mind, but she did not voice it.","She had a premonition that asking such a question would sadden her mother.","Siyu's mouth hung open. She didn't rush to refute, but after thinking for a long time, she said, \"When the Great Way prevails, the world belongs to all?\"","She hesitated, adding: \"But that's just a beautiful ideal.\" People were born into distinctions of nobility and baseness. If everyone were equal, how would nobles like them find their place? Moreover, since ancient times, only men studied and achieved merit; women managed the household and raised children. How could women achieve merit and establish careers?","Siyu couldn't understand, yet she faintly felt that the world her mother described was beautiful.","Her mother said: \"Then do you think, if such a world truly existed, you would still fear your father?\"","Siyu fell silent.","If it were really as her mother said, with everyone equal, and her father no longer the most revered person under heaven, no longer arbitrarily holding power over life and death, then naturally he wouldn't be so terrifying.","But such thoughts were too radical. Siyu didn't dare to dwell on them further.","Siyu voluntarily forgot this conversation. Young as she was, she knew such talk was better not spread abroad.","Yet perhaps without even realizing it herself, this dialogue had a profound impact on her soul.","As she grew older, Siyu's troubles also began to multiply.","Changchun Palace was the place most beloved by the children in the palace. Every one of Siyu's siblings had enjoyed a happy childhood there, and Siyu got along very well with all of them.","Before, she was the youngest in the palace. Everyone yielded to her and loved to tease her. But after the Fourth Prince was born, things changed—she could tease the Fourth Prince now.","The Fourth Prince's mother was Consort Ye Qiong, the Consort of Jing. Consort Ye also often visited Changchun Palace, but Siyu's mother was not particularly warm towards her. Consort Ye never seemed angered by this. Siyu vaguely sensed a hint of ingratiation in Consort Ye's attitude towards her mother.","As a junior, it wasn't her place to inquire into the affairs of adults. Naturally, Siyu was biased towards her own mother, so she was only close to Consort Xian Nie, Concubine Li, and others, maintaining a neutral distance from Consort Ye.","However, this subtle ingratiation from Consort Ye gradually faded as the Fourth Prince grew older.","Consort Ye visited Changchun Palace less and less frequently, and the Fourth Prince also stopped coming as often.","Several times, Siyu clearly saw the Fourth Prince on the palace path outside Changchun Palace. Just as she was about to greet him, he would spot her, turn around, and run away.","Siyu was troubled. She shared this trouble with the Eldest Princess, but the Eldest Princess advised her, \"Have less contact with the Fourth Prince.\"","Siyu was stunned. She had never expected to hear such words from the Eldest Princess, who always valued harmony and affection among siblings the most.","She wanted to ask more, but the Second Princess stopped her.","Second Princess privately told her: \"Since Fourth Imperial Brother entered the court, he has often vied for supremacy with the Crown Prince.\"","Imperial princes enter the court at fourteen. In the short span of a year since Fourth Prince entered the court, he had already shown discord with the Crown Prince on four occasions.","It was then that Siyu understood that Concubine Ye's previous distance had been an early sign.","Siyu knew very well her mother's respect for the Empress, her care for Eldest Princess and the Crown Prince. Her mother and Concubine Ye, she and Fourth Imperial Brother, were destined to drift apart.","The following several years were the most oppressive of Siyu's life.","First, barbarian enemies invaded the southern border. Eldest Princess led the Red-Tassel Guard's female generals to the southern front to meet the enemy. Though they bravely defeated the invaders, Eldest Princess herself was injured and bedridden for half a year before she could walk again.","Later, Second Princess got married, but just three days later, Concubine An in the palace passed away. Second Princess was heartbroken. A month later, news of a pregnancy came, but Second Princess's condition was too poor, and the child was not carried to term.","Soon after, Eldest Imperial Brother took a wife, and Crown Prince Brother also became engaged to a Crown Princess.","Of course, these were actually happy events. At least the little niece brought Siyu much joy. The Crown Princess was also her familiar Anshu.","Anshu lived in the palace for two years, residing in the Changchun Palace. Siyu kept her company every day, and their relationship grew closer and closer.","At the same time, the relationship between Crown Prince Brother and Fourth Imperial Brother grew increasingly tense and hostile.","Siyu once asked her mother: \"Why doesn't Father Emperor mediate their relationship?\"","Her mother replied: \"Your father also needs to test the Crown Prince's capabilities.\"","Siyu had heard of a southern custom called \"gu-raising,\" which involved placing various insects together to fight until only one survived.","She felt her father's method was no different from \"gu-raising.\"","A chill ran through Siyu's entire body.","In Siyu's view, Fourth Imperial Brother contending with Crown Prince Brother was a foolish choice. Crown Prince Brother was intelligent and benevolent, and the legitimate heir of the imperial family. That Father Emperor had long ago established him as Crown Prince showed his intentions clearly. Given that, why contend with Crown Prince Brother?","Wouldn't it be better to be a carefree prince, like Eldest Imperial Brother or Third Imperial Brother?","And Concubine Ye, why didn't she advise Fourth Imperial Brother?","During that time, the atmosphere in the palace was very tense. All inspections in Changchun Palace became stricter. Her mother even sent Aunt Yanhe and Xiao Li to the Eastern Palace to oversee Crown Prince Brother's food, clothing, and other matters.","Her mother's supervision of her also became unprecedentedly strict. She and Anshu couldn't even leave the gates of Changchun Palace.","For three whole months, Father Emperor and Crown Prince Brother did not visit Changchun Palace—a situation Siyu had never experienced before.","Three months later, she was finally allowed to go out. But then she learned that Fourth Imperial Brother had been demoted to a commoner and confined to the Southern Mountain Retreat, while Concubine Ye had \"suddenly caught a chill and passed away.\"","In the heat of summer, Concubine Ye caught a chill?","Siyu watched her mother stand under the osmanthus tree in the courtyard for a very, very long time.","She quietly walked over and heard her mother murmuring, \"I wonder if you would regret your initial choice, knowing this outcome?\"","Siyu guessed the \"you\" in her mother's words referred to Concubine Ye.","She silently wiped the tears from the corner of her eye and leaned against her mother's back.","The princesses of Siyu's generation seemed to marry rather late.","Eldest Princess, needless to say, finally had Jiang Huai become her consort when she was twenty-three.","Second Princess also didn't marry until she was twenty.","When Siyu was eighteen, her mother secretly asked if she had anyone in mind.","Siyu shook her head frantically. She had only two hobbies in life: delicious food and gossip.","The former was probably inherited from her birth mother, the latter influenced by her adoptive mother.","Marriage? After hearing so many stories from her mother, ordinary men simply couldn't catch her eye.","Fortunately, she was a princess, with a mother who doted on her, a father who couldn't defy her mother, a future emperor who was her fond older brother, and a future empress who was her cousin.","If she didn't marry, no one would dare comment.","But when fate arrives, no one can stop it.","It was an utterly ordinary day. Siyu took her fourth and fifth younger sisters out of the palace to see the world. It coincided with the parade of new imperial examination graduates. Sitting by the window on the second floor of the capital's largest restaurant, Baiwei Tower, Siyu's eyes immediately fell on the most handsome man in the parade.","Later, she investigated and found the man's name was Cheng Ke, the new Tanhua (Third Place Graduate), originally from Yuzhou.","Yuzhou? Siyu knew that was her birth mother's hometown. Her name \"Siyu\" originated from there.","Siyu's interest in Cheng Ke grew even greater. But having heard so many of her mother's stories, she worried Cheng Ke might also be a social climber, or that he might have had a sweetheart back home but yielded to her princess status.","So Siyu first sent people to Yuzhou to investigate Cheng Ke thoroughly, checking all his family connections and social dealings, confirming he had no childhood sweethearts, close female friends, fiancées, or unattainable loves.","Then, borrowing from storybook plots, she disguised herself as a man, pretending to be a young eunuch following Third Imperial Brother to observe Cheng Ke's character up close.","People in the palace could hardly bear to watch her antics, but her father, thinking she finally had a chance to marry after finding someone she liked, didn't stop her. Instead, he had everyone help.","After accidentally revealing her female identity once, Siyu then claimed she was a young lady from a princely household, a cousin of Third Prince.","Cheng Ke believed it.","As they spent more time together, Siyu increasingly sensed Cheng Ke's growing affection for her.","But Siyu still didn't dare confirm Cheng Ke's sincerity. Her mother noticed her dilemma and spoke to her father.","The next day, her father summoned Cheng Ke to the palace, saying he intended to arrange a marriage between Cheng Ke and a palace princess.","Siyu didn't expect Cheng Ke to refuse so firmly. Even when her father promised \"you may still serve as an official after wedding the princess,\" Cheng Ke remained unmoved.","Her father asked if Cheng Ke already had someone in mind.","Cheng Ke answered \"yes,\" but refused to give the lady's name, fearing it might damage her reputation.","Only when her father mentioned her false identity did Cheng Ke finally admit it.","Behind a screen wall, Siyu's face flushed crimson with shyness. Turning, she saw her mother's eyes filled with smiles.","Feeling awkward, she acted coquettishly, tugging at her mother's sleeve.","She heard her mother say: \"Didn't you always want to go out when you were little? After you marry, go see Yuzhou.\"","Siyu was stunned, then her eyes welled up with tears.","Her birth mother's greatest regret in life was being unable to return to her hometown.","By letting her go to Yuzhou, her mother was allowing her to see her birth mother's homeland in her stead.","But Siyu very much wanted to ask her mother: What about your hometown?","Not the external Qi family, but your true hometown, that free and equal hometown.","Siyu ultimately did not ask.","Just like in the past, she didn't want to sadden her mother."]}]);
